sc exit\",\n   134\t        fit(displayWorkspace),\n   135\t        \"Load project instructions\",\n   136\t        fit(projectFile),\n   137\t        \"Trust saved for future workspace files.\",\n   138\t        \"Rules/integrations require trust.\",\n   139\t        \"Default mode follows trust.\",\n   140\t        \"Trusted: auto · untrusted: review\",\n   141\t        \"Explicit mode still applies.\",\n   142\t        ...(statusMessage ? [fit(statusMessage)] : []),\n   143\t        \"\",\n   144\t        ...rows,\n   145\t      ].join(\"\\n\"));\n   146\t    };\n   147\t\n   148\t    const finish = (decision: WorkspaceTrustDecision) => {\n   149\t      if (complete) return;\n   150\t      complete = true;\n   151\t      input.removeListener(\"keypress\", onKeypress);\n   152\t      input.removeListener(\"close\", onClose);\n   153\t      try { input.setRawMode(oldRawMode); } catch {}\n   154\t      if (decision === \"exit\") {\n   155\t        try { input.pause(); } catch {}\n#!/usr/bin/env node\nimport { Command } from \"commander\";\nimport * as path from \"node:path\";\nimport * as fs from \"node:fs\";\nimport { execSync, spawnSync } from \"node:child_process\";\nimport { fileURLToPath } from \"node:url\";\nimport { AutonomousAgent } from \"./agent.js\";\nimport { ApplicationCore } from \"./core/app.js\";\nimport { InteractiveRepl } from \"./repl.js\";\nimport { LocalLlmClient } from \"./client.js\";\nimport { SessionManager } from \"./session.js\";\nimport { SkillManager } from \"./skills.js\";\nimport { McpClientManager } from \"./mcp.js\";\nimport { PluginManager } from \"./plugins.js\";\nimport { HarnessConfig } from \"./types.js\";\nimport { FlightPlayer } from \"./flight.js\";\nimport { WorktreeManager } from \"./worktree.js\";\nimport { HunkStager } from \"./stager.js\";\nimport { BenchmarkEvaluator } from \"./evaluator.js\";\nimport { SynthesizerEngine } from \"./synthesizer.js\";\nimport { BrowserDriver } from \"./browser.js\";\nimport { KnowledgeGraph } from \"./knowledge.js\";\nimport { TaskStateNotFoundError } from \"./core/state.js\";\nimport { buildConfig as buildConfigOrThrow, loadEnvironment } from \"./config.js\";\nimport { describeTarget, registerProviderCommands } from \"./provider_cli.js\";\nimport { UsageLedger } from \"./usage.js\";\nimport { DOCTOR_EXIT, DOCTOR_SCHEMA_VERSION, doctorExitCode, redactDiagnostic, renderDoctorJson, renderDoctorText, runDoctor, runRepairs } from \"./doctor.js\";\nimport { promptWorkspaceTrust } from \"./startup_trust.js\";\n\nfunction collectDeliverableFile(value: string, previous: string[] = []): string[] {\n  return [...previous, value];\n}\n\n/** Configuration errors (unknown provider, missing model or base URL) end the command with a message, not a trace. */\nfunction buildConfig(options: any): HarnessConfig {\n  try {\n    return buildConfigOrThrow(options);\n  } catch (err: any) {\n    console.error(pc.red(`Configuration error: ${err?.message ?? err}`));\n    process.exit(2);\n  }\n}\nimport { registerOperationCommands } from \"./operation_cli.js\";\nimport pc from \"picocolors\";\n\nimport * as os from \"node:os\";\n\nconst __filename = fileURLToPath(import.meta.url);\nconst __dirname = path.dirname(__filename);\n\n// Keep the lease for the full frontend/sidecar lifetime, including synchronous\n// TUI dispatch. Maintenance recovery acquires its own exclusive lease instead.\nconst startupArgs = process.argv.slice(2);\nconst { acquireClientLease, releaseClientLease, clientInvocationKind } = await import(\"./core/client_lease.js\");\nconst invocationKind = clientInvocationKind(startupArgs);\nconst startupReadOnly = invocationKind === \"metadata\" || (startupArgs[0] === \"upgrade\" && startupArgs.includes(\"--check\"));\n// `upgrade --check` is read-only, so it must not replay a transaction. It also\n// must not load configuration while a restore journal says that config may be\n// only partially applied. Refuse before loadEnvironment() and let a normal\n// managed 