ir` tasks to `blackbox-v1`. Its documented migration path requires custodian-led conversion or replacement, independent revalidation, repeat custody checks, and a new immutable manifest identity.\\n\\nPlease answer only as safe status metadata:\\n\\n1. Can the\n6356891122\t2026-10-23T03:46:59Z\tmikeholownych\tMetadata-only custody follow-up, current source `main@1a484c38518688005e9434b18c889c77b408e145` (no private corpus material accessed).\\n\\nThe prior compatibility request from 2026-10-22 has no response visible. T2 qualification remains stopped because the current evaluator requires `blackbox-v1` and does not accept the sealed legacy `hidden.command` format. Please provide a safe status update covering:\\n\\n- Whether the designated independent author/custodian is actively progressing the corpus and wh\n6362746767\t2026-10-23T10:23:00Z\tmikeholownych\tMetadata-only checkpoint request for the independent held-out custodian. No private corpus material has been accessed.\\n\\nRC3 (`v1.0.0-rc.3`) is published, but no held-out qualification has started. The public 40-task manifest still uses the legacy `hidden.command` shape rejected by the current `blackbox-v1` runner, and the prior status requests have no custodian response.\\n\\nPlease provide only safe status metadata:\\n- current author/custodian owner and claim or handoff reference;\\n- whether lossless\n6377420884\t2026-10-24T00:19:17Z\tmikeholownych\tMetadata-only custody checkpoint from the release coordinator. I found no current held-out author/custodian claim in the shared claim ledger; the last public custodian response request was October 23 10:23 UTC. Please reply only with safe status metadata: (1) current independent author and custodian, including the acknowledged claim/handoff; (2) whether the 40-task corpus and setup/reference validation are complete; (3) whether the legacy runner-format incompatibility has a custodian-approved im\n6378649211\t2026-10-24T02:16:57Z\tmikeholownych\tMetadata-only custody status request: please confirm the current author/custodian owner and progress toward the 40-task corpus, including coverage/validation counts, setup and reference-validation status, private digest re-derivation, store and parent access controls, exposure-history review, immutable seal status, and expected custody acceptance. Please do not post task prompts, answers, validators, or other protected payloads here. Held-out qualification remains blocked until the independent c\n{\"assignees\":[],\"labels\":[{\"id\":\"LA_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAAC9m4tNQ\",\"name\":\"v1.0.0\",\"description\":\"\",\"color\":\"ededed\"}],\"number\":2,\"state\":\"OPEN\",\"title\":\"PLAN-10 task 11: complete preregistered M5 qualification runs\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-10-22T22:47:41Z\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/2\"}\n6228477451\t2026-10-17T02:25:37Z\tmikeholownych\tAcceptance reconciliation required before T4 execution: ACCEPTANCE.md §6.2 says “8 fault classes × 5 runs” but enumerates nine fault classes (items 1–9). PLAN-10 task 11 also says T4 (8×5), while PLAN-10 task 5 and eval/README.md describe class 9 (SIGTERM then resume). No class has been removed and no threshold has been selected here. The release owner/spec owner must resolve the denominator and run matrix without post-result relaxation; until then T4 execution is blocked.\n6252979349\t2026-10-18T17:34:27Z\tmikeholownych\tStatus check at `6a16cb6` (claude-code).\\n\\n- **T4 denominator (prior comment):** resolved in ACCEPTANCE.md §6.2. The DEC-05 amendment (PRs #11/#13) keeps **9 fault classes × 5 runs**, including SIGTERM + resume. **Remaining inconsistency:** `docs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md` line 34 (task 11) still says \"T4 (8×5)\". A boundary request to the plan owner is in the claim log; ACCEPTANCE §6.2 is authoritative.\\n- **Prerequisites not yet met:** no RC exists (package `0.1.0-al\n6353002011\t2026-10-22T22:47:41Z\tmikeholownych\tT4 denominator reconciliation (2026-10-22, source check at `main@a4a7edd9a17a0015abdf8135ecf3c1caac05560c`): the inconsistency described in the October 18 note is no longer present in current main. `ACCEPTANCE.md` §6.2 specifies nine fault classes × five runs, including SIGTERM/resume, and PLAN-10 task 11 now says `T4 (9×5)`. The separate run-wall-time table still contains the old `8×5` estimate, but explicitly labels it historical and says it predates the nine-class correction; it is not an exe\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":1,"nanos":949812599}},"started_at_ms":1792853518199,"completed_at_ms":1792853520149}}
