{"timestamp":"2026-10-24T15:24:08.694Z","ordinal":295056,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a16e80-c6ef-7860-a1e5-4a3c06b2279c","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016adccd97468481a0880fabf7adffe33b","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"The startup folder-trust prompt is already implemented in Nexus’s current release line. I verified it in `origin/main` at `e624de0` and confirmed it is included in RC4. It asks whether to trust the folder before loading project instructions, remembers trusted folders, and offers **Trust and continue**, **Continue without trusting**, or **Exit**.\n\nThe mismatch is your local checkout: it is on `main` at `db1ca55`, which predates that change, and has unrelated dirty files. So launching Nexus from that checkout won’t show the prompt. The shared checkout is untouched.\n\nAcceptance is still **IN_PROGRESS**; this confirms the feature is present, not that the release is accepted."}],"phase":"final_answer"},"started_at_ms":1792855447296,"completed_at_ms":1792855448694}}
