{"timestamp":"2026-10-24T15:24:24.078Z","ordinal":295060,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"task_complete","root_turn_id":"01a16e80-c6ef-7860-a1e5-4a3c06b2279c","turn_id":"01a16e80-c6ef-7860-a1e5-4a3c06b2279c","last_agent_message":"The startup folder-trust prompt is already implemented in Nexus’s current release line. I verified it in `origin/main` at `e624de0` and confirmed it is included in RC4. It asks whether to trust the folder before loading project instructions, remembers trusted folders, and offers **Trust and continue**, **Continue without trusting**, or **Exit**.\n\nThe mismatch is your local checkout: it is on `main` at `db1ca55`, which predates that change, and has unrelated dirty files. So launching Nexus from that checkout won’t show the prompt. The shared checkout is untouched.\n\nAcceptance is still **IN_PROGRESS**; this confirms the feature is present, not that the release is accepted.","started_at":1792855295,"completed_at":1792855464,"duration_ms":168337,"time_to_first_token_ms":5875}}
