{"timestamp":"2026-10-24T16:10:15.288Z","ordinal":296034,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a16e83-5895-7063-abd1-ce44552ab742","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-d2457cac-c6e8-4708-a17b-5c76f679c7d3","process_id":"85184","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","gh pr view 196 --json body --jq '.body'"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"gh pr view 196 --json body --jq '.body'"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"## Reproduced release blocker\n\nCross-runner qualification for the published `v1.0.0-rc.4` was dispatched from exact `main` revision `72e769348fe8a978a576627a4802cb6b68ced779` in workflow run `40103980794`. Both Ubuntu 22.04 and 24.04 builds completed, but archive comparison failed at byte 19. The 22.04 archive matches the published RC4 archive; the 24.04 archive differs. I downloaded the immutable workflow artifacts and confirmed the extracted package trees are byte-identical, including identical `MANIFEST.sha256`. The first tar header differs in its device-number fields, which changes the tar checksum and archive digest. This leaves `REQ-REL-114` unqualified for RC4.\n\n## Fix\n\nGenerate the package archive with the pinned build container so host-specific tar metadata does not affect output bytes. The change preserves package payload, version, and compatibility metadata.\n\n## Candidate\n\n- Head: `585a675fc616cea5d72c8166bf6b47bab3c46540`\n- Base: `72e769348fe8a978a576627a4802cb6b68ced779`\n- Scope: `scripts/package-linux.sh` only\n- Independent review: ACCEPT by `plan05_readonly_review` at this exact candidate; patch SHA-256 `a34a2211eef52d580c6e300b2ce88b7115b23e4cf60fb011b896af4cd009f20`\n- Static checks: `bash -n` and `git diff --check` pass\n\nNo local test suite was run because the repository's `SUITE` claim remains held by `KimiCode-defect-scan`. Exact-head hosted CI and a fresh cross-runner RC5 comparison are required. RC4 itself remains immutable; this PR cannot retroactively make its failed reproduction pass.\n\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":377716762}},"started_at_ms":1792858214910,"completed_at_ms":1792858215288}}
