{"timestamp":"2026-10-24T16:37:15.703Z","ordinal":296683,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a16e83-5895-7063-abd1-ce44552ab742","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016adcdeba597481a087e63b785bce4b2e","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"Yes, that’s the startup behavior you meant: ask whether to trust the current folder before loading its project instructions, with options to trust, continue without trusting, or exit.\n\nI checked the version your `nexus` command currently runs: it is **v1.0.0-rc.3**. That tag does not contain the startup trust prompt, which explains why you don’t see it. The prompt is present in the newer RC4 source at [startup_trust.ts](/var/tmp/nexus-main-f827-gates/cli/src/startup_trust.ts:88) and is called during startup in [index.ts](/var/tmp/nexus-main-f827-gates/cli/src/index.ts:208). It will appear when you run a build containing that source; your current RC3 install won’t show it."}],"phase":"final_answer"},"started_at_ms":1792859834388,"completed_at_ms":1792859835703}}
