udflare-artifacts-vertical-slice_agent-collab-worker_package.json/owner.json\\n.git/nexus-claims/FILE_experiments_cloudflare-artifacts-vertical-slice_fork-worker_package.json/owner.json\\n.git/nexus-claims/FILE_package.json/owner.json\\n.git/nexus-claims/FILE_scripts_generate_sbom.sh/owner.json\\n.git/nexus-claims/FILE_scripts_release-tools_package-lock.json/owner.json\\n.git/nexus-claims/FILE_scripts_release-tools_package.json/owner.json\\n.git/nexus-claims/FILE_scripts_repro-identity.mjs/owner.json\\n.git/nexus-claims/PLAN-05_PR-5B_CODEQL_CLIENT_NORMALIZE/owner.json\\n.git/nexus-claims/PLAN-10_HOST_PREFLIGHT_CURRENT_SOURCE/owner.json\\n.git/nexus-claims/PLAN-12_INDEPENDENT_CLOSURE_REVIEW/owner.json\\n.git/nexus-claims/PLAN-C1_POST_CONTEST_STATUS_AND_DEPENDENCY_COVERAGE/owner.json\\n.git/nexus-claims/POST_CONTEST_DEP_UPDATE_PR126/owner.json\\n.git/nexus-claims/RELEASE_PUBLISHER/owner.json\\n.git/nexus-claims/SEC_CODEQL_CLIENT_REGEX/owner.json\\n.git/nexus-claims/SEC_CODEQL_PGREP_PATTERN/owner.json\\n.git/nexus-claims/SEC_DEMO_GIT_CLEANUP_RACE/owner.json\\n.git/nexus-claims/SUITE/owner.json\\n\\nRELEASE STATUS DOCS\\ndocs/v1.0.0/EVIDENCE.md:28:| Live cloud client | Checkout build `db1ca55` (`/home/mike/nexus-code/cli/dist`), using the operator's existing provider connections: ChatGPT via the Codex CLI sign-in; OpenRouter via the crush credential. |\\ndocs/v1.0.0/EVIDENCE.md:97:- **No product qualification exists.** \\\"Blocked\\\" is established, from reproduced defects. \\\"Qualified\\\" cannot be: there is no held-out, fault-injection or standalone evidence, and the tasks used in the historical pilot were tuned.\\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:13:| [DEC-05](#dec-05-v1-evaluation-protocol-and-thresholds) | Evaluation protocol and thresholds | 40 held-out T2 tasks, 5 runs, 2 peers, thresholds below | Needs an external author (see actions) |\\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:14:| [DEC-06](#dec-06-supported-providers-for-v1) | Supported providers | Local OpenAI-compatible + OpenRouter supported; others experimental until live-verified | No |\\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:81:- 40 held-out T2 tasks, at least 20 from external repositories at pinned commits, across JS/TS, Python, Rust and Go, with at least 6 per class (bugfix, feature, refactor, debug).\\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:102:**Task authorship.** The owner authorized agent authorship for the T2 tasks on 2026-10-14. A separately-run agent session authors the held-out tasks. It is given only the task schema and the external repositories, with no access to Nexus source, the development set, or tuning history. Its sha256 manifest is committed before the RC freeze. The qualification report must state that the authors were agents, not humans.\\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:104:**Inference environment.** All runs go through the homelab-ai gateway, which is the only inference path (owner, 2026-10-14). There is no direct worker access and no extra GPU. Every run, Nexus and peers alike, is serial on one gateway-backed model. Wall time is the critical-path cost (PLAN-10). Live cloud connections (ChatGPT sign-in, OpenRouter) may be used for small-spend checks, but are not used for matched comparisons. One reason: `openrouter/free` routed 3 requests to 3 different models in the 2026-10-14 verify run, which breaks model matching.\\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:114:| **Supported** | OpenRouter | Live-verified 2026-10-14 at db1ca55 (`evidence/live/verify_openrouter.json`); re-verify at RC with a **pinned** model (not `openrouter/free`). |\\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:215:| X4 | **Partly resolved 2026-10-14:** the existing ChatGPT sign-in and OpenRouter connections are authorized for small-spend checks; both were live-verified at db1ca55. Optional: add OpenAI API-key or Anthropic keys if those providers should be listed as supported. | DEC-06 | M5 (optional) |\\ndocs/v1.0.0/AUDIT.md:23:| Runtime services | The local inference gateway is configured in `~/.config/nexus/config.env`: endpoint `https://10.0.8.5:8443/v1`, model `engineering/b0`, key redacted, `LOCAL_HARNESS_SHELL=bash`. The repo-tracked `cli/.env` holds LM Studio defaults (`localhost:1234`, key \\\"local\\\"). **The audit sent no requests to the gateway.** With owner authorization (2026-10-14, small spend), it made live cloud calls through the existing ChatGPT sign-in and OpenRouter connections: two `providers verify` runs and one `nexus run` bug-fix task. See EVIDENCE §3. | RT (values redacted) |\\ndocs/v1.0.0/AUDIT.md:24:| External dependencies | Node ≥ 20 (runtime), GitHub Releases (installer), optional bubblewrap/Docker (sandbox), optional cloud providers (OpenRouter, OpenAI, Anthropic, ChatGPT/Copilot OAuth, compatible), optional MCP servers, DuckDuckGo (default `search_web`). | SRC |\\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:25:2. **RC artifact construction.** After the required owner authorization, create the version-matched RC tag on that exact source commit and use the repository release workflow to build and publish the RC artifacts. Record the workflow run, tag commit, artifact digests, and provenance. The workflow-produced artifacts are the candidates for qualification; a local build or a different commit is not interchangeable. RC artifact publication is not product qualification or final release acceptance.\\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:48:| REQ-QUAL-101 | ACC-QUAL-T2 | Installed-RC held-out T2 qualification |\\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:50:| REQ-QUAL-108 | ACC-TUI-STEER, ACC-TUI-A11Y, ACC-TUI-MANUAL | CI PTY checks and installed-RC real-terminal matrix |\\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:82:| E5 | Cloud, small spend: ChatGPT sign-in (experimental tier) and OpenRouter with a pinned model; OpenAI and Anthropic keys if added | Provider verify; one live task per supported cloud provider |\\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:141:| P-plain | Bare OpenAI-compatible `/models` and chat. No tokenize, no capacity headers. | Standalone T2 subset (≥ 10 held-out tasks) × 3 runs; T4 classes 1, 3, 4, 7 × 3 | T2 correctness ≥ (gateway-direct T2 correctness on the same tasks − 10 pts). False VERIFIED = 0. T4 truthful = 100%. Context source reported as `client_default` or an operator override, with no error. |\\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:153:| OpenRouter, pinned model | Supported | `providers verify` PASS, plus one live small task (a §6-style bug fix) reaching a correct outcome |\\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:158:## 5. Terminal acceptance (REQ-QUAL-108)\\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:189:### 5.3 Manual real-terminal matrix (E3)\\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:211:### 6.1 T2 held-out (ACC-QUAL-T2)\\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:216:- Set `T2_TASKS` to the custodian-approved, sealed task directory and `T2_OUT` to a new, empty, run-specific output directory. Do not use the disclosed `eval/tasks` development set as held-out evidence. Preserve all three outputs and their manifests; never reuse an output directory for a retry.\\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:337:- [ ] The exact-RC evidence gate passes from the clean RC worktree and is bound to the exact RC source commit and installed RC artifact. Run the checker with the custodian-approved, immutable qualification record and evidence directory:\\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:339:  The version 1 record contains `sourceCommit` (full commit ID), `rcTag` (for example `v1.0.0-rc.1`), `artifactSha256`, `artifactProvenance` (`sourceCommit`, `artifactSha256`, and a hashed provenance report), `independentAcceptance` (`disposition`, `reviewer`, `implementers`, zero `blockingDefects`, and a hashed report reference), and one `requirements` entry for every B/RR row. For `ACCEPT WITH DEFECTS`, include each non-blocking defect with its owner disposition; unresolved or blocking defects fail. Each requirement entry records its status and one or more hashed evidence files covering the exact criteria required by the ledger and the §1.1 qualification-onl…2469 tokens truncated…n-and-evaluation.md:6:| Release class | **BLOCKER** for any v1 maturity claim: held-out matched evaluation, fault-injection qualification, standalone live qualification, scoring integrity. RELEASE-REQUIRED: T3 long tasks, a T4 smoke test in CI, a PTY terminal matrix. |\\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md:7:| Requirements | REQ-QUAL-101, REQ-QUAL-102, REQ-QUAL-103, REQ-QUAL-104, REQ-QUAL-105, REQ-QUAL-106, REQ-QUAL-107, REQ-QUAL-108 |\\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md:23:- a held-out task set;\\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md:44:   - The held-out half is authored by someone other than the implementer and stored outside the repo until the freeze. Its manifest of sha256 hashes is committed before the RC freeze.\\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md:83:8. **REQ-QUAL-108. Terminal matrix.** PTY scripted runs in CI (existing `tui_*_e2e`, plus the new ACC-SAFE and ACC-PROC scripts). A manual matrix covers {xterm, kitty, tmux, VS Code terminal, GNOME Terminal} × {80x24, 40x14, 200x60}, checking: approval safety, paste, resize, cancel, narrow hints and NO_COLOR. Screenshots are archived.\\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/B_providers.md:18:- Config (config.ts:16-40): env load order = install `cli/.env` (no override) -> `~/.config/nexus/config.env` (override) -> **cwd `.env` (override:true, any key)**. Credential authority snapshot (operator env + config.env) taken before cwd `.env` (client.ts:77-101); provider selection, provider base URL, disclosure authorization and stored-token binding use that snapshot. Everything else (TLS/Node env, timeouts, recovery policy, LOCAL_LLM_ENDPOINT/FALLBACKS, provider key env vars) reads live `process.env`.\\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/B_providers.md:20:- Trust boundaries: disclosure gate = `disclosureClass` (providers.ts:181) -> `classifyDestination` (egress.ts:107) string-based; cloud destinations require authorization (client.ts:509-520); every outbound body passes `InformationFlowBoundary.evaluateEgress`. Credentials: env -> `~/.config/nexus/credentials.json` (0600, atomic, credentials.ts:68-75) -> other clients' files read-only.\\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/B_providers.md:58:listModels hang: STILL PENDING after 3000ms                                <-- PRV-05\\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/B_providers.md:59:generateEmbedding hang: STILL PENDING after 3000ms                         <-- PRV-05\\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/G_contest_eval.md:6:- **Eval:** the harness is sound for matched T2 fixture runs. The only results come from a 6-task pilot that is self-declared as tuned. No held-out set, no T3/T4, no fault injection. It cannot qualify v1 task quality as it stands.\\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/G_contest_eval.md:89:| CON-012 | S4 | Doc staleness | docs/CLOUDFLARE_CONTEST_CRITICAL_PATH_ASSESSMENT.md:11,34,88-90 | DOC-CLAIM. The doc dated 2026-10-02 says \\\"Nexus currently has no Cloudflare Worker\\\". This is now false and the doc is not marked superseded. CONTEST.md:65 and :89 *correctly* say \\\"blocked pending clean-account acceptance\\\". | Reviewer confusion. | Mark the doc HISTORICAL. |\\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/G_contest_eval.md:92:| EVL-001 | S1 (v1 task-quality claim) | Qualification evidence | eval/README.md:42,47-58; docs/reviews/evidence/eval_pilot_2026-10-13/RESULT.md:62-63 | DOC-CLAIM + SOURCE. The only scored evidence is 6 in-repo T2 fixture tasks. RESULT.md itself says \\\"These six tasks were used to find and fix the issues … it does not qualify Nexus. Qualification needs a fresh task set.\\\" Missing: held-out tasks, the T3 long-task set, the T4 fault injector, the T3 fact-sheet scorer, and runs on the release candidate. The measured builds are 76f4081, ed17e99 and 4fcbe68-dirty; their rebased equivalents (fe576f1, d116e99, 0090f9c) are on main, but db1ca55 itself was never evaluated. | No basis for a v1 claim about task quality. The pilot verdict was \\\"NOT QUALIFIED (false VERIFIED=2)\\\". The rerun had 0 false VERIFIED, but on tuned tasks. | A v1 protocol is in §7. |\\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/G_contest_eval.md:128:- **Credential custody in the broker is careful.** Checks on owner, 0400 mode, nlink and inode-before/after; O_NOFOLLOW; buffers zero-filled after use; a reflection scan over all git objects; error output limited to an allowlist of codes (demo-transport.mjs:152-185,375-391). Executables are bound by file descriptor (linux-bound-exec). Git config is hardened (no system or global config, no hooks, no credential helper, `followRedirects=false`, protocol allowlist) at :192-212. Tests are RUNTIME-verified: demo-transport 8/8; artifact-token-response 14 revoke cases plus 8 post-revoke cases; credential-lifecycle 25 assertions; linux-bound-exec; classify-revoke 11 cases; worker token-response 10/10; work-state-contract 2/2.\\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/G_contest_eval.md:151:- **G3: generated-code containment** (network and file reads). To qualify, add tests in which generated code attempts `fetch('http://example.com')` and reads `/home/*/.config`. Expected: blocked once netns is added.\\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/G_contest_eval.md:154:- **G6: task difficulty and discrimination.** 4 of 6 pilot tasks were 10/10 for Nexus (ceiling). To qualify, calibrate a held-out set so that no task is solved by every agent 5/5.\\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/G_contest_eval.md:176:| EVL-R1 | **Held-out set:** at least 40 T2 tasks (proposal). At least 50% from external repos at pinned commits (JS/TS, Python, Rust, Go). The held-out half is authored by someone other than the Nexus developer and kept outside the repo (encrypted or private) until the freeze. The 6 pilot tasks plus the routing engx T01-T12 count as a *development* set only. | workflow | BLOCKER for any v1 quality claim | The manifest lists task sha256s committed *before* the release-candidate (RC) freeze. Tasks are revealed after scoring. |\\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/prv/tls.mts:4:const s = https.createServer({ key: fs.readFileSync(`${D}/k.pem`), cert: fs.readFileSync(`${D}/c.pem`) }, (q, r) => { console.log(\\\"server saw auth header:\\\", q.headers[\\\"authorization\\\"] ? \\\"present\\\" : \\\"none\\\"); r.end('{\\\"data\\\":[]}'); });\\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/prv/probe.mts:48:const capped = (p: Promise<any>, ms: number) => Promise.race([p.then(() => \\\"resolved\\\", (e) => \\\"rejected:\\\" + e.message.slice(0, 60)), new Promise(r => setTimeout(() => r(`STILL PENDING after ${ms}ms`), ms))]);\\n\\nPR DETAILS\\n{\\\"baseRefName\\\":\\\"main\\\",\\\"headRefOid\\\":\\\"fba2faf613836b96043dcc07e86d8b54004ab2e0\\\",\\\"number\\\":197,\\\"reviewDecision\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"state\\\":\\\"OPEN\\\",\\\"statusCheckRollup\\\":[{\\\"__typename\\\":\\\"CheckRun\\\",\\\"completedAt\\\":\\\"2026-10-24T16:14:46Z\\\",\\\"conclusion\\\":\\\"SUCCESS\\\",\\\"detailsUrl\\\":\\\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40109386846/job/120917736131\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"test-matrix (22)\\\",\\\"startedAt\\\":\\\"2026-10-24T15:58:23Z\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"COMPLETED\\\",\\\"workflowName\\\":\\\"CI\\\"},{\\\"__typename\\\":\\\"CheckRun\\\",\\\"completedAt\\\":\\\"2026-10-24T15:59:32Z\\\",\\\"conclusion\\\":\\\"SUCCESS\\\",\\\"detailsUrl\\\":\\\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40109386876/job/120917736554\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"javascript-typescript\\\",\\\"startedAt\\\":\\\"2026-10-24T15:58:23Z\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"COMPLETED\\\",\\\"workflowName\\\":\\\"CodeQL\\\"},{\\\"__typename\\\":\\\"CheckRun\\\",\\\"completedAt\\\":\\\"2026-10-24T16:15:05Z\\\",\\\"conclusion\\\":\\\"SUCCESS\\\",\\\"detailsUrl\\\":\\\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40109386846/job/120917736027\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"test-matrix (24)\\\",\\\"startedAt\\\":\\\"2026-10-24T15:58:23Z\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"COMPLETED\\\",\\\"workflowName\\\":\\\"CI\\\"},{\\\"__typename\\\":\\\"CheckRun\\\",\\\"completedAt\\\":\\\"2026-10-24T16:36:42Z\\\",\\\"conclusion\\\":\\\"SUCCESS\\\",\\\"detailsUrl\\\":\\\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40109386846/job/120921561486\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"linux-x86_64\\\",\\\"startedAt\\\":\\