{"timestamp":"2026-10-24T16:40:57.321Z","ordinal":296875,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_01a16ec9-6ee9-7b33-9aef-31daadeb5b54","author":"/root/plan05_readonly_review","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/plan05_readonly_review\nPayload:\n**CHANGES_REQUIRED** — exact head `fba2faf613836b96043dcc07e86d8b54004ab2e0` reviewed against current main `f827d5159160de3a52c2f0ed96d423451f659867`. Full current-base diff hash: `b9681dd631b68ec3d3680860a567ac56bbab3c431105fb3b8b0494a8f0e4d9b1`.\n\nThe `edit_file` and `patch_file` changes in [file_ops.rs](/home/mike/nexus-code/core/src/file_ops.rs:634) check the opened descriptor size, cap reads at 8 MiB + 1, and reject growth beyond the limit. The tests cover oversize rejection without modification and the exact boundary for `edit_file`. Those source changes are unchanged from the older-base candidate, so its focused results remain relevant to them; I did not run tests.\n\nThe current-base diff also **reverts the merged archive reproducibility fix** in `scripts/package-linux.sh`: it removes the pinned-container tar/gzip path and output-path canonicalization present on current main. That reintroduces the known cross-runner archive-byte mismatch and can break container builds given a relative output directory. Rebase or otherwise preserve the current-main packaging changes before treating this as an acceptable candidate. The added evidence README still identifies its original test base, `e624de0`; it does not establish current-head CI. `git diff --check` was clean."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a16ec6-5068-7a43-a634-88dec514377c","create_time":1792860057.321505}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"user_input_order":15209}}
