{"timestamp":"2026-10-24T16:43:25.819Z","ordinal":296992,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a16ec6-5068-7a43-a634-88dec514377c","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-bdda6dd3-55c3-4863-9104-ce3f7093e7a9","process_id":"64800","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","printf 'READINESS CLAIM\\n'; jq -c '{agent,host,branch,worktree,scope,since,status,base,head}' /home/mike/nexus-code/.git/nexus-claims/FILE_docs_v1.0.0_READINESS.md/owner.json 2>/dev/null || true; printf '\\nREADINESS EXCERPT\\n'; rg -n -C 2 'RC4|rc\\.4|cross.runner|held.out|terminal|acceptance status|IN_PROGRESS' docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md | tail -120"],"cwd":"file:///var/tmp/nexus-main-41b-gates","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"printf 'READINESS CLAIM\\n'; jq -c '{agent,host,branch,worktree,scope,since,status,base,head}' /home/mike/nexus-code/.git/nexus-claims/FILE_docs_v1.0.0_READINESS.md/owner.json 2>/dev/null || true; printf '\\nREADINESS EXCERPT\\n'; rg -n -C 2 'RC4|rc\\.4|cross.runner|held.out|terminal|acceptance status|IN_PROGRESS' docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md | tail -120"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"READINESS CLAIM\n{\"agent\":\"codex-root\",\"host\":\"mike-dev\",\"branch\":\"v1/readiness-rc4-refresh\",\"worktree\":\"/home/mike/nexus-wt/readiness-rc4-refresh\",\"scope\":\"Append a fresh, exact-revision release-readiness checkpoint reconciling source/CI, RC3 E5 evidence, held-out custody, and Ubuntu terminal setup; preserve historical snapshots and do not claim acceptance.\",\"since\":\"2026-10-24T01:10:30Z\",\"status\":\"claimed; refreshing current exact-main readiness snapshot; preserve prior snapshots; independent review required; no release acceptance claim\",\"base\":\"be2cd2f255414f554572c86baa884d9271ff5ea1\",\"head\":\"9b8a3ec\"}\n\nREADINESS EXCERPT\n105-\n106-## Current state update (2026-10-21 15:26 UTC, `7d6673f`)\n--\n110-**Campaign status:** `NEXUS_V1_CONVERGENCE_ACTIVE`\n111-\n112:**Acceptance status:** `IN_PROGRESS`\n113-\n114-**Release status:** no Nexus v1.0.0 RC or stable publication exists. Publication authorization is granted and remains gated on independent acceptance.\n--\n117-- **Requirements gate:** `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` was independently rerun with isolated HOME/XDG on exact `7d6673f` and passed: 123 rows (109 tested, 5 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open). Eleven requirements remain explicitly deferred to exact-RC qualification: `REQ-AGT-002`, `REQ-AGT-010`, `REQ-PRV-003`, `REQ-REL-005`, `REQ-AGT-110`, `REQ-PRV-111`, `REQ-REL-114`, `REQ-QUAL-101`, `REQ-QUAL-107`, `REQ-QUAL-108`, and `REQ-QUAL-109`. This source-stage gate pass does not satisfy those qualification requirements.\n118-- **Contest:** the contest is over; no contest freeze applies. The contest-contract check has been retired and is not a release gate. Historical contest artifacts remain evidence of past activity only.\n119:- **Qualification and release:** PR #102 contributes synthetic host-preflight evidence only. Private held-out custody/schema compatibility, T2/T3/T4 qualification, live provider and standalone checks, exact-RC reproducibility, the five-environment by three-size human terminal matrix, and independent RC acceptance remain outstanding. No RC has been constructed, installed, or accepted.\n120-\n121-This update supersedes the 14:56 UTC `8f4504e` checkpoint below for current state. Earlier evidence remains bound to its recorded revisions.\n--\n125-**Separate historical candidate branch:** `6151a231e9179c109cfbe8cff87e0a4148587b6a` (`v1/candidate-1`)\n126-**Campaign status:** `NEXUS_V1_CONVERGENCE_ACTIVE`\n127:**Acceptance status:** `IN_PROGRESS`\n128-\n129:Exact-source CI and requirements enforcement pass on `8f4504e`, but held-out custody and corpus compatibility, installed-RC qualification, independent RC acceptance, and final publication remain incomplete. No v1.0.0 RC or stable release exists. Publication authorization is granted and remains gated on acceptance.\n130-\n131-This checkpoint reconciles the candidate ledger and acceptance procedure against recorded source and test evidence. It is not a release approval. Historical inspection sections below are preserved as audit evidence and do not represent current branch state where superseded by the 2026-10-21 update.\n--\n136-- **PR and contest state:** PR #8 remains a draft integration-to-`main` candidate. Its CI and CodeQL checks are green, but it is not a release acceptance or publication. PR #102 is open at `3756afe05dbd75c4e6929d87cd50facbb8ab1748`, based on `8f4504e`, to record a synthetic qualification-host preflight; its CodeQL and TypeScript checks passed and its Node matrix was still running at this checkpoint. The preflight report records 10/10 checks using only an empty synthetic marker store; it does not establish private corpus custody or qualification acceptance. The contest has concluded; no contest freeze applies. Historical contest artifacts remain historical evidence only.\n137-- **Requirements enforcement:** `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` passed on exact source tree `8f4504e` (tree `2a0799c8a32e88e34322b712cf937d73cbe4d637`), with isolated `HOME`/XDG: 123 rows (109 tested, 5 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open). Eleven rows remain below the ordinary tested threshold pending their approved exact-RC evidence: `REQ-AGT-002`, `REQ-AGT-010`, `REQ-PRV-003`, `REQ-REL-005`, `REQ-AGT-110`, `REQ-PRV-111`, `REQ-REL-114`, `REQ-QUAL-101`, `REQ-QUAL-107`, `REQ-QUAL-108`, and `REQ-QUAL-109`. The pre-RC checker pass does not imply those RC gates have passed or authorize an acceptance claim.\n138:- **Evaluator and qualification-host boundary:** Source fixtures for cgroup resource limits, process-tree cleanup, workspace storage, and staged Git-history isolation are in the integration source suite and passed its exact-source CI. A synthetic host preflight at source `8f4504e` recorded 10/10 checks and is being documented in PR #102. Neither source fixtures nor the synthetic-host report establish access separation against the custodian's real store or permit held-out execution before custody acceptance.\n139:- **Held-out corpus and custody:** Public T2 manifest `eval/heldout-manifest.json` remains the 40-task identity `50895b84a604fbfd45ed82e29cbef4ba795d7fffbe6611af23bfbc9851f3e89b`; T3 public manifest identity remains `85fb9cafbe18e846bd64fb13eb4bfa0f92df0792bc93d12adaa685e04c9f1383`. Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) has no custodian response since 2026-10-21 12:21 UTC. Current evaluator qualification rejects the sealed T2 corpus's legacy `hidden.command` format; the documented path requires a custodian-owned compatible immutable successor and repeated custody checks. Private digest re-derivation, exposure history, setup/reference validation, effective access separation, and current custody acceptance remain unverified here. No payload, validator, reference solution, or hidden answer was accessed, and no held-out run has started.\n140:- **Other qualification gates:** No installed-RC provider or standalone matrix, T2/T3/T4 scored qualification, exact-RC cross-runner reproducibility, or independent RC acceptance exists. `ACCEPTANCE.md` §5.3 and `scripts/terminal-acceptance/README.md` define the human five-environment × three-size matrix and evidence capture; all 15 real-terminal cells remain unrun because no RC is installed. Automated PTY results do not replace those operator results.\n141-- **Version, RC, and publication:** Root and CLI package versions remain `0.1.0-alpha.2`. GitHub currently lists only alpha pre-releases `v0.1.0-alpha.1` and `v0.1.0-alpha.2`; no `v1.0.0-rc.N` artifact/tag or stable v1.0.0 tag, npm package, or GitHub release exists. Follow the staged lifecycle in `ACCEPTANCE.md`: pre-RC source gates, RC construction, artifact-bound RC gates, installed-RC qualification and independent G6 acceptance, then stable promotion/publication and post-publication verification.\n142-\n--\n150-\n151-- **Authoritative integration and CI:** `origin/v1/integration` is `6a16cb60635c9182f13be1635d5f44eddebdcde0`, merge commit for PR #45, whose only changed file was `docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md`. PR #45 exact-head CI run `39144798481` and CodeQL run `39144798415` passed; independent read-only review accepted exact head `8041c0dbe1a982b2a9e275083f336eb4c5b768b3`. Post-merge CodeQL run `39146982807` passed. Post-merge CI run `39146982849` is in progress on exact `6a16cb6`: Cloudflare and Node 20/22/24 passed; Linux `linux-x86_64` is still executing the CLI suite. This checkpoint does not combine its status with results from another revision.\n152:- **PR and evaluator state:** PRs #9, #13, #15, #16, #44, and #45 are integrated. PR #33 remains open at `0ca77e5ee64f80db02e2b16178c5be551ce5de0c` on stale base `faf95803714a3c543f5c59bc0610ca6291a6184d`. Its exact CI run `39141771002` passed on that old head, but independent review found qualification preflight does not account for host-source mounts created unconditionally by `agentSandboxArgv`. The finding is recorded in comment `6252102243`; a read-only source inventory and shared-mount-plan remediation target are in comment `6252621855`. Owner handoff request `6252543078` has no response as of this checkpoint. The evaluator claim remains protected. Do not execute held-out tasks until this boundary is fixed, exact-head validated, and independently accepted.\n153-- **Requirements enforcement:** `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` ran in a detached worktree at exact `6a16cb60635c9182f13be1635d5f44eddebdcde0` with isolated `HOME` and failed as required. It reports 123 rows (109 tested, 5 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open) and 11 below threshold: `REQ-AGT-002`, `REQ-AGT-010`, `REQ-PRV-003`, `REQ-REL-005`, `REQ-AGT-110`, `REQ-PRV-111`, `REQ-REL-114`, `REQ-QUAL-101`, `REQ-QUAL-107`, `REQ-QUAL-108`, and `REQ-QUAL-109`. The exact result is recorded in the claims log and was sent to the ledger owner in PR #17 comment `6252582027`; no ledger status changed.\n154:- **Held-out custody and qualification:** The custodian previously accepted the sealed 40-task manifest identity `50895b84a604fbfd45ed82e29cbef4ba795d7fffbe6611af23bfbc9851f3e89b` and its private digest/reference validation. This does not establish evaluator acceptance or T2 qualification. The implementing agent has not accessed private payloads. No held-out run has started because evaluator confidentiality preflight remains unaccepted and corpus/evaluator schema compatibility is unresolved.\n155:- **Other qualification and release gates:** Provider/standalone, T3/T4, cross-runner reproducibility, qualification-host validation, and human five-environment × three-size terminal acceptance remain incomplete. Package version remains `0.1.0-alpha.2`; no RC artifact/tag, stable tag, npm publication, or GitHub release exists. Publication authorization remains granted but gated on accepted exact-RC evidence.\n156-\n157-The 16:19 UTC `4bce876` checkpoint below remains as historical evidence for that revision.\n--\n160-\n161-- **Authoritative integration and CI:** `origin/v1/integration` is `4bce8760893b222789b76011a477dd61988ecba6`, merge commit for PR #44. PR #44 was merged from exact head `86b30f54b0fe087befbce8be258ae3bd3ff7cfa2` on base `faf95803714a3c543f5c59bc0610ca6291a6184d`; exact PR CI run `39141379739`, CodeQL run `39141379747`, and the `javascript-typescript` check passed. Independent read-only review accepted the only post-review delta. Post-merge CodeQL run `39144374432` passed on `4bce876`. Post-merge CI run `39144374445` is still running Node 20/22/24; its Cloudflare contract job passed. Exact integration CI on the parent `faf9580` passed as run `39139084949`, but it does not replace checks on `4bce876`.\n162:- **PR state:** PRs #9, #13, #15, #16, and #44 are integrated. PR #9's stale readiness changes were merged earlier and are retained in history.