ning 40 external-repository T2 tasks pinned to full 40-hex baseline commits across Go (10), JavaScript (10), Python (10), and Rust (10), and across bugfix (10), debug (10), feature (10), and refactor (10).\n186-  - Custody record: `docs/reviews/evidence/v1/HELDOUT_CUSTODY/custody-report-2026-10-18.md` (updated at `ce3f590`).\n187:  - **Distinction of evidence:** Independent public metadata review (`codex-lead`) verified and accepted the committed manifest digest (`50895b84…`), 40 unique task IDs, 10×4 class/language balance, 40 full pinned commits, and schema/digest fields without inspecting private payloads. Private payload validation (2 rounds per task in bounded `SUITE` windows: fresh clone → checkout → setup → pre-patch regression pass → pre-patch hidden fail → reference patch apply → post-patch hidden pass → post-patch regression pass), rejection/quarantine of one provenance-contaminated batch (`author-b9` at `/home/mike/nexus-heldout-v2-quarantine/b9-contaminated-2026-10-18T0235Z/`), per-session exec-log audits for clean replacement authors (`author-b8c`, `author-b9c`), and store access tightening (`/home/mike/nexus-heldout-v2` mode `0700`, `tasks/` and `reference/` mode `0500` read-only) are custodian-attested in `custody-report-2026-10-18.md`. Earlier author-exposed packages (`v12`, `v15`, `v16`, `v17`, `v18`) recorded in historical sections below are superseded development/pilot artifacts and are never used for held-out qualification.\n188-- **Evaluator isolation and kernel resource contract (PRs [#10](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/10), [#18](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/18), [#19](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/19)):**\n189-  - `blackbox-v1` oracle separation (`2c70d39`, PR #10) runs private oracle checks outside the candidate workspace while mounting the candidate workspace read-only (`--ro-bind`), superseding the historical shared-workspace oracle exposure noted in the 2026-10-17 review below.\n190-  - Repository workspace history isolation (`96aeef2`, PR #18, `eval/workspace.mjs`) stages external-repo tasks via `git init` + ancestor-only fetch (`--no-tags`, `--no-write-fetch-head`) without `--shared`, `objects/info/alternates`, remotes, tags, or post-baseline commits, preventing candidates from reading upstream fix commits in git history.\n191:  - Kernel-enforced resource contract (`91406bd`, PR #19, `eval/resources.mjs`, `eval/cgroup_supervisor.mjs`, `scripts/ensure-ci-user-cgroups.sh`) executes each task phase (setup, candidate sandbox, hidden/regression, oracle) inside a transient delegated `systemd --user` scope with verified cgroup v2 `CPUQuota`, `MemoryMax`, `MemorySwapMax=0`, `TasksMax`, `memory.oom.group=1`, dedicated size-capped tmpfs `workspaceRoot` storage enforcement, and `cgroup.kill` process-tree cleanup verified to `populated == 0`. These controls are source-implemented, independently reviewed, and CI-tested (`1,152/1,152` on `0cee0b7`, run `39104943950`), not live qualification results. Qualification-host provisioning (`nexus-eval` account, narrow sudoers rule, dedicated tmpfs mount, and frozen `config.resources` profile) remains a prerequisite before running held-out T2/T3/T4 workloads.\n192-- **Governance, tokenizer, and acceptance lifecycle reconciliations (PRs [#11](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/11)–[#15](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/15), [#17](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/17)):**\n193-  - `DEC-05` amendment (`f771a3c`, PR #11) and `ACCEPTANCE.md` §6.2 (`77102c5`, PR #13) resolve the historical eight-vs-nine T4 denominator conflict by retaining all **9 fault classes × 5 runs** (including SIGTERM + `run --resume`).\n--\n219-## Historical evidence: Review update (2026-10-17 03:10 UTC; pilot packages superseded by `heldout-v2` above)\n220-\n221:This section records the historical inspection at `e1759cae9cf399e2d2586d05bfea3f86b757c412`. The pilot package attempts and their failures r