{"timestamp":"2026-10-24T16:47:17.886Z","ordinal":297190,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_01a16ecf-3d7d-76c3-9d4f-4e7461d5a4dd","author":"/root/plan05_readonly_review","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/plan05_readonly_review\nPayload:\n**CHANGES_REQUIRED** — PR #183 head `02487c8b6f0ed311e72a3c806e533ada9576e3a8` is based on `0a80759de65d2d6909d1d259d1cbd11c5b9321f5`, while current main is `41b381ddac182b7f0c783b33df5f1355518f465b`. The current-main diff spans 44 files, not just `cli/src/git.ts` and its test.\n\nIt reverts merged fixes, including the 8 MiB `edit_file`/`patch_file` read bounds in [core/src/file_ops.rs](/home/mike/nexus-code/core/src/file_ops.rs:634), the pinned-container archive normalization in `scripts/package-linux.sh`, and startup-trust and retention changes. The file-read rollback directly reintroduces the unbounded reads PR #197 fixed. Rebase onto current main and preserve those changes before reconsidering this PR.\n\nThe intended `commitChanges` patch appears to address the requested cases: it resets `.nexus` index entries without changing working-tree contents, excludes root `.nexus` with top-anchored pathspecs, clears inherited pathspec-mode variables, and includes tests for staged modifications/deletions/additions, negated excludes, literal-pathspec mode, and nested workspaces. I did not run tests. The passing checks shown for this PR are on its stale head/base and do not validate a refreshed candidate."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a16ec6-5068-7a43-a634-88dec514377c","create_time":1792860437.8856585}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"user_input_order":15215}}
