{"timestamp":"2026-10-24T16:48:57.838Z","ordinal":297252,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a16ec6-5068-7a43-a634-88dec514377c","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016adce178905881a08294fc5d575182c7","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"Understood. You meant a **folder-trust prompt before Nexus starts a session**: show the workspace and project instruction file, offer **trust and continue / continue without trusting / exit**, and remember the trust choice.\n\nThat flow is already in the current source, but your installed `nexus` is **RC3**, which predates it. There’s also a behavior difference: the source ties trust to the default mode (`trusted → auto`, `untrusted → review`), while the screenshot says tool approvals follow the user’s permission settings. I haven’t changed anything in the dirty shared checkout.\n\nShould I keep the existing trust-to-mode behavior, or adjust the prompt so folder trust controls project instructions and integrations while leaving approval settings unchanged?"}],"phase":"final_answer"},"started_at_ms":1792860536605,"completed_at_ms":1792860537838}}
