{"timestamp":"2026-10-24T16:51:06.035Z","ordinal":297389,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_060b64278a9dfb15016adce1f95c5c81a0a9d0ae0434bb4254","status":"completed","call_id":"call_6d8cbd39a6a54328ba2975053738c193","name":"exec","input":"const nums=[191,193,194,195,196,197];\nconst rs=await Promise.all(nums.map(n=>tools.exec_command({cmd:`gh pr view ${n} --json body,files --jq '{body:.body,files:[.files[].path]}'`,\"workdir\":\"/home/mike/nexus-code\",\"yield_time_ms\":10000,\"max_output_tokens\":1400})));\nfor (const r of rs) text(r.output);\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a16ed1-0bd9-75c0-b3f2-6fda13432e3d","create_time":1792860665.3632956}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-24T16:51:06.210Z","ordinal":297390,"type":"token_usage_record","payload":{"thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a16ed1-0bd9-75c0-b3f2-6fda13432e3d","session_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","root_turn_id":"01a16ed1-0bd9-75c0-b3f2-6fda13432e3d","response_id":"resp_060b64278a9dfb15016adce1f0ce7c81a0a055bfda75686e54","usage":{"input_tokens":124971,"cached_input_tokens":123264,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":1051,"reasoning_output_tokens":943,"total_tokens":126022},"turn_token_usage":{"input_tokens":1684649,"cached_input_tokens":1640576,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":9064,"reasoning_output_tokens":6777,"total_tokens":1693713},"thread_token_usage":{"input_tokens":5402832846,"cached_input_tokens":5345216384,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":15037313,"reasoning_output_tokens":8572705,"total_tokens":5417870159}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-24T16:51:07.821Z","ordinal":297391,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a16ed1-0bd9-75c0-b3f2-6fda13432e3d","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-3b5f0ce0-8f83-4bf9-b00c-3f798bfd41ee","process_id":"85916","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","gh pr view 196 --json body,files --jq '{body:.body,files:[.files[].path]}'"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"gh pr view 196 --json body,files --jq '{body:.body,files:[.files[].path]}'"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"{\"body\":\"## Reproduced release blocker\\n\\nCross-runner qualification for the published `v1.0.0-rc.4` was dispatched from exact `main` revision `72e769348fe8a978a576627a4802cb6b68ced779` in workflow run `40103980794`. Both Ubuntu 22.04 and 24.04 builds completed, but archive comparison failed at byte 19. The 22.04 archive matches the published RC4 archive; the 24.04 archive differs. I downloaded the immutable workflow artifacts and confirmed the extracted package trees are byte-identical, including identical `MANIFEST.sha256`. The first tar header differs in its device-number fields, which changes the tar checksum and archive digest. This leaves `REQ-REL-114` unqualified for RC4.\\n\\n## Fix\\n\\nGenerate the package archive with the same digest-pinned build container used for the Rust build so host-specific tar metadata does not affect output bytes. The change preserves package payload, version, and compatibility metadata. Both the CI and tagged release workflows set this exact builder image.\\n\\n## Current candidate\\n\\n- Head: `da5f26925b4379187e1f96a8ccf924209b7ebb84`\\n- Base: `e624de04ca6ddebc3b08bf8e13375011d227c7e8`\\n- Scope: `scripts/package-linux.sh` only\\n- Independent review: ACCEPT by `plan05_readonly_review` at this exact head; net patch SHA-256 `a34a2211eef52d580c6e300b2ce88b7115b23e4cf60fb011b896af4cd009f20`\\n- Exact-head CI: CodeQL, JavaScript/TypeScript analysis, CodeRabbit, Node 22 and Node 24 passed. Linux x86_64 package/reproducibility/SBOM/smoke/installer job is in progress in run `40108251357`.\\n- Current main CI on the exact base (`40105438204`) and CodeQL (`40105438209`) passed.\\n- No local test suite was run because the repository's `SUITE` claim remains held by `KimiCode-defect-scan`.\\n\\nA fresh exact-head CI and a new cross-runner comparison against a newly built RC are required. RC4 remains immutable; this PR cannot retroactively change its failed reproduction result.\\n\",\"files\":[\"scripts/package-linux.sh\"]}\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":426136858}},"started_at_ms":1792860667394,"completed_at_ms":1792860667820}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-24T16:51:07.829Z","ordinal":297392,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a16ed1-0bd9-75c0-b3f2-6fda13432e3d","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-549fc748-363a-4062-be47-0c53d551bc3e","process_id":"81148","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","gh pr view 195 --json body,files --jq '{body:.body,files:[.files[].path]}'"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"gh pr view 195 --json body,files --jq '{body:.body,files:[.files[].path]}'"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"{\"body\":\"## Defect\\n\\n`file_info` is the metadata tool, but for every regular file it `mmap`s the whole file and iterates every byte to compute `line_count`, with no `MAX_READ_BYTES` check. `read_file` refuses files above 8 MB unless paged; `file_info` would still scan a multi-gigabyte file, blocking the single Rust bridge and faulting pages into memory.\\n\\nPre-fix probe on an 8 MB + 1 file returned `line_count: Some(8388609)`.\\n\\n## Fix\\n\\nOnly compute `line_count`/binary detection when the file is within `MAX_READ_BYTES`, the same limit the read tool uses. Larger files still report `size_bytes`, type, permissions and timestamps, with `line_count: None` (already the case for binary/unreadable files).\\n\\n## Verification\\n\\n- New regression fails pre-fix (`Some(8388609) != None`) and passes now.\\n- `cargo test --bin harness-core file_ops::` 16/16; full `cargo test --bin harness-core` 35/35.\\n- `git diff --check`: pass.\\n- Evidence: `docs/reviews/evidence/v1/DEFECT-FILE-INFO-UNBOUNDED-20261024/README.md`.\\n\\n## Residuals\\n\\nNo line count above 8 MB (use `read_file --offset/--length` or `wc -l`); mmap/SIGBUS on concurrent truncation and whole-file `edit_file`/`patch_file` are pre-existing and out of scope.\\n\\n## Coordination\\n\\nTook over the stale `FILE_core_src_file_ops.rs` claim (owner branch merged as PR #52, no PID, 6 days old; recorded as BROKEN_CLAIM). Independent review and exact-head CI to follow.\",\"files\":[\"core/src/file_ops.rs\",\"docs/reviews/evidence/v1/DEFECT-FILE-INFO-UNBOUNDED-20261024/README.md\"]}\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":462790548}},"started_at_ms":1792860667366,"completed_at_ms":1792860667829}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-24T16:51:07.854Z","ordinal":297393,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a16ed1-0bd9-75c0-b3f2-6fda13432e3d","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-98ae3645-6cab-4583-9f32-09976a349fc3","process_id":"72900","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","gh pr view 193 --json body,files --jq '{body:.body,files:[.files[].path]}'"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"gh pr view 193 --json body,files --jq '{body:.body,files:[.files[].path]}'"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"{\"body\":\"## Defect\\n\\n`McpClientManager.addServer` persisted `~/.config/nexus/mcp.json` with the default `0644` mode and a `0755` directory, while a server definition's `env` may carry its own token. It also parsed the existing config inside `catch {}`, so an unparseable file was treated as empty and replaced — silently dropping every other server — and the caller was still told \\\"Saved\\\".\\n\\nPre-fix probe: mode `644`, dir `755`, existing `keep` server gone after adding a server to a config with a trailing comma.\\n\\n## Fix\\n\\n- `~/.config/nexus` is created/tightened to `0700`; the config is written to a `0600` temporary file and renamed atomically (following an existing symlink target).\\n- Existing config is parsed and validated first; a non-object or unparseable file is left byte-for-byte untouched.\\n- `addServer` returns `persisted`/`persistError`; the REPL wizard and `/mcp add` report the failure instead of claiming the config was saved.\\n\\n## Verification\\n\\n- New `cli/test/mcp.test.ts`: 2/2; pre-fix fails with `config mode 644 leaks a server token` and with the overwritten-config assertion.\\n- `workspace_trust.test.ts` + new tests: 7/7; `tsc`; `git diff --check`.\\n- Evidence: `docs/reviews/evidence/v1/DEFECT-MCP-CONFIG-PERSIST-20261024/README.md`.\\n\\n## Residuals\\n\\nUnchmod-able config directory fails closed; a dangling symlink is replaced; an unparseable config must be fixed by the operator before persisting.\\n\\n## Coordination\\n\\nUnclaimed slice; independent review and exact-head CI to follow.\",\"files\":[\"cli/src/mcp.ts\",\"cli/src/repl.ts\",\"cli/src/slash/extension_commands.ts\",\"cli/test/mcp.test.ts\",\"docs/reviews/evidence/v1/DEFECT-MCP-CONFIG-PERSIST-20261024/README.md\"]}\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":448036431}},"started_at_ms":1792860667406,"completed_at_ms":1792860667854}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-24T16:51:07.917Z","ordinal":297394,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a16ed1-0bd9-75c0-b3f2-6fda13432e3d","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-cbddc7df-ddb6-4f19-987d-62cb3b6908e6","process_id":"89853","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","gh pr view 194 --json body,files --jq '{body:.body,files:[.files[].path]}'"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"gh pr view 194 --json body,files --jq '{body:.body,files:[.files[].path]}'"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"{\"body\":\"## Summary\\n\\nFixes the RC cross-runner reproducibility workflow's compare job, which failed before execution because it used the `actions/upload-artifact` commit as the `actions/download-artifact` pin.\\n\\nBoth download steps now use the verified `actions/download-artifact` v4 commit `d3f86a106a0bac45b974a628896c90dbdf5c8093`. The upload-artifact pins and tagged RC source remain unchanged.\\n\\n## Validation\\n\\n- Exact base: `be2cd2f255414f554572c86baa884d9271ff5ea1`\\n- `actionlint .github/workflows/repro.yml`: passed\\n- `git diff --check`: passed\\n- Independent review: ACCEPT; same two-line patch identity as the reviewed candidate\\n- Exact PR CI pending\\n\\nThis workflow fix enables the published RC4 cross-runner build comparison to complete. It does not qualify the RC or change release acceptance status.\\n\",\"files\":[\".github/workflows/repro.yml\"]}\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":475003109}},"started_at_ms":1792860667439,"completed_at_ms":1792860667914}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-24T16:51:07.937Z","ordinal":297395,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a16ed1-0bd9-75c0-b3f2-6fda13432e3d","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-a3d91d95-96dc-490e-8110-65b6adfa510d","process_id":"37502","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","gh pr view 191 --json body,files --jq '{body:.body,files:[.files[].path]}'"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"gh pr view 191 --json body,files --jq '{body:.body,files:[.files[].path]}'"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"{\"body\":\"## Defect\\n\\n`isPublicIp`, `isSafeOutboundUrl`/`safeFetch` and `classifyLocality` treated the NAT64 well-known prefix `64:ff9b::/96` as ordinary public IPv6. Its low 32 bits are the destination IPv4 address, so on an IPv6-only/NAT64 network `http://[64:ff9b::7f00:1]/` reaches `127.0.0.1` and passes the SSRF guard. The locality classifier also reported `EXTERNAL_PUBLIC`, allowing an external-boundary policy to send data to a loopback/private service.\\n\\nPre-fix: `isPublicIp(\\\"64:ff9b::7f00:1\\\") === true`, `isSafeOutboundUrl(\\\"http://[64:ff9b::7f00:1]/\\\").safe === true`, `classifyLocality(\\\"http://[64:ff9b::7f00:1]:8000\\\") === EXTERNAL_PUBLIC`.\\n\\n## Fix\\n\\n- Classify `64:ff9b::/96` by the embedded IPv4 address (loopback, RFC1918, CGNAT, link-local, documentation, multicast/reserved rejected; public embedded addresses stay reachable).\\n- Reject the RFC 8215 local-use `64:ff9b:1::/48`.\\n- Reuse one `classifyIpv4Trust` helper for IPv4 literals, IPv4-mapped addresses and NAT64 in `classifyLocality`.\\n\\n## Verification\\n\\n- `fetch_web_ssrf.test.ts`: 10/10; new assertions fail on pre-fix `tools.ts`.\\n- `egress.test.ts`: 28/28; `ACC-TRUST-02` fails on pre-fix `egress.ts`.\\n- Combined 38/38; `tsc`; `git diff --check`: pass.\\n- Evidence: `docs/reviews/evidence/v1/DEFECT-NAT64-SSRF-20261024/README.md`.\\n\\n## Residuals\\n\\nOperator-specific NAT64 prefixes (`/64`, `/56`, `/40`, `/32`) cannot be recognized from the address alone; Teredo/6to4 behavior unchanged.\\n\\n## Coordination\\n\\nUnclaimed slice; independent review and exact-head CI to follow.\",\"files\":[\"cli/src/core/egress.ts\",\"cli/src/tools.ts\",\"cli/test/egress.test.ts\",\"cli/test/fetch_web_ssrf.test.ts\",\"docs/reviews/evidence/v1/DEFECT-NAT64-SSRF-20261024/README.md\"]}\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":539063243}},"started_at_ms":1792860667394,"completed_at_ms":1792860667933}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-24T16:51:07.955Z","ordinal":297396,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a16ed1-0bd9-75c0-b3f2-6fda13432e3d","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-c1530e04-399b-4f72-a13c-4373fff10096","process_id":"65440","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","gh pr view 197 --json body,files --jq '{body:.body,files:[.files[].path]}'"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"gh pr view 197 --json body,files --jq '{body:.body,files:[.files[].path]}'"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"{\"body\":\"## Defect\\n\\n`edit_file` and `patch_file` read the entire target with `read_to_string` and no size check. `read_file` refuses files above `MAX_READ_BYTES` (8 MB) and `file_info` now stops counting above it, but a model naming a multi-gigabyte workspace file can still make the single Rust bridge allocate the whole file (plus replacement/diff copies), blocking or OOM-ing the agent.\\n\\nPre-fix probe: an 8 MB + 1 file was edited and rewritten by both tools.\\n\\n## Fix\\n\\nCheck the opened descriptor's size before reading; above `MAX_READ_BYTES`, return a clear error and leave the file untouched. Cap the read with `take(MAX_READ_BYTES + 1)` and re-check so growth after the size check stays bounded. `write_file` is unchanged (its content already arrived in memory).\\n\\n## Verification\\n\\n- New edit and patch tests fail pre-fix (oversized file modified) and pass now; both assert byte-identical content and an error naming the 8 MB limit.\\n- `cargo test --bin harness-core file_ops::` 18/18; full `cargo test --bin harness-core` 37/37.\\n- `git diff --check`: pass.\\n- Evidence: `docs/reviews/evidence/v1/DEFECT-EDIT-FILE-UNBOUNDED-20261024/README.md`.\\n\\n## Residuals\\n\\nAt/below 8 MB is still read whole; no streaming/partial edits for larger files; concurrent growth after the capped read is not prevented; binary handling unchanged.\\n\\n## Coordination\\n\\nUnclaimed slice on the unclaimed `core/src/file_ops.rs` after the previous slice merged. Independent review and exact-head CI to follow.\",\"files\":[\"core/src/file_ops.rs\",\"docs/reviews/evidence/v1/DEFECT-EDIT-FILE-UNBOUNDED-20261024/README.md\"]}\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":478930621}},"started_at_ms":1792860667473,"completed_at_ms":1792860667952}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-24T16:51:09.494Z","ordinal":297397,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a16ed2-c636-72c1-89dc-94ca6d1cffda","call_id":"call_6d8cbd39a6a54328ba2975053738c193","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 3.4 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"body\":\"## Defect\\n\\n`isPublicIp`, `isSafeOutboundUrl`/`safeFetch` and `classifyLocality` treated the NAT64 well-known prefix `64:ff9b::/96` as ordinary public IPv6. Its low 32 bits are the destination IPv4 address, so on an IPv6-only/NAT64 network `http://[64:ff9b::7f00:1]/` reaches `127.0.0.1` and passes the SSRF guard. The locality classifier also reported `EXTERNAL_PUBLIC`, allowing an external-boundary policy to send data to a loopback/private service.\\n\\nPre-fix: `isPublicIp(\\\"64:ff9b::7f00:1\\\") === true`, `isSafeOutboundUrl(\\\"http://[64:ff9b::7f00:1]/\\\").safe === true`, `classifyLocality(\\\"http://[64:ff9b::7f00:1]:8000\\\") === EXTERNAL_PUBLIC`.\\n\\n## Fix\\n\\n- Classify `64:ff9b::/96` by the embedded IPv4 address (loopback, RFC1918, CGNAT, link-local, documentation, multicast/reserved rejected; public embedded addresses stay reachable).\\n- Reject the RFC 8215 local-use `64:ff9b:1::/48`.\\n- Reuse one `classifyIpv4Trust` helper for IPv4 literals, IPv4-mapped addresses and NAT64 in `classifyLocality`.\\n\\n## Verification\\n\\n- `fetch_web_ssrf.test.ts`: 10/10; new assertions fail on pre-fix `tools.ts`.\\n- `egress.test.ts`: 28/28; `ACC-TRUST-02` fails on pre-fix `egress.ts`.\\n- Combined 38/38; `tsc`; `git diff --check`: pass.\\n- Evidence: `docs/reviews/evidence/v1/DEFECT-NAT64-SSRF-20261024/README.md`.\\n\\n## Residuals\\n\\nOperator-specific NAT64 prefixes (`/64`, `/56`, `/40`, `/32`) cannot be recognized from the address alone; Teredo/6to4 behavior unchanged.\\n\\n## Coordination\\n\\nUnclaimed slice; independent review and exact-head CI to follow.\",\"files\":[\"cli/src/core/egress.ts\",\"cli/src/tools.ts\",\"cli/test/egress.test.ts\",\"cli/test/fetch_web_ssrf.test.ts\",\"docs/reviews/evidence/v1/DEFECT-NAT64-SSRF-20261024/README.md\"]}\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"body\":\"## Defect\\n\\n`McpClientManager.addServer` persisted `~/.config/nexus/mcp.json` with the default `0644` mode and a `0755` directory, while a server definition's `env` may carry its own token. It also parsed the existing config inside `catch {}`, so an unparseable file was treated as empty and replaced — silently dropping every other server — and the caller was still told \\\"Saved\\\".\\n\\nPre-fix probe: mode `644`, dir `755`, existing `keep` server gone after adding a server to a config with a trailing comma.\\n\\n## Fix\\n\\n- `~/.config/nexus` is created/tightened to `0700`; the config is written to a `0600` temporary file and renamed atomically (following an existing symlink target).\\n- Existing config is parsed and validated first; a non-object or unparseable file is left byte-for-byte untouched.\\n- `addServer` returns `persisted`/`persistError`; the REPL wizard and `/mcp add` report the failure instead of claiming the config was saved.\\n\\n## Verification\\n\\n- New `cli/test/mcp.test.ts`: 2/2; pre-fix fails with `config mode 644 leaks a server token` and with the overwritten-config assertion.\\n- `workspace_trust.test.ts` + new tests: 7/7; `tsc`; `git diff --check`.\\n- Evidence: `docs/reviews/evidence/v1/DEFECT-MCP-CONFIG-PERSIST-20261024/README.md`.\\n\\n## Residuals\\n\\nUnchmod-able config directory fails closed; a dangling symlink is replaced; an unparseable config must be fixed by the operator before persisting.\\n\\n## Coordination\\n\\nUnclaimed slice; independent review and exact-head CI to follow.\",\"files\":[\"cli/src/mcp.ts\",\"cli/src/repl.ts\",\"cli/src/slash/extension_commands.ts\",\"cli/test/mcp.test.ts\",\"docs/reviews/evidence/v1/DEFECT-MCP-CONFIG-PERSIST-20261024/README.md\"]}\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"body\":\"## Summary\\n\\nFixes the RC cross-runner reproducibility workflow's compare job, which failed before execution because it used the `actions/upload-artifact` commit as the `actions/download-artifact` pin.\\n\\nBoth download steps now use the verified `actions/download-artifact` v4 commit `d3f86a106a0bac45b974a628896c90dbdf5c8093`. The upload-artifact pins and tagged RC source remain unchanged.\\n\\n## Validation\\n\\n- Exact base: `be2cd2f255414f554572c86baa884d9271ff5ea1`\\n- `actionlint .github/workflows/repro.yml`: passed\\n- `git diff --check`: passed\\n- Independent review: ACCEPT; same two-line patch identity as the reviewed candidate\\n- Exact PR CI pending\\n\\nThis workflow fix enables the published RC4 cross-runner build comparison to complete. It does not qualify the RC or change release acceptance status.\\n\",\"files\":[\".github/workflows/repro.yml\"]}\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"body\":\"## Defect\\n\\n`file_info` is the metadata tool, but for every regular file it `mmap`s the whole file and iterates every byte to compute `line_count`, with no `MAX_READ_BYTES` check. `read_file` refuses files above 8 MB unless paged; `file_info` would still scan a multi-gigabyte file, blocking the single Rust bridge and faulting pages into memory.\\n\\nPre-fix probe on an 8 MB + 1 file returned `line_count: Some(8388609)`.\\n\\n## Fix\\n\\nOnly compute `line_count`/binary detection when the file is within `MAX_READ_BYTES`, the same limit the read tool uses. Larger files still report `size_bytes`, type, permissions and timestamps, with `line_count: None` (already the case for binary/unreadable files).\\n\\n## Verification\\n\\n- New regression fails pre-fix (`Some(8388609) != None`) and passes now.\\n- `cargo test --bin harness-core file_ops::` 16/16; full `cargo test --bin harness-core` 35/35.\\n- `git diff --check`: pass.\\n- Evidence: `docs/reviews/evidence/v1/DEFECT-FILE-INFO-UNBOUNDED-20261024/README.md`.\\n\\n## Residuals\\n\\nNo line count above 8 MB (use `read_file --offset/--length` or `wc -l`); mmap/SIGBUS on concurrent truncation and whole-file `edit_file`/`patch_file` are pre-existing and out of scope.\\n\\n## Coordination\\n\\nTook over the stale `FILE_core_src_file_ops.rs` claim (owner branch merged as PR #52, no PID, 6 days old; recorded as BROKEN_CLAIM). Independent review and exact-head CI to follow.\",\"files\":[\"core/src/file_ops.rs\",\"docs/reviews/evidence/v1/DEFECT-FILE-INFO-UNBOUNDED-20261024/README.md\"]}\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"body\":\"## Reproduced release blocker\\n\\nCross-runner qualification for the published `v1.0.0-rc.4` was dispatched from exact `main` revision `72e769348fe8a978a576627a4802cb6b68ced779` in workflow run `40103980794`. Both Ubuntu 22.04 and 24.04 builds completed, but archive comparison failed at byte 19. The 22.04 archive matches the published RC4 archive; the 24.04 archive differs. I downloaded the immutable workflow artifacts and confirmed the extracted package trees are byte-identical, including identical `MANIFEST.sha256`. The first tar header differs in its device-number fields, which changes the tar checksum and archive digest. This leaves `REQ-REL-114` unqualified for RC4.\\n\\n## Fix\\n\\nGenerate the package archive with the same digest-pinned build container used for the Rust build so host-specific tar metadata does not affect output bytes. The change preserves package payload, version, and compatibility metadata. Both the CI and tagged release workflows set this exact builder image.\\n\\n## Current candidate\\n\\n- Head: `da5f26925b4379187e1f96a8ccf924209b7ebb84`\\n- Base: `e624de04ca6ddebc3b08bf8e13375011d227c7e8`\\n- Scope: `scripts/package-linux.sh` only\\n- Independent review: ACCEPT by `plan05_readonly_review` at this exact head; net patch SHA-256 `a34a2211eef52d580c6e300b2ce88b7115b23e4cf60fb011b896af4cd009f20`\\n- Exact-head CI: CodeQL, JavaScript/TypeScript analysis, CodeRabbit, Node 22 and Node 24 passed. Linux x86_64 package/reproducibility/SBOM/smoke/installer job is in progress in run `40108251357`.\\n- Current main CI on the exact base (`40105438204`) and CodeQL (`40105438209`) passed.\\n- No local test suite was run because the repository's `SUITE` claim remains held by `KimiCode-defect-scan`.\\n\\nA fresh exact-head CI and a new cross-runner comparison against a newly built RC are required. RC4 remains immutable; this PR cannot retroactively change its failed reproduction result.\\n\",\"files\":[\"scripts/package-linux.sh\"]}\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"body\":\"## Defect\\n\\n`edit_file` and `patch_file` read the entire target with `read_to_string` and no size check. `read_file` refuses files above `MAX_READ_BYTES` (8 MB) and `file_info` now stops counting above it, but a model naming a multi-gigabyte workspace file can still make the single Rust bridge allocate the whole file (plus replacement/diff copies), blocking or OOM-ing the agent.\\n\\nPre-fix probe: an 8 MB + 1 file was edited and rewritten by both tools.\\n\\n## Fix\\n\\nCheck the opened descriptor's size before reading; above `MAX_READ_BYTES`, return a clear error and leave the file untouched. Cap the read with `take(MAX_READ_BYTES + 1)` and re-check so growth after the size check stays bounded. `write_file` is unchanged (its content already arrived in memory).\\n\\n## Verification\\n\\n- New edit and patch tests fail pre-fix (oversized file modified) and pass now; both assert byte-identical content and an error naming the 8 MB limit.\\n- `cargo test --bin harness-core file_ops::` 18/18; full `cargo test --bin harness-core` 37/37.\\n- `git diff --check`: pass.\\n- Evidence: `docs/reviews/evidence/v1/DEFECT-EDIT-FILE-UNBOUNDED-20261024/README.md`.\\n\\n## Residuals\\n\\nAt/below 8 MB is still read whole; no streaming/partial edits for larger files; concurrent growth after the capped read is not prevented; binary handling unchanged.\\n\\n## Coordination\\n\\nUnclaimed slice on the unclaimed `core/src/file_ops.rs` after the previous slice merged. Independent review and exact-head CI to follow.\",\"files\":[\"core/src/file_ops.rs\",\"docs/reviews/evidence/v1/DEFECT-EDIT-FILE-UNBOUNDED-20261024/README.md\"]}\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a16ed1-0bd9-75c0-b3f2-6fda13432e3d","create_time":1792860669.4945014}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
