{"timestamp":"2026-10-24T16:51:19.322Z","ordinal":297405,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a16ed1-0bd9-75c0-b3f2-6fda13432e3d","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-55ba0908-a932-40fb-941c-70e3e42f9a5d","process_id":"15845","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","sed -n '1,180p' .github/workflows/release.yml; rg -n 'rc\\.\\*|v1\\.0\\.0-rc|tag_name|release.yml' .github/workflows docs/v1.0.0 docs/releases -g '!**/node_modules/**'"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-wt/rc5-version-sync","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '1,180p' .github/workflows/release.yml","name":"release.yml","path":".github/workflows/release.yml"},{"type":"search","cmd":"rg -n \"rc\\\\.\\\\*|v1\\\\.0\\\\.0-rc|tag_name|release.yml\" .github/workflows docs/v1.0.0 docs/releases -g '!**/node_modules/**'","query":"rc\\.\\*|v1\\.0\\.0-rc|tag_name|release.yml","path":"workflows"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"name: Release\n\non:\n  push:\n    tags: [\"v*.*.*\"]\n\npermissions:\n  contents: write\n  id-token: write\n  attestations: write\n\njobs:\n  package:\n    runs-on: ubuntu-22.04\n    permissions:\n      contents: write\n      id-token: write\n      attestations: write\n    env:\n      NEXUS_BUILD_CONTAINER_IMAGE: rust:1.95.0-bookworm@sha256:4c2fd73ef19c5ef9d54bee03b06b2839a392604fbfcd578ed948b71b37c1d7fb\n    steps:\n      - uses: actions/checkout@11d5960a326750d5838078e36cf38b85af677262 # v4\n        with:\n          fetch-depth: 0\n      - run: sudo apt-get update\n      - run: sudo apt-get install --yes acl make bubblewrap build-essential meson ninja-build pkg-config libcap-dev\n      - run: bash scripts/ensure-ci-bubblewrap.sh\n      - run: bash scripts/ensure-ci-user-cgroups.sh\n      - name: Mount a dedicated capped tmpfs for evaluator resource fixtures\n        run: |\n          root=/mnt/nexus-eval-release\n          sudo install -d -o \"$USER\" -g \"$USER\" -m 0711 \"$root\"\n          sudo mount -t tmpfs -o size=128m,mode=0711,uid=\"$(id -u)\",gid=\"$(id -g)\" nexus-eval-release \"$root\"\n          echo \"NEXUS_EVAL_TEST_WORKSPACE_ROOT=$root\" >> \"$GITHUB_ENV\"\n          runtime_root=/opt/nexus-eval-ci-runtime\n          sudo install -d -o \"$USER\" -g \"$USER\" -m 0711 \"$runtime_root\"\n          echo \"NEXUS_EVAL_TEST_RUNTIME_ROOT=$runtime_root\" >> \"$GITHUB_ENV\"\n      - uses: dtolnay/rust-toolchain@b725eda525362e7cf34af9a7243cac1e3f01a7ec # stable\n      - name: Install cargo tools (audit, deny, about, cyclonedx)\n        run: |\n          CARGO_HOME=\"${CARGO_HOME:-$HOME/.cargo}\"\n          export CARGO_HOME\n          mkdir -p \"$CARGO_HOME/bin\"\n          echo \"$CARGO_HOME/bin\" >> \"$GITHUB_PATH\"\n          export PATH=\"$CARGO_HOME/bin:$PATH\"\n          cargo install cargo-audit --locked --version 0.22.2\n          curl -fsSL https://github.com/EmbarkStudios/cargo-deny/releases/download/0.20.2/cargo-deny-0.20.2-x86_64-unknown-linux-musl.tar.gz | tar -xz -C \"$RUNNER_TEMP\"\n          mv \"$RUNNER_TEMP/cargo-deny-0.20.2-x86_64-unknown-linux-musl/cargo-deny\" \"$CARGO_HOME/bin/\"\n          curl -fsSL https://github.com/EmbarkStudios/cargo-about/releases/download/0.9.2/cargo-about-0.9.2-x86_64-unknown-linux-musl.tar.gz | tar -xz -C \"$RUNNER_TEMP\"\n          mv \"$RUNNER_TEMP/cargo-about-0.9.2-x86_64-unknown-linux-musl/cargo-about\" \"$CARGO_HOME/bin/\"\n          curl -fsSL https://github.com/CycloneDX/cyclonedx-rust-cargo/releases/download/cargo-cyclonedx-0.5.9/cargo-cyclonedx-x86_64-unknown-linux-musl.tar.xz | tar -xJ -C \"$RUNNER_TEMP\"\n          mv \"$RUNNER_TEMP/cargo-cyclonedx-x86_64-unknown-linux-musl/cargo-cyclonedx\" \"$CARGO_HOME/bin/\"\n          curl -fsSL https://github.com/CycloneDX/cyclonedx-cli/releases/download/v0.33.1/cyclonedx-linux-x64 -o \"$CARGO_HOME/bin/cyclonedx\"\n          chmod +x \"$CARGO_HOME/bin/cyclonedx\"\n      - uses: actions/setup-node@49933ea5288caeca8642d1e84afbd3f7d6820020 # v4\n        with:\n          node-version: 22\n          cache: npm\n          cache-dependency-path: cli/package-lock.json\n      - name: Install selected Node runtime for isolated evaluation commands\n        run: |\n          node_runtime=\"$(readlink -f \"$(command -v node)\")\"\n          npm_cli=\"$(readlink -f \"$(command -v npm)\")\"\n          npm_root=\"$(dirname \"$(dirname \"$npm_cli\")\")\"\n          case \"$npm_root\" in */lib/node_modules/npm) ;; *) echo \"Unexpected setup-node npm package path\" >&2; exit 1 ;; esac\n          test -f \"$npm_root/package.json\"\n          sudo install -o root -g root -m 0755 \"$node_runtime\" /usr/bin/node\n          sudo install -d -o root -g root -m 0755 /usr/lib/nexus-ci/npm\n          sudo cp -a \"$npm_root/.\" /usr/lib/nexus-ci/npm/\n          sudo chown -hR root:root /usr/lib/nexus-ci/npm\n          sudo chmod 0755 /usr/lib/nexus-ci/npm/bin/npm-cli.js\n          sudo ln -sfn /usr/lib/nexus-ci/npm/bin/npm-cli.js /usr/bin/npm\n          test \"$(/usr/bin/node --version)\" = \"$(node --version)\"\n          test \"$(env PATH=/usr/bin:/bin /usr/bin/npm --version)\" = \"$(npm --version)\"\n      - name: Require a version-matched tag on main\n        run: |\n          git fetch origin main --no-tags\n          git merge-base --is-ancestor \"$GITHUB_SHA\" origin/main\n          test \"${GITHUB_REF_NAME#v}\" = \"$(node -p 'require(\"./package.json\").version')\"\n          node scripts/sync-version.mjs --check --tag \"$GITHUB_REF_NAME\"\n          test -f \"docs/releases/${GITHUB_REF_NAME}.md\" || { echo \"Missing docs/releases/${GITHUB_REF_NAME}.md\" >&2; exit 1; }\n      - name: Require a stable tag to be a version-only commit on its RC\n        if: ${{ !contains(github.ref_name, '-') }}\n        # The checkout has full history and tags (fetch-depth: 0). The checker runs from the RC's own copy so a stable\n        # commit cannot replace it; branch and tag protection remain the control over the workflow file itself.\n        run: |\n          rc=\"$(git tag --points-at \"$GITHUB_SHA^\" | grep -E \"^${GITHUB_REF_NAME//./\\\\.}-rc\\.[0-9]+$\" | sort -V | tail -n 1 || true)\"\n          test -n \"$rc\" || { echo \"the parent of $GITHUB_REF_NAME is not a ${GITHUB_REF_NAME}-rc.N tag\" >&2; exit 1; }\n          git show \"$rc:scripts/check-version-only-diff.mjs\" > \"$RUNNER_TEMP/check-version-only-diff.mjs\"\n          node \"$RUNNER_TEMP/check-version-only-diff.mjs\" \"$rc\" \"$GITHUB_SHA\"\n      - run: npm ci --prefix cli\n      - run: npm --prefix cli run build\n      - run: cargo test --locked --manifest-path core/Cargo.toml\n      - run: cargo build --locked --release --manifest-path core/Cargo.toml --bin harness-core --bin nexus-tui\n      - run: npm --prefix cli test\n      - run: bash scripts/security_gates.sh\n      - run: bash scripts/package-linux.sh \"$GITHUB_REF_NAME\" \"$RUNNER_TEMP/dist\"\n      - run: bash scripts/package-linux.sh \"$GITHUB_REF_NAME\" \"$RUNNER_TEMP/repro-check\"\n      - run: cmp \"$RUNNER_TEMP/dist/nexus-linux-x86_64-$GITHUB_REF_NAME.tar.gz\" \"$RUNNER_TEMP/repro-check/nexus-linux-x86_64-$GITHUB_REF_NAME.tar.gz\"\n      - run: cmp \"$RUNNER_TEMP/dist/SHA256SUMS\" \"$RUNNER_TEMP/repro-check/SHA256SUMS\"\n      - run: cmp \"$RUNNER_TEMP/dist/THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.txt\" \"$RUNNER_TEMP/repro-check/THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.txt\"\n      - run: cyclonedx validate --input-file \"$RUNNER_TEMP/dist/sbom.cdx.json\" --fail-on-errors\n      - run: cmp \"$RUNNER_TEMP/dist/sbom.cdx.json\" \"$RUNNER_TEMP/repro-check/sbom.cdx.json\"\n      - run: cmp \"$RUNNER_TEMP/dist/install.sh\" \"$RUNNER_TEMP/repro-check/install.sh\"\n      - run: bash scripts/smoke-package.sh \"$RUNNER_TEMP/dist/nexus-linux-x86_64-$GITHUB_REF_NAME.tar.gz\"\n      - run: bash scripts/installer-smoke.sh \"$GITHUB_WORKSPACE/install.sh\" \"$RUNNER_TEMP/dist/nexus-linux-x86_64-$GITHUB_REF_NAME.tar.gz\"\n      - name: Attest build provenance\n        uses: actions/attest-build-provenance@92c65d2898f1f53cfdc910b962cecff86e7f8fcc # v1\n        with:\n          subject-path: |\n            ${{ runner.temp }}/dist/nexus-linux-x86_64-${{ github.ref_name }}.tar.gz\n            ${{ runner.temp }}/dist/SHA256SUMS\n      # RC tags (vX.Y.Z-rc.N) publish a prerelease: the workflow-produced RC is the qualification candidate\n      # (ACCEPTANCE §1.1 stage 2). Stable tags only build an unpublished draft (stage 5); it is published by hand with\n      # `gh release edit <tag> --draft=false` after the stable artifact checks and the signed acceptance disposition.\n      - uses: softprops/action-gh-release@3bb12739c298aeb8a4eeaf626c5b8d85266b0e65 # v2\n        with:\n          files: ${{ runner.temp }}/dist/*\n          body_path: docs/releases/${{ github.ref_name }}.md\n          prerelease: ${{ contains(github.ref_name, '-') }}\n          draft: ${{ !contains(github.ref_name, '-') }}\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.3.md:1:# Nexus Code v1.0.0-rc.3 release candidate\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.3.md:27:The release workflow for `v1.0.0-rc.3` is expected to produce the version-matched Linux archive, `SHA256SUMS`, SBOM, notices, installer, and provenance. The workflow run, tag commit, artifact digests, and qualification evidence must be recorded before this candidate can be accepted. Local builds are not interchangeable with the workflow-produced artifacts.\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.2.md:1:# Nexus Code v1.0.0-rc.2 release candidate\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.2.md:20:- As tagged, this candidate declares Node.js 20 or newer. Node.js 20 reached upstream end of life on 2026-04-30, and DEC-12 now requires Node.js 22 or newer for v1.0.0, so `v1.0.0-rc.2` is not promotable to v1.0.0; a later candidate carries the Node.js 22 floor.\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.2.md:27:The release workflow for `v1.0.0-rc.2` produces the version-matched Linux archive, `SHA256SUMS`, SBOM, notices, installer, and provenance. The workflow run, tag commit, artifact digests, and qualification evidence must be recorded before this candidate can be accepted. Local builds are not interchangeable with the workflow-produced artifacts.\n.github/workflows/repro.yml:7:        description: Published v1.0.0 RC tag with lock-pinned release tools (for example v1.0.0-rc.4)\n.github/workflows/repro.yml:44:            echo \"Expected a v1.0.0-rc.N tag; received an invalid tag.\" >&2\ndocs/v1.0.0/README.md:50:5. Cut `v1.0.0-rc.1` only when G0–G4 pass. Then run ACCEPTANCE §4–§8 against the **installed** RC.\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.1.md:1:# Nexus Code v1.0.0-rc.1 release candidate\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.1.md:23:The release workflow builds the version-matched archive, `SHA256SUMS`, SBOM, notices, installer, and provenance for tag `v1.0.0-rc.1`. The workflow outputs and their digests are the qualification candidate; a local build is not interchangeable.\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.4.md:1:# Nexus Code v1.0.0-rc.4 release candidate\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.4.md:38:The release workflow for `v1.0.0-rc.4` is expected to produce the version-matched Linux archive, `SHA256SUMS`, SBOM, notices, installer, and provenance. The workflow run, tag commit, artifact digests, and qualification evidence must be recorded before this candidate can be accepted. Local builds are not interchangeable with the workflow-produced artifacts.\ndocs/releases/PROTECTIONS.md:14:| Default workflow token | `read`; workflows request extra permissions themselves (`release.yml`: `contents`, `id-token`, `attestations` write) |\ndocs/releases/PROTECTIONS.md:43:   commit `M`. The RC tag `v1.0.0-rc.N` goes on `M`, which is on `main`, so `release.yml`'s ancestry check passes.\ndocs/releases/PROTECTIONS.md:48:   keeps `S` in `main`'s history. Tag `v1.0.0` goes on `S`. `release.yml` verifies it is version-only on `rc.N`.\ndocs/releases/PROTECTIONS.md:53:4. **Publication.** `release.yml` creates the stable release as a draft. `gh release edit v1.0.0 --draft=false` is not\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:77:| REQ-REL-002 | release.yml | Release is gated on main ancestry, a version match, the full suite, a same-runner byte-reproducible package, and package and installer smoke tests. | `.github/workflows/release.yml` | RT (CI log 905/905) | tested | N | Cross-runner reproducibility unproven | ACC-SUP-08 | K | SPEC-07 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:188:| REQ-REL-103 | Audit | A single version across tag, package.json files, Cargo and the core handshake. | compatibility / supportability | `core/Cargo.toml:3`; `release.yml` | TEST (ACC-PKG-03; test:cli/test/engine_handshake.test.ts, core/tests/rpc_shutdown.rs) | tested | ACC-PKG-03 | **B** | REL-04 | SPEC-06 / PLAN-06 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:198:| REQ-REL-109 | TOP_TIER D4 | Provenance attestation; tag-pinned installer asset. | supply chain | `release.yml` | TEST (ACC-SUP-03; test:release.yml, install.sh) | tested | ACC-SUP-03 | RR | REL-09 | SPEC-07 / PLAN-07 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:200:| REQ-REL-111 | Audit; DEC-12 | CI matrix for Node 22/24; release, reproducibility and evaluator builds use Node 22; pinned toolchain and MSRV, engines field, dist freshness (untracked). | compatibility | `ci.yml`, `release.yml`, `repro.yml` | At exact candidate `7c46a6d52095588f48579d9a96c5b2d526bdb3d9`, PR #150 CI run `39866110578` passed both required matrix jobs (Node 22 job `120128589470`; Node 24 job `120128589221`). The same revision declares Node `>=22` in both package manifests, uses pinned Rust/MSRV, sets release and reproducibility packaging to Node 22, and runs the `cli/dist` freshness check in the matrix and package workflows. Exact-candidate Linux packaging remains a separate active source gate; this row covers ACC-SUP-05 only. | tested | ACC-SUP-05 | RR | REL-13, MNT-01 | SPEC-07 / PLAN-07 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:201:| REQ-REL-112 | REL-004 (carried) | SECURITY.md, CHANGELOG.md, release body taken from release notes. | supportability | root, `release.yml` | TEST (ACC-SUP-06; test:SECURITY.md, CHANGELOG.md, release.yml) | tested | ACC-SUP-06 | RR | HIST-07, MNT-05 | SPEC-07 / PLAN-07 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:133:- Release line: `v1.0.0-rc.N` prereleases, then `v1.0.0`.\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:159:This supersedes the earlier Node ≥ 20 decision. The immutable `v1.0.0-rc.2` tag targets `19d6f0a80e21f9b640a46ee12200c4f5f6d967a4`, whose package engine and workflows still use Node 20; that tag is not a qualifying RC under this decision.\ndocs/v1.0.0/AUDIT.md:22:| Build entry points | `make build` (cargo release + `tsc`), `make test` (cargo test + `npm --prefix cli test` + `scripts/security_gates.sh`), `scripts/package-linux.sh`, `scripts/smoke-package.sh`, `scripts/installer-smoke.sh`. CI: `.github/workflows/ci.yml` (contest contract job + `linux-x86_64`), `release.yml` (tag-triggered). A dead `.gitlab-ci.yml` also exists. | SRC |\ndocs/v1.0.0/AUDIT.md:274:| REL-09 | S3 | RR | Integrity | `release.yml` | SRC | No provenance | REQ-REL-109 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/AUDIT.md:283:| MNT-05 | S4 | RR | Changelog | `release.yml:47` | RT | Curated notes not shown | REQ-REL-112 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ROADMAP.md:30:| **RC1** | After PLAN-09 task 7's pre-RC source-ledger reconciliation and enforce gate, tag `v1.0.0-rc.1` (owner approves publishing a prerelease; X7) | RC build installed through the documented command | G0–G4 green on the exact RC source; pre-RC requirements enforcement passed | <1 ed |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:341:  The version 1 record contains `sourceCommit` (full commit ID), `rcTag` (for example `v1.0.0-rc.1`), `artifactSha256`, `artifactProvenance` (`sourceCommit`, `artifactSha256`, and a hashed provenance report), `independentAcceptance` (`disposition`, `reviewer`, `implementers`, zero `blockingDefects`, and a hashed report reference), and one `requirements` entry for every B/RR row. For `ACCEPT WITH DEFECTS`, include each non-blocking defect with its owner disposition; unresolved or blocking defects fail. Each requirement entry records its status and one or more hashed evidence files covering the exact criteria required by the ledger and the §1.1 qualification-only map. Every criterion evidence file must be a JSON object with top-level `sourceCommit`, `rcTag`, and `artifactSha256` values exactly matching the validated qualification record, current RC source commit, and installed RC artifact. A digest-valid report copied from another source revision, RC tag, or artifact is rejected. A B row recorded as `tested` also needs a non-empty `qualificationNotApplicable.reason` and a `qualificationNotApplicable.decision` matching the approved per-requirement exception table and a matching applicability declaration in DECISIONS.md; an unrelated or record-supplied decision is rejected. Evidence paths must be relative regular files under the evidence root, with no symlinks. Missing, unknown, stale, mismatched, or incomplete evidence fails the gate. The checker requires a clean worktree, rejects `--ledger` overrides, enforces source-ledger thresholds outside the explicit §1.1 lifecycle rows, and requires the exact-RC record itself to meet the normal status threshold for every row. It never mutates the source ledger or relaxes a requirement's B/RR record threshold. The checker validates source/tag/artifact identity bindings and evidence hashes; it does not authenticate the reviewer or prove that the artifact was built from the source commit. The approved release workflow must independently verify build provenance/attestation, and the designated custodian and independent reviewer must verify their respective approvals and custody evidence.\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-06-packaged-product-parity.md:22:- `.github/workflows/release.yml`\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-06-packaged-product-parity.md:33:| 3 | `scripts/sync-version.mjs` writes `package.json` → `cli/package.json` + `core/Cargo.toml` (and `Cargo.lock` via `cargo update -p harness-core --offline`). Run it now to set Cargo to `0.1.0-alpha.2`. The release workflow asserts equality with the tag. | new script; `core/Cargo.toml:3`; `release.yml:27-31` | — |\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-06-packaged-product-parity.md:58:| `release.yml` negative check: a job step runs `sync-version.mjs --check` and fails on mismatch | ACC-PKG-03 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-07-supply-chain-and-release-engineering.md:26:| 2 | Third-party notices: install cargo-about and the npm license checker in CI. Use `about.toml` with an allowlist (MIT, Apache-2.0, BSD-2/3, ISC, Unicode-3.0, Zlib, MPL-2.0 only if reviewed). Have `package-linux.sh` write `THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.txt` and upload it as an asset. | `package-linux.sh:22`; `release.yml` | 1 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-07-supply-chain-and-release-engineering.md:27:| 3 | `cargo deny check licenses advisories` in CI. Make `security_gates.sh` fail if `cargo-audit`/`cargo-deny` is missing, and delete `audit_rust_deps.py`. | `security_gates.sh:84-97`; `ci.yml`; `release.yml` | 1 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-07-supply-chain-and-release-engineering.md:28:| 4 | Build the SBOM from lockfiles with cyclonedx-npm and cargo-cyclonedx, merge and validate, and attach it to the release. Replace `generate_sbom.sh` and update `make sbom`. | `scripts/generate_sbom.sh`; `Makefile`; `release.yml` | — |\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-07-supply-chain-and-release-engineering.md:29:| 5 | Add provenance with `actions/attest-build-provenance` on the tarball and SHA256SUMS, and upload `install.sh` as a release asset. The installer optionally runs `gh attestation verify` when `gh` is available. | `release.yml:44-48`; `install.sh` | — |\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-07-supply-chain-and-release-engineering.md:33:| 9 | Write `SECURITY.md` (private reporting via GitHub Security Advisories, supported versions, 7-day acknowledgement target) and `CHANGELOG.md` (back-filled from docs/releases). Set the release body from `docs/releases/<tag>.md` (`body_path`), and fail if that file is missing. | root; `release.yml` | — |\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:19:**Exact source gates:** `origin/main` and the signed `v1.0.0-rc.3` tag resolve to source commit `1b9791f07d301c885fe48f04a796203583ab5a5c`. Exact-main CI [39923089278](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/39923089278) and CodeQL [39923089363](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/39923089363) completed successfully on that commit. CI passed Node 22, Node 24, Linux CLI tests, security gates, requirements checks, two-build package reproducibility, SBOM validation, package smoke, and installer smoke. `node scripts/sync-version.mjs --check --tag v1.0.0-rc.3` and `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` passed at the same source; the latter reports 123 rows (108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open), with 12 explicit exact-RC qualification deferrals. This is source-gate evidence, not product acceptance.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:21:**RC3 artifact publication and provenance:** The annotated tag object is `dd68c222c57d0be0a4245a5b88092ff9df69201f`; its PGP signature verified good and it points to the source commit above. Release workflow [39927176480](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/39927176480) completed successfully and published the [v1.0.0-rc.3 prerelease](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/releases/tag/v1.0.0-rc.3). The workflow-produced Linux x86-64 archive is `nexus-linux-x86_64-v1.0.0-rc.3.tar.gz`, SHA-256 `efb446d2760f2e1aa7890e9d786b8a2ba8e4ebb784fbcac1e66afe827428864d`; `SHA256SUMS` is `9288edb4655a19caa40e1598c0a642ab7f7e93aafbb187c2bfc8cfa9e19f116f`; the CycloneDX SBOM is `3a3176b4b3890c1bc07fb7b3acd80f7372f043819e6a8b296346d014b07f9d3a`. Downloaded checksums and SBOM sidecars passed. GitHub attestations for the archive and `SHA256SUMS` verified against the Release workflow, run `39927176480`, tag `v1.0.0-rc.3`, and source `1b9791f`.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:23:**Installed-candidate and checkpoint-choice observation:** The published installer completed with `NEXUS_VERIFY_ATTESTATION=1` and installed RC3 under `/home/mike/.local/lib/nexus/v1.0.0-rc.3`; installer provenance records the exact archive digest and source revision. `/home/mike/.local/bin/nexus --version` reports `1.0.0-rc.3 (1b9791f07d30)`. The previous RC1 directory remains installed at `/home/mike/.local/lib/nexus/v1.0.0-rc.1` for rollback. The coordinator reported an automated PTY probe of the installed default TUI using a synthetic Git workspace, fake credential-shaped canary, and unreachable loopback endpoint. The reported probe displayed the five choices and selected cancel before inference. Its transcript/capture was not retained in the release evidence tree, so this observation is unarchived and was not independently verified in the readiness review. It is diagnostic context only: it does not establish the checkpoint-choice gate, the five-environment by three-size human terminal matrix, or provider/task qualification.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:35:**Checkpoint failure:** `/home/mike/.local/bin/nexus` resolves to the installed `v1.0.0-rc.1` package and reports `1.0.0-rc.1 (cb364c386c42)`. That immutable package lacks checkpoint choices, so the reported failure before turn start is reproducible by version identity and will persist on RC1. The fix is integrated in PR #147 (TUI/sidecar) and PR #153 (legacy REPL): before starting a turn, Nexus asks the operator whether to use read-only mode, continue in the configured mode without a rollback checkpoint, create the checkpoint with the sensitive-content risk acknowledged, cancel, or enter a different instruction. Both PRs passed exact-head checks, and the subsequent exact-main CI on `dac465d` passed. No replacement package has been installed. The public release page still has RC1 only; RC2 has a tag but no published release, and RC3 has neither tag nor release.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:53:**RC identity and publication:** Remote immutable tags remain `v1.0.0-rc.1` at `cb364c386c42faa53b67e04cacc81d7e01520779` and `v1.0.0-rc.2` at `19d6f0a80e21f9b640a46ee12200c4f5f6d967a4`; both predate the accepted Node 22 floor and checkpoint-choice fix. `node scripts/sync-version.mjs --check` passes at exact main and reports all components at `1.0.0-rc.2`. No accepted RC or stable v1.0.0 tag/release is established. A new candidate must use the next RC identity after source CI and release prerequisites pass, then undergo installed-artifact qualification.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:67:**RC identity and publication:** Remote immutable tags are `v1.0.0-rc.1` at `cb364c386c42faa53b67e04cacc81d7e01520779` and `v1.0.0-rc.2` at `19d6f0a80e21f9b640a46ee12200c4f5f6d967a4`; both predate the accepted Node 22 floor. GitHub currently publishes RC1 as a prerelease; RC2 has a tag but no published release. No accepted RC or stable v1.0.0 tag/release is established. The next candidate needs a fresh RC3 identity after its source/version checks; it must be installed and qualified before acceptance.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:79:The public `v1.0.0-rc.1` release remains the only published v1 candidate. `v1.0.0-rc.2` points to older source and is nonqualifying under the Node 22 decision. There is no accepted RC or stable release. Held-out custody, provider/standalone qualification, T2/T3/T4, cross-runner reproducibility, installed-RC packaging and qualification, five-terminal by three-size human evidence, and independent acceptance remain incomplete. Campaign status is `NEXUS_V1_CONVERGENCE_ACTIVE`; acceptance remains `IN_PROGRESS`; publication authorization remains granted and gated.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:93:**RC and publication:** The published `v1.0.0-rc.1` tag resolves to `cb364c386c42faa53b67e04cacc81d7e01520779`, an ancestor of current `main`, and is not an artifact built from current source. Its published asset digest is `8d7dd32f3d00adb98d4f0ea2c6a484ea8e04fc547b4d78b21b060000eda22b9d`. The next candidate needs a new immutable identity, currently expected to be `v1.0.0-rc.2`, with synchronized version metadata and release notes. Exact-RC artifact/install checks, held-out T2, provider and standalone qualification, T3/T4, cross-runner reproducibility, the five-environment by three-size human terminal matrix, independent RC acceptance, and stable-promotion disposition remain outstanding. Publication authorization is granted but gated on those results. No stable `v1.0.0` tag or release exists.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:141:- **Version, RC, and publication:** Root and CLI package versions remain `0.1.0-alpha.2`. GitHub currently lists only alpha pre-releases `v0.1.0-alpha.1` and `v0.1.0-alpha.2`; no `v1.0.0-rc.N` artifact/tag or stable v1.0.0 tag, npm package, or GitHub release exists. Follow the staged lifecycle in `ACCEPTANCE.md`: pre-RC source gates, RC construction, artifact-bound RC gates, installed-RC qualification and independent G6 acceptance, then stable promotion/publication and post-publication verification.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:199:  - `.github/workflows/release.yml` and `scripts/check-version-only-diff.mjs` (`a7126aa`, PR #21) build RC tags (`vX.Y.Z-rc.N`) as prereleases and build stable tags (`vX.Y.Z`) as **unpublished drafts** (`draft: true`), requiring via the RC's own checker that a stable tag is a single commit directly on its `vX.Y.Z-rc.N` parent changing only synchronized version metadata.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:266:| `REQ-REL-114` | open (workflow enforced at `86bdbe6`; RC run pending) | `.github/workflows/repro.yml` and `scripts/repro-identity.mjs` (PR #20 `86bdbe6`) enforce fail-closed tag/commit/clean-tree/toolchain/artifact identity across Ubuntu 22.04 and 24.04 builders, covered by `repro_identity.test.ts`. Live execution on an actual RC tag remains pending RC construction. | Final RC tag and `.github/workflows/repro.yml` run | Release engineering | Dispatch `repro.yml` against the exact `v1.0.0-rc.1` tag/commit and archive both runner manifests and comparison evidence. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:285:| G2 package | `linux-x86_64` job in run `39108774170` passed double-build byte comparison, CycloneDX SBOM validation, `smoke-package.sh`, and `installer-smoke.sh`; `repro.yml` (`86bdbe6`) and draft-then-publish `release.yml` (`a7126aa`) are integrated. | Source/CI packaging green; Stage 2/3 workflow-built RC archive and cross-runner `repro.yml` dispatch pending RC tag. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:292:2. **Stage 1 — Pre-RC source gates & integration to `main`:** Merge `v1/integration` to `main` (PR #8) once all pre-RC source checks pass, synchronize version metadata to `1.0.0-rc.1` (`scripts/sync-version.mjs`), add `docs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.1.md`, and verify green source CI on `main`.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:293:3. **Stage 2 — RC artifact construction:** Tag `v1.0.0-rc.1` on the verified `main` commit and build/publish the prerelease RC candidate via `.github/workflows/release.yml`, recording the workflow run, tag commit, artifact digests, and provenance attestation.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:294:4. **Stage 3 — RC artifact gates:** Run `ACC-SUP-01/02/03/06/08` and dispatch `.github/workflows/repro.yml` (`REQ-REL-114`) against the exact `v1.0.0-rc.1` tag and commit.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:295:5. **Stage 4 — Installed-RC qualification:** Install the workflow-produced `v1.0.0-rc.1` package via the documented installer and execute `ACCEPTANCE.md` §§4–8 (standalone/provider matrix, CI/scripted/manual terminal matrix, T2 40×5 held-out comparison, T4 9×5 fault matrix, T3 8×5 long-task matrix, install matrix, SPEC-09 §3.2 docs checklist, and §8 independent acceptance). Archive all evidence under `docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/v1.0.0-rc.1/`.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:296:6. **Stage 5 — G6 decision, version-only stable promotion, draft verification, and publication:** After G6 passes on the accepted RC, create the version-only `v1.0.0` commit directly on the accepted RC commit (enforced by `scripts/check-version-only-diff.mjs` in `release.yml`), run source CI, tag `v1.0.0` to build the unpublished draft release, complete Stage 5 stable artifact/install/attestation checks, record the signed G6 and Stage 5 disposition, and publish the draft release (`gh release edit v1.0.0 --draft=false`).\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-06-packaged-product-parity.md:74:- `release.yml` fails if the four values differ from the tag.\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/F_requirements_history.md:71:| REQ-REL-10 | B8/D1/D2 | Build identity in `--version`/doctor; CI on every branch | TOP_TIER B8 | Implemented (cli/src/build_identity.ts; .github/workflows/ci.yml, release.yml; legacy .gitlab-ci.yml also present) | N |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/F_requirements_history.md:132:| HIST-07 | S2 | Release/supply chain | scripts/generate_sbom.sh:32-94; .github/workflows/release.yml | SOURCE: SBOM from direct deps only; not part of release workflow; no signing/attestation; no SECURITY.md. REL-002/003/004 marked DEMONSTRATED; REL-004 patch obligation now live (public prereleases) | No vulnerability intake path; SBOM incomplete | Lockfile-derived SBOM in release, SECURITY.md, provenance |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/F_requirements_history.md:153:| 12 | SCAN-002 non-bypassable gates | security_gates.sh:14-23; run in ci.yml:58, release.yml:37 | HOLDS |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/F_requirements_history.md:198:| REQ-REL-V1-02 | SECURITY.md + CHANGELOG + lockfile-derived validated SBOM + checksum signing/provenance in release workflow | REL-002..004 obligations now live | RELEASE-REQUIRED | release.yml produces SBOM validated by cyclonedx-cli; attestation present |\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-07-supply-chain-and-release-engineering.md:57:- **Provenance.** Add `permissions: id-token: write, attestations: write` to release.yml and a step `actions/attest-build-provenance@v1` with `subject-path` set to the tarball and SHA256SUMS. Docs: `gh attestation verify <tarball> -R mikeholownych/nexus-code`.\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/E_distribution.md:16:| .github/workflows/ci.yml, release.yml | full read + `gh run list/view --log` (CI run 38540767677) |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/E_distribution.md:32:- **Release pipeline.** A tag `v*.*.*` triggers `release.yml`. The workflow checks that the tag commit is an ancestor of origin/main and that the tag matches `package.json` version. It then runs `npm ci`, the cli build, `cargo test --locked`, the release build, `npm test`, and security_gates. Next it runs `package-linux.sh` twice and `cmp`s the outputs (a reproducibility check), then `smoke-package.sh` and `installer-smoke.sh`. Finally `softprops/action-gh-release` uploads `nexus-linux-x86_64-<tag>.tar.gz` + `SHA256SUMS`, setting prerelease when the tag contains `-`. Release notes come from `generate_release_notes`; `docs/releases/*.md` is not used.\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/E_distribution.md:62:| REL-04 | S2 | versioning | core/Cargo.toml:3 (`1.2.1`) vs package.json:3 / cli/package.json:3 (`0.1.0-alpha.2`); doctor.ts:491-492; local tags v1.1.0/v1.2.0/v1.2.1 | RUNTIME. A fresh clean install gives `WARN engine.binary: The engine reports version 1.2.1, the CLI 0.1.0-alpha.2 → Rebuild with make build`. Every release user sees a warning, and its remedy is impossible in a packaged install (there is no Makefile). Local v1.x tags (not on origin, not ancestors of main, no release.yml at those commits, so not publishable by accident) conflict with the future v1.0.0 ordering. | A permanent false warning on a healthy install trains users to ignore doctor. Version identity is inconsistent across components. | Single-source the version: release workflow asserts Cargo.toml == package.json == cli/package.json == tag. Delete stale local v1.x tags. Make doctor remedies context-aware (packaged → \"reinstall\"). |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/E_distribution.md:67:| REL-09 | S3 | integrity | install.sh:33-35; release.yml:44-48 | SOURCE. SHA256SUMS is fetched from the same release as the archive. There is no signature, cosign/sigstore, or GitHub build-provenance attestation, and the installer script itself is served from mutable `main`. | A compromise of the release or repo is not detectable. The checksum only protects against transport corruption. | v1: add `actions/attest-build-provenance` (verifiable with `gh attestation verify`), or minisign/cosign signatures. Offer an installer pinned to a tag URL. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/E_distribution.md:71:| REL-13 | S3 | CI coverage | .github/workflows/ci.yml:41-66; release.yml | SOURCE + RUNTIME (CI log). There is one OS/arch (ubuntu-22.04 x86_64) and Node 20 only on GitHub; Node 22/24 is not tested, while the developer runs 24.21.0. Rust uses `dtolnay/rust-toolchain@stable`, with no `rust-toolchain.toml` and no `rust-version` in Cargo.toml, so the toolchain floats. There is no `engines` field in package.json. Nothing asserts that tracked `cli/dist` equals a build of `cli/src`. There is no musl/arm/macOS, which matches the docs. Positive: the PTY e2e suites run in CI (905 tests, 0 skipped). | Breakage on newer Node or a future stable Rust is caught late. Reproducibility depends on whatever \"stable\" is on release day. | Add a Node matrix (20, 22, 24). Pin the toolchain file and MSRV. Add an `engines` field. Add a `git diff --exit-code cli/dist` step after the build. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/E_distribution.md:76:| MNT-05 | S4 | changelog | docs/releases/*.md; release.yml:47 | SOURCE + RUNTIME. The GitHub release bodies are only \"Full Changelog: compare…\". The curated notes in docs/releases are not attached, and there is no CHANGELOG.md. | Users on GitHub do not see known limits or breaking changes (e.g. `spawn_subagent max_steps` removed). | Use `body_path: docs/releases/${tag}.md`, and fail the release if the file is missing. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/E_distribution.md:125:  - The tag must be on main and match package.json (release.yml:27-31).\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/E_distribution.md:150:| E-R3 | One version everywhere: tag == package.json == cli/package.json == Cargo.toml. A fresh install's doctor shows no version warning. | compat | BLOCKER | A release.yml assertion, plus smoke-package asserting no `warn` on `engine.binary`. |\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":710238062}},"started_at_ms":1792860678611,"completed_at_ms":1792860679321}}
