{"timestamp":"2026-10-24T16:51:39.692Z","ordinal":297423,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_060b64278a9dfb15016adce2179d7c81a0bc2112bb2d4bdd2f","status":"completed","call_id":"call_a33e64eb22dc4218bb9013415284cc98","name":"exec","input":"const patch=\"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Add File: /home/mike/nexus-wt/rc5-version-sync/docs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.5.md\\n+# Nexus Code v1.0.0-rc.5 release candidate\\n+\\n+**Maturity:** release candidate; prerelease, not stable.\\n+\\n+**Status:** this candidate is for exact-artifact qualification. It does not establish independent acceptance or authorize stable v1.0.0 promotion. Qualification results must identify the workflow-produced package and its digest.\\n+\\n+This release packages the Nexus Code Linux x86-64 client: the TypeScript CLI and sidecar, production Node dependencies, Rust `harness-core`, and Ratatui `nexus-tui`.\\n+\\n+## Changes since RC4\\n+\\n+- Corrects SSRF and locality classification for IPv6 NAT64 addresses. The well-known NAT64 prefix is checked against its embedded IPv4 destination, and the local-use NAT64 prefix is rejected.\\n+- Protects saved MCP server configuration that may contain credentials: the configuration directory and file use owner-only permissions, writes are atomic, and malformed or invalid existing configuration is preserved instead of being overwritten. Save failures are reported to the user.\\n+- Bounds `file_info` line counting and binary detection to the 8 MiB read limit. Larger files still return metadata without scanning their full contents.\\n+- Bounds `edit_file` and `patch_file` whole-file reads to the same 8 MiB limit. Oversized targets are left unchanged and receive a clear error.\\n+- Makes Linux package archives reproducible across supported build runners by creating them with the pinned release builder, removing host-specific archive metadata differences.\\n+- Corrects the cross-runner workflow's pinned artifact-download action so the exact published-candidate comparison can execute.\\n+\\n+The REPL PTY cleanup change is test-harness reliability work and does not change product behavior. These source changes and their CI results do not replace RC5 artifact checks, cross-runner qualification, or installed-package qualification.\\n+\\n+## Runtime requirements\\n+\\n+- Linux x86-64 with glibc 2.35 or newer.\\n+- Node.js 22 or newer.\\n+- An OpenAI-compatible inference endpoint, local or explicitly selected provider.\\n+\\n+The archive does not include Node.js. Rust and Cargo are not required at runtime. No other OS or architecture is claimed.\\n+\\n+## Candidate assets\\n+\\n+The release workflow for `v1.0.0-rc.5` is expected to produce the version-matched Linux archive, `SHA256SUMS`, SBOM, notices, installer, and provenance. The workflow run, tag commit, artifact digests, and qualification evidence must be recorded before this candidate can be accepted. Local builds are not interchangeable with the workflow-produced artifacts.\\n*** End Patch\";\nconst r=await tools.apply_patch(patch);\ntext(r);\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a16ed1-0bd9-75c0-b3f2-6fda13432e3d","create_time":1792860695.634038}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-24T16:51:39.720Z","ordinal":297424,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a16ed1-0bd9-75c0-b3f2-6fda13432e3d","item":{"type":"FileChange","id":"exec-a82f653b-8041-43a4-8999-1a6e39e3c233","changes":{"/home/mike/nexus-wt/rc5-version-sync/docs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.5.md":{"type":"add","content":"# Nexus Code v1.0.0-rc.5 release candidate\n\n**Maturity:** release candidate; prerelease, not stable.\n\n**Status:** this candidate is for exact-artifact qualification. It does not establish independent acceptance or authorize stable v1.0.0 promotion. Qualification results must identify the workflow-produced package and its digest.\n\nThis release packages the Nexus Code Linux x86-64 client: the TypeScript CLI and sidecar, production Node dependencies, Rust `harness-core`, and Ratatui `nexus-tui`.\n\n## Changes since RC4\n\n- Corrects SSRF and locality classification for IPv6 NAT64 addresses. The well-known NAT64 prefix is checked against its embedded IPv4 destination, and the local-use NAT64 prefix is rejected.\n- Protects saved MCP server configuration that may contain credentials: the configuration directory and file use owner-only permissions, writes are atomic, and malformed or invalid existing configuration is preserved instead of being overwritten. Save failures are reported to the user.\n- Bounds `file_info` line counting and binary detection to the 8 MiB read limit. Larger files still return metadata without scanning their full contents.\n- Bounds `edit_file` and `patch_file` whole-file reads to the same 8 MiB limit. Oversized targets are left unchanged and receive a clear error.\n- Makes Linux package archives reproducible across supported build runners by creating them with the pinned release builder, removing host-specific archive metadata differences.\n- Corrects the cross-runner workflow's pinned artifact-download action so the exact published-candidate comparison can execute.\n\nThe REPL PTY cleanup change is test-harness reliability work and does not change product behavior. These source changes and their CI results do not replace RC5 artifact checks, cross-runner qualification, or installed-package qualification.\n\n## Runtime requirements\n\n- Linux x86-64 with glibc 2.35 or newer.\n- Node.js 22 or newer.\n- An OpenAI-compatible inference endpoint, local or explicitly selected provider.\n\nThe archive does not include Node.js. Rust and Cargo are not required at runtime. No other OS or architecture is claimed.\n\n## Candidate assets\n\nThe release workflow for `v1.0.0-rc.5` is expected to produce the version-matched Linux archive, `SHA256SUMS`, SBOM, notices, installer, and provenance. The workflow run, tag commit, artifact digests, and qualification evidence must be recorded before this candidate can be accepted. Local builds are not interchangeable with the workflow-produced artifacts.\n"}},"status":"completed","stdout":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA /home/mike/nexus-wt/rc5-version-sync/docs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.5.md\n","stderr":""},"started_at_ms":1792860699718,"completed_at_ms":1792860699719}}
