{"timestamp":"2026-10-24T16:53:08.595Z","ordinal":297501,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_01a16ed4-9773-7610-bce3-c23351cd516c","author":"/root/plan05_readonly_review","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/plan05_readonly_review\nPayload:\n**CHANGES_REQUIRED** — the uncommitted RC5 note is based on exact source `41b381ddac182b7f0c783b33df5f1355518f465b`.\n\n- [docs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.5.md](/home/mike/nexus-wt/rc5-version-sync/docs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.5.md:13) says `file_info` binary detection is bounded “to the 8 MiB read limit.” In the merged implementation, binary detection is a fixed 1 KiB probe; the 8 MiB cap applies to line counting. Suggested wording: “Bounds `file_info` line counting to 8 MiB while retaining a fixed 1 KiB binary probe. Larger files still return metadata without full line-count scanning.”\n\nThe other listed PR #191–197 changes match the merged source at a high level. The test-only PTY cleanup is appropriately distinguished, and the note does not claim qualification or acceptance. I did not run tests or access qualification material.\n\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a16ed1-0bd9-75c0-b3f2-6fda13432e3d","create_time":1792860788.595047}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"user_input_order":15222}}
