{"timestamp":"2026-10-24T16:54:16.023Z","ordinal":297568,"type":"token_usage_record","payload":{"thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a16ed1-0bd9-75c0-b3f2-6fda13432e3d","session_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","root_turn_id":"01a16ed1-0bd9-75c0-b3f2-6fda13432e3d","response_id":"resp_060b64278a9dfb15016adce2b6576c81a093b65255cb31ea53","usage":{"input_tokens":156086,"cached_input_tokens":154624,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":100,"reasoning_output_tokens":83,"total_tokens":156186},"turn_token_usage":{"input_tokens":4519035,"cached_input_tokens":4443136,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":23429,"reasoning_output_tokens":17339,"total_tokens":4542464},"thread_token_usage":{"input_tokens":5405667232,"cached_input_tokens":5348018944,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":15051678,"reasoning_output_tokens":8583267,"total_tokens":5420718910}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-24T16:54:16.862Z","ordinal":297569,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"function_call_output","id":"fco_01a16ed5-a21e-7933-8466-eacbc59037ff","call_id":"call_d8e381f9a3c548df9ec6be6187986bd6","output":"{\"agents\":[{\"agent_name\":\"/root\",\"agent_status\":\"running\"},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/context_rc_gate_audit\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"**RC.4 qualification refresh — exact tag `v1.0.0-rc.4`, source commit `57b9285c6cead27b2260bf3113b3fc0b847f8169`.** The GitHub prerelease is published, with the workflow-produced Linux archive and release assets. Release workflow **40090364770**, CI **40086738643**, and CodeQL **40086738747** completed successfully on that commit. The archive’s GitHub asset digest is `sha256:07867e26077e5eec6f2cb665c4c34045a116669cacbe7f81f62f40b6fac8b806`. This establishes a published candidate, not an accepted release.\\n\\n| Qualification lane | Current public evidence |\\n|---|---|\\n| Provider / standalone | **No RC.4-bound qualification found.** The latest provider record is for RC.3 (`docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.3/providers/e5-provider-verification-20261023T1659Z.json`): ChatGPT and pinned OpenRouter verification passed, but the record says the required live engineering task remains incomplete. The standalone dry run is from alpha.2 and explicitly says it is not qualification evidence; it also found that the harness-supplied context limit masked native discovery. |\\n| T2 / T3 / T4 | **Incomplete.** The readiness record says the sealed T2 corpus uses legacy `hidden.command`, incompatible with the current `blackbox-v1` runner; no held-out qualification had started. It records T2/T3/T4 and long-task/fault-injection qualification as outstanding. No `rc.4` qualification evidence directory is present in the tagged tree or current `origin/main` tree. |\\n| Cross-runner | **Attempted; gate failed before comparison.** Run [40092008160](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40092008160), dispatched for RC.4, resolved the published tag and built the exact RC on Ubuntu 22.04 and 24.04. Its `compare` job failed during setup: GitHub could not resolve the `actions/download-artifact` reference in the workflow. Thus no runner-to-runner or published-asset hash comparison completed. |\\n| Human terminal matrix | **Incomplete; no cells claimed passed.** The tagged worksheet is unfilled. It requires all 15 terminal/size combinations, per-cell evidence, and two screenshots per cell; scripted PTY runs do not count. The readiness checkpoint says the required desktop environment was unavailable. |\\n\\nThe tagged release notes accurately say RC.4 is an exact-artifact qualification candidate, not an accepted RC: [docs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.4.md](docs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.4.md). The readiness checkpoint is stale: it still calls RC.3 the latest published candidate and describes earlier source state, despite RC.4’s publication.\\n\\n**Next executable action:** correct the pinned `actions/download-artifact` reference in the cross-runner workflow on `main`, then rerun it for `v1.0.0-rc.4`. That can complete the artifact comparison without provider inference or held-out access; it does not unblock the custodian-dependent T2 lane.\"}},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/heldout_public_coverage_audit\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"No change since the prior check at `origin/main@be2cd2f255414f554572c86baa884d9271ff5ea1`: Issue #1 still ends with coordinator comment #6378649211, with no custodian acknowledgment or handoff. PR #16 remains closed with no new custody acceptance, and current claims show no held-out author/custodian owner.\\n\\nThe manifests and historical attestations are unchanged. Qualification remains blocked pending explicit independent custodian ownership and acceptance, plus a custodian-approved T2 compatibility or supersession path. No files or private material were accessed.\"}},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/plan05_readonly_review\",\"agent_status\":\"running\"}]