{"timestamp":"2026-10-24T16:56:32.726Z","ordinal":297709,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_01a16ed7-b4d5-7843-a03d-6f10418145f0","author":"/root/plan05_readonly_review","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/plan05_readonly_review\nPayload:\n**CHANGES_REQUIRED** — reviewed staged diff SHA-256 `f93e5607b4f7895fb507cc38b5f757fbaed55ab99e5244482923f86fadb74d9e` at base `41b381ddac182b7f0c783b33df5f1355518f465b`.\n\nThe pathspec environment sanitization, root-anchored `.nexus` reset, and tests for malformed excludes, nested workspaces, and staged state look sound. The staged-state regression also checks that worktree contents survive while `.nexus` changes stay out of the commit.\n\nOne compatibility gap remains: [git.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/commit-exclusion-refresh/cli/src/git.ts:164) resets against `HEAD` unconditionally. In an initialized but unborn repository, `HEAD` does not resolve, so `commitChanges` fails before staging or making its first commit; the previous `git add`/`git commit` flow supported that case. Handle unborn `HEAD` while still removing staged `.nexus` entries, and add a regression that verifies ordinary files commit while `.nexus` remains excluded.\n\nNo tests were run. `git diff --check` is clean."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a16ed1-0bd9-75c0-b3f2-6fda13432e3d","create_time":1792860992.725962}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"user_input_order":15229}}
