{"timestamp":"2026-10-24T16:58:33.847Z","ordinal":297805,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a16ed1-0bd9-75c0-b3f2-6fda13432e3d","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016adce3b8650481a089f20a507c09496a","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"That explains why you didn’t see it: the installed `nexus` command is **v1.0.0-rc.3**. That tag doesn’t show the folder-trust prompt in its startup path.\n\nThe prompt is present in **RC4** and current `origin/main`. It offers “Trust and continue,” “Continue without trusting,” and “Exit,” and shows whether project instructions such as `AGENTS.md` were found. The [RC4 release](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/releases/tag/v1.0.0-rc.4) includes a GitHub installer.\n\nIf you install RC4 and the prompt still doesn’t appear for a folder, Nexus may already remember that folder as trusted. RC4 is still an unaccepted release candidate; this does **not** mean v1.0.0 has been accepted or released."}],"phase":"final_answer"},"started_at_ms":1792861112422,"completed_at_ms":1792861113847}}
