{"timestamp":"2026-10-24T17:02:32.239Z","ordinal":298035,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_01a16edd-312f-79b2-8a5d-fad40603109c","author":"/root/plan05_readonly_review","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/plan05_readonly_review\nPayload:\n**ACCEPT** for the refreshed diff, SHA-256 `c6d90dee84810f10b637ed9d01c382fb792832540d324ed8af243c720f3fe85a`, against base `41b381ddac182b7f0c783b33df5f1355518f465b`.\n\nThe unborn-HEAD branch now verifies that `HEAD` is a symbolic ref whose branch is absent, then removes only staged root `.nexus` entries from the index with `git rm --cached`; workspace files remain untouched. Detached or malformed `HEAD` paths fail closed. The regression covers a first commit with pre-staged `.nexus` state, and the existing tests cover nested workspaces, pathspec environment, malformed excludes, and staged state.\n\nA valid symbolic `HEAD` pointing to a missing branch is treated as an unborn branch, consistent with Git’s representation of a fresh repository. `git diff --check` is clean. I did not run tests."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a16ed9-c60e-7103-9ada-b7f9a638664b","create_time":1792861352.2397318}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"user_input_order":15241}}
