{"timestamp":"2026-10-24T17:04:24.791Z","ordinal":298166,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_060b64278a9dfb15016adce516dae881a090c1d0a7f315fc8a","status":"completed","call_id":"call_6ea7bf9e78b6443aa07a2d6eb701a143","name":"exec","input":"const r=await Promise.all([\n tools.exec_command({cmd:\"ssh -G ubuntu-desktop 2>/dev/null | awk '/^(hostname|user|port|identityfile) / {print}' | head -10; ssh -o BatchMode=yes -o ConnectTimeout=5 ubuntu-desktop 'hostname; printf \\\"DISPLAY=%s WAYLAND_DISPLAY=%s\\\\n\\\" \\\"$DISPLAY\\\" \\\"$WAYLAND_DISPLAY\\\"; command -v xterm kitty gnome-terminal tmux code' 2>&1 | head -20\",workdir:\"/home/mike/nexus-code\",yield_time_ms:10000,max_output_tokens:1200}),\n tools.exec_command({cmd:\"git show origin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md | sed -n '/5.3/,/5.4/p'; git -C /home/mike/nexus-wt/qual108-terminal-worksheet status --short --branch 2>/dev/null; git -C /home/mike/nexus-wt/qual108-terminal-worksheet log -1 --format='%H %cI %s' 2>/dev/null; cat .git/nexus-claims/FILE_docs_v1.0.0_TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md/owner.json 2>/dev/null || true\",workdir:\"/home/mike/nexus-code\",yield_time_ms:10000,max_output_tokens:2500})\n]);\nfor(let i=0;i<r.length;i++)text(JSON.stringify({i,...r[i]}));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a16ed9-c60e-7103-9ada-b7f9a638664b","create_time":1792861462.867094}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-24T17:04:24.878Z","ordinal":298167,"type":"token_usage_record","payload":{"thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a16ed9-c60e-7103-9ada-b7f9a638664b","session_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","root_turn_id":"01a16ed9-c60e-7103-9ada-b7f9a638664b","response_id":"resp_060b64278a9dfb15016adce5111e4c81a08a20b1dff2fb459e","usage":{"input_tokens":184569,"cached_input_tokens":183936,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":988,"reasoning_output_tokens":659,"total_tokens":185557},"turn_token_usage":{"input_tokens":6863068,"cached_input_tokens":6776576,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":26857,"reasoning_output_tokens":17225,"total_tokens":6889925},"thread_token_usage":{"input_tokens":5416077276,"cached_input_tokens":5358275456,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":15099133,"reasoning_output_tokens":8612703,"total_tokens":5431176409}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-24T17:04:25.787Z","ordinal":298168,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a16ed9-c60e-7103-9ada-b7f9a638664b","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-a7fbc444-5c7e-46ab-a460-db24a1ed51da","process_id":"21411","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","git show origin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md | sed -n '/5.3/,/5.4/p'; git -C /home/mike/nexus-wt/qual108-terminal-worksheet status --short --branch 2>/dev/null; git -C /home/mike/nexus-wt/qual108-terminal-worksheet log -1 --format='%H %cI %s' 2>/dev/null; cat .git/nexus-claims/FILE_docs_v1.0.0_TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md/owner.json 2>/dev/null || true"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"git show origin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md | sed -n '/5.3/,/5.4/p'; git -C /home/mike/nexus-wt/qual108-terminal-worksheet status --short --branch 2>/dev/null; git -C /home/mike/nexus-wt/qual108-terminal-worksheet log -1 --format='%H %cI %s' 2>/dev/null; cat .git/nexus-claims/FILE_docs_v1.0.0_TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md/owner.json 2>/dev/null || true"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"| ACC-TUI-MANUAL | §5.3 on the installed RC across five required terminal environments and three required sizes | Every cell passes; screenshots and per-cell verdicts are archived. |\n\n## 4. Standalone and provider qualification (REQ-PRV-106, REQ-PRV-111, REQ-QUAL-107)\n\n### 4.1 Clean-HOME procedure\n\n1. `export HOME=$(mktemp -d)`.\n2. Install the RC with the documented command.\n3. Create `~/.config/nexus/config.env` containing only:\n   - `LOCAL_LLM_ENDPOINT=http://127.0.0.1:<proxy>/v1`\n   - `LOCAL_LLM_MODEL=<id as listed by the proxy>`\n   - `LOCAL_LLM_API_KEY=REDACTED\n\n   No gateway token file, no homelab paths, no `NODE_*` overrides.\n4. Start `node eval/standalone/plain_proxy.mjs --upstream <gateway> --token-file <operator token> [--emulate <kind>]`. The gateway token stays with the proxy and never reaches the Nexus HOME.\n5. Run `nexus doctor --json` and archive it. It must report the server kind and context source with no `gateway` capability.\n\n### 4.2 Standalone matrix\n\n| Profile | What Nexus sees | Runs | Pass condition |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| P-plain | Bare OpenAI-compatible `/models` and chat. No tokenize, no capacity headers. | Standalone T2 subset (≥ 10 held-out tasks) × 3 runs; T4 classes 1, 3, 4, 7 × 3 | T2 correctness ≥ (gateway-direct T2 correctness on the same tasks − 10 pts). False VERIFIED = 0. T4 truthful = 100%. Context source reported as `client_default` or an operator override, with no error. |\n| P-llamacpp | Emulated llama.cpp `/props` and overflow body | Same tasks × 1 run; plus the forced-overflow case (context limit set to 8k) | Context discovered from `/props`. Overflow gives one compact-and-retry, then success or an actionable error. |\n| P-vllm | Emulated `max_model_len` and vLLM overflow body | Same as P-llamacpp | Same, with the context source `max_model_len` |\n| P-ollama | Emulated `/api/show` and Ollama overflow body | Same as P-llamacpp | Same, with the context source `ollama_show` |\n| Conformance | CI fixtures for llama.cpp, vLLM, LM Studio and Ollama shapes | CI | All pass (ACC-INF-01, -02, -05) |\n\nACC-INF-10 passes only when every row passes. The release notes state the scope in the form required by DEC-16.\n\n### 4.3 Provider matrix (E5)\n\n| Provider | Tier (DEC-06) | Required for v1.0.0 |\n|---|---|---|\n| OpenRouter, pinned model | Supported | `providers verify` PASS, plus one live small task (a §6-style bug fix) reaching a correct outcome |\n| ChatGPT sign-in | Experimental | Verify PASS recorded (already PASS at db1ca55; repeat on the RC) |\n| OpenAI API key, Anthropic | Experimental unless keys are added | If promoted: verify PASS plus one live task. Otherwise NOT RUN, and they are labelled experimental. |\n| Copilot | Experimental | Not required |\n\n## 5. Terminal acceptance (REQ-QUAL-108)\n\n### 5.1 CI PTY suites (E1)\n\nThese must pass:\n\n- `tui_approval_input_e2e`\n- `tui_diff_e2e`\n- `tui_maturity_e2e`\n- `tui_model_picker_e2e`\n- `tui_multiline_e2e`\n- `tui_surface_e2e`\n- new: `repl_approval_e2e`\n- new: `process_lifecycle_e2e`\n- new: `startup_unreachable_e2e`\n- new: the package PTY smoke\n\n### 5.2 Scripted PTY scenarios against the installed RC (E3, mock gateway)\n\nThese are ports of `evidence/D_pty/`.\n\n| Scenario | Pass condition |\n|---|---|\n| s1 startup, unreachable endpoint | The endpoint is named, with a fix hint. The turn ends with guidance in ≤ 2.5 min. |\n| s2 approval under continuous typing, paste and burst, at 40×14 | No decision is made by stray input. A deliberate key decides. |\n| s3 completion | The outcome is shown in words: VERIFIED, REGRESSION_FREE or UNVERIFIED. |\n| s4–s6 cancel and steer | Cancel is acknowledged within 1 frame and idle within 5 s. Steering is applied. |\n| s7 resume | The prior conversation is shown. |\n| s8–s9 cancel or quit during a tool | Zero surviving processes. |\n| r1a / r1d REPL approvals | DENIED for a lone Enter and for a typed-ahead `y`. |\n\n### 5.3 Manual real-terminal matrix (E3)\n\nTerminals: xterm, kitty (kitty keyboard protocol on), tmux 3.x inside GNOME Terminal, VS Code integrated terminal, GNOME Terminal. Sizes: 80×24, 40×14, 200×60.\n\nFor each terminal × size, check:\n\n1. Launch `nexus` (the TUI appears).\n2. Approval panel. Type continuously across it. Paste 3 lines. Approve with a deliberate key.\n3. Shift+Enter or Alt+Enter multiline.\n4. Resize during streaming.\n5. Esc during `sleep 30` (no survivors).\n6. Ctrl-C twice (clean terminal restore: echo on, no stray escape codes).\n7. NO_COLOR.\n\nRecord PASS/FAIL per cell, with a screenshot of the approval panel and the post-exit terminal state.\n\n**Gate:** zero FAIL on checks 2, 5 and 6, which are safety checks. Other FAILs need a written disposition (fix, or a documented known limitation).\n\n## 6. Task-quality qualification (REQ-QUAL-101 to REQ-QUAL-106, REQ-QUAL-109)\n\nEnvironment: E4 (gateway direct), serial runs, with matched model fingerprint, budgets and env (REQ-QUAL-102).\n\n### 6.1 T2 held-out (ACC-QUAL-T2)\n\n- 40 sealed tasks. The manifest is committed before RC1, and authorship is recorded (agent-authored, DEC-05).\n- 5 runs × {Nexus RC, Goose, OpenCode}.\n- Before execution, freeze three qualification configs at `eval/configs/v1-t2-nexus.json`, `eval/configs/v1-t2-goose.json`, and `eval/configs/v1-t2-opencode.json`. Each must set `qualification: true`, identify the same model fingerprint and sampling settings, and record equal context/output and task budgets; the Nexus config must identify the installed RC and its package digest. Do not derive these files from the pilot configs by silently inheriting or changing settings.\n- Set `T2_TASKS` to the custodian-approved, sealed task directory and `T2_OUT` to a new, empty, run-specific output directory. Do not use the disclosed `eval/tasks` development set as held-out evidence. Preserve all three outputs and their manifests; never reuse an output directory for a retry.\n- Run each config serially, with identical task selection and five runs per task:\n\n  ```bash\n  set -euo pipefail\n  : \"${T2_TASKS:?set the sealed task directory}\"\n  : \"${T2_OUT:?set a new unique output directory}\"\n  test ! -e \"$T2_OUT\"\n  node eval/run.mjs --config eval/configs/v1-t2-nexus.json --tasks \"$T2_TASKS\" --out \"$T2_OUT/nexus\" --runs 5\n  node eval/run.mjs --config eval/configs/v1-t2-goose.json --tasks \"$T2_TASKS\" --out \"$T2_OUT/goose\" --runs 5\n  node eval/run.mjs --config eval/configs/v1-t2-opencode.json --tasks \"$T2_TASKS\" --out \"$T2_OUT/opencode\" --runs 5\n  node eval/score.mjs --pairs \"$T2_OUT/nexus/results.jsonl\" \"$T2_OUT/goose/results.jsonl\" \"$T2_OUT/opencode/results.jsonl\"\n  ```\n\n  Record the resolved `T2_TASKS`, unique `T2_OUT`, config digests, installed RC identity, model fingerprint, and exact commands in the frozen run record before starting. A failed or interrupted invocation remains evidence; any permitted infrastructure rerun uses the accepted rerun procedure and is retained separately. Do not score until all required runs and manifests exist. The scorer accepts exactly the Nexus, Goose and OpenCode result files.\n\n### 6.2 T4 fault injection (ACC-QUAL-T4)\n\n9 fault classes × 5 runs on the Nexus RC. The configured faults run through `eval/run.mjs` and `eval/model_proxy.mjs`; the hanging-command and full-disk cases use task fixtures, and SIGTERM-then-resume uses the runner case (DEC-05 amendment, 2026-10-17: the union of the distinct scenarios below):\n\n1. refused connection mid-turn\n2. 5xx / overloaded\n3. stream cut mid-tool-call\n4. output-limit truncation\n5. hanging test command\n6. disk full\n7. context overflow at 32k\n8. malformed tool-call JSON\n9. SIGTERM then `run --resume`\n\n### 6.3 T3 long tasks (ACC-QUAL-T3)\n\n- 8 tasks × 5 runs. Each run must have ≥ 60 steps, ≥ 2 compactions and scripted steering.\n\n### 6.4 Thresholds (DEC-05; all must hold)\n\n| Metric | Gate |\n|---|---|\n| False VERIFIED (T2 + T3 + T4) | **= 0** |\n| T2 pooled hidden-test correctness | ≥ 60% and ≥ best matched peer − 10 pts |\n| T2 per class (bugfix, feature, refactor, debug) | ≥ 40% |\n| Crash rate (all Nexus runs) | ≤ 2% |\n| Regression rate | ≤ 5% |\n| T4 truthful outcome | = 100% |\n| T4 hang beyond budget + 5 min | = 0 |\n| T3 false-absence | = 0 |\n| T3 false-presence | = 0 |\n| T3 steering honoured | ≥ 95% |\n| Operator interventions in `run` mode | = 0 |\n\nThe scorer output `verdict.md` lists each metric with its Wilson 95% interval, along with the infrastructure reruns and the excluded contaminated runs.\n\n## 7. Install, upgrade, rollback, uninstall (ACC-PLAT; E2)\n\n| Case | Command | Pass condition |\n|---|---|---|\n| Fresh install, each image with Node ≥ 22 | Documented one-line command with `NEXUS_VERSION=<rc>`, then the no-version command after v1.0.0 is published | Installed. `nexus --version` equals the RC. `nexus doctor` shows no version warning and an empty stderr. |\n| No Node / Node 20 | Same | Clear prerequisite message before download or state change. HOME untouched. |\n| Upgrade alpha.2 → RC | Same, with the tag | Symlink swapped. Old version retained. User state intact. |\n| Rollback RC → alpha.2 | Same, with the old tag | Works. |\n| Repair | Delete a file in the version dir, then reinstall | Repaired (REQ-REL-105). Same-version reinstall preserves working files if package fails verification. |\n| Uninstall (documented manual) | Commands from the quickstart | Only Nexus-owned paths removed. `~/.config/nexus` and `~/.nexus` retained. |\n| Checksum tamper | installer-smoke | Refused. The existing install is unchanged. |\n| Attestation | `gh attestation verify <tarball> -R mikeholownych/nexus-code` | PASS |\n| Upgrade self-test failure | `nexus upgrade` (broken candidate package) | Refused. Staging verified before switch; if post-switch verification fails, launcher atomically rolls back to previous target and journal records `rolled_back`. |\n| Upgrade crash recovery | `nexus upgrade --recover` | Idempotent recovery. Cleans incomplete staging, restores unverified launcher symlink, verifies functional installation. |\n| Backup restore | `nexus upgrade --restore-backup <state-backup-directory>` | Snapshot of configuration and complete durable state restored from a recognized private backup directory (`backup.json`, `state/`, optional `config/`), with strict 0600 file / 0700 directory modes. A canonical `config.env.bak.*` path restores configuration only. Arbitrary files and tar archives are rejected. Run it through the stable `nexus` launcher; close existing legacy clients, then keep version-pinned legacy binaries and direct old entry points offline until the durable restore journal is cleared. |\n| Incompatible downgrade | `nexus upgrade --version <v> --allow-downgrade` (incompatible state schema) | Refused fail-closed with actionable state schema explanation. Existing installation unchanged. |\n\n## 8. Independent acceptance (REQ-AGT-110, ACC-CONT-10)\n\nThe reviewer is supplied by the owner (X5) and did not implement the work under review.\n\nThe reviewer receives:\n\n- the RC package;\n- this file;\n- the REQUIREMENTS ledger;\n- SPEC-04;\n- read access to the evidence directory.\n\nThe reviewer performs:\n\n1. An independent re-run of a sample. At minimum:\n   - ACC-SAFE-01, 03, 09;\n   - ACC-PROC-02;\n   - ACC-TRUST-01, 02;\n   - ACC-CONT-01, 03;\n   - ACC-VER-01, 03;\n   - ACC-PKG-01;\n   - 5 random T2 tasks;\n   - 2 T4 classes.\n2. One live long task (≥ 60 steps, ≥ 2 compactions) on the RC through the gateway, including one kill and resume.\n3. A review of the scorer verdict and of contamination handling.\n\n**Output:** `docs/reviews/<date>-v1-rc-independent-acceptance.md` with an ACCEPT, ACCEPT WITH DEFECTS, or REJECT verdict per area. \"Accept with defects\" needs an owner disposition for every defect, and for a blocker area the only acceptable disposition is a fix.\n\n## 9. Contest (separate product; not a client gate)\n\nThe contest submission is complete and judging has concluded. No contest freeze applies (DEC-13 status amendment); post-contest hardening is tracked separately from client v1.0.0 acceptance and is accepted by:\n\n| ID | Check |\n|---|---|\n| CON-A1 | Ordinary maintained package/experiment checks build `agent-collab-worker`. `worker.config.json` has the configured name, and the bundle contains the `/work-state` handler. Do not restore the retired `cloudflare-contest-contract` status check. |\n| CON-A2 | Broker negative tests: caller-supplied env paths and URLs are ignored. A host outside `*.artifacts.cloudflare.net` is refused. |\n| CON-A3 | On a clean VM, `install.sh --fresh` followed by `post-install-qualify.py` passes. |\n| CON-A4 | `sudo -l` for the demo user shows only fixed argv. `sudo setpriv --reuid=0 id` is denied. |\n| CON-A5 | One clean-account `--mode cloudflare --agents real` run, with a committed, redacted run record. |\n| CON-A6 | The video source commits are tagged and published, or the docs state that they are unpublished. |\n\n## 10. Release decision (G6)\n\nG6 passes only when every item below holds. It authorizes a version-only stable commit from the accepted RC source, followed by its source checks, stable tag, and unpublished draft candidate; it does not authorize making stable assets publicly available. RC tags are candidate construction inputs governed by §1.1; an RC tag or its successful build does not satisfy this release decision.\n\n- [ ] G0–G4 automated gates pass on the final RC commit (§3).\n- [ ] RC artifact gates pass on the workflow-produced RC, including ACC-SUP-01/02/03/06/08; record the exact source commit, workflow run, and artifact digest.\n- [ ] §4 standalone and provider matrix: all rows PASS.\n- [ ] §5 terminal acceptance: CI, scripted and manual gates PASS.\n- [ ] §6 thresholds: all hold.\n- [ ] §7 install matrix: all rows PASS.\n- [ ] §8 independent acceptance: ACCEPT, or ACCEPT WITH DEFECTS with owner dispositions and no blocker defects outstanding.\n- [ ] The pre-RC source gate passes from a clean source worktree: `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce`. Every B/RR source row outside the §1.1 qualification-only map must be ≥ `tested`. A mapped row below `tested` is reported as deferred; this result does not accept or qualify it.\n- [ ] The exact-RC evidence gate passes from the clean RC worktree and is bound to the exact RC source commit and installed RC artifact. Run the checker with the custodian-approved, immutable qualification record and evidence directory:\n  `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce --qualification-record <record.json> --rc-artifact <installed-rc-package> --evidence-root <evidence-directory>`.\n  The version 1 record contains `sourceCommit` (full commit ID), `rcTag` (for example `v1.0.0-rc.1`), `artifactSha256`, `artifactProvenance` (`sourceCommit`, `artifactSha256`, and a hashed provenance report), `independentAcceptance` (`disposition`, `reviewer`, `implementers`, zero `blockingDefects`, and a hashed report reference), and one `requirements` entry for every B/RR row. For `ACCEPT WITH DEFECTS`, include each non-blocking defect with its owner disposition; unresolved or blocking defects fail. Each requirement entry records its status and one or more hashed evidence files covering the exact criteria required by the ledger and the §1.1 qualification-only map. Every criterion evidence file must be a JSON object with top-level `sourceCommit`, `rcTag`, and `artifactSha256` values exactly matching the validated qualification record, current RC source commit, and installed RC artifact. A digest-valid report copied from another source revision, RC tag, or artifact is rejected. A B row recorded as `tested` also needs a non-empty `qualificationNotApplicable.reason` and a `qualificationNotApplicable.decision` matching the approved per-requirement exception table and a matching applicability declaration in DECISIONS.md; an unrelated or record-supplied decision is rejected. Evidence paths must be relative regular files under the evidence root, with no symlinks. Missing, unknown, stale, mismatched, or incomplete evidence fails the gate. The checker requires a clean worktree, rejects `--ledger` overrides, enforces source-ledger thresholds outside the explicit §1.1 lifecycle rows, and requires the exact-RC record itself to meet the normal status threshold for every row. It never mutates the source ledger or relaxes a requirement's B/RR record threshold. The checker validates source/tag/artifact identity bindings and evidence hashes; it does not authenticate the reviewer or prove that the artifact was built from the source commit. The approved release workflow must independently verify build provenance/attestation, and the designated custodian and independent reviewer must verify their respective approvals and custody evidence.\n- [ ] Docs checklist (SPEC-09 §3.2) is signed off.\n- [ ] Release notes state the standalone scope (DEC-16), the provider tiers (DEC-06), the experimental surfaces (DEC-03, DEC-07) and the known limitations.\n- [ ] Owner approval to publish (X7).\n\nAfter G6, complete source checks on the exact stable-version commit before tagging, then complete the stable artifact checks in §1.1 stage 5 before publishing the draft. A failure keeps publication blocked and requires remediation plus the applicable requalification; do not mark the campaign released until published artifacts are independently verified.\n\n**Outcome recording.** The release decision record goes in `docs/releases/v1.0.0.md`, with links to every evidence directory.\n{\"agent\":\"/root\",\"host\":\"mike-dev\",\"branch\":\"v1/terminal-matrix-rc3\",\"worktree\":\"/home/mike/nexus-wt/terminal-matrix-rc3\",\"base\":\"1b9791f07d301c885fe48f04a796203583ab5a5c\",\"since\":\"2026-10-23T09:20:00Z\",\"scope\":\"Bind unfilled REQ-QUAL-108 human terminal worksheet to published RC3 identity and prepare exact operator procedure; no results claimed\",\"reviewer\":\"plan05_readonly_review\",\"review_disposition\":\"ACCEPT\",\"reviewed_at\":\"2026-10-23T09:30:00Z\",\"status\":\"ready_to_push_after_SUITE\",\"head\":\"986eed029f46aa59a302b3a1d61c86a42d953e99\"}\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":26916}},"started_at_ms":1792861465787,"completed_at_ms":1792861465787}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-24T17:04:25.835Z","ordinal":298169,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a16ed9-c60e-7103-9ada-b7f9a638664b","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-44e3654c-75d9-4ec7-a449-7889ff88307d","process_id":"85501","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","ssh -G ubuntu-desktop 2>/dev/null | awk '/^(hostname|user|port|identityfile) / {print}' | head -10; ssh -o BatchMode=yes -o ConnectTimeout=5 ubuntu-desktop 'hostname; printf \"DISPLAY=%s WAYLAND_DISPLAY=%s\\n\" \"$DISPLAY\" \"$WAYLAND_DISPLAY\"; command -v xterm kitty gnome-terminal tmux code' 2>&1 | head -20"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"ssh -G ubuntu-desktop 2>/dev/null | awk '/^(hostname|user|port|identityfile) / {print}' | head -10; ssh -o BatchMode=yes -o ConnectTimeout=5 ubuntu-desktop 'hostname; printf \"DISPLAY=%s WAYLAND_DISPLAY=%s\\n\" \"$DISPLAY\" \"$WAYLAND_DISPLAY\"; command -v xterm kitty gnome-terminal tmux code' 2>&1 | head -20"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"user mike\nhostname ubuntu-desktop\nport 22\nidentityfile ~/.ssh/id_rsa\nidentityfile ~/.ssh/id_ecdsa\nidentityfile ~/.ssh/id_ecdsa_sk\nidentityfile ~/.ssh/id_ed25519\nidentityfile ~/.ssh/id_ed25519_sk\nidentityfile ~/.ssh/id_xmss\nidentityfile ~/.ssh/id_dsa\nssh: Could not resolve hostname ubuntu-desktop: Name or service not known\r\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":33702}},"started_at_ms":1792861465835,"completed_at_ms":1792861465835}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-24T17:04:27.106Z","ordinal":298170,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a16ede-f1e2-7a90-b84e-72c9da8381df","call_id":"call_6ea7bf9e78b6443aa07a2d6eb701a143","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 2.3 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"i\":0,\"chunk_id\":\"36771f\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000033702,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":82,\"output\":\"user mike\\nhostname ubuntu-desktop\\nport 22\\nidentityfile ~/.ssh/id_rsa\\nidentityfile ~/.ssh/id_ecdsa\\nidentityfile ~/.ssh/id_ecdsa_sk\\nidentityfile ~/.ssh/id_ed25519\\nidentityfile ~/.ssh/id_ed25519_sk\\nidentityfile ~/.ssh/id_xmss\\nidentityfile ~/.ssh/id_dsa\\nssh: Could not resolve hostname ubuntu-desktop: Name or service not known\\r\\n\"}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"i\":1,\"chunk_id\":\"195613\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000026916,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":4479,\"output\":\"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 4479)\\nTotal output lines: 229\\n\\n| ACC-TUI-MANUAL | §5.3 on the installed RC across five required terminal environments and three required sizes | Every cell passes; screenshots and per-cell verdicts are archived. |\\n\\n## 4. Standalone and provider qualification (REQ-PRV-106, REQ-PRV-111, REQ-QUAL-107)\\n\\n### 4.1 Clean-HOME procedure\\n\\n1. `export HOME=$(mktemp -d)`.\\n2. Install the RC with the documented command.\\n3. Create `~/.config/nexus/config.env` containing only:\\n   - `LOCAL_LLM_ENDPOINT=http://127.0.0.1:<proxy>/v1`\\n   - `LOCAL_LLM_MODEL=<id as listed by the proxy>`\\n   - `LOCAL_LLM_API_KEY=REDACTED   No gateway token file, no homelab paths, no `NODE_*` overrides.\\n4. Start `node eval/standalone/plain_proxy.mjs --upstream <gateway> --token-file <operator token> [--emulate <kind>]`. The gateway token stays with the proxy and never reaches the Nexus HOME.\\n5. Run `nexus doctor --json` and archive it. It must report the server kind and context source with no `gateway` capability.\\n\\n### 4.2 Standalone matrix\\n\\n| Profile | What Nexus sees | Runs | Pass condition |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| P-plain | Bare OpenAI-compatible `/models` and chat. No tokenize, no capacity headers. | Standalone T2 subset (≥ 10 held-out tasks) × 3 runs; T4 classes 1, 3, 4, 7 × 3 | T2 correctness ≥ (gateway-direct T2 correctness on the same tasks − 10 pts). False VERIFIED = 0. T4 truthful = 100%. Context source reported as `client_default` or an operator override, with no error. |\\n| P-llamacpp | Emulated llama.cpp `/props` and overflow body | Same tasks × 1 run; plus the forced-overflow case (context limit set to 8k) | Context discovered from `/props`. Overflow gives one compact-and-retry, then success or an actionable error. |\\n| P-vllm | Emulated `max_model_len` and vLLM overflow body | Same as P-llamacpp | Same, with the context source `max_model_len` |\\n| P-ollama | Emulated `/api/show` and Ollama overflow body | Same as P-llamacpp | Same, with the context source `ollama_show` |\\n| Conformance | CI fixtures for llama.cpp, vLLM, LM Studio and Ollama shapes | CI | All pass (ACC-INF-01, -02, -05) |\\n\\nACC-INF-10 passes only when every row passes. The release notes state the scope in the form required by DEC-16.\\n\\n### 4.3 Provider matrix (E5)\\n\\n| Provider | Tier (DEC-06) | Required for v1.0.0 |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| OpenRouter, pinned model | Supported | `providers verify` PASS, plus one live small task (a §6-style bug fix) reaching a correct outcome |\\n| ChatGPT sign-in | Experimental | Verify PASS recorded (already PASS at db1ca55; repeat on the RC) |\\n| OpenAI API key, Anthropic | Experimental unless keys are added | If promoted: verify PASS plus one live task. Otherwise NOT RUN, and they are labelled experimental. |\\n| Copilot | Experimental | Not required |\\n\\n## 5. Terminal acceptance (REQ-QUAL-108)\\n\\n### 5.1 CI PTY suites (E1)\\n\\nThese must pass:\\n\\n- `tui_approval_input_e2e`\\n- `tui_diff_e2e`\\n- `tui_maturity_e2e`\\n- `tui_model_picker_e2e`\\n- `tui_multiline_e2e`\\n- `tui_surface_e2e`\\n- new: `repl_approval_e2e`\\n- new: `process_lifecycle_e2e`\\n- new: `startup_unreachable_e2e`\\n- new: the package PTY smoke\\n\\n### 5.2 Scripted PTY scenarios against the installed RC (E3, mock gateway)\\n\\nThese are ports of `evidence/D_pty/`.\\n\\n| Scenario | Pass condition |\\n|---|---|\\n| s1 startup, unreachable endpoint | The endpoint is named, with a fix hint. The turn ends with guidance in ≤ 2.5 min. |\\n| s2 approval under continuous typing, paste and burst, at 40×14 | No decision is made by stray input. A deliberate key decides. |\\n| s3 completion | The outcome is shown in words: VERIFIED, REGRESSION_FREE or UNVERIFIED. |\\n| s4–s6 cancel and steer | Cancel is acknowledged within 1 frame and idle within 5 s. Steering is applied. |\\n| s7 resume | The prior conversation is shown. |\\n| s8–s9 cancel or quit during a tool | Zero surviving processes. |\\n| r1a / r1d REPL approvals | DENIED for a lone Enter and for a typed-ahead `y`. |\\n\\n### 5.3 Manual real-terminal matrix (E3)\\n\\nTerminals: xterm, kitty (kitty keyboard protocol on), tmux 3.x inside GNOME Terminal, VS Code integrated terminal, GNOME Terminal. Sizes: 80×24, 40×14, 200×60.\\n\\nFor each terminal × size, check:\\n\\n1. Launch `nexus` (the TUI appears).\\n2. Approval panel. Type continuously across it. Paste 3 lines. Approve with a deliberate key.\\n3. Shift+Enter or Alt+Enter multiline.\\n4. Resize during streaming.\\n5. Esc during `sleep 30` (no survivors).\\n6. Ctrl-C twice (clean terminal restore: echo on, no stray escape codes).\\n7. NO_COLOR.\\n\\nRecord PASS/FAIL per cell, with a screenshot of the approval panel and the post-exit terminal state.\\n\\n**Gate:** zero FAIL on checks 2, 5 and 6, which are safety checks. Other FAILs need a written disposition (fix, or a documented known limitation).\\n\\n## 6. Task-quality qualification (REQ-QUAL-101 to REQ-QUAL-106, REQ-QUAL-109)\\n\\nEnvironment: E4 (gateway direct), serial runs, with matched model fingerprint, budgets and env (REQ-QUAL-102).\\n\\n### 6.1 T2 held-out (ACC-QUAL-T2)\\n\\n- 40 sealed tasks. The manifest is committed before RC1, and authors…1979 tokens truncated…rsion-only stable commit from the accepted RC source, followed by its source checks, stable tag, and unpublished draft candidate; it does not authorize making stable assets publicly available. RC tags are candidate construction inputs governed by §1.1; an RC tag or its successful build does not satisfy this release decision.\\n\\n- [ ] G0–G4 automated gates pass on the final RC commit (§3).\\n- [ ] RC artifact gates pass on the workflow-produced RC, including ACC-SUP-01/02/03/06/08; record the exact source commit, workflow run, and artifact digest.\\n- [ ] §4 standalone and provider matrix: all rows PASS.\\n- [ ] §5 terminal acceptance: CI, scripted and manual gates PASS.\\n- [ ] §6 thresholds: all hold.\\n- [ ] §7 install matrix: all rows PASS.\\n- [ ] §8 independent acceptance: ACCEPT, or ACCEPT WITH DEFECTS with owner dispositions and no blocker defects outstanding.\\n- [ ] The pre-RC source gate passes from a clean source worktree: `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce`. Every B/RR source row outside the §1.1 qualification-only map must be ≥ `tested`. A mapped row below `tested` is reported as deferred; this result does not accept or qualify it.\\n- [ ] The exact-RC evidence gate passes from the clean RC worktree and is bound to the exact RC source commit and installed RC artifact. Run the checker with the custodian-approved, immutable qualification record and evidence directory:\\n  `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce --qualification-record <record.json> --rc-artifact <installed-rc-package> --evidence-root <evidence-directory>`.\\n  The version 1 record contains `sourceCommit` (full commit ID), `rcTag` (for example `v1.0.0-rc.1`), `artifactSha256`, `artifactProvenance` (`sourceCommit`, `artifactSha256`, and a hashed provenance report), `independentAcceptance` (`disposition`, `reviewer`, `implementers`, zero `blockingDefects`, and a hashed report reference), and one `requirements` entry for every B/RR row. For `ACCEPT WITH DEFECTS`, include each non-blocking defect with its owner disposition; unresolved or blocking defects fail. Each requirement entry records its status and one or more hashed evidence files covering the exact criteria required by the ledger and the §1.1 qualification-only map. Every criterion evidence file must be a JSON object with top-level `sourceCommit`, `rcTag`, and `artifactSha256` values exactly matching the validated qualification record, current RC source commit, and installed RC artifact. A digest-valid report copied from another source revision, RC tag, or artifact is rejected. A B row recorded as `tested` also needs a non-empty `qualificationNotApplicable.reason` and a `qualificationNotApplicable.decision` matching the approved per-requirement exception table and a matching applicability declaration in DECISIONS.md; an unrelated or record-supplied decision is rejected. Evidence paths must be relative regular files under the evidence root, with no symlinks. Missing, unknown, stale, mismatched, or incomplete evidence fails the gate. The checker requires a clean worktree, rejects `--ledger` overrides, enforces source-ledger thresholds outside the explicit §1.1 lifecycle rows, and requires the exact-RC record itself to meet the normal status threshold for every row. It never mutates the source ledger or relaxes a requirement's B/RR record threshold. The checker validates source/tag/artifact identity bindings and evidence hashes; it does not authenticate the reviewer or prove that the artifact was built from the source commit. The approved release workflow must independently verify build provenance/attestation, and the designated custodian and independent reviewer must verify their respective approvals and custody evidence.\\n- [ ] Docs checklist (SPEC-09 §3.2) is signed off.\\n- [ ] Release notes state the standalone scope (DEC-16), the provider tiers (DEC-06), the experimental surfaces (DEC-03, DEC-07) and the known limitations.\\n- [ ] Owner approval to publish (X7).\\n\\nAfter G6, complete source checks on the exact stable-version commit before tagging, then complete the stable artifact checks in §1.1 stage 5 before publishing the draft. A failure keeps publication blocked and requires remediation plus the applicable requalification; do not mark the campaign released until published artifacts are independently verified.\\n\\n**Outcome recording.** The release decision record goes in `docs/releases/v1.0.0.md`, with links to every evidence directory.\\n{\\\"agent\\\":\\\"/root\\\",\\\"host\\\":\\\"mike-dev\\\",\\\"branch\\\":\\\"v1/terminal-matrix-rc3\\\",\\\"worktree\\\":\\\"/home/mike/nexus-wt/terminal-matrix-rc3\\\",\\\"base\\\":\\\"1b9791f07d301c885fe48f04a796203583ab5a5c\\\",\\\"since\\\":\\\"2026-10-23T09:20:00Z\\\",\\\"scope\\\":\\\"Bind unfilled REQ-QUAL-108 human terminal worksheet to published RC3 identity and prepare exact operator procedure; no results claimed\\\",\\\"reviewer\\\":\\\"plan05_readonly_review\\\",\\\"review_disposition\\\":\\\"ACCEPT\\\",\\\"reviewed_at\\\":\\\"2026-10-23T09:30:00Z\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"ready_to_push_after_SUITE\\\",\\\"head\\\":\\\"986eed029f46aa59a302b3a1d61c86a42d953e99\\\"}\\n\"}"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a16ed9-c60e-7103-9ada-b7f9a638664b","create_time":1792861467.1065516}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
