int`; keep comments; modular typed code.\n./docs/reviews/evidence/qualification_2026-10-12/trust_inference.md:68:- Remediation: load workspace-scoped plugins/MCP only after an explicit, persisted per-workspace trust decision (hash of the config/plugin\n./docs/reviews/evidence/nexus-ratatui-facelift-2026-10-03/repl-after.txt:43:  /init               Scaffold AGENTS.md rules file in workspace\n./docs/reviews/evidence/nexus-ratatui-facelift-2026-10-03/repl-session.typescript:51:  /init               Scaffold AGENTS.md rules file in workspace\r\n./docs/reviews/evidence/qualification_2026-10-12/peers.md:17:| **2. Context / long tasks** | `/compact`; `model_auto_compact_token_limit`, `model_context_window`; `/status` shows context usage; `codex resume`; `/fork` copies a chat to a new chat or worktree; `tool_output_token_limit`; resumable state in a SQLite DB (`sqlite_home`); AGENTS.md (`project_doc_max_bytes`, fallback filenames); memories [CX-CFG][CX-SLASH][CX-CLI]. | Auto-compaction at a per-model threshold, `/autocompact <tokens>`, `/compact [focus]`, `/context`; after compaction re-injects CLAUDE.md/startup content, a structured summary, up to 5 most-recent files and invoked skill bodies (5k cap each) [CC-CTX]. Rewind menu can \"summarize from/up to here\" [CC-CKPT]. `--continue/--resume`, `/branch`, `--fork-session`; resume-from-summary dialog for idle >1h, >100k-token sessions [CC-SESS]. CLAUDE.md, AGENTS.md, auto memory [CC-OV]. Subagent `autoCompactWindow` (2.1.296) [CC-CHG]. | `compaction.auto` (default true), `compaction.prune` (old tool outputs, default false), `compaction.reserved` token buffer [OC-CFG]. Per-model `limit.context/output` for custom providers [OC-PROV]. `instructions` file globs [OC-CFG]. | Auto-compact at min(80% of window, 225k tokens) (`GOOSE_AUTO_COMPACT_THRESHOLD`/`_TOKEN_LIMIT`); `/compact`; fallback strategies summarize/truncate/clear/prompt (`GOOSE_CONTEXT_STRATEGY`); headless defaults to summarize [GS-CTX]. | Ollama: warns 2k default ctx \"silently discards context\"; aider sets `num_ctx` to fit each request + 8k reply [AI-OLLAMA]. (No compaction feature verified this session.) |\n./docs/reviews/evidence/qualification_2026-10-12/peers.md:56:8. After compaction, project instructions (AGENTS.md-equivalent) and recently edited files are re-injected [CC-CTX].\n./docs/reviews/evidence/nexus-ratatui-facelift-2026-10-03/repl-before.txt:49:  /init               Scaffold AGENTS.md rules file in workspace\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":44968}},"started_at_ms":1792861568671,"completed_at_ms":1792861568677}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-24T17:06:09.645Z","ordinal":298254,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a16ee0-826d-7d72-b490-382d0d338b97","call_id":"call_bfc0919943ad4f02a617d3d93755c98e","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 2.1 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 116270)\nTotal output lines: 125\n\nrg: packages: No such file or directory (os error 2)\ncli/test/workspace_trust.test.ts:33:describe(\"workspace trust\", () => {\ndocs/superpowers/plans/2026-10-04-nexus-tui-phase3b-slash-commands.md:432:  { name: \"onboard\", usage: \"/onboard\", summary: \"Scan the workspace and write a tailored AGENTS.md\" },\ndocs/superpowers/plans/2026-10-04-nexus-tui-phase3b-slash-commands.md:662:    \"Wrote a tailored AGENTS.md.\",\n./docs/superpowers/plans/2026-10-04-nexus-tui-phase3b-slash-commands.md:432:  { name: \"onboard\", usage: \"/onboard\", summary: \"Scan the workspace and write a tailored AGENTS.md\" },\n./docs/superpowers/plans/2026-10-04-nexus-tui-phase3b-slash-commands.md:662:    \"Wrote a tailored AGENTS.md.\",\n./cli/test/workspace_trust.test.ts:33:describe(\"workspace trust\", () => {\ncli/test/harness.test.ts:2310:  test(\"scanAndOnboardWorkspace discovers stack and writes AGENTS.md with diagram\", () => {\ncli/test/harness.test.ts:2333:      assert.strictEqual(fs.existsSync(path.join(tmpDir, \"AGENTS.md\")), true);\ncli/test/harness.test.ts:2334:      const content = fs.readFileSync(path.join(tmpDir, \"AGENTS.md\"), \"utf-8\");\ncli/test/inference_transport.test.ts:95:      frame({ choices: [{ index: 0, delta: { tool_calls: [{ index: 0, function: { arguments: 'th\":\"AGENTS.md\"}' } }] } }] }) +\ncli/test/inference_transport.test.ts:104:        assert.deepEqual(m.tool_calls?.map((t) => [t.id, t.function.name, t.function.arguments]), [[\"c1\", \"read_file\", '{\"path\":\"AGENTS.md\"}']]);\n./nexus-session-session_20261014_091558_9m78.json:32:      \"content\": \"You are Nexus Code, an autonomous AI software engineering agent running in a Linux shell environment.\\nYou solve coding problems, build features, fix bugs, and refactor codebases by iteratively exploring, reading, editing, and verifying files.\\n\\n### Operating Rules:\\n1. EXPLORE FIRST: Before editing files, always explore the workspace using `file_tree`, `list_dir`, `find_files`, `search_code`, or `read_file`. For large files, use `outline_file` first to inspect class/function signatures without loading the entire file into context.\\n2. HIGH-EFFICIENCY BATCHING: Prefer `batch_read` to read multiple files concurrently in a single turn, and `file_info` to inspect metadata without loading whole files.\\n3. PRECISE EDITS & PATCHES: When modifying existing files, use `edit_file` with unique snippets or `patch_file` with unified diffs.\\n4. PLANNING: Use `update_plan` only for work with three or more distinct phases (not for a fix and its test); update it alongside other tool calls.\\n5. VERIFICATION: After making code changes, use `run_command` with bash/zsh commands to run tests, builds, or linting (e.g. `cargo check`, `cargo test`, `npm test`, `pytest`).\\n6. SELF-CORRECTION: If a command or tool returns an error, analyze the error message, identify the root cause, and fix it.\\n7. AUTONOMOUS COMPLETION: Keep executing tools until the entire task is thoroughly resolved. When everything is verified and done, invoke `task_completed` with a short summary of what changed and how it was checked.\\n8. BOUNDED CONTEXT: Your context window is limited, and earlier tool output is compacted out of the conversation as you work; your own messages are what carry forward. After inspecting large output you will rely on later, state its key findings in a line or two (with file and symbol references) before moving on; do not restate small files or narrate routine steps. Re-read earlier output only when you need a specific detail you did not record or it may have changed.\\n\\n### Recommended Tool Usage Exemplar:\\nExample: Modifying a specific function using edit_file\\nModel:\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\\"tool\\\": \\\"edit_file\\\",\\n  \\\"arguments\\\": {\\n    \\\"path\\\": \\\"src/utils.ts\\\",\\n    \\\"target_content\\\": \\\"export function add(a: number, b: number): number {\\\\n  return a - b;\\\\n}\\\",\\n    \\\"replacement_content\\\": \\\"export function add(a: number, b: number): number {\\\\n  return a + b;\\\\n}\\\"\\n  }\\n}\\n```\\n\\n\\nAlways explain your reasoning before or alongside your tool calls.\\n\\n### Shell Environment:\\n- Active Shell: bash (standard GNU/Linux shell environment)\\n- Workspace directory: /home/mike/nexus-code\\n- Test command (Nexus verifies with it): `make test`\\n\\n### Project Instructions (loaded from AGENTS.md):\\n# Project Guidelines & Agent Instructions\\n\\n## Commands\\n- Build: `make build` or `cargo build` or `npm run build`\\n- Test: `make test` or `cargo test` or `npm test`\\n- Lint: `cargo clippy` or `npm run lint`\\n\\n## Code Conventions\\n- Maintain documentation integrity and keep existing comments.\\n- Always run tests after making changes to verify correctness.\\n- Keep functions modular and clearly typed.\\n\\n### Specialized Agent Skills Available:\\nYou have access to specialized skills. If a user task matches a skill's description, call the `activate_skill` tool with the skill's name to load its specialized workflows and guidelines into context.\\n\\n- **graphify**: Use for any question about a codebase, its architecture, file relationships, or project content — especially when graphify-out/ exists, where the question should be treated as a graphify query first. Turns any input (code, docs, papers, images, videos) into a persistent knowledge graph with god nodes, community detection, and query/path/explain tools.\\n- **gstack**: Router for the gstack skill suite. (gstack)\\n- **autoplan**: Auto-review pipeline — reads the full CEO, design, eng, and DX review skills from disk and runs them sequentially with auto-decisions using 6 decision principles. (gstack)\\n- **autoresearch-v2**: Autonomous skill improvement loop inspired by Karpathy's autoresearch. Analyzes any skill, generates evals, runs baseline, then iteratively improves through autonomous experiments. v2: streamlined setup, blind scoring, resume capability, explicit execution protocol. Trigger with '/autoresearch-v2' followed by a skill name or file path. Examples: '/autoresearch-v2 seo-content-optimizer', '/autoresearch-v2 path/to/SKILL.md'.\\n- **benchmark**: Performance regression detection using the browse daemon. (gstack)\\n- **benchmark-models**: Cross-model benchmark for gstack skills. (gstack)\\n- **boris**: |\\n- **browse**: Fast headless browser for QA testing and site dogfooding. (gstack)\\n- **bubbletea-v2**: >\\n- **canary**: Post-deploy canary monitoring. (gstack)\\n- **careful**: Safety guardrails for destructive commands. (gstack)\\n- **codex**: OpenAI Codex CLI wrapper — three modes. (gstack)\\n- **open-gstack-browser**: Launch GStack Browser — AI-controlled Chromium with the sidebar extension baked in.\\n- **context-restore**: Restore working context saved earlier by /context-save. (gstack)\\n- **context-save**: Save working context. (gstack)\\n- **cso**: Chief Security Officer mode. (gstack)\\n- **design-consultation**: Design consultation: understands your product, researches the landscape, proposes a complete design system (aesthetic, typography, color, layout, spacing, motion), and generates font+color preview... (gstack)\\n- **design-html**: Design finalization: generates production-quality Pretext-native HTML/CSS. (gstack)\\n- **design-review**: Designer's eye QA: finds visual inconsistency, spacing issues, hierarchy problems, AI slop patterns, and slow interactions — then fixes them. (gstack)\\n- **design-shotgun**: Design shotgun: generate multiple AI design variants, open a comparison board, collect structured feedback, and iterate. (gstack)\\n- **devex-review**: Live developer experience audit. (gstack)\\n- **diagram**: Turn an English description (or mermaid source) into a diagram triplet: the source, an editable .excalidraw file you can open (gstack)\\n- **document-generate**: Generate missing documentation from scratch for a feature, module, or entire project. (gstack)\\n- **document-release**: Post-ship documentation update. (gstack)\\n- **excalidraw-diagram**: Use when someone asks to sketch a system, map out a workflow, or build an editable visual diagram. Default for all diagram requests.\\n- **freeze**: Restrict file edits to a specific directory for the session. (gstack)\\n- **gitlab-operations**: >\\n- **glab**: GitLab CLI (glab) for merge requests, issues, and CI/CD pipelines. Use when working with GitLab repositories for MR creation/review, issue management, pipeline debugging, or any GitLab API operations. Triggers on GitLab URLs, mentions of \\\"merge request\\\" or \\\"MR\\\" (not \\\"PR\\\"), gitlab.com, or glab commands.\\n- **gstack-upgrade**: Upgrade gstack to the latest version.\\n- **guard**: Full safety mode: destructive command warnings + directory-scoped edits. (gstack)\\n- **health**: Code quality dashboard. (gstack)\\n- **impeccable**: Use when the user wants to design, redesign, shape, critique, audit, polish, clarify, distill, harden, optimize, adapt, animate, colorize, extract, or otherwise improve a frontend interface. Covers websites, landing pages, dashboards, product UI, app shells, components, forms, settings, onboarding, and empty states. Handles UX review, visual hierarchy, information architecture, cognitive load, accessibility, performance, responsive behavior, theming, anti-patterns, typography, fonts, spacing, layout, alignment, color, motion, micro-interactions, UX copy, error states, edge cases, i18n, and reusable design systems or tokens. Also use for bland designs that need to become bolder or more delightful, loud designs that should become quieter, live browser iteration on UI elements, or ambitious visual effects that should feel technically extraordinary. Not for backend-only or non-UI tasks.\\n- **investigate**: Systematic debugging with root cause investigation. (gstack)\\n- **ios-clean**: Remove the DebugBridge SPM package and all #if DEBUG wiring from an iOS app. (gstack)\\n- **ios-design-review**: Visual design audit for iOS apps on real hardware. (gstack)\\n- **ios-fix**: Autonomous iOS bug fixer. (gstack)\\n- **ios-qa**: Live-device iOS QA for SwiftUI apps. (gstack)\\n- **ios-sync**: Regenerate the iOS debug bridge against the latest upstr…111270 tokens truncated…[name|diff <id> [base]|prune [n]]\",\"summary\":\"Save, compare or prune workspace snapshots\"},{\"name\":\"checkpoints\",\"usage\":\"/checkpoints\",\"summary\":\"List workspace snapshots\"},{\"name\":\"undo\",\"usage\":\"/undo\",\"summary\":\"Roll the workspace back to the last snapshot\"},{\"name\":\"worktree\",\"usage\":\"/worktree [status|merge|discard]\",\"summary\":\"Manage the speculative git worktree\"},{\"name\":\"audit\",\"usage\":\"/audit [count]\",\"summary\":\"Recent tool executions\"},{\"name\":\"receipt\",\"usage\":\"/receipt\",\"summary\":\"Turn outcome, verifier evidence and validation receipt\"},{\"name\":\"test\",\"usage\":\"/test [pattern]\",\"summary\":\"Run the project's test suite\"},{\"name\":\"copy\",\"usage\":\"/copy [diff|code|last]\",\"summary\":\"Copy the diff, code blocks or the last reply\"},{\"name\":\"paste\",\"usage\":\"/paste\",\"summary\":\"Put the clipboard into the composer\"},{\"name\":\"sessions\",\"usage\":\"/sessions\",\"summary\":\"Saved sessions\"},{\"name\":\"save\",\"usage\":\"/save [name]\",\"summary\":\"Save this session\"},{\"name\":\"resume\",\"usage\":\"/resume [id]\",\"summary\":\"Load a saved session (the latest by default)\"},{\"name\":\"history\",\"usage\":\"/history [query|run <n>]\",\"summary\":\"Search earlier prompts or run one again\"},{\"name\":\"export\",\"usage\":\"/export [