{"timestamp":"2026-10-24T17:17:14.870Z","ordinal":298653,"type":"token_usage_record","payload":{"thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a16eea-52ae-7e20-b7bc-6460b8b8bcfa","session_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","root_turn_id":"01a16eea-52ae-7e20-b7bc-6460b8b8bcfa","response_id":"resp_060b64278a9dfb15016adce81966f481a09e394edaec4e15a5","usage":{"input_tokens":149720,"cached_input_tokens":148480,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":150,"reasoning_output_tokens":34,"total_tokens":149870},"turn_token_usage":{"input_tokens":446224,"cached_input_tokens":443008,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":1509,"reasoning_output_tokens":967,"total_tokens":447733},"thread_token_usage":{"input_tokens":5424437233,"cached_input_tokens":5366518784,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":15128951,"reasoning_output_tokens":8630552,"total_tokens":5439566184}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-24T17:17:16.600Z","ordinal":298654,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a16eea-52ae-7e20-b7bc-6460b8b8bcfa","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-29ca0b79-fdf4-4ff6-a47e-e81142bd0e1f","process_id":"58170","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","sed -n '1,240p' scripts/sync-version.mjs; sed -n '1,240p' docs/v1.0.0/README.md; sed -n '1,240p' docs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.5.md"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-wt/rc5-version-sync","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '1,240p' scripts/sync-version.mjs","name":"sync-version.mjs","path":"scripts/sync-version.mjs"},{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '1,240p' docs/v1.0.0/README.md","name":"README.md","path":"docs/v1.0.0/README.md"},{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '1,240p' docs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.5.md","name":"v1.0.0-rc.5.md","path":"docs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.5.md"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"// The root package.json version is the single source of truth (REQ-REL-103). This writes it into cli/package.json,\n// cli/package-lock.json, core/Cargo.toml and core/Cargo.lock; `--check` only reports drift and exits 1 when any file\n// disagrees (run in CI and the release workflow). `--tag vX.Y.Z` additionally requires the tag to match.\nimport fs from \"node:fs\";\nimport path from \"node:path\";\nimport { fileURLToPath } from \"node:url\";\n\nconst root = path.resolve(path.dirname(fileURLToPath(import.meta.url)), \"..\");\nconst args = process.argv.slice(2);\nconst check = args.includes(\"--check\");\nconst tagIndex = args.indexOf(\"--tag\");\nconst tag = tagIndex >= 0 ? args[tagIndex + 1] : undefined;\n\nconst version = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(path.join(root, \"package.json\"), \"utf8\")).version;\nif (!/^\\d+\\.\\d+\\.\\d+(-[0-9A-Za-z.]+)?$/.test(version)) throw new Error(`package.json version '${version}' is not SemVer`);\n\nconst drift = [];\nconst update = (rel, transform) => {\n  const file = path.join(root, rel);\n  const before = fs.readFileSync(file, \"utf8\");\n  const after = transform(before);\n  if (after === before) return;\n  drift.push(rel);\n  if (!check) fs.writeFileSync(file, after);\n};\n\nconst jsonVersion = (text, paths) => {\n  const data = JSON.parse(text);\n  for (const p of paths) {\n    let node = data;\n    for (const key of p.slice(0, -1)) node = node?.[key];\n    if (node && typeof node === \"object\" && p[p.length - 1] in node) node[p[p.length - 1]] = version;\n  }\n  return JSON.stringify(data, null, 2) + \"\\n\";\n};\n\nupdate(\"cli/package.json\", (t) => jsonVersion(t, [[\"version\"]]));\nupdate(\"cli/package-lock.json\", (t) => jsonVersion(t, [[\"version\"], [\"packages\", \"\", \"version\"]]));\nupdate(\"core/Cargo.toml\", (t) => t.replace(/^(\\[package\\][^[]*?\\nversion = )\"[^\"]*\"/s, `$1\"${version}\"`));\nupdate(\"core/Cargo.lock\", (t) => t.replace(/(\\[\\[package\\]\\]\\nname = \"harness-core\"\\nversion = )\"[^\"]*\"/, `$1\"${version}\"`));\n\nif (tag !== undefined && tag !== `v${version}`) {\n  console.error(`tag ${tag} does not match package.json version ${version}`);\n  process.exit(1);\n}\nif (drift.length) {\n  console.error(`${check ? \"version drift\" : \"updated to \" + version}: ${drift.join(\", \")}`);\n  if (check) process.exit(1);\n} else {\n  console.log(`all components at ${version}`);\n}\n# Nexus Code v1.0.0: audit and planning package\n\nThis package is the evidence-based path from `v0.1.0-alpha.2` (audited at `db1ca55`, 2026-10-14) to v1.0.0.\n\n**Verdict: v1.0.0 readiness is BLOCKED.** Candidate source revision `6151a231e9179c109cfbe8cff87e0a4148587b6a` passed an isolated `make build` and full `make test` run on 2026-10-16 (Rust 281/281; CLI 1087/1087; zero skipped). This is source-suite evidence, not RC qualification. Held-out task quality, T3/T4 qualification, standalone/provider qualification, the manual terminal matrix, package/install matrix on the RC, and independent RC acceptance remain incomplete. See [the current readiness reconciliation](READINESS.md) for exact open requirements and gates. The contest entry remains a separate track; judging has concluded and no contest freeze applies.\n\n## How to read it\n\n| If you want to… | Read |\n|---|---|\n| Understand what Nexus is today, what was examined, and what is wrong | [AUDIT.md](AUDIT.md) |\n| See current release readiness and remaining actions | [READINESS.md](READINESS.md) |\n| See every requirement (historical and new), its status, blocker class, and how it is accepted | [REQUIREMENTS.md](REQUIREMENTS.md) |\n| Know the order of work, the effort, and the critical path | [ROADMAP.md](ROADMAP.md) |\n| Implement a workstream | Its spec in [specs/](specs/), then its plan in [plans/](plans/) |\n| Qualify a release candidate | [ACCEPTANCE.md](ACCEPTANCE.md) |\n| Check what was actually run and what it proves | [EVIDENCE.md](EVIDENCE.md) and [evidence/](evidence/) |\n| See the decisions taken (all resolved under delegated owner authority) and the remaining owner actions | [DECISIONS.md](DECISIONS.md) |\n| Run several agents on this plan at once without collisions | [CONCURRENCY.md](CONCURRENCY.md) (also referenced from the root `AGENTS.md`) |\n\n## Workstreams\n\n| # | Workstream | Spec | Plan | Milestone | Blockers |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 01 | Safe execution defaults and approval integrity | [SPEC-01](specs/SPEC-01-safe-execution-defaults.md) | [PLAN-01](plans/PLAN-01-safe-execution-defaults.md) | M1 | SEC-101, 102, 103, 119 |\n| 02 | Process ownership, cancellation, resource bounds | [SPEC-02](specs/SPEC-02-process-ownership-and-bounds.md) | [PLAN-02](plans/PLAN-02-process-ownership-and-bounds.md) | M1 | AGT-109, SEC-106 |\n| 03 | Untrusted workspace inputs and egress boundary | [SPEC-03](specs/SPEC-03-untrusted-inputs-and-egress.md) | [PLAN-03](plans/PLAN-03-untrusted-inputs-and-egress.md) | M1 | SEC-110, 111, 115, 116 |\n| 04 | Continuity, resume, durable work units | [SPEC-04](specs/SPEC-04-continuity-and-durable-work.md) | [PLAN-04](plans/PLAN-04-continuity-and-durable-work.md) | M3 | AGT-101, 102 |\n| 05 | Standalone local inference and provider robustness | [SPEC-05](specs/SPEC-05-standalone-local-inference.md) | [PLAN-05](plans/PLAN-05-standalone-local-inference.md) | M3/M5 | PRV-101, 102, 106 |\n| 06 | Packaged product parity, launcher, versioning, doctor | [SPEC-06](specs/SPEC-06-packaged-product-parity.md) | [PLAN-06](plans/PLAN-06-packaged-product-parity.md) | M0/M2 | REL-101, 102, 103 |\n| 07 | Supply chain, compliance, release engineering | [SPEC-07](specs/SPEC-07-supply-chain-and-release-engineering.md) | [PLAN-07](plans/PLAN-07-supply-chain-and-release-engineering.md) | M2 | REL-107 |\n| 08 | Persistence hygiene | [SPEC-08](specs/SPEC-08-persistence-hygiene.md) | [PLAN-08](plans/PLAN-08-persistence-hygiene.md) | M0/M4 | (prerequisite: PER-103) |\n| 09 | Requirements governance and documentation truth | [SPEC-09](specs/SPEC-09-requirements-governance-and-docs.md) | [PLAN-09](plans/PLAN-09-requirements-governance-and-docs.md) | M0/M6 | OPS-101, 103 |\n| 10 | v1 qualification and evaluation | [SPEC-10](specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md) | [PLAN-10](plans/PLAN-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md) | M3/M5 | QUAL-101 to 107 |\n| 11 | Verification and tool-call integrity | [SPEC-11](specs/SPEC-11-verification-and-tool-call-integrity.md) | [PLAN-11](plans/PLAN-11-verification-and-tool-call-integrity.md) | M1/M3 | AGT-112, 113, 114 |\n| 12 | In-place CLI and TUI upgrade | [SPEC-12](specs/SPEC-12-cli-and-tui-upgrade.md) | [PLAN-12](plans/PLAN-12-cli-and-tui-upgrade.md) | M2 | REL-115 |\n| C1 | Contest (separate product; post-contest maintenance; no freeze applies) | [SPEC-C1](specs/SPEC-C1-contest-submission-track.md) | [PLAN-C1](plans/PLAN-C1-contest-submission-track.md) | post-contest | — (not a client gate) |\n\n\n## How to execute\n\n0. If more than one agent (or person) will implement in parallel, read [CONCURRENCY.md](CONCURRENCY.md) first. It covers slice claims, worktrees, hot files, the gateway lock and merge order.\n1. **Start with M0** (ROADMAP). Merge PLAN-08 PR-8a first, so that test runs stop writing into the real `~/.nexus`. Then land PLAN-06 PR-6a (version sync) and PLAN-09 PR-9a (ledger checker, historical banners, cheap doc fixes).\n2. **M1 is the critical path.** Work through PLAN-01, PLAN-02, PLAN-03 and PLAN-11 PR-11a/b in the PR slices listed. Each plan names its safe change boundary, code locations, tests and rollback.\n3. **For every PR:**\n   - update the matching REQUIREMENTS rows (status, test reference, commit);\n   - keep `scripts/check_requirements.mjs` green;\n   - run `make test` on a snapshot copy, never while editing (tasks/lessons.md).\n4. M2 and M4 run in parallel with M1/M3. Held-out task authoring (agent-authored, as authorised) and the standalone proxy start during M1.\n5. Cut `v1.0.0-rc.1` only when G0–G4 pass. Then run ACCEPTANCE §4–§8 against the **installed** RC.\n\n## Conventions\n\n- **Requirement IDs.** `REQ-<AREA>-0xx` marks a commitment carried over from history. `REQ-<AREA>-1xx` marks a new v1 requirement.\n- **Finding IDs.** These are owned by the scoped evidence files: AGT, VER, PRV, SEC, PER, TUI, REL, DX, MNT, HIST, EVL, CON, PERF, DOC.\n- **Acceptance IDs.** `ACC-<AREA>-NN`. Each is defined in its spec, or in ACCEPTANCE §3.1.\n- **Evidence labels.** SRC, TEST, RT, MEAS, DOC, HIST, INF, UNV (REQUIREMENTS §1).\n- **Status ladder.** open → partial → implemented → tested → visually-accepted → product-qualified. Independent acceptance is recorded separately.\n\nThis package supersedes the Issue #12 matrices and the PHASE and WP documents as the source of current requirements. Those documents remain as historical record.\n# Nexus Code v1.0.0-rc.5 release candidate\n\n**Maturity:** release candidate; prerelease, not stable.\n\n**Status:** this candidate is for exact-artifact qualification. It does not establish independent acceptance or authorize stable v1.0.0 promotion. Qualification results must identify the workflow-produced package and its digest.\n\nThis release packages the Nexus Code Linux x86-64 client: the TypeScript CLI and sidecar, production Node dependencies, Rust `harness-core`, and Ratatui `nexus-tui`.\n\n## Changes since RC4\n\n- Corrects SSRF and locality classification for IPv6 NAT64 addresses. The well-known NAT64 prefix is checked against its embedded IPv4 destination, and the local-use NAT64 prefix is rejected.\n- Protects saved MCP server configuration that may contain credentials: the configuration directory and file use owner-only permissions, writes are atomic, and malformed or invalid existing configuration is preserved instead of being overwritten. Save failures are reported to the user.\n- Bounds `file_info` line counting to 8 MiB while retaining a fixed 1 KiB binary probe. Larger files still return metadata without full line-count scanning.\n- Bounds `edit_file` and `patch_file` whole-file reads to the same 8 MiB limit. Oversized targets are left unchanged and receive a clear error.\n- Makes Linux package archives reproducible across supported build runners by creating them with the pinned release builder, removing host-specific archive metadata differences.\n- Corrects the cross-runner workflow's pinned artifact-download action so the exact published-candidate comparison can execute.\n\nThe REPL PTY cleanup change is test-harness reliability work and does not change product behavior. These source changes and their CI results do not replace RC5 artifact checks, cross-runner qualification, or installed-package qualification.\n\n## Runtime requirements\n\n- Linux x86-64 with glibc 2.35 or newer.\n- Node.js 22 or newer.\n- An OpenAI-compatible inference endpoint, local or explicitly selected provider.\n\nThe archive does not include Node.js. Rust and Cargo are not required at runtime. No other OS or architecture is claimed.\n\n## Candidate assets\n\nThe release workflow for `v1.0.0-rc.5` is expected to produce the version-matched Linux archive, `SHA256SUMS`, SBOM, notices, installer, and provenance. The workflow run, tag commit, artifact digests, and qualification evidence must be recorded before this candidate can be accepted. Local builds are not interchangeable with the workflow-produced artifacts.\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":707111515}},"started_at_ms":1792862235893,"completed_at_ms":1792862236600}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-24T17:17:17.570Z","ordinal":298655,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a16eea-b382-7372-9790-42e758e8ed47","call_id":"call_16c526de8ae94d9cb9cbcfa2c175fbde","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 2.7 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"// The root package.json version is the single source of truth (REQ-REL-103). This writes it into cli/package.json,\n// cli/package-lock.json, core/Cargo.toml and core/Cargo.lock; `--check` only reports drift and exits 1 when any file\n// disagrees (run in CI and the release workflow). `--tag vX.Y.Z` additionally requires the tag to match.\nimport fs from \"node:fs\";\nimport path from \"node:path\";\nimport { fileURLToPath } from \"node:url\";\n\nconst root = path.resolve(path.dirname(fileURLToPath(import.meta.url)), \"..\");\nconst args = process.argv.slice(2);\nconst check = args.includes(\"--check\");\nconst tagIndex = args.indexOf(\"--tag\");\nconst tag = tagIndex >= 0 ? args[tagIndex + 1] : undefined;\n\nconst version = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(path.join(root, \"package.json\"), \"utf8\")).version;\nif (!/^\\d+\\.\\d+\\.\\d+(-[0-9A-Za-z.]+)?$/.test(version)) throw new Error(`package.json version '${version}' is not SemVer`);\n\nconst drift = [];\nconst update = (rel, transform) => {\n  const file = path.join(root, rel);\n  const before = fs.readFileSync(file, \"utf8\");\n  const after = transform(before);\n  if (after === before) return;\n  drift.push(rel);\n  if (!check) fs.writeFileSync(file, after);\n};\n\nconst jsonVersion = (text, paths) => {\n  const data = JSON.parse(text);\n  for (const p of paths) {\n    let node = data;\n    for (const key of p.slice(0, -1)) node = node?.[key];\n    if (node && typeof node === \"object\" && p[p.length - 1] in node) node[p[p.length - 1]] = version;\n  }\n  return JSON.stringify(data, null, 2) + \"\\n\";\n};\n\nupdate(\"cli/package.json\", (t) => jsonVersion(t, [[\"version\"]]));\nupdate(\"cli/package-lock.json\", (t) => jsonVersion(t, [[\"version\"], [\"packages\", \"\", \"version\"]]));\nupdate(\"core/Cargo.toml\", (t) => t.replace(/^(\\[package\\][^[]*?\\nversion = )\"[^\"]*\"/s, `$1\"${version}\"`));\nupdate(\"core/Cargo.lock\", (t) => t.replace(/(\\[\\[package\\]\\]\\nname = \"harness-core\"\\nversion = )\"[^\"]*\"/, `$1\"${version}\"`));\n\nif (tag !== undefined && tag !== `v${version}`) {\n  console.error(`tag ${tag} does not match package.json version ${version}`);\n  process.exit(1);\n}\nif (drift.length) {\n  console.error(`${check ? \"version drift\" : \"updated to \" + version}: ${drift.join(\", \")}`);\n  if (check) process.exit(1);\n} else {\n  console.log(`all components at ${version}`);\n}\n# Nexus Code v1.0.0: audit and planning package\n\nThis package is the evidence-based path from `v0.1.0-alpha.2` (audited at `db1ca55`, 2026-10-14) to v1.0.0.\n\n**Verdict: v1.0.0 readiness is BLOCKED.** Candidate source revision `6151a231e9179c109cfbe8cff87e0a4148587b6a` passed an isolated `make build` and full `make test` run on 2026-10-16 (Rust 281/281; CLI 1087/1087; zero skipped). This is source-suite evidence, not RC qualification. Held-out task quality, T3/T4 qualification, standalone/provider qualification, the manual terminal matrix, package/install matrix on the RC, and independent RC acceptance remain incomplete. See [the current readiness reconciliation](READINESS.md) for exact open requirements and gates. The contest entry remains a separate track; judging has concluded and no contest freeze applies.\n\n## How to read it\n\n| If you want to… | Read |\n|---|---|\n| Understand what Nexus is today, what was examined, and what is wrong | [AUDIT.md](AUDIT.md) |\n| See current release readiness and remaining actions | [READINESS.md](READINESS.md) |\n| See every requirement (historical and new), its status, blocker class, and how it is accepted | [REQUIREMENTS.md](REQUIREMENTS.md) |\n| Know the order of work, the effort, and the critical path | [ROADMAP.md](ROADMAP.md) |\n| Implement a workstream | Its spec in [specs/](specs/), then its plan in [plans/](plans/) |\n| Qualify a release candidate | [ACCEPTANCE.md](ACCEPTANCE.md) |\n| Check what was actually run and what it proves | [EVIDENCE.md](EVIDENCE.md) and [evidence/](evidence/) |\n| See the decisions taken (all resolved under delegated owner authority) and the remaining owner actions | [DECISIONS.md](DECISIONS.md) |\n| Run several agents on this plan at once without collisions | [CONCURRENCY.md](CONCURRENCY.md) (also referenced from the root `AGENTS.md`) |\n\n## Workstreams\n\n| # | Workstream | Spec | Plan | Milestone | Blockers |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 01 | Safe execution defaults and approval integrity | [SPEC-01](specs/SPEC-01-safe-execution-defaults.md) | [PLAN-01](plans/PLAN-01-safe-execution-defaults.md) | M1 | SEC-101, 102, 103, 119 |\n| 02 | Process ownership, cancellation, resource bounds | [SPEC-02](specs/SPEC-02-process-ownership-and-bounds.md) | [PLAN-02](plans/PLAN-02-process-ownership-and-bounds.md) | M1 | AGT-109, SEC-106 |\n| 03 | Untrusted workspace inputs and egress boundary | [SPEC-03](specs/SPEC-03-untrusted-inputs-and-egress.md) | [PLAN-03](plans/PLAN-03-untrusted-inputs-and-egress.md) | M1 | SEC-110, 111, 115, 116 |\n| 04 | Continuity, resume, durable work units | [SPEC-04](specs/SPEC-04-continuity-and-durable-work.md) | [PLAN-04](plans/PLAN-04-continuity-and-durable-work.md) | M3 | AGT-101, 102 |\n| 05 | Standalone local inference and provider robustness | [SPEC-05](specs/SPEC-05-standalone-local-inference.md) | [PLAN-05](plans/PLAN-05-standalone-local-inference.md) | M3/M5 | PRV-101, 102, 106 |\n| 06 | Packaged product parity, launcher, versioning, doctor | [SPEC-06](specs/SPEC-06-packaged-product-parity.md) | [PLAN-06](plans/PLAN-06-packaged-product-parity.md) | M0/M2 | REL-101, 102, 103 |\n| 07 | Supply chain, compliance, release engineering | [SPEC-07](specs/SPEC-07-supply-chain-and-release-engineering.md) | [PLAN-07](plans/PLAN-07-supply-chain-and-release-engineering.md) | M2 | REL-107 |\n| 08 | Persistence hygiene | [SPEC-08](specs/SPEC-08-persistence-hygiene.md) | [PLAN-08](plans/PLAN-08-persistence-hygiene.md) | M0/M4 | (prerequisite: PER-103) |\n| 09 | Requirements governance and documentation truth | [SPEC-09](specs/SPEC-09-requirements-governance-and-docs.md) | [PLAN-09](plans/PLAN-09-requirements-governance-and-docs.md) | M0/M6 | OPS-101, 103 |\n| 10 | v1 qualification and evaluation | [SPEC-10](specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md) | [PLAN-10](plans/PLAN-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md) | M3/M5 | QUAL-101 to 107 |\n| 11 | Verification and tool-call integrity | [SPEC-11](specs/SPEC-11-verification-and-tool-call-integrity.md) | [PLAN-11](plans/PLAN-11-verification-and-tool-call-integrity.md) | M1/M3 | AGT-112, 113, 114 |\n| 12 | In-place CLI and TUI upgrade | [SPEC-12](specs/SPEC-12-cli-and-tui-upgrade.md) | [PLAN-12](plans/PLAN-12-cli-and-tui-upgrade.md) | M2 | REL-115 |\n| C1 | Contest (separate product; post-contest maintenance; no freeze applies) | [SPEC-C1](specs/SPEC-C1-contest-submission-track.md) | [PLAN-C1](plans/PLAN-C1-contest-submission-track.md) | post-contest | — (not a client gate) |\n\n\n## How to execute\n\n0. If more than one agent (or person) will implement in parallel, read [CONCURRENCY.md](CONCURRENCY.md) first. It covers slice claims, worktrees, hot files, the gateway lock and merge order.\n1. **Start with M0** (ROADMAP). Merge PLAN-08 PR-8a first, so that test runs stop writing into the real `~/.nexus`. Then land PLAN-06 PR-6a (version sync) and PLAN-09 PR-9a (ledger checker, historical banners, cheap doc fixes).\n2. **M1 is the critical path.** Work through PLAN-01, PLAN-02, PLAN-03 and PLAN-11 PR-11a/b in the PR slices listed. Each plan names its safe change boundary, code locations, tests and rollback.\n3. **For every PR:**\n   - update the matching REQUIREMENTS rows (status, test reference, commit);\n   - keep `scripts/check_requirements.mjs` green;\n   - run `make test` on a snapshot copy, never while editing (tasks/lessons.md).\n4. M2 and M4 run in parallel with M1/M3. Held-out task authoring (agent-authored, as authorised) and the standalone proxy start during M1.\n5. Cut `v1.0.0-rc.1` only when G0–G4 pass. Then run ACCEPTANCE §4–§8 against the **installed** RC.\n\n## Conventions\n\n- **Requirement IDs.** `REQ-<AREA>-0xx` marks a commitment carried over from history. `REQ-<AREA>-1xx` marks a new v1 requirement.\n- **Finding IDs.** These are owned by the scoped evidence files: AGT, VER, PRV, SEC, PER, TUI, REL, DX, MNT, HIST, EVL, CON, PERF, DOC.\n- **Acceptance IDs.** `ACC-<AREA>-NN`. Each is defined in its spec, or in ACCEPTANCE §3.1.\n- **Evidence labels.** SRC, TEST, RT, MEAS, DOC, HIST, INF, UNV (REQUIREMENTS §1).\n- **Status ladder.** open → partial → implemented → tested → visually-accepted → product-qualified. Independent acceptance is recorded separately.\n\nThis package supersedes the Issue #12 matrices and the PHASE and WP documents as the source of current requirements. Those documents remain as historical record.\n# Nexus Code v1.0.0-rc.5 release candidate\n\n**Maturity:** release candidate; prerelease, not stable.\n\n**Status:** this candidate is for exact-artifact qualification. It does not establish independent acceptance or authorize stable v1.0.0 promotion. Qualification results must identify the workflow-produced package and its digest.\n\nThis release packages the Nexus Code Linux x86-64 client: the TypeScript CLI and sidecar, production Node dependencies, Rust `harness-core`, and Ratatui `nexus-tui`.\n\n## Changes since RC4\n\n- Corrects SSRF and locality classification for IPv6 NAT64 addresses. The well-known NAT64 prefix is checked against its embedded IPv4 destination, and the local-use NAT64 prefix is rejected.\n- Protects saved MCP server configuration that may contain credentials: the configuration directory and file use owner-only permissions, writes are atomic, and malformed or invalid existing configuration is preserved instead of being overwritten. Save failures are reported to the user.\n- Bounds `file_info` line counting to 8 MiB while retaining a fixed 1 KiB binary probe. Larger files still return metadata without full line-count scanning.\n- Bounds `edit_file` and `patch_file` whole-file reads to the same 8 MiB limit. Oversized targets are left unchanged and receive a clear error.\n- Makes Linux package archives reproducible across supported build runners by creating them with the pinned release builder, removing host-specific archive metadata differences.\n- Corrects the cross-runner workflow's pinned artifact-download action so the exact published-candidate comparison can execute.\n\nThe REPL PTY cleanup change is test-harness reliability work and does not change product behavior. These source changes and their CI results do not replace RC5 artifact checks, cross-runner qualification, or installed-package qualification.\n\n## Runtime requirements\n\n- Linux x86-64 with glibc 2.35 or newer.\n- Node.js 22 or newer.\n- An OpenAI-compatible inference endpoint, local or explicitly selected provider.\n\nThe archive does not include Node.js. Rust and Cargo are not required at runtime. No other OS or architecture is claimed.\n\n## Candidate assets\n\nThe release workflow for `v1.0.0-rc.5` is expected to produce the version-matched Linux archive, `SHA256SUMS`, SBOM, notices, installer, and provenance. The workflow run, tag commit, artifact digests, and qualification evidence must be recorded before this candidate can be accepted. Local builds are not interchangeable with the workflow-produced artifacts.\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a16eea-52ae-7e20-b7bc-6460b8b8bcfa","create_time":1792862237.5701773}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
