{"timestamp":"2026-10-24T17:17:24.294Z","ordinal":298661,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a16eea-52ae-7e20-b7bc-6460b8b8bcfa","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-0167ed8a-7c44-4be6-aeb6-7b169490fde3","process_id":"69088","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","rg -n -i \"RC|version-only|version transition|stable|prerelease|tag|authorization|stage-5|pre-RC|pre RC\" docs/v1.0.0 docs/releases | head -200; git status --short --branch; cat .git/nexus-claims/RELEASE_PUBLISHER/owner.json"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-wt/rc5-version-sync","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"rg -n -i \"RC|version-only|version transition|stable|prerelease|tag|authorization|stage-5|pre-RC|pre RC\" docs/v1.0.0 docs/releases | head -200; git status --short --branch; cat .git/nexus-claims/RELEASE_PUBLISHER/owner.json"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"failed","aggregated_output":"docs/v1.0.0/README.md:5:**Verdict: v1.0.0 readiness is BLOCKED.** Candidate source revision `6151a231e9179c109cfbe8cff87e0a4148587b6a` passed an isolated `make build` and full `make test` run on 2026-10-16 (Rust 281/281; CLI 1087/1087; zero skipped). This is source-suite evidence, not RC qualification. Held-out task quality, T3/T4 qualification, standalone/provider qualification, the manual terminal matrix, package/install matrix on the RC, and independent RC acceptance remain incomplete. See [the current readiness reconciliation](READINESS.md) for exact open requirements and gates. The contest entry remains a separate track; judging has concluded and no contest freeze applies.\ndocs/v1.0.0/README.md:26:| 02 | Process ownership, cancellation, resource bounds | [SPEC-02](specs/SPEC-02-process-ownership-and-bounds.md) | [PLAN-02](plans/PLAN-02-process-ownership-and-bounds.md) | M1 | AGT-109, SEC-106 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/README.md:50:5. Cut `v1.0.0-rc.1` only when G0–G4 pass. Then run ACCEPTANCE §4–§8 against the **installed** RC.\ndocs/v1.0.0/README.md:57:- **Evidence labels.** SRC, TEST, RT, MEAS, DOC, HIST, INF, UNV (REQUIREMENTS §1).\ndocs/v1.0.0/README.md:60:This package supersedes the Issue #12 matrices and the PHASE and WP documents as the source of current requirements. Those documents remain as historical record.\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.5.md:1:# Nexus Code v1.0.0-rc.5 release candidate\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.5.md:3:**Maturity:** release candidate; prerelease, not stable.\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.5.md:5:**Status:** this candidate is for exact-artifact qualification. It does not establish independent acceptance or authorize stable v1.0.0 promotion. Qualification results must identify the workflow-produced package and its digest.\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.5.md:9:## Changes since RC4\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.5.md:15:- Makes Linux package archives reproducible across supported build runners by creating them with the pinned release builder, removing host-specific archive metadata differences.\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.5.md:18:The REPL PTY cleanup change is test-harness reliability work and does not change product behavior. These source changes and their CI results do not replace RC5 artifact checks, cross-runner qualification, or installed-package qualification.\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.5.md:26:The archive does not include Node.js. Rust and Cargo are not required at runtime. No other OS or architecture is claimed.\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.5.md:30:The release workflow for `v1.0.0-rc.5` is expected to produce the version-matched Linux archive, `SHA256SUMS`, SBOM, notices, installer, and provenance. The workflow run, tag commit, artifact digests, and qualification evidence must be recorded before this candidate can be accepted. Local builds are not interchangeable with the workflow-produced artifacts.\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.1.md:1:# Nexus Code v1.0.0-rc.1 release candidate\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.1.md:3:**Maturity:** release candidate; prerelease, not stable.\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.1.md:5:**Status:** prepared for exact-artifact qualification. This candidate does not establish independent acceptance or authorize stable v1.0.0 promotion. Qualification results will be recorded against the workflow-produced artifact and its digest.\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.1.md:7:This candidate packages the Nexus Code Linux x86-64 client: the TypeScript CLI and sidecar, production Node dependencies, Rust `harness-core`, and Ratatui `nexus-tui`. It is intended to exercise the version-matched package, installer, supply-chain outputs, and the required provider, standalone, held-out, cross-runner, and terminal qualification gates.\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.1.md:11:The v1.0.0 candidate includes the product, security, continuity, provider, terminal, and packaging work accumulated since the 0.1.0 alpha releases. See the repository changelog for the implemented feature summary. Release-critical behavior remains subject to the exact-RC acceptance process in [`ACCEPTANCE.md`](../v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md).\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.1.md:19:The archive does not include Node.js. Rust and Cargo are not required at runtime. No other OS or architecture is claimed.\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.1.md:23:The release workflow builds the version-matched archive, `SHA256SUMS`, SBOM, notices, installer, and provenance for tag `v1.0.0-rc.1`. The workflow outputs and their digests are the qualification candidate; a local build is not interchangeable.\ndocs/releases/rulesets/release-tags.json:2:  \"name\": \"v1-immutable-release-tags\",\ndocs/releases/rulesets/release-tags.json:3:  \"target\": \"tag\",\ndocs/releases/rulesets/release-tags.json:4:  \"enforcement\": \"active\",\ndocs/releases/rulesets/release-tags.json:5:  \"conditions\": { \"ref_name\": { \"include\": [\"refs/tags/v*\"], \"exclude\": [] } },\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.2.md:1:# Nexus Code v1.0.0-rc.2 release candidate\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.2.md:3:**Maturity:** release candidate; prerelease, not stable.\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.2.md:5:**Status:** this candidate is for exact-artifact qualification. It does not establish independent acceptance or authorize stable v1.0.0 promotion. Qualification results must identify the workflow-produced package and its digest.\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.2.md:9:## Changes since RC1\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.2.md:15:These source changes and their CI results do not replace RC2 artifact checks or installed-package qualification.\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.2.md:20:- As tagged, this candidate declares Node.js 20 or newer. Node.js 20 reached upstream end of life on 2026-04-30, and DEC-12 now requires Node.js 22 or newer for v1.0.0, so `v1.0.0-rc.2` is not promotable to v1.0.0; a later candidate carries the Node.js 22 floor.\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.2.md:23:The archive does not include Node.js. Rust and Cargo are not required at runtime. No other OS or architecture is claimed.\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.2.md:27:The release workflow for `v1.0.0-rc.2` produces the version-matched Linux archive, `SHA256SUMS`, SBOM, notices, installer, and provenance. The workflow run, tag commit, artifact digests, and qualification evidence must be recorded before this candidate can be accepted. Local builds are not interchangeable with the workflow-produced artifacts.\ndocs/v1.0.0/EVIDENCE.md:7:- SRC: source inspection\ndocs/v1.0.0/EVIDENCE.md:22:| Source | `db1ca55`. Exported with `git archive` to `<scratch>/snap` (non-git), and separately cloned to `<scratch>/clone`, checked out at `db1ca55`. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/EVIDENCE.md:32:| Run | Environment | Commands | Outcome | Archive |\ndocs/v1.0.0/EVIDENCE.md:44:| Run | Command | Result | Request ids | Archive |\ndocs/v1.0.0/EVIDENCE.md:57:| `evidence/A2_verification.md` | Parser, verifier, tokens | `a2probe/{parser,tester,tokens,stager}_probe.ts`; 8 targeted test files (53/54; the 1 failure is environmental) |\ndocs/v1.0.0/EVIDENCE.md:63:| `evidence/G_contest_eval.md` | Contest and eval | `npm test --prefix demo`; slice and Worker builds; broker tests; `sha256sum -c` (bundle FAILED, experiment archives OK); `gpgv` |\ndocs/v1.0.0/EVIDENCE.md:74:   - The stale local tags were deleted by the **owner**, not by the audit (X1).\ndocs/v1.0.0/EVIDENCE.md:77:5. **Nothing was committed, pushed, tagged, deployed or published by the audit.**\ndocs/v1.0.0/EVIDENCE.md:79:   - modified `cli/src/agent.ts` (+3 lines);\ndocs/v1.0.0/EVIDENCE.md:83:   These changes are uncommitted. HEAD stayed at `db1ca55`. All tests and builds in this audit ran on clean exports of `db1ca55` (B1, B2), and the live runs used the checkout's prebuilt `cli/dist`, which matched `db1ca55` source (E §4). So these edits are **not** part of the tested revision. Whoever owns them must decide whether to keep or discard them.\ndocs/v1.0.0/EVIDENCE.md:90:| All RT and MEAS rows in AUDIT §5 | On the RC (G5) | The scripts in `evidence/` are ported into `cli/test` by the plans. The remaining manual probes (installer, doctor, memory) follow ACCEPTANCE §7 and ACC-PROC-05/06. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/EVIDENCE.md:91:| L1–L3 | On the RC | With pinned models (ACCEPTANCE §4.3) |\ndocs/v1.0.0/EVIDENCE.md:92:| PTY scenarios | On the RC | ACCEPTANCE §5.2, against the installed package |\ndocs/v1.0.0/EVIDENCE.md:99:- **Terminal evidence** comes from `pyte` emulation plus the repository's PTY suites. Real emulators (kitty keyboard protocol, tmux, VS Code) were not exercised.\ndocs/v1.0.0/EVIDENCE.md:102:- **Platforms:** only Linux x86-64 was exercised. Other distributions only had their installer failure messages checked in docker.\ndocs/v1.0.0/SHA256SUMS:59:8e82f6bcc4f165873b339ef895d14acee8ad2c0b21420a9f539bee36a195b52c  evidence/a2probe/stager_probe.ts\ndocs/releases/rulesets/protected-branches.json:4:  \"enforcement\": \"active\",\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.3.md:1:# Nexus Code v1.0.0-rc.3 release candidate\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.3.md:3:**Maturity:** release candidate; prerelease, not stable.\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.3.md:5:**Status:** this candidate is for exact-artifact qualification. It does not establish independent acceptance or authorize stable v1.0.0 promotion. Qualification results must identify the workflow-produced package and its digest.\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.3.md:9:## Changes since RC2\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.3.md:12:- Adds an interactive checkpoint decision when sensitive content cannot be persisted, allowing the user to choose read-only, continue without a rollback checkpoint, create a checkpoint after acknowledging the sensitivity warning, cancel, or revise the instruction. This behavior must be verified from the installed candidate; RC1 and RC2 do not contain it.\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.3.md:15:These source changes and their CI results do not replace RC3 artifact checks or installed-package qualification.\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.3.md:23:The archive does not include Node.js. Rust and Cargo are not required at runtime. No other OS or architecture is claimed.\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.3.md:27:The release workflow for `v1.0.0-rc.3` is expected to produce the version-matched Linux archive, `SHA256SUMS`, SBOM, notices, installer, and provenance. The workflow run, tag commit, artifact digests, and qualification evidence must be recorded before this candidate can be accepted. Local builds are not interchangeable with the workflow-produced artifacts.\ndocs/releases/v0.1.0-alpha.2.md:3:**Maturity:** alpha, pre-1.0 SemVer prerelease.\ndocs/releases/v0.1.0-alpha.2.md:5:**Status:** published as a GitHub prerelease on 2026-10-14 (release workflow run 38539108878); assets verified against `SHA256SUMS`.\ndocs/releases/v0.1.0-alpha.2.md:7:This is the second 0.x alpha. Like `v0.1.0-alpha.1`, it is not a stable release; install it by pinning `NEXUS_VERSION=v0.1.0-alpha.2`.\ndocs/releases/v0.1.0-alpha.2.md:17:- **Durable compaction.** Each compaction is committed in order (archive, task state, session) with fsync; recovery ignores uncommitted archive entries. A compaction that cannot be written stops the turn as `PERSISTENCE_FAILED`. `/compact` issued during work is queued and runs at the next settled step.\ndocs/releases/v0.1.0-alpha.2.md:18:- **Provider capabilities and token accounting.** Context size and output allowance are discovered from the provider's `/models` when advertised (homelab-ai gateway, vLLM). When the gateway offers `/v1/tokenize`, Nexus counts the exact request body it is about to send; counts are labelled by source. `--strict-token-count` requires a provider count. Standalone servers keep working on client estimates.\ndocs/releases/v0.1.0-alpha.2.md:43:The archive does not include Node.js. Rust and Cargo are not required at runtime. No other OS or architecture is claimed.\ndocs/releases/v0.1.0-alpha.2.md:50:The release workflow builds the versioned archive and checksum from a matching `v0.1.0-alpha.2` tag. The published assets match these names, and the archive verifies against the published `SHA256SUMS`.\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.4.md:1:# Nexus Code v1.0.0-rc.4 release candidate\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.4.md:3:**Maturity:** release candidate; prerelease, not stable.\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.4.md:5:**Status:** this candidate is for exact-artifact qualification. It does not establish independent acceptance or authorize stable v1.0.0 promotion. Qualification results must identify the workflow-produced package and its digest.\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.4.md:9:## Changes since RC3\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.4.md:14:- Strips terminal control characters from decoded HTML and web-search text before displaying untrusted results.\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.4.md:15:- Normalizes slash and backslash separators before checking archive symlink targets, rejecting targets whose normalized destination escapes the package root.\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.4.md:23:- Locks the npm release tools used for notices and the SBOM, rejects deprecated packages in that lock, and adds a cross-runner workflow that rebuilds a published RC on Ubuntu 22.04 and 24.04 and compares the archive, compatibility metadata, checksums, notices, SBOM and installer with the published assets.\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.4.md:26:These source changes and their CI results do not replace RC4 artifact checks or installed-package qualification.\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.4.md:34:The archive does not include Node.js. Rust and Cargo are not required at runtime. No other OS or architecture is claimed.\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.4.md:38:The release workflow for `v1.0.0-rc.4` is expected to produce the version-matched Linux archive, `SHA256SUMS`, SBOM, notices, installer, and provenance. The workflow run, tag commit, artifact digests, and qualification evidence must be recorded before this candidate can be accepted. Local builds are not interchangeable with the workflow-produced artifacts.\ndocs/releases/PROTECTIONS.md:3:The branch and release-tag rulesets below were observed active through the GitHub API on 2026-10-18.\ndocs/releases/PROTECTIONS.md:12:| Rulesets | Active `v1-protected-branches` (25340146) and `v1-immutable-release-tags` (25340148) |\ndocs/releases/PROTECTIONS.md:21:enforce what GitHub *can* check: required CI, no history rewriting, and immutable release tags.\ndocs/releases/PROTECTIONS.md:26:- no deletion and no force-push;\ndocs/releases/PROTECTIONS.md:28:  only** (`allowed_merge_methods: [\"merge\"]`). A squash or rebase merge would create new commits, leaving the RC tag\ndocs/releases/PROTECTIONS.md:29:  commit or the stable commit `S` off `main`;\ndocs/releases/PROTECTIONS.md:35:`rulesets/release-tags.json` covers `refs/tags/v*`:\ndocs/releases/PROTECTIONS.md:36:- tags can be created, but never moved or deleted.\ndocs/releases/PROTECTIONS.md:38:No bypass actors are defined. To repair a mistaken tag, the owner disables the ruleset, records why, and enables it again.\ndocs/releases/PROTECTIONS.md:42:1. **RC source to `main`.** PR #8 (`v1/integration` to `main`) needs the required checks. It is merged with a merge\ndocs/releases/PROTECTIONS.md:43:   commit `M`. The RC tag `v1.0.0-rc.N` goes on `M`, which is on `main`, so `release.yml`'s ancestry check passes.\ndocs/releases/PROTECTIONS.md:44:   Creating a tag is allowed.\ndocs/releases/PROTECTIONS.md:45:2. **RC rebuild.** A fix is merged through PRs, and a new tag `rc.N+1` is created. Old RC tags stay as evidence.\ndocs/releases/PROTECTIONS.md:46:3. **Stable promotion.** Commit `S` changes only the version and sits directly on the accepted RC commit `M`. A PR\ndocs/releases/PROTECTIONS.md:48:   keeps `S` in `main`'s history. Tag `v1.0.0` goes on `S`. `release.yml` verifies it is version-only on `rc.N`.\ndocs/releases/PROTECTIONS.md:49:   - With strict \"up to date\" checks, any merge to `main` between the RC and the stable commit would force an update\ndocs/releases/PROTECTIONS.md:50:     merge into the PR branch. `S` would then no longer be directly on the RC, which is the deadlock that keeping\ndocs/releases/PROTECTIONS.md:52:   - Process rule: **nothing else merges to `main` between the accepted RC and the stable tag.**\ndocs/releases/PROTECTIONS.md:53:4. **Publication.** `release.yml` creates the stable release as a draft. `gh release edit v1.0.0 --draft=false` is not\ndocs/releases/PROTECTIONS.md:58:- **Actions SHA pinning** (`sha_pinning_required`). This would break the current workflows, which pin actions by tag,\ndocs/releases/PROTECTIONS.md:72:gh api -X POST \"$R/rulesets\" --input docs/releases/rulesets/release-tags.json\ndocs/releases/PROTECTIONS.md:76:gh api \"$R/rulesets\" -q '.[] | \"\\(.id) \\(.name) \\(.enforcement)\"'\ndocs/releases/PROTECTIONS.md:82:tag. A PR with green required checks should still merge.\ndocs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md:35:- **Hot-file claims** use the same mechanism with the name `FILE_<path with / replaced by _>`, for example `FILE_cli_src_agent.ts`. See §4.\ndocs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md:41:| Resource | Rule |\ndocs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md:43:| Source | One `git worktree` per claimed slice: `git worktree add ../nexus-wt/<slice> -b v1/<plan>-<slice> origin/main`. Never edit `~/nexus-code` itself. It is the owner's checkout, and `/usr/local/bin/nexus` runs from it. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md:45:| HOME and state | Until PLAN-08 PR-8a lands, every test, build and probe run sets `HOME=$(mktemp -d)` and `XDG_CONFIG_HOME=\"$HOME/.config\"`. After PR-8a, the test setup enforces this, but scripts and probes outside `npm test` must still set it. **Never** run anything that writes to the real `~/.nexus` or `~/.config/nexus`. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md:46:| Test runs | Full suites run on a **snapshot copy** of the worktree (`git worktree add` at the commit under test, or `git archive`), never on the tree being edited. `tsx` reads `src/` live. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md:60:| `cli/src/agent.ts` | 01, 02, 03, 04, 05, 11 | Claim required. Keep each change local to the line ranges the plan names. Rebase immediately before merge and re-run that slice's tests on the rebased snapshot. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md:61:| `cli/src/index.ts` | 01, 03, 04, 06, 08, 10, 11 | Claim required. **PLAN-06 PR-6b (unified launcher) lands first.** Other plans add commands and flags afterwards. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md:62:| `cli/src/tools.ts` | 01, 02, 03, 06, 11 | Claim required. **PLAN-02 PR-2b (signal plumbing) lands before PLAN-03 PR-3c (`safeFetch`)**. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md:63:| `cli/src/sidecar.ts` | 01, 02, 03, 05, 08 | Claim required |\ndocs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md:64:| `cli/src/doctor.ts` | 01, 03, 05, 06, 08 | Claim required. Each plan adds **new check functions** in separate blocks. Only PLAN-06 PR-6d changes existing checks. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md:65:| `cli/src/client.ts` | 03, 05, 08, 11 | Claim required. **PLAN-03 PR-3a (env layering) lands before any PLAN-05 slice.** |\ndocs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md:66:| `cli/src/repl.ts` | 01, 05, 08 | Claim required |\ndocs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md:67:| `cli/src/config.ts`, `security.ts`, `sandbox.ts`, `mcp.ts`, `plugins.ts` | 01, 03 | Claim required. PLAN-01 PR-1e and PLAN-03 must not run at the same time on `sandbox.ts` or `security.ts`. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md:68:| `cli/src/core/capabilities.ts` | 01, 02 | **PLAN-01 PR-1a (effect classes) lands first.** PLAN-02 PR-2c adds schema fields afterwards. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md:69:| `cli/src/tester.ts` | 01, 11 | **PLAN-01 PR-1c lands before PLAN-11 PR-11b/11c.** |\ndocs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md:70:| `cli/src/core/state.ts` | 04, 08 | **PLAN-08 PR-8a (HOME isolation) lands before everything.** |\ndocs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md:71:| `core/src/runner.rs`, `core/src/main.rs` | 01, 02, 06 | Claim required. The protocol version number is owned by PLAN-02 PR-2a. PLAN-06 PR-6c only reads it. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md:72:| `core/src/bin/nexus_tui/{live_state,live_view}.rs` | 01, 02 | Claim required |\ndocs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md:76:| `docs/USER_MANUAL.md`, `ARCHITECTURE.md`, `CLOUD_PROVIDERS.md`, `quickstart.md` | 05, 09 and doc tasks in every plan | Edit only the sections your slice changes. Hold a short `FILE_` claim. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md:88:5. Pushing, tagging, publishing and changing GitHub state (issues, milestones, releases) are **owner-approved actions** (DECISIONS X-list). Agents prepare them and do not perform them.\ndocs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md:109:| M3 | (a) PLAN-04 (`agent.ts` turn, operation runner). (b) PLAN-05 (`client.ts`, provider modules). (c) PLAN-10 harness (`eval/`, no product files). (d) Held-out task authoring by the agent author, **outside the repository**: no access to Nexus source or the development set (DEC-05). |\ndocs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md:115:- The held-out task author must not see Nexus source, the development tasks or tuning history. It runs in a separate session with only the task schema and external repositories. Its output is sealed by a sha256 manifest committed before RC1.\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/repro/agt_repro.test.ts:5:import { AutonomousAgent } from \"../snap/cli/src/agent.js\";\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/repro/agt_repro.test.ts:6:import { ApplicationCore } from \"../snap/cli/src/core/app.js\";\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/repro/agt_repro.test.ts:45:  console.log(\"R1 file:\", JSON.stringify(fs.readFileSync(path.join(ws, \"notes.txt\"), \"utf8\")), \"git:\", execSync(\"git status --porcelain\", { cwd: ws }).toString().trim());\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/repro/agt_repro.test.ts:53:  const first = new ApplicationCore(cfg(gw, ws)); quiet(first.getAgent());\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/repro/agt_repro.test.ts:55:  const second = new ApplicationCore(cfg(gw, ws)); quiet(second.getAgent());\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/repro/agt_repro.test.ts:61:  const third = new ApplicationCore(cfg(gw, ws)); quiet(third.getAgent());\ndocs/v1.0.0/AUDIT.md:21:| Versions | `package.json` and `cli/package.json`: `0.1.0-alpha.2`. **`core/Cargo.toml`: `1.2.1`** (mismatch, REL-04). Tags on origin: `v0.1.0-alpha.1` and `v0.1.0-alpha.2`, both GitHub prereleases. Local-only tags `v1.1.0`, `v1.2.0`, `v1.2.1` (never on the remote, per the owner and `git ls-remote`). | RT |\ndocs/v1.0.0/AUDIT.md:22:| Build entry points | `make build` (cargo release + `tsc`), `make test` (cargo test + `npm --prefix cli test` + `scripts/security_gates.sh`), `scripts/package-linux.sh`, `scripts/smoke-package.sh`, `scripts/installer-smoke.sh`. CI: `.github/workflows/ci.yml` (contest contract job + `linux-x86_64`), `release.yml` (tag-triggered). A dead `.gitlab-ci.yml` also exists. | SRC |\ndocs/v1.0.0/AUDIT.md:25:| Runtime services | The local inference gateway is configured in `~/.config/nexus/config.env`: endpoint `https://10.0.8.5:8443/v1`, model `engineering/b0`, key redacted, `LOCAL_HARNESS_SHELL=bash`. The repo-tracked `cli/.env` holds LM Studio defaults (`localhost:1234`, key \"local\"). **The audit sent no requests to the gateway.** With owner authorization (2026-10-14, small spend), it made live cloud calls through the existing ChatGPT sign-in and OpenRouter connections: two `providers verify` runs and one `nexus run` bug-fix task. See EVIDENCE §3. | RT (values redacted) |\ndocs/v1.0.0/AUDIT.md:26:| External dependencies | Node ≥ 20 (runtime), GitHub Releases (installer), optional bubblewrap/Docker (sandbox), optional cloud providers (OpenRouter, OpenAI, Anthropic, ChatGPT/Copilot OAuth, compatible), optional MCP servers, DuckDuckGo (default `search_web`). | SRC |\ndocs/v1.0.0/AUDIT.md:31:### 2.1 Established commitments (sources: README, quickstart, USER_MANUAL, COMPACTION_AND_CONTINUITY, CLOUD_PROVIDERS, release notes, Issue #12 and later reviews; ledger in REQUIREMENTS §2)\ndocs/v1.0.0/AUDIT.md:47:- **No default step ceiling.** Turns end on completion, cancel, stagnation or failure.\ndocs/v1.0.0/AUDIT.md:79:## 3. Architecture as implemented\ndocs/v1.0.0/AUDIT.md:89:            ApplicationCore / AutonomousAgent.runTurn  (cli/src/agent.ts, 5.4k lines)\ndocs/v1.0.0/AUDIT.md:117:- **Task state.** `~/.nexus/tasks/<id>.json`, written as a full atomic rewrite on each progress event. The compaction archive is `<id>.history.jsonl` (append + fsync).\ndocs/v1.0.0/AUDIT.md:120:- **Recovery.** `recoverFromTaskState` restores messages and objective, and filters uncommitted archive entries. **Except:** `run --resume` discards the restored conversation (AGT-01), and work units skip the commit protocol (AGT-02).\ndocs/v1.0.0/AUDIT.md:132:- Source greps for spot checks.\ndocs/v1.0.0/AUDIT.md:136:| Agent loop and core (`cli/src/agent.ts`, `core/{turn,app,execution_tracking,objective,provider_recovery,operation_runner}.ts`, `team.ts`) | 9 | Full read | A_core_agent | — |\ndocs/v1.0.0/AUDIT.md:138:| Verification and parsing: `parser, tester, evaluator, synthesizer, stager, tokens, fewshots, image, clipboard, build_identity`, `core/{findings, operation, candidate, roles}` | 14 | Full read (findings and operation: targeted) + probes | A2_verification | — |\ndocs/v1.0.0/AUDIT.md:139:| Providers: `client.ts`, `protocols/*`, `providers, provider_cli, provider_connect, model_catalog, credentials, oauth, config, usage, search_web, onboard, embeddings`, `core/{provider_capabilities, egress}` | 17 | Full read (embeddings, egress: targeted) + mock probes | B_providers; this file (provider_connect, read by lead) | `evaluateEgress` deep logic reviewed only for classification |\ndocs/v1.0.0/AUDIT.md:140:| Tools, security, persistence: `tools, safe_fs, sandbox, security, session, session_export, checkpoint, flight, evidence, git, worktree, mcp, plugins, skills, browser, lsp, file_diff, syntax, diagnostics, workspace_trust`, `core/{authority, resources, durable_file, persistence_protection, capabilities, workspace_path, independent_check, tool_groups}` | 28 | Full read for security-critical files. Grep or skim for session_export, file_diff, syntax, diagnostics, resources, browser, lsp, mcp transports. | C_tools_security_persistence; this file (workspace_trust, workspace_path, tool_groups, independent_check, approval_review, read by lead) | MCP remote transports, browser.ts and lsp.ts got only a skim review: **qualification gap** |\ndocs/v1.0.0/AUDIT.md:141:| Rust harness-core: `core/src/{main, file_ops, runner, search, git_ops, cst, trigram}.rs`, `core/tests` | 9 | main/runner full read; file_ops mostly full (delimiter validator 400-575 skipped); others grep + runtime | C | file_ops.rs:400-575 not reviewed |\ndocs/v1.0.0/AUDIT.md:142:| Rust TUI: `core/src/bin/nexus_tui.rs` + 14 modules | 15 | Targeted read of the approval, input and cancel paths + **real PTY runs**. composer, diff_view, markdown, highlight, models, review, slash, sidecar.rs, redact are exercised indirectly and by the repo PTY suites. | D_terminal + D_pty/ | Line review of the rendering modules: excluded (covered by PTY behaviour) |\ndocs/v1.0.0/AUDIT.md:145:| Generated `cli/dist` (86 files) | 86 | Byte-diffed against a fresh build of HEAD: identical except build-info | E | Not reviewed as source (generated) |\ndocs/v1.0.0/AUDIT.md:148:| Experiments archives (routing, thermal, context-validation; 147) | 147 | READMEs + `sha256sum -c` | G | Raw data not re-analysed |\ndocs/v1.0.0/AUDIT.md:171:| SEC-01 | S1 