ation, including environment values, at the user's request; it is distinct from the PERS-002 enumerated transcript/flight/audit/checkpoint/cache/crash artifacts and is not a protected vault. Static template/theme/dummy-browser/worktree-exclude/scorecard writers inspected do not accept arbitrary task payload. This is a bounded CLI write-path inventory, not a universal claim about every external process or OS crash artifact.\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/terminal-matrix-worksheet/docs/WP01_INDEPENDENT_IMPLEMENTATION_REVIEW.md:15:An independent, adversarial implementation review was conducted on the delivered artifacts for Nexus Issue #12 Work Package 01 (`WP-01: Capability Registry & Common Execution Spine`). The review evaluated whether the implementation satisfies the normative contracts established in the operator-accepted Phase 4 implementation work packages (`docs/PHASE4_IMPLEMENTATION_WORK_PACKAGES.md`) and the Phase 3 implementation decomposition (`docs/PHASE3_IMPLEMENTATION_DECOMPOSITION.md`).\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/terminal-matrix-worksheet/docs/WP01_INDEPENDENT_IMPLEMENTATION_REVIEW.md:23:- **Working Tree State:** Clean (no untracked modifications prior to review artifact creation)\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/terminal-matrix-worksheet/docs/WP01_INDEPENDENT_IMPLEMENTATION_REVIEW.md:112:32. `browser_screenshot` — IDENTICAL\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/terminal-matrix-worksheet/docs/WP01_INDEPENDENT_IMPLEMENTATION_REVIEW.md:221:- **Canonical Rebuild:** `npm --prefix cli run build` executed cleanly. `git status --porcelain` showed zero changes in `cli/dist/`, proving generated artifacts are 100% reproducible.\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/terminal-matrix-worksheet/docs/WP01_INDEPENDENT_IMPLEMENTATION_REVIEW.md:15:An independent, adversarial implementation review was conducted on the delivered artifacts for Nexus Issue #12 Work Package 01 (`WP-01: Capability Registry & Common Execution Spine`). The review evaluated whether the implementation satisfies the normative contracts established in the operator-accepted Phase 4 implementation work packages (`docs/PHASE4_IMPLEMENTATION_WORK_PACKAGES.md`) and the Phase 3 implementation decomposition (`docs/PHASE3_IMPLEMENTATION_DECOMPOSITION.md`).\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/terminal-matrix-worksheet/docs/WP01_INDEPENDENT_IMPLEMENTATION_REVIEW.md:23:- **Working Tree State:** Clean (no untracked modifications prior to review artifact creation)\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/terminal-matrix-worksheet/docs/WP01_INDEPENDENT_IMPLEMENTATION_REVIEW.md:112:32. `browser_screenshot` — IDENTICAL\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/terminal-matrix-worksheet/docs/WP01_INDEPENDENT_IMPLEMENTATION_REVIEW.md:221:- **Canonical Rebuild:** `npm --prefix cli run build` executed cleanly. `git status --porcelain` showed zero changes in `cli/dist/`, proving generated artifacts are 100% reproducible.\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/terminal-matrix-worksheet/docs/PHASE3_CORRECTIONS_VERIFICATION.md:47:  - **Comprehensive State Coverage:** Section 11.1 and Section 21 (`INC-05`) mandate accounting for tracked modified files, relevant untracked files in the working directory (e.g. staged via `git add -A` before computing `git write-tree`, or indexed in a working-tree hash manifest), generated artifacts where applicable, and content-hashing fallbacks in non-Git workspaces.\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/terminal-matrix-worksheet/.github/workflows/release.yml:80:      - name: Require a stable tag to be a version-only commit on its RC\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/terminal-matrix-worksheet/.github/workflows/release.yml:82:        # The checkout has full history and tags (fetch-depth: 0). The checker runs from the RC's own copy so a stable\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/terminal-matrix-worksheet/.github/workflows/release.yml:111:      # RC tags (vX.Y.Z-rc.N) publish a prerelease: the workflow-produced RC is the qualification candidate\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/terminal-matrix-worksheet/.github/workflows/release.yml:113:      # `gh release edit <tag> --draft=false` after the stable artifact checks and the signed acceptance dispo