l BrowserDriver directly. Remote navigate uses host fetch; local file navigation reads host-visible paths; click/type search the stored DOM and report simulated interactions; screenshot writes a constant 1x1 PNG but reports 1280x720. CDP availability helper sets a flag but interaction methods do not use CDP. /browse is another operator wrapper over the driver.\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/terminal-matrix-worksheet/docs/PHASE1_SYSTEM_RECONSTRUCTION.md:74:| Browser tools | EXPERIMENTALLY_WIRED | BOUNDED | browser.ts, agent, CLI /browse | Unit tests validate simulation/data mechanics. | Not actual CDP interaction despite helper/description; screenshot placeholder. Remote fetch is host-networked. |\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/terminal-matrix-worksheet/docs/PHASE1_SYSTEM_RECONSTRUCTION.md:88:| Validation | TestRunResult, verifiedWorktreeCompletion boolean, SynthesizerState, tool output, evaluator result. | Discovery success advisory; configured verifier alone authorizes auto merge. TDD/evaluator/manual test have separate result semantics. | No durable validation artifact bound to exact mutation set/workspace/commit. | #11 tests prove configured success/failure behavior, not semantic quality of trusted command. |\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/terminal-matrix-worksheet/docs/PHASE1_SYSTEM_RECONSTRUCTION.md:108:| Browser | Driver workspace, but local absolute reads/screenshot writes are direct TS. | Does not use bridge controls; click/type simulated. | Host fetch network; no live CDP action implementation. | Results become model messages but aren't live browser validation. |\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/terminal-matrix-worksheet/docs/PHASE1_SYSTEM_RECONSTRUCTION.md:128:| Browser | browser_navigate, browser_screenshot, browser_click, browser_type, browser_console_logs | Direct TS BrowserDriver; simulated behavior. |\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/terminal-matrix-worksheet/docs/PHASE1_SYSTEM_RECONSTRUCTION.md:163:| Browser simulation/execution | CONFIRMED_ON_BE829EC | Click/type simulated; screenshot placeholder; CDP flag not used for interactions. |\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/terminal-matrix-worksheet/docs/PHASE1_SYSTEM_RECONSTRUCTION.md:190:| Existing docs/ARCHITECTURE.md claims more unified Rust security boundary than code | Medium doc risk | Source comparison straightforward | Update docs after review of this reconstruction. |\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/terminal-matrix-worksheet/docs/PHASE1_SYSTEM_RECONSTRUCTION.md:204:| Browser tool means browser execution | Simulated click/type/screenshot | Model can receive outputs not backed by a live browser action. |\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/terminal-matrix-worksheet/docs/PHASE1_SYSTEM_RECONSTRUCTION.md:237:- No implementation or tests were changed. This file is the sole intended repository artifact for Phase 1.\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/terminal-matrix-worksheet/docs/ISSUE12_POST_WP05_CLOSURE_ASSESSMENT.md:54:All reconciliation conclusions are derived strictly from local authoritative repository artifacts in accordance with the established governance hierarchy:\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/terminal-matrix-worksheet/.github/workflows/repro.yml:7:        description: 'RC tag to package and compare (e.g. v1.0.0-rc.1)'\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/terminal-matrix-worksheet/.github/workflows/repro.yml:32:          # The workflow definition must be the RC's own: dispatch it on the tag, not a branch.\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/terminal-matrix-worksheet/.github/workflows/repro.yml:76:      - uses: actions/upload-artifact@ea165f8d65b6e75b540449e92b4886f43607fa02 # v4\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/terminal-matrix-worksheet/.github/workflows/repro.yml:81:      - uses: actions/upload-artifact@ea165f8d65b6e75b540449e92b4886f43607fa02 # v4\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/terminal-matrix-worksheet/.github/workflows/repro.yml:98:      - uses: actions/download-artifact@d3f86a106a0bac45b974a628896c90dbdf5c8093 # v4\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/terminal-matrix-worksheet/.github/workflows/repro.yml:105:          ARCHIVE=\"nexus-linux-x86_64-$VERSION.tar.gz\"\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/terminal-matrix-worksheet/.github/workflows/repro.yml:106:          for f in \"$ARCHIVE\" SHA256SUMS THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.txt sbom.cdx.json install.sh; do cmp \"$A/$f\" \"$B/$f\"; done\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/terminal-matrix-worksheet/.github/workflows/repro.yml:111:      - uses: actions/upload-artifact@ea165f8d65b6e75b540449e92b4886f43607fa02 # v4\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/terminal-matrix-worksheet/docs/DEVELOPMENT.md:21:Create and inspect a candidate locally. Set `NEXUS_VERSION` to the release tag being built; for an RC, use its RC tag, and for a stable release, use its stable tag:\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/terminal-matrix-worksheet/.github/workflows/ci.yml:157:      - uses: actions/upload-artifact@ea165f8d65b6e75b540449e92b4886f43607fa02 # v4\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/terminal-matrix-worksheet/docs/CLOUDFLARE_CONTEST_CRITICAL_PATH_ASSESSMENT.md:13:Nexus currently has no Cloudflare Worker or Artifacts integration. The contest submission is due October 14 and asks for a 5–10 minute demo, open-source code, and run instructions. Artifacts entered open beta on October 1 and is available on Workers Paid plans. The remaining schedule is short, so the first engineering task must prove the real Cloudflare repository lifecycle before building a polished interface. [Contest brief](https://www.cloudflare.com/git-competition/), [submission requirements](https://www.cloudflare.com/git-competition/submit/), [Artifacts open-beta announcement](https://developers.cloudflare.com/changelog/post/2026-10-01-artifacts-open-beta/)\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/terminal-matrix-worksheet/docs/CLOUDFLARE_CONTEST_CRITICAL_PATH_ASSESSMENT.md:92:**Artifacts:** no Artifact binding, namespace setup, repo adapter, scoped token issuance, Git remote, or Artifact-backed persistence exists. The Artifact Worker binding is designed to create/import/fork and inspect repositories and issue repo-scoped Git tokens; standard Git clients can clone/push. The demo must prove this vertical slice with a real account and namespace. [Workers binding](https://developers.cloudflare.com/artifacts/api/workers-binding/), [Workers getting started](https://developers.cloudflare.com/artifacts/get-started/workers/)\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/terminal-matrix-worksheet/docs/CLOUDFLARE_CONTEST_CRITICAL_PATH_ASSESSMENT.md:175:- Simple second reviewer/agent with a distinct role and a structured findings artifact.\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/terminal-matrix-worksheet/docs/REPOSITORY_QUALITY.md:49:- Release immutability and release-environment controls: coordinate with the designated publisher and accepted RC/stable draft lifecycle before enabling. Do not strand an active release or assume immutable tags make assets immutable.\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/terminal-matrix-worksheet/docs/REPOSITORY_QUALITY.md:57:Dependabot covers GitHub Actions, CLI npm dependencies, core Cargo dependencies, the contest demo, and the Cloudflare artifact experiment package roots and nested manifests. The contest has concluded, and no contest freeze applies. Dependabot does not auto-merge updates. Review security advisories and CI; SHA pinning does not replace dependency monitoring.\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/terminal-matrix-worksheet/docs/REPOSITORY_QUALITY.md:49:- Release immutability and release-environment controls: coordinate with the designated publisher and accepted RC/stable draft lifecycle before enabling. Do not strand an active release or assume immutable tags make assets immutable.\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/terminal-matrix-worksheet/docs/REPOSITORY_QUALITY.md:57:Dependabot covers GitHub Actions, CLI npm dependencies, core Cargo dependencies, the contest demo, and the Cloudflare artifact experiment package roots and nested manifests. The contest has concluded, and no contest freeze applies. Dependabot does not auto-merge updates. Review security advisories and CI; SHA pinning does not replace dependency monitoring.\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/terminal-matrix-worksheet/docs/USER_MANUAL.md:290:| `/image <path> [prompt]` | Ingest multi-modal image / screenshot into vision model context |\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/terminal-matrix-worksheet/docs/CLOUDFLARE_CONTEST.md:21:| Nexus collaboration service | Work-state contract, ref retrieval and validation | [`experiments/cloudflare-artifacts-vertical-slice/agent-collab-worker`](../experiments/cloudflare-artifacts-vertical-slice/agent-collab-worker/) |\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/terminal-matrix-worksheet/docs/CLOUDFLARE_CONTEST.md:25:| Shared fixture | Small TypeScript contract-change task | [`experiments/cloudflare-artifacts-vertical-slice/agent-collab-fixture`](../experiments/cloudflare-artifacts-vertical-slice/agent-collab-fixture/) |\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/terminal-matrix-worksheet/docs/CLOUDFLARE_CONTEST.md:31:The published tree includes `demo/` and `experiments/cloudflare-artifacts-vertical-slice/` manifests and lockfiles. The intended target is Ubuntu 24.04 or newer on x86-64, Node.js 22.18 or newer, npm, Git, `curl`, `sudo`, and `setpriv` (from `util-linux`). The `cf` CLI uses Node 22.18 or newer. The restricted validator additionally requires a root-owned `/usr/bin/node`, a working `nobody` identity (UID/GID 65534), and passwordless sudo for its fixed `chown`, `rm`, and `setpriv` operations. Do not run the generated-code validator on a shared or production host. A Cloudflare account must be allowed to create Artifacts repositories and deploy Workers. Real-agent mode also needs a Chat Completions-compatible inference endpoint that can produce the requested TypeScript changes. The captured recording used a private inference service; a judge must supply an endpoint and credentials they control.\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/terminal-matrix-worksheet/docs/CLOUDFLARE_CONTEST.md:40:   npm ci --prefix experiments/cloudflare-artifacts-vertical-slice\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/terminal-matrix-worksheet/docs/CLOUDFLARE_CONTEST.md:43:2. Create a unique Artifacts namespace and repository with the Cloudflare Artifacts REST API. The current Cloudflare API uses the account-level `/artifacts/namespaces` and namespace `/repos` routes; creating a repository returns its ID, remote URL, and initial repo token. Push a single baseline commit to `main` before running the demo. For API token scope and exact response fields, use [Cloudflare’s Artifacts REST API guide](https://developers.cloudflare.com/artifacts/api/rest-api/). The baseline commit is the parent from which this run publishes isolated refs.\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/terminal-matrix-worksheet/docs/CLOUDFLARE_CONTEST.md:45:4. Deploy the Worker with a private JSON secrets file containing `EXPERIMENT_AUTH`. Create the file outside the repository with mode `0600`, pass it to `cf deploy --secrets-file`, and delete it after the deployment. The Worker bearer in that file must match the root-owned `0400` file `/etc/nexus-cloudflare-broker/worker.bearer`; the Artifacts Git token belongs in `/etc/nexus-cloudflare-broker/artifacts-git.token`. Keep both tokens out of shell history, source, `.env.example`, and logs. Cloudflare’s `cf` CLI accepts JSON or `.env` secrets files and uploads secrets with the Worker version; see [the deploy reference](https://developers.cloudflare.com/cf/projects/).\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/terminal-matrix-worksheet/docs/CLOUDFLARE_CONTEST.md:48:   npm run typecheck --prefix experiments/cloudflare-artifacts-vertical-slice\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/terminal-matrix-worksheet/docs/CLOUDFLARE_CONTEST.md:49:   npm run deploy --prefix experiments/cloudflare-artifacts-vertical-slice -- --secrets-file /absolute/path/to/private-secrets.json\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/terminal-matrix-worksheet/docs/WP05_EGRESS_PROTECTION_EVIDENCE.md:144:- `make verify-reproducibility`: **Byte-identical artifacts verified**.\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/terminal-matrix-worksheet/docs/WP05_EGRESS_PROTECTION_EVIDENCE.md:145:- Pre-WP-05 closure audit artifacts verified byte-identical:\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/terminal-matrix-worksheet/demo/lib/restricted-code-executor.mjs:161:\t\t\t\treturn { ok: false, phase: \"test-artifact\", exitCode: null, identity };\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/terminal-matrix-worksheet/docs/WP05_EGRESS_PROTECTION_EVIDENCE.md:144:- `make verify-reproducibility`: **Byte-identical artifacts verified**.\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/terminal-matrix-worksheet/docs/WP05_EGRESS_PROTECTION_EVIDENCE.md:145:- Pre-WP-05 closure audit artifacts verified byte-identical:\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/terminal-matrix-worksheet/docs/ISSUE12_FINAL_ACCEPTANCE_MATRIX.md:92:| PERS-002 | 14: Persistence & Recovery | Nexus MUST NOT create uncontrolled, unredacted durable copies of credentials or classified sensitive data through session transcripts (`~/.nexus/sessions/`), flight logs (`.nexus/flights/`), audit logs, checkpoints, caches, or crash artifacts. | Serialization owners (`SessionManager`, `FlightRecorder`) MUST apply sensitive-data protection policies prior to writing records to disk. | Phase 2 §18 | `cli/src/session.ts:52-83`, `cli/src/core/state.ts:285-296`; direct synthetic disk reproduction confirmed plaintext in session JSON. Additional raw paths: `cli/src/checkpoint.ts:89-107`, `cli/src/knowledge.ts:68-84`; accepted CRED-003 evidence covers FlightRecorder/audit only. | PARTIALLY_DEMONSTRATED_BLOCKING | FlightRecorder and audit sinks now redact credentials, but SessionManager persists raw `messages` through `DurableStateManager` JSON serialization. A synthetic bearer fixture was read back from the durable session file in plaintext. Checkpoint snapshots and knowledge persistence also lack the demonstrated sanitizer boundary. This violates PERS-002's explicit durable-copy invariant. | Closure blocker |\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/terminal-matrix-worksheet/docs/ISSUE12_FINAL_ACCEPTANCE_MATRIX.md:110:| SCAN-004 | 18: Security Scanning | No known applicable HIGH or CRITICAL security vulnerability may survive in a supported release or deployment artifact. Documentation of a known High/Critical vulnerability does NOT constitute remediation; remediation, upgrade, or component removal is required. | Any release artifact containing an unresolved High or Critical CVE MUST be rejected at the release gate. | Phase 2 §22 | `scripts/security_gates.sh, scripts/audit_rust_deps.py`; cli/test/security_gates.test.ts, make test | DEMONSTRATED | None | Satisfied |\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/terminal-matrix-worksheet/docs/ISSUE12_FINAL_ACCEPTANCE_MATRIX.md:112:| REL-001 | 19: Release & SBOM | Nexus build and packaging infrastructure SHOULD preserve sufficient component identity, dependency definitions, and provenance metadata across dependency ecosystems so that built artifacts can be reliably associated with their source and dependency composition. Byte-identical deterministic builds are classified as a future maturity goal rather than an immediate architectural mandate. | Build configurations preserve explicit dependency specifications (e.g., lockfiles or equivalent manifests) to enable reproducible resolution across clean build environments. | Phase 2 §23 | `scripts/generate_sbom.sh, Makefile`; make verify-reproducibility | DEMONSTRATED | None | Satisfied |\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/terminal-matrix-worksheet/docs/ISSUE12_FINAL_ACCEPTANCE_MATRIX.md:113:| REL-002 | 19: Release & SBOM | Release artifacts MUST be assigned immutable, cryptographically verifiable identities and provenance records, including content digests (SHA-256) and source commit bindings. | Every distributable binary MUST be traceable back to an exact Git commit and clean build environment. | Phase 2 §23 | `scripts/generate_sbom.sh, Makefile`; make verify-reproducibility | DEMONSTRATED | None | Satisfied |\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/terminal-matrix-worksheet/docs/ISSUE12_FINAL_ACCEPTANCE_MATRIX.md:124:| SEGR-002 | 21: Intentional Segregation | Independent evaluators, verifiers, and external assessment tools MUST operate within the `INDEPENDENT` domain, receiving only the candidate artifact, specification, and declared provenance, without inheriting internal planner reasoning, conversation history, or persistent memory. | An independent benchmark evaluator MUST evaluate code without access to private agent scratchpads. | Phase 2 §25 | `core/tests/segregation_boundary.rs, cli/test/system_journey.test.ts`; cargo test, cli/test/system_journey.test.ts | DEMONSTRATED | None | Satisfied |\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/terminal-matrix-worksheet/docs/CLOUD_PROVIDERS.md:25:  - **Sign in with GitHub (unofficial)** — the VS Code Copilot device-code sign-in, for Copilot subscriptions.\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/terminal-matrix-worksheet/docs/CLOUD_PROVIDERS.md:31:**Unofficial sign-ins** reuse another vendor's OAuth client identity (Codex CLI, VS Code Copilot), as opencode and\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/terminal-matrix-worksheet/.github/dependabot.yml:28:    directory: /experiments/cloudflare-artifacts-vertical-slice\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/terminal-matrix-worksheet/.github/dependabot.yml:33:    directory: /experiments/cloudflare-artifacts-vertical-slice/agent-collab-fixture\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/terminal-matrix-worksheet/.github/dependabot.yml:38:    directory: /experiments/cloudflare-artifacts-vertical-slice/agent-collab-worker\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":586512409}},"started_at_ms":1792862666095,"completed_at_ms":1792862666682}}
