 containing an unresolved High or Critical CVE MUST be rejected at the release gate. | Phase 2 §22 | `scripts/security_gates.sh, scripts/audit_rust_deps.py`; cli/test/security_gates.test.ts, make test | DEMONSTRATED | None | Satisfied |\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/terminal-matrix-worksheet/docs/ISSUE12_FINAL_ACCEPTANCE_MATRIX.md:112:| REL-001 | 19: Release & SBOM | Nexus build and packaging infrastructure SHOULD preserve sufficient component identity, dependency definitions, and provenance metadata across dependency ecosystems so that built artifacts can be reliably associated with their source and dependency composition. Byte-identical deterministic builds are classified as a future maturity goal rather than an immediate architectural mandate. | Build configurations preserve explicit dependency specifications (e.g., lockfiles or equivalent manifests) to enable reproducible resolution across clean build environments. | Phase 2 §23 | `scripts/generate_sbom.sh, Makefile`; make verify-reproducibility | DEMONSTRATED | None | Satisfied |\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/terminal-matrix-worksheet/docs/ISSUE12_FINAL_ACCEPTANCE_MATRIX.md:113:| REL-002 | 19: Release & SBOM | Release artifacts MUST be assigned immutable, cryptographically verifiable identities and provenance records, including content digests (SHA-256) and source commit bindings. | Every distributable binary MUST be traceable back to an exact Git commit and clean build environment. | Phase 2 §23 | `scripts/generate_sbom.sh, Makefile`; make verify-reproducibility | DEMONSTRATED | None | Satisfied |\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/terminal-matrix-worksheet/docs/ISSUE12_FINAL_ACCEPTANCE_MATRIX.md:124:| SEGR-002 | 21: Intentional Segregation | Independent evaluators, verifiers, and external assessment tools MUST operate within the `INDEPENDENT` domain, receiving only the candidate artifact, specification, and declared provenance, without inheriting internal planner reasoning, conversation history, or persistent memory. | An independent benchmark evaluator MUST evaluate code without access to private agent scratchpads. | Phase 2 §25 | `core/tests/segregation_boundary.rs, cli/test/system_journey.test.ts`; cargo test, cli/test/system_journey.test.ts | DEMONSTRATED | None | Satisfied |\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/terminal-matrix-worksheet/docs/CLOUD_PROVIDERS.md:25:  - **Sign in with GitHub (unofficial)** — the VS Code Copilot device-code sign-in, for Copilot subscriptions.\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/terminal-matrix-worksheet/docs/CLOUD_PROVIDERS.md:31:**Unofficial sign-ins** reuse another vendor's OAuth client identity (Codex CLI, VS Code Copilot), as opencode and\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/terminal-matrix-worksheet/.github/dependabot.yml:28:    directory: /experiments/cloudflare-artifacts-vertical-slice\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/terminal-matrix-worksheet/.github/dependabot.yml:33:    directory: /experiments/cloudflare-artifacts-vertical-slice/agent-collab-fixture\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/terminal-matrix-worksheet/.github/dependabot.yml:38:    directory: /experiments/cloudflare-artifacts-vertical-slice/agent-collab-worker\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a16eee-fedb-7732-9ae7-8cbb47107b53","create_time":1792862667.6214094}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
