{"timestamp":"2026-10-24T17:29:35.708Z","ordinal":299080,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_01a16ef5-f6db-70d3-b7fa-b642f7b3ae70","author":"/root/plan05_readonly_review","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/plan05_readonly_review\nPayload:\n**ACCEPT** for exact head `3d5fd0912d91839de6e6c0fb528046ad1b09afff` against base `41b381ddac182b7f0c783b33df5f1355518f465b`. The two-file diff hash matches the previously reviewed `0b475a5f…1d901c`; no unstaged changes were present.\n\nThe verification now checks Git’s actual ignore result for each protected path and fails closed when a higher-priority repository rule defeats the local exclude. The added tests cover leading whitespace, later negation, and that conflict case. The supplied 8/8 focused-test result is not independently rerun; `git diff --check` is clean.\n\nMinor note: repeated calls under a persistent higher-priority conflict append another rule before failing. This does not bypass the fail-closed behavior, but avoiding duplicate appends would keep retries bounded."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a16eee-fedb-7732-9ae7-8cbb47107b53","create_time":1792862975.7076979}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"user_input_order":15284}}
