{"timestamp":"2026-10-24T17:31:37.195Z","ordinal":299183,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a16eee-fedb-7732-9ae7-8cbb47107b53","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016adceb7714b481a0a1b5ddf3d83cdf9e","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"That screenshot is the startup flow you meant. **It’s implemented in PR #186 and included in the RC4 source**: the prompt offers “Trust and continue,” “Continue without trusting,” and “Exit,” and shows whether it found `AGENTS.md` or another project instruction file.\n\nThe `nexus` installed here reports **v1.0.0-rc.3**, which predates that change. That explains why launching it doesn’t show the prompt. I haven’t changed the installed version or the shared checkout. RC4 is still a candidate; this does not change acceptance status.\n\n[PR #186](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/186) · [startup trust implementation](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/blob/main/cli/src/startup_trust.ts)\n\n"}],"phase":"final_answer","memory_citation":{"entries":[{"path":"MEMORY.md","lineStart":777,"lineEnd":789,"note":"release status must be rechecked against exact candidate and acceptance gates"}],"rolloutIds":["01a14262-6554-7912-9e3b-5f24d58b12c0"]}},"started_at_ms":1792863095121,"completed_at_ms":1792863097195}}
