{"timestamp":"2026-10-24T17:40:11.329Z","ordinal":299541,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a16ef8-1479-7bc1-b23e-862a144e9535","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-c74b0bda-b2e4-4208-a239-68330f1b2e4a","process_id":"61109","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","sed -n '1,320p' eval/infra.mjs\nsed -n '1,260p' eval/README.md\nsed -n '1,240p' docs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '1,320p' eval/infra.mjs","name":"infra.mjs","path":"eval/infra.mjs"},{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '1,260p' eval/README.md","name":"README.md","path":"eval/README.md"},{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '1,240p' docs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md","name":"SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md","path":"docs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"#!/usr/bin/env node\n// Marks runs that failed on infrastructure (the agent never reached the model), so they are rerun rather than scored as\n// task failures. Signatures are each agent's own connection-failure message; Nexus reports INFERENCE_FAILED, or records\n// in turn.providerRecovery how long it waited for an unavailable provider (over a minute: the run measured the outage).\n// usage: eval/infra.mjs <out-dir-of-one-config>   → prints \"task run\" per infrastructure failure\nimport fs from \"node:fs\";\nimport path from \"node:path\";\n\nconst SIGNATURES = {\n  goose: /Network error: Could not connect to/,\n  opencode: /Cannot connect to API: Unable to connect/,\n  aider: /litellm\\.(InternalServerError|APIConnectionError).*Connection\\s+error/s,\n  nexus: null,\n};\n/** Total time a Nexus run waited for an unavailable provider, from its JSON report. */\nfunction recoveryWaitMs(stdout) {\n  try {\n    const report = JSON.parse(stdout.slice(stdout.indexOf(\"{\"), stdout.lastIndexOf(\"}\") + 1));\n    return (report.turn?.providerRecovery ?? []).reduce((sum, r) => sum + (r.waitedMs ?? 0), 0);\n  } catch {\n    return 0;\n  }\n}\n\nconst dir = process.argv[2];\nfor (const line of fs.readFileSync(path.join(dir, \"results.jsonl\"), \"utf8\").split(\"\\n\").filter(Boolean)) {\n  const r = JSON.parse(line);\n  const logs = path.join(dir, r.logs ?? \"\");\n  const text = [\"agent.stdout.json\", \"agent.stderr.log\"].map((f) => (fs.existsSync(path.join(logs, f)) ? fs.readFileSync(path.join(logs, f), \"utf8\") : \"\")).join(\"\\n\");\n  const sig = SIGNATURES[r.agent];\n  const infra = r.error || (r.agent === \"nexus\" ? r.turn?.reason === \"INFERENCE_FAILED\" || !r.turn || recoveryWaitMs(fs.existsSync(path.join(logs, \"agent.stdout.json\")) ? fs.readFileSync(path.join(logs, \"agent.stdout.json\"), \"utf8\") : \"\") > 60_000 : sig?.test(text) && !r.hiddenPass);\n  if (infra) console.log(`${r.task} ${r.run}`);\n}\n# Evaluation harness (qualification assessment §9)\n\n`run.mjs` runs tasks against one agent configuration and appends a JSON line per run; `score.mjs` reports the scores\nseparately (never combined), per task and configuration, with 95 % Wilson intervals.\n\n```bash\nnode eval/run.mjs --config eval/configs/gateway-engineering-deep.json --out eval/out/<label> [--only id,id] [--runs N]\nnode eval/score.mjs eval/out/<label>/results.jsonl          # markdown table; --json for machine output\n```\n\nEach run: a fresh workspace (the task's `fixture`, or its `repo.url` at `repo.commit`, cached in `eval/.cache`), a fresh\n`HOME`, the agent with the task's budgets and a wall-clock timeout, then the task's **hidden** tests (copied in only\nafter the agent has stopped) and its `regression` command. `manifest.json` records the harness build (commit, dirty),\nthe configuration (secrets in `env` masked), host and Node version; per-run logs go to `logs/<task>-<run>/`.\n\n## Task format (`eval/tasks/<id>/task.json`)\n\n| Field | Meaning |\n|---|---|\n| `id`, `tier` | T1 smoke (scripted model, CI), T2 standard, T3 long-task, T4 fault-injected |\n| `fixture` or `repo` | a directory in the task, or `{ \"url\", \"commit\" }` (external repositories at pinned commits) |\n| `setup` | shell commands run in the workspace before the agent (e.g. `npm ci`) |\n| `objective` | the operator text given to the agent |\n| `steps`, `minutes` | budgets (defaults from the configuration: 300 steps, 120 min) |\n| `hidden` | `{ dir, into, command, timeoutSec }` — tests the agent never sees; pass = artifact correct |\n| `regression` | `{ command }` — the repository's own suite after the run |\n\n## Scores\n\ncompletion claimed · artifact correct (hidden tests) · false VERIFIED (VERIFIED while hidden tests fail) · regressions\nintroduced · timed out / harness errors · wall time, steps, tokens (median). Context qualifier (`contextNotRetained`) is\nrecorded per run.\n\n## Pre-registered thresholds (from the assessment, fixed before any live run)\n\n- false VERIFIED = 0 across all runs;\n- T2 hidden-test pass rate (pooled over all T2 runs of a configuration, point estimate, 95 % intervals reported) ≥ the\n  best matched peer on the same local model **minus 10 percentage points**; and no task where that peer passes ≥ 4/5\n  runs while Nexus passes ≤ 1/5. (Fixed 2026-10-13, before the first scored run. Rationale: at ~50 runs per\n  configuration the 95 % interval half-width near 50 % is ~13 points, so a tighter margin is not distinguishable from\n  noise and a looser one would accept a clear loss; the per-task guard stops a pooled rate hiding a task class Nexus\n  cannot do.) The 6-task pilot is directional only; qualification needs the full task set;\n- T3: false-absence claims = 0 and steering constraints honoured in ≥ 95 % of runs;\n- T4: truthful bounded outcome in 100 % of fault runs;\n- ≥ 5 runs per task-configuration, per-task results with 95 % intervals.\n\n## Status\n\n| Part | State |\n|---|---|\n| Runner, scorer, manifest, per-run logs | done |\n| T1 self-test (`selftest-add`, scripted model, in `make test` via `cli/test/eval_harness.test.ts`) | done |\n| Nexus adapter | done |\n| Peer adapters (OpenCode, Goose, Aider, Codex) | not started |\n| T2/T3 task set (pilot 12, external repos, hidden tests) | not started |\n| T3 fact-sheet scorer (absence claims) and steering checks | not started |\n| T4 fault injector | not started |\n| Live runs | blocked on inference hours, cloud budget and peer installs (operator decision) |\n\n## Pilot 2026-10-13 (4 h appliance window)\n\nConfigurations `configs/pilot-*.json`: Nexus, Aider 0.86.2, OpenCode 1.18.35, Goose 1.27.2, all on\n`engineering/lead` (Qwen3.6-35B-A3B Q4_K_M, llama.cpp b11347) through the appliance gateway, 64k context. Six T2\nfixture tasks (`t2-*`; each hidden test checked to fail on the fixture and pass on a reference fix kept outside the\nrepo). Budgets 60 steps / 20 min per task (Nexus steps; others by wall clock). The four agents run concurrently on the\nsame worker, so wall times include queueing.\n\nDeviations from §9, recorded before the run: fixture tasks rather than external repositories at pinned commits; T2\nonly (no T3/T4 — the window is too short); Codex CLI excluded (the gateway does not serve `/v1/responses`); Aider runs\none `--message` exchange with `--yes-always` (its non-interactive mode); no cloud configuration (operator decision);\nruns per task as many as the window allows, run-major, target 5.\n# SPEC-10: v1 qualification and task-quality evaluation\n\n| | |\n|---|---|\n| Status | Ready. Protocol and thresholds fixed by [DEC-05](../DECISIONS.md#dec-05-v1-evaluation-protocol-and-thresholds); task authorship needs owner action X2. |\n| Release class | **BLOCKER** for any v1 maturity claim: held-out matched evaluation, fault-injection qualification, standalone live qualification, scoring integrity. RELEASE-REQUIRED: T3 long tasks, a T4 smoke test in CI, a PTY terminal matrix. |\n| Requirements | REQ-QUAL-101, REQ-QUAL-102, REQ-QUAL-103, REQ-QUAL-104, REQ-QUAL-105, REQ-QUAL-106, REQ-QUAL-107, REQ-QUAL-108 |\n| Findings | EVL-001, EVL-002, EVL-003, EVL-004, EVL-005, HIST-08, PRV G1/G2, TUI gaps (kitty/real terminals), VER-07 |\n| Plan | [PLAN-10](../plans/PLAN-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md) |\n| Acceptance | ACCEPTANCE.md §4–§7 |\n\n## 1. Problem\n\nThe only scored task-quality evidence is a 6-task, in-repo T2 fixture pilot (`docs/reviews/evidence/eval_pilot_2026-10-13/RESULT.md`), and its own write-up says it was used for tuning: \"it does not qualify Nexus\".\n\n| Run | Result | Peer |\n|---|---|---|\n| First pilot | NOT QUALIFIED (2 false VERIFIED) | — |\n| Rerun on ed17e99 | 26/30, 0 false VERIFIED | Goose 80% |\n\nBoth results are on tuned tasks. The following are missing entirely:\n\n- a held-out task set;\n- T3 long tasks;\n- T4 fault injection;\n- a run on the release commit (db1ca55 was never evaluated).\n\nScoring integrity issues:\n\n- **EVL-002.** Any Nexus run without a parsed turn (for example a crash) is rerun as \"infrastructure\". Peers are rerun only on a connection-error signature. This biases results in Nexus's favour and hides the crash rate.\n- **EVL-003.** Hidden tests are readable by the agent, and contaminated runs still count in pooled rates.\n- **EVL-004.** Model identity is recorded as an alias only. No sampling settings are recorded. The full operator env is inherited.\n- **EVL-005.** Recovery, intervention and cost metrics are missing.\n\n`nexus eval` (the SWE-bench-style command) scores the repo's last commit instead of the agent's change, and runs `git checkout` in the operator's workspace (VER-07). It must not be used for any published number.\n\nStandalone live inference evidence is absent (HIST-08; SPEC-05). Real-terminal coverage (kitty, tmux, VS Code, xterm) is not established. pyte emulation cannot answer kitty keyboard queries (D §6).\n\n## 2. Requirements\n\n1. **REQ-QUAL-101. Held-out matched evaluation.**\n   - At least 40 tasks (DEC-05).\n   - At least 50% come from external repositories at pinned commits, covering JS/TS, Python, Rust and Go.\n   - The held-out half is authored by someone other than the implementer and stored outside the repo until the freeze. Its manifest of sha256 hashes is committed before the RC freeze.\n   - The pilot tasks and the routing engx tasks are the *development* set only.\n2. **REQ-QUAL-102. Matched conditions.** Each run records:\n   - a clean RC commit;\n   - a model fingerprint: weights sha256, server kind and build, and sampling (temperature 0, or a fixed seed where supported);\n   - identical step and minute budgets;\n   - an allow-listed environment;\n   - serial execution, or recorded queueing.\n\n   A run with any field missing is invalid.\n3. **REQ-QUAL-103. Repetitions and peers.** At least 5 runs per (task, config). Matched peers are Goose and OpenCode on the same model (DEC-05).\n4. **REQ-QUAL-104. Metrics, reported separately.**\n   - hidden-test correctness;\n   - completion claimed;\n   - **false VERIFIED** (hard gate = 0);\n   - regressions (repo suite, plus a pre/post diff of previously passing tests);\n   - crash rate and timeout rate;\n   - bounded-failure truthfulness;\n   - operator interventions (= 0 in `run` mode);\n   - tokens and wall time per correct task.\n5. **REQ-QUAL-105. T4 fault injection.** At least 8 fault classes × 5 runs:\n   1. gateway refuses connections mid-turn;\n   2. 5xx/overloaded;\n   3. stream cut mid-tool-call;\n   4. output-limit truncation;\n   5. hanging test command;\n   6. workspace disk full;\n   7. context overflow at 32k;\n   8. malformed tool-call JSON;\n   9. SIGTERM mid-turn, then resume.\n\n   Gate (proposal): 100% truthful outcome, 0 false VERIFIED, 0 hangs beyond budget + 5 minutes.\n6. **REQ-QUAL-106. Scoring integrity.**\n   - Infrastructure reruns are symmetric and evidence-based: the endpoint was unreachable before the first model call.\n   - Contaminated runs are excluded from pooled rates.\n   - Hidden tests are not readable by the agent uid.\n   - The scorer logs every replacement.\n   - `nexus eval` is labelled experimental and excluded from claims (DEC-07).\n7. **REQ-QUAL-107. Standalone and provider matrix.** The live standalone set (a T2 subset of ≥ 10 tasks plus a T4 subset) is run through the gateway-stripping proxy in its plain profile and its emulated-server profiles (DEC-16). `providers verify` is run live for each provider listed as supported (DEC-06). Receipts are archived.\n8. **REQ-QUAL-108. Terminal matrix.** PTY scripted runs in CI (existing `tui_*_e2e`, plus the new ACC-SAFE and ACC-PROC scripts). A manual matrix covers {xterm, kitty, tmux, VS Code terminal, GNOME Terminal} × {80x24, 40x14, 200x60}, checking: approval safety, paste, resize, cancel, narrow hints and NO_COLOR. Screenshots are archived.\n9. **REQ-QUAL-109 (RELEASE-REQUIRED).** T3 long tasks: at least 8 tasks × 5 runs, each over 60 steps and with at least 2 compactions. Gates: false-absence = 0 and steering honoured ≥ 95% (eval/README thresholds).\n10. **REQ-QUAL-110 (RELEASE-REQUIRED).** A T4 smoke (scripted model, 2 fault cases) and the T1 self-test run in `make test`.\n\n## 3. Design\n\n- **Harness fixes** in `eval/infra.mjs:31` and `eval/score.mjs:16-21,48-84`:\n  - classify a run as infrastructure only when `first_model_request_at` is missing **and** an endpoint-unreachable signature is present, for every agent;\n  - add `replaced_by` logging;\n  - exclude `contaminated: true` runs from pooled rates;\n  - add the new metric columns.\n- **Hidden-test isolation.** Hidden tests live in a directory owned by a separate `nexus-eval` uid with mode 0700, and are copied into the workspace after the agent exits (`run.mjs:57-59,178`).\n- **Fingerprint.** `eval/fingerprint.mjs` queries `/v1/models` and the server-specific endpoints (SPEC-05 `ServerKind`) and records the weights hash supplied in the config. A run is refused without it.\n- **Fault injector.** `eval/faults/proxy.mjs` is an HTTP proxy in front of the model server that injects faults 1–4 and 7–8 by schedule. Faults 5, 6 and 9 are injected by the task fixture or the runner.\n- **Task authoring.** Use a `task.json` schema with `{repo, commit, prompt, hidden_tests, fail_to_pass, pass_to_pass, class, difficulty}`. Calibrate so that no task is solved 5/5 by every agent (EVL G6).\n\n## 4. Procedure and evidence\n\n- See [ACCEPTANCE.md](../ACCEPTANCE.md) §4–§7 for the qualification runbook, environments and pass/fail table.\n- All runs are archived under `docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/<rc>/`, with the manifest, raw JSONL, the scorer output and SHA256SUMS.\n\n## 5. Dependencies\n\n- SPEC-01 (`run` mode needs an explicit `--yes`).\n- SPEC-02 (cancel and SIGTERM semantics).\n- SPEC-04 (resume).\n- SPEC-05 (server kind, receipts).\n- DEC-05, DEC-06 and DEC-07 (all resolved). Owner actions X2, X3 and X4 are needed.\n- Hardware: the homelab inference host, reached through its gateway only, is the sole inference path (DEC-16). Every agent's runs are serial on it.\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":45713}},"started_at_ms":1792863611328,"completed_at_ms":1792863611329}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-24T17:40:12.318Z","ordinal":299542,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a16eff-ad9d-7882-8aad-58ee005b1c4a","call_id":"call_a17a0b1acabd47999c59076f500a2b62","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 2.1 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"#!/usr/bin/env node\n// Marks runs that failed on infrastructure (the agent never reached the model), so they are rerun rather than scored as\n// task failures. Signatures are each agent's own connection-failure message; Nexus reports INFERENCE_FAILED, or records\n// in turn.providerRecovery how long it waited for an unavailable provider (over a minute: the run measured the outage).\n// usage: eval/infra.mjs <out-dir-of-one-config>   → prints \"task run\" per infrastructure failure\nimport fs from \"node:fs\";\nimport path from \"node:path\";\n\nconst SIGNATURES = {\n  goose: /Network error: Could not connect to/,\n  opencode: /Cannot connect to API: Unable to connect/,\n  aider: /litellm\\.(InternalServerError|APIConnectionError).*Connection\\s+error/s,\n  nexus: null,\n};\n/** Total time a Nexus run waited for an unavailable provider, from its JSON report. */\nfunction recoveryWaitMs(stdout) {\n  try {\n    const report = JSON.parse(stdout.slice(stdout.indexOf(\"{\"), stdout.lastIndexOf(\"}\") + 1));\n    return (report.turn?.providerRecovery ?? []).reduce((sum, r) => sum + (r.waitedMs ?? 0), 0);\n  } catch {\n    return 0;\n  }\n}\n\nconst dir = process.argv[2];\nfor (const line of fs.readFileSync(path.join(dir, \"results.jsonl\"), \"utf8\").split(\"\\n\").filter(Boolean)) {\n  const r = JSON.parse(line);\n  const logs = path.join(dir, r.logs ?? \"\");\n  const text = [\"agent.stdout.json\", \"agent.stderr.log\"].map((f) => (fs.existsSync(path.join(logs, f)) ? fs.readFileSync(path.join(logs, f), \"utf8\") : \"\")).join(\"\\n\");\n  const sig = SIGNATURES[r.agent];\n  const infra = r.error || (r.agent === \"nexus\" ? r.turn?.reason === \"INFERENCE_FAILED\" || !r.turn || recoveryWaitMs(fs.existsSync(path.join(logs, \"agent.stdout.json\")) ? fs.readFileSync(path.join(logs, \"agent.stdout.json\"), \"utf8\") : \"\") > 60_000 : sig?.test(text) && !r.hiddenPass);\n  if (infra) console.log(`${r.task} ${r.run}`);\n}\n# Evaluation harness (qualification assessment §9)\n\n`run.mjs` runs tasks against one agent configuration and appends a JSON line per run; `score.mjs` reports the scores\nseparately (never combined), per task and configuration, with 95 % Wilson intervals.\n\n```bash\nnode eval/run.mjs --config eval/configs/gateway-engineering-deep.json --out eval/out/<label> [--only id,id] [--runs N]\nnode eval/score.mjs eval/out/<label>/results.jsonl          # markdown table; --json for machine output\n```\n\nEach run: a fresh workspace (the task's `fixture`, or its `repo.url` at `repo.commit`, cached in `eval/.cache`), a fresh\n`HOME`, the agent with the task's budgets and a wall-clock timeout, then the task's **hidden** tests (copied in only\nafter the agent has stopped) and its `regression` command. `manifest.json` records the harness build (commit, dirty),\nthe configuration (secrets in `env` masked), host and Node version; per-run logs go to `logs/<task>-<run>/`.\n\n## Task format (`eval/tasks/<id>/task.json`)\n\n| Field | Meaning |\n|---|---|\n| `id`, `tier` | T1 smoke (scripted model, CI), T2 standard, T3 long-task, T4 fault-injected |\n| `fixture` or `repo` | a directory in the task, or `{ \"url\", \"commit\" }` (external repositories at pinned commits) |\n| `setup` | shell commands run in the workspace before the agent (e.g. `npm ci`) |\n| `objective` | the operator text given to the agent |\n| `steps`, `minutes` | budgets (defaults from the configuration: 300 steps, 120 min) |\n| `hidden` | `{ dir, into, command, timeoutSec }` — tests the agent never sees; pass = artifact correct |\n| `regression` | `{ command }` — the repository's own suite after the run |\n\n## Scores\n\ncompletion claimed · artifact correct (hidden tests) · false VERIFIED (VERIFIED while hidden tests fail) · regressions\nintroduced · timed out / harness errors · wall time, steps, tokens (median). Context qualifier (`contextNotRetained`) is\nrecorded per run.\n\n## Pre-registered thresholds (from the assessment, fixed before any live run)\n\n- false VERIFIED = 0 across all runs;\n- T2 hidden-test pass rate (pooled over all T2 runs of a configuration, point estimate, 95 % intervals reported) ≥ the\n  best matched peer on the same local model **minus 10 percentage points**; and no task where that peer passes ≥ 4/5\n  runs while Nexus passes ≤ 1/5. (Fixed 2026-10-13, before the first scored run. Rationale: at ~50 runs per\n  configuration the 95 % interval half-width near 50 % is ~13 points, so a tighter margin is not distinguishable from\n  noise and a looser one would accept a clear loss; the per-task guard stops a pooled rate hiding a task class Nexus\n  cannot do.) The 6-task pilot is directional only; qualification needs the full task set;\n- T3: false-absence claims = 0 and steering constraints honoured in ≥ 95 % of runs;\n- T4: truthful bounded outcome in 100 % of fault runs;\n- ≥ 5 runs per task-configuration, per-task results with 95 % intervals.\n\n## Status\n\n| Part | State |\n|---|---|\n| Runner, scorer, manifest, per-run logs | done |\n| T1 self-test (`selftest-add`, scripted model, in `make test` via `cli/test/eval_harness.test.ts`) | done |\n| Nexus adapter | done |\n| Peer adapters (OpenCode, Goose, Aider, Codex) | not started |\n| T2/T3 task set (pilot 12, external repos, hidden tests) | not started |\n| T3 fact-sheet scorer (absence claims) and steering checks | not started |\n| T4 fault injector | not started |\n| Live runs | blocked on inference hours, cloud budget and peer installs (operator decision) |\n\n## Pilot 2026-10-13 (4 h appliance window)\n\nConfigurations `configs/pilot-*.json`: Nexus, Aider 0.86.2, OpenCode 1.18.35, Goose 1.27.2, all on\n`engineering/lead` (Qwen3.6-35B-A3B Q4_K_M, llama.cpp b11347) through the appliance gateway, 64k context. Six T2\nfixture tasks (`t2-*`; each hidden test checked to fail on the fixture and pass on a reference fix kept outside the\nrepo). Budgets 60 steps / 20 min per task (Nexus steps; others by wall clock). The four agents run concurrently on the\nsame worker, so wall times include queueing.\n\nDeviations from §9, recorded before the run: fixture tasks rather than external repositories at pinned commits; T2\nonly (no T3/T4 — the window is too short); Codex CLI excluded (the gateway does not serve `/v1/responses`); Aider runs\none `--message` exchange with `--yes-always` (its non-interactive mode); no cloud configuration (operator decision);\nruns per task as many as the window allows, run-major, target 5.\n# SPEC-10: v1 qualification and task-quality evaluation\n\n| | |\n|---|---|\n| Status | Ready. Protocol and thresholds fixed by [DEC-05](../DECISIONS.md#dec-05-v1-evaluation-protocol-and-thresholds); task authorship needs owner action X2. |\n| Release class | **BLOCKER** for any v1 maturity claim: held-out matched evaluation, fault-injection qualification, standalone live qualification, scoring integrity. RELEASE-REQUIRED: T3 long tasks, a T4 smoke test in CI, a PTY terminal matrix. |\n| Requirements | REQ-QUAL-101, REQ-QUAL-102, REQ-QUAL-103, REQ-QUAL-104, REQ-QUAL-105, REQ-QUAL-106, REQ-QUAL-107, REQ-QUAL-108 |\n| Findings | EVL-001, EVL-002, EVL-003, EVL-004, EVL-005, HIST-08, PRV G1/G2, TUI gaps (kitty/real terminals), VER-07 |\n| Plan | [PLAN-10](../plans/PLAN-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md) |\n| Acceptance | ACCEPTANCE.md §4–§7 |\n\n## 1. Problem\n\nThe only scored task-quality evidence is a 6-task, in-repo T2 fixture pilot (`docs/reviews/evidence/eval_pilot_2026-10-13/RESULT.md`), and its own write-up says it was used for tuning: \"it does not qualify Nexus\".\n\n| Run | Result | Peer |\n|---|---|---|\n| First pilot | NOT QUALIFIED (2 false VERIFIED) | — |\n| Rerun on ed17e99 | 26/30, 0 false VERIFIED | Goose 80% |\n\nBoth results are on tuned tasks. The following are missing entirely:\n\n- a held-out task set;\n- T3 long tasks;\n- T4 fault injection;\n- a run on the release commit (db1ca55 was never evaluated).\n\nScoring integrity issues:\n\n- **EVL-002.** Any Nexus run without a parsed turn (for example a crash) is rerun as \"infrastructure\". Peers are rerun only on a connection-error signature. This biases results in Nexus's favour and hides the crash rate.\n- **EVL-003.** Hidden tests are readable by the agent, and contaminated runs still count in pooled rates.\n- **EVL-004.** Model identity is recorded as an alias only. No sampling settings are recorded. The full operator env is inherited.\n- **EVL-005.** Recovery, intervention and cost metrics are missing.\n\n`nexus eval` (the SWE-bench-style command) scores the repo's last commit instead of the agent's change, and runs `git checkout` in the operator's workspace (VER-07). It must not be used for any published number.\n\nStandalone live inference evidence is absent (HIST-08; SPEC-05). Real-terminal coverage (kitty, tmux, VS Code, xterm) is not established. pyte emulation cannot answer kitty keyboard queries (D §6).\n\n## 2. Requirements\n\n1. **REQ-QUAL-101. Held-out matched evaluation.**\n   - At least 40 tasks (DEC-05).\n   - At least 50% come from external repositories at pinned commits, covering JS/TS, Python, Rust and Go.\n   - The held-out half is authored by someone other than the implementer and stored outside the repo until the freeze. Its manifest of sha256 hashes is committed before the RC freeze.\n   - The pilot tasks and the routing engx tasks are the *development* set only.\n2. **REQ-QUAL-102. Matched conditions.** Each run records:\n   - a clean RC commit;\n   - a model fingerprint: weights sha256, server kind and build, and sampling (temperature 0, or a fixed seed where supported);\n   - identical step and minute budgets;\n   - an allow-listed environment;\n   - serial execution, or recorded queueing.\n\n   A run with any field missing is invalid.\n3. **REQ-QUAL-103. Repetitions and peers.** At least 5 runs per (task, config). Matched peers are Goose and OpenCode on the same model (DEC-05).\n4. **REQ-QUAL-104. Metrics, reported separately.**\n   - hidden-test correctness;\n   - completion claimed;\n   - **false VERIFIED** (hard gate = 0);\n   - regressions (repo suite, plus a pre/post diff of previously passing tests);\n   - crash rate and timeout rate;\n   - bounded-failure truthfulness;\n   - operator interventions (= 0 in `run` mode);\n   - tokens and wall time per correct task.\n5. **REQ-QUAL-105. T4 fault injection.** At least 8 fault classes × 5 runs:\n   1. gateway refuses connections mid-turn;\n   2. 5xx/overloaded;\n   3. stream cut mid-tool-call;\n   4. output-limit truncation;\n   5. hanging test command;\n   6. workspace disk full;\n   7. context overflow at 32k;\n   8. malformed tool-call JSON;\n   9. SIGTERM mid-turn, then resume.\n\n   Gate (proposal): 100% truthful outcome, 0 false VERIFIED, 0 hangs beyond budget + 5 minutes.\n6. **REQ-QUAL-106. Scoring integrity.**\n   - Infrastructure reruns are symmetric and evidence-based: the endpoint was unreachable before the first model call.\n   - Contaminated runs are excluded from pooled rates.\n   - Hidden tests are not readable by the agent uid.\n   - The scorer logs every replacement.\n   - `nexus eval` is labelled experimental and excluded from claims (DEC-07).\n7. **REQ-QUAL-107. Standalone and provider matrix.** The live standalone set (a T2 subset of ≥ 10 tasks plus a T4 subset) is run through the gateway-stripping proxy in its plain profile and its emulated-server profiles (DEC-16). `providers verify` is run live for each provider listed as supported (DEC-06). Receipts are archived.\n8. **REQ-QUAL-108. Terminal matrix.** PTY scripted runs in CI (existing `tui_*_e2e`, plus the new ACC-SAFE and ACC-PROC scripts). A manual matrix covers {xterm, kitty, tmux, VS Code terminal, GNOME Terminal} × {80x24, 40x14, 200x60}, checking: approval safety, paste, resize, cancel, narrow hints and NO_COLOR. Screenshots are archived.\n9. **REQ-QUAL-109 (RELEASE-REQUIRED).** T3 long tasks: at least 8 tasks × 5 runs, each over 60 steps and with at least 2 compactions. Gates: false-absence = 0 and steering honoured ≥ 95% (eval/README thresholds).\n10. **REQ-QUAL-110 (RELEASE-REQUIRED).** A T4 smoke (scripted model, 2 fault cases) and the T1 self-test run in `make test`.\n\n## 3. Design\n\n- **Harness fixes** in `eval/infra.mjs:31` and `eval/score.mjs:16-21,48-84`:\n  - classify a run as infrastructure only when `first_model_request_at` is missing **and** an endpoint-unreachable signature is present, for every agent;\n  - add `replaced_by` logging;\n  - exclude `contaminated: true` runs from pooled rates;\n  - add the new metric columns.\n- **Hidden-test isolation.** Hidden tests live in a directory owned by a separate `nexus-eval` uid with mode 0700, and are copied into the workspace after the agent exits (`run.mjs:57-59,178`).\n- **Fingerprint.** `eval/fingerprint.mjs` queries `/v1/models` and the server-specific endpoints (SPEC-05 `ServerKind`) and records the weights hash supplied in the config. A run is refused without it.\n- **Fault injector.** `eval/faults/proxy.mjs` is an HTTP proxy in front of the model server that injects faults 1–4 and 7–8 by schedule. Faults 5, 6 and 9 are injected by the task fixture or the runner.\n- **Task authoring.** Use a `task.json` schema with `{repo, commit, prompt, hidden_tests, fail_to_pass, pass_to_pass, class, difficulty}`. Calibrate so that no task is solved 5/5 by every agent (EVL G6).\n\n## 4. Procedure and evidence\n\n- See [ACCEPTANCE.md](../ACCEPTANCE.md) §4–§7 for the qualification runbook, environments and pass/fail table.\n- All runs are archived under `docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/<rc>/`, with the manifest, raw JSONL, the scorer output and SHA256SUMS.\n\n## 5. Dependencies\n\n- SPEC-01 (`run` mode needs an explicit `--yes`).\n- SPEC-02 (cancel and SIGTERM semantics).\n- SPEC-04 (resume).\n- SPEC-05 (server kind, receipts).\n- DEC-05, DEC-06 and DEC-07 (all resolved). Owner actions X2, X3 and X4 are needed.\n- Hardware: the homelab inference host, reached through its gateway only, is the sole inference path (DEC-16). Every agent's runs are serial on it.\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a16ef8-1479-7bc1-b23e-862a144e9535","create_time":1792863612.3179355}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
