{"timestamp":"2026-10-24T17:42:57.052Z","ordinal":299638,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_01a16f02-311c-77e2-adb3-e9caf254eba9","author":"/root/context_rc_gate_audit","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/context_rc_gate_audit\nPayload:\n**Read-only audit at `origin/main@41b381ddac182b7f0c783b33df5f1355518f465b`.** No evaluator qualification or tests were run, and no held-out payloads or private validators were read. The worktree was already dirty; I left it untouched.\n\n**Containment controls:** Source and synthetic fixtures cover all requested limits. `eval/resources.mjs:15-75, 78-105` validates the resource profile, requires a dedicated size-capped tmpfs and delegated systemd scope, then reads back a successful containment probe. `eval/cgroup_supervisor.mjs:25-45` applies and verifies CPU, memory, swap, and pids limits before starting the payload. `eval/run.mjs:107-113, 176-181, 322-325, 544-558, 624-650` requires these resources for qualification and passes them to setup, candidate, and check execution. The resource wrapper permits an uncontained path when `resources` is absent (`eval/resources.mjs:111-114`), but qualification preflight rejects that configuration.\n\n`cli/test/eval_integrity.test.ts:580-652` contains production-helper fixtures for memory, pids, tmpfs storage, CPU throttling, timeouts, and processes escaping their session. The host preflight evidence from `6383623` reports 10/10 synthetic checks passed, including applied limits and cleanup; evaluator source files have not changed between that commit and this main revision. This is host-preflight evidence, not held-out qualification.\n\n**Process cleanup fails closed in source:** `eval/cgroup_supervisor.mjs:61-90` kills remaining cgroup processes and reports failure unless the cgroup becomes empty. `eval/resources.mjs:143-148` treats a missing report, supervisor error, or unclean cgroup as a containment problem. The synthetic fixtures at `eval_integrity.test.ts:638-648` exercise an escaped process.\n\n**Hidden-test boundary:** Qualification rejects legacy in-process hidden validators (`eval/validate.mjs:39-48`; `eval/run.mjs:641-643`). The black-box oracle keeps expected values in the evaluator and executes the candidate entrypoint in a separate sandbox (`eval/oracle.mjs:64-115, 125-150`). The synthetic oracle fixture at `eval_integrity.test.ts:266-328` probes access and output leakage. Legacy hardening is explicitly limited to pilot use in `eval/README.md:213-219`.\n\n**Git and filesystem isolation:** `eval/workspace.mjs:13-20, 23-37` builds a fresh workspace from the pinned commit and rejects alternates, remotes, extra refs/reflog commits, and unreachable objects. `eval/isolate.mjs:92-115, 139-215, 266-311` verifies sandbox mount sources against protected paths, creates isolated user/PID/network namespaces, and mounts the workspace, isolated home, proxy socket, and approved runtime paths. `eval/run.mjs:33-47` includes task and configured custody paths in the protected set for qualification. The synthetic fixture at `eval_integrity.test.ts:654-792` combines the production workspace stager with `agentSandboxArgv`, checks future solution and dangling Git objects, and probes synthetic external-store paths. This is source inspection of a fixture; it was not executed in this audit.\n\n**Fixture composition gap:** The test exercises workspace staging plus candidate sandbox together, while the resource stress test exercises `runIsolated`/`spawnContained`. I did not find one fixture that composes `agentSandboxArgv` with `spawnContained` and asserts both the candidate boundary and cgroup limits in the same run. Source wiring does pass the candidate’s wrapped sandbox to `spawnContained` (`eval/run.mjs:544-558`), so this is an additional integration-proof gap, not a confirmed production defect.\n\n**Claims and next safe slice:** The current claim ledger shows the host-preflight claim released and candidate-integrity work archived as merged. I found no active claim on the evaluator files; PR #200 and its active Git-exclusion claim concern separate `git_exclude` paths. The smallest useful follow-up is a **test-only** synthetic regression in `cli/test/eval_integrity.test.ts` that runs `agentSandboxArgv` through `spawnContained` with a pinned synthetic repo, future-object canary, and external private-file canary, then verifies denied reads and clean cgroup termination. Claim that test file and SUITE before implementing or running it."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a16ef8-1479-7bc1-b23e-862a144e9535","create_time":1792863777.0523114}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"user_input_order":15304}}
