connector_id":"connector_76869538009648d5b282a4bb21c3d157","first_turn_id":"01a156f3-6561-78e2-9f56-cd2b1db5d742","server_name":"codex_apps","tool_name":"github.list_pr_changed_filenames"},{"connector_id":"connector_76869538009648d5b282a4bb21c3d157","first_turn_id":"01a156f3-6561-78e2-9f56-cd2b1db5d742","server_name":"codex_apps","tool_name":"github.get_pr_diff"},{"connector_id":"connector_76869538009648d5b282a4bb21c3d157","first_turn_id":"01a156f3-6561-78e2-9f56-cd2b1db5d742","server_name":"codex_apps","tool_name":"github.fetch_file"},{"connector_id":"connector_76869538009648d5b282a4bb21c3d157","first_turn_id":"01a156f3-6561-78e2-9f56-cd2b1db5d742","server_name":"codex_apps","tool_name":"github.rerun_failed_workflow_run_jobs"},{"connector_id":"connector_76869538009648d5b282a4bb21c3d157","first_turn_id":"01a156f6-7b50-7a00-9fbb-818f2ac4eed4","server_name":"codex_apps","tool_name":"github.fetch"},{"first_turn_id":"01a156f6-7b50-7a00-9fbb-818f2ac4eed4","server_name":"mcp-agent-mail","tool_name":"fetch_topic"},{"first_turn_id":"01a15e3e-2987-7e62-9699-29ab11a9d023","plugin_id":"claude-mem@claude-mem-local","server_name":"mcp-search","tool_name":"search"},{"connector_id":"connector_76869538009648d5b282a4bb21c3d157","first_turn_id":"01a162a0-311d-7271-a76d-8992331bb312","server_name":"codex_apps","tool_name":"github.fetch_pr_file_patch"},{"connector_id":"connector_76869538009648d5b282a4bb21c3d157","first_turn_id":"01a16af7-b30b-7543-b5d3-5d0470af8bf9","server_name":"codex_apps","tool_name":"github.search_branches"},{"connector_id":"connector_76869538009648d5b282a4bb21c3d157","first_turn_id":"01a16b07-bb74-7501-b966-9445743dc69f","server_name":"codex_apps","tool_name":"github.fetch_issue"},{"first_turn_id":"01a16e23-3d1b-7571-9aa1-825e60ce3175","server_name":"mcp-agent-mail","tool_name":"create_agent_identity"}],"status":"complete"}}],"resume_metadata":{"last_started_turn_id":"01a16ef8-1479-7bc1-b23e-862a144e9535","multi_agent_version":"v2","previous_turn_settings":{"comp_hash":"3000","model":"gpt-6-luna","realtime_active":false},"turn_attribution":{"initiating_agent_path":null,"parent_turn_id":null,"root_turn_id":"01a16ef8-1479-7bc1-b23e-862a144e9535","turn_id":"01a16ef8-1479-7bc1-b23e-862a144e9535","turn_trigger":"goal"}},"retained_context":{"assistant_messages":[{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016adceb2a09c881a0a23e7e391fe245b6","order":15286,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a16ef6-9e7d-7261-9026-9087b223231e","text":"The memory service reports: “Claude rejected the request because its five-hour usage allowance is exhausted.” I’ll continue from the repository state and verify the startup flow you highlighted.\n\nI’ll check the current source and claims first, then trace whether Nexus has a folder-trust prompt on startup and what behavior it currently uses.","turn_id":"01a16eee-fedb-7732-9ae7-8cbb47107b53"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016adceb4d464081a0bd8163b2515137fb","order":15287,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a16ef7-2917-7ba3-a7d2-a5ff54c3c3c2","text":"I found the startup trust work in the repository history: PR #186 is already merged to `main`, but the currently published RC4 tag predates it. I’m checking what the merged flow actually prompts about, because your screenshot also includes an explicit “Load project instructions / Check AGENTS.md” step that may be a separate missing behavior.","turn_id":"01a16eee-fedb-7732-9ae7-8cbb47107b53"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016adceb7714b481a0a1b5ddf3d83cdf9e","order":15288,"phase":"final_answer","revision":"retained_01a16ef7-d16f-72c1-b7ed-b5c17935a662","text":"That screenshot is the startup flow you meant. **It’s implemented in PR #186 and included in the RC4 source**: the prompt offers “Trust and continue,” “Continue without trusting,” and “Exit,” and shows whether it found `AGENTS.md` or another project instruction file.\n\nThe `nexus` installed here reports **v1.0.0-rc.3**, which predates that change. That explains why launching it doesn’t show the prompt. I haven’t changed the installed version or the shared checkout. RC4 is still a candidate; this does not change acceptance status.\n\n[PR #186](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/186) · [startup trust implementation](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/blob/main/cli/src/startup_trust.ts)\n\n\u003coai-mem-citation\u003e\n\u003ccitation_entries\u003e\nMEMORY.md:777-789|note=[release status must be rechecked against exact candidate and acceptance gates]\n\u003c/citation_entries\u003e\n\u003crollout_ids\u003e\n01a14262-6554-7912-9e3b-5f24d58b12c0\n\u003c/rollout_ids\u003e\n\u003c/oai-mem-citation\u003e","turn_id":"01a16eee-fedb-7732-9ae7-8cbb47107b53"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016adceb8d224481a094399349036a389f","order":15289,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a16ef8-2239-7403-a9aa-90adfaf0581a","text":"I confirmed the startup trust screen is already in RC4 source, while the installed binary is RC3. I’m returning to the release critical path now: I’ll inspect the active Git exclusion fix and its review note, and refresh the pending Linux CI check before deciding the next safe integration step.","turn_id":"01a16ef8-1479-7bc1-b23e-862a144e9535"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016adcebe7d68081a0a0cd65dd21a747be","order":15290,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a16ef9-845f-7f33-ba73-88070d297e15","text":"The reviewer’s retry concern is real: I added a regression assertion, and it fails because retries append another `.nexus/` rule. I’m fixing the retry path so it still adds a rule after a later same-file negation, but stops appending when Git continues to reject an already-added positive rule.","turn_id":"01a16ef8-1479-7bc1-b23e-862a144e9535"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016adcec18ba2c81a092b57dd6c983e261","order":15293,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a16efa-4371-77b2-8c38-351b005881a2","text":"The focused regression now passes (8/8), and the independent reviewer accepted the amended diff at its exact hash. PR #198 is a separate change in `cli/src/git.ts` and `cli/test/git_commit.test.ts`, so it does not overlap this fix. I’m doing a type check, recording the refreshed review in the claims ledger, and then I’ll prepare this slice for exact-head CI.","turn_id":"01a16ef8-1479-7bc1-b23e-862a144e9535"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016adcec6619d881a0ae48f9ba85ad214e","order":15294,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a16efb-715b-7c61-a0b1-51f378bb0600","text":"The fix is committed and pushed as PR #200 against exact `main` base `41b381d`. Its focused tests, type check, and independent review pass; I’m monitoring exact-head CI now. The other exclusion PR #198 is separate and its Linux job is still being actively polled rather than restarted.","turn_id":"01a16ef8-1479-7bc1-b23e-862a144e9535"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016adcee170e1881a0b6844cc595b0d2f5","order":15302,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a16f02-0d77-7310-b2a4-b35c5f715529","text":"PR #200 has an exact-head CI run underway; CodeQL and CodeRabbit passed, and the Node 22/24 jobs are currently marked active. The older PR #198 Linux job also remains active with no terminal result, so I’m leaving both runs intact and not restarting them. I also refreshed the source requirements gate on exact `main@41b381d`: enforcement and RC4 version synchronization pass; the 12 exact-RC items remain deferred, not satisfied.","turn_id":"01a16ef8-1479-7bc1-b23e-862a144e9535"}],"assistant_messages_incomplete":true,"incomplete":false,"next_order":15305,"sender_deliveries":[{"order":7850,"receiver_message_id":"fco_01a15e0d-46de-72f1-8e85-967b05e2dfc6","receiver_turn_id":"01a15e0b-8f5d-7b40-aa6b-62735e71e8a0","text":"\u003e\u003e\u003e SENDER USER MESSAGES START\nReceived message: fco_01a15e0d-46de-72f1-8e85-967b05e2dfc6\nSource thread: 01a139bf-d0bf-74e0-b96