{"timestamp":"2026-10-24T17:46:33.602Z","ordinal":299837,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a16f03-b5c2-7ab2-ba06-07db849a401d","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-4690eb20-8bf4-4263-8cda-068e6c78d551","process_id":"2204","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","gh release list --repo mikeholownych/nexus-code --limit 12; gh run view 40117358437 --repo mikeholownych/nexus-code --json status,conclusion,jobs; gh pr checks 199 --repo mikeholownych/nexus-code; gh pr checks 200 --repo mikeholownych/nexus-code; git show origin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md | sed -n '70,170p'; git show origin/main:docs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md | rg -n 'REQ-(QUAL-101|QUAL-107|QUAL-108|QUAL-109|REL-114|PRV-111|AGT-110|AGT-002)'"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"gh release list --repo mikeholownych/nexus-code --limit 12; gh run view 40117358437 --repo mikeholownych/nexus-code --json status,conclusion,jobs; gh pr checks 199 --repo mikeholownych/nexus-code; gh pr checks 200 --repo mikeholownych/nexus-code; git show origin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md | sed -n '70,170p'; git show origin/main:docs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md | rg -n 'REQ-(QUAL-101|QUAL-107|QUAL-108|QUAL-109|REL-114|PRV-111|AGT-110|AGT-002)'"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"v1.0.0-rc.4\tPre-release\tv1.0.0-rc.4\t2026-10-24T11:54:37Z\nv1.0.0-rc.3\tPre-release\tv1.0.0-rc.3\t2026-10-23T09:06:11Z\nv1.0.0-rc.1\tPre-release\tv1.0.0-rc.1\t2026-10-21T18:54:41Z\nv0.1.0-alpha.2\tPre-release\tv0.1.0-alpha.2\t2026-10-14T09:10:47Z\nv0.1.0-alpha.1\tPre-release\tv0.1.0-alpha.1\t2026-10-13T20:11:01Z\n{\"conclusion\":\"\",\"jobs\":[{\"completedAt\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"conclusion\":\"\",\"databaseId\":120941283115,\"name\":\"test-matrix (22)\",\"startedAt\":\"2026-10-24T17:42:46Z\",\"status\":\"in_progress\",\"steps\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40117358437/job/120941283115\"},{\"completedAt\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"conclusion\":\"\",\"databaseId\":120941283319,\"name\":\"test-matrix (24)\",\"startedAt\":\"2026-10-24T17:42:46Z\",\"status\":\"in_progress\",\"steps\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40117358437/job/120941283319\"}],\"status\":\"in_progress\"}\nCodeQL\tpass\t4s\thttps://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/runs/120940077666\t\ntest-matrix (22)\tpending\t0\thttps://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40116869410/job/120939840944\t\ntest-matrix (24)\tpending\t0\thttps://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40116869410/job/120939841097\t\nCodeRabbit\tpass\t0\t\tReview skipped: manual review required for this OSS repository\njavascript-typescript\tpass\t1m12s\thttps://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40116869423/job/120939840992\t\nCodeQL\tpass\t2s\thttps://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/runs/120939864459\t\ntest-matrix (22)\tpending\t0\thttps://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40116819381/job/120939693459\t\njavascript-typescript\tpass\t54s\thttps://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40116819484/job/120939693870\t\ntest-matrix (24)\tpending\t0\thttps://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40116819381/job/120939693293\t\nCodeRabbit\tpass\t0\t\tReview skipped: manual review required for this OSS repository\n   - a `SHA256SUMS` file.\n\n   Secrets are redacted before commit.\n5. Any step that cannot run in the available environment is recorded as **NOT RUN** with its reason. A NOT RUN on a blocker gate fails the gate.\n\n## 2. Environments\n\n| ID | Environment | Used for |\n|---|---|---|\n| E1 | GitHub Actions: ubuntu-22.04 and ubuntu-24.04; Node 22 and 24; pinned Rust | Unit, integration and PTY suites; packaging; reproducibility |\n| E2 | Docker clean images: ubuntu:22.04, ubuntu:24.04, debian:12, fedora:40. Each with no Node, then with Node 20, Node 22 and Node 24. Non-root user. | Installer, upgrade, rollback, uninstall, platform failure messages |\n| E3 | Operator dev box: Linux x86-64, real terminals (xterm, kitty, tmux, VS Code terminal, GNOME Terminal) | Terminal matrix, live sessions |\n| E4 | Homelab-ai gateway, the **only** inference path (DEC-16): direct, and through `eval/standalone/plain_proxy.mjs` | Task-quality runs, standalone qualification, T3/T4 |\n| E5 | Cloud, small spend: ChatGPT sign-in (experimental tier) and OpenRouter with a pinned model; OpenAI and Anthropic keys if added | Provider verify; one live task per supported cloud provider |\n\n## 3. Gate checklist (G0–G4: automated acceptance IDs)\n\nEvery ACC ID below is defined in the linked spec. The plan for each spec names the test that implements it. Run each check at the lifecycle stage dictated by its acceptance method in §1.1: source-applicable checks before the RC tag; checks requiring the RC archive, attestation, release, or installed package after RC construction; environment-specific checks in their declared environment. Bind every result to the exact source commit and, when artifact-dependent, the RC package digest. A source test or local build does not replace an artifact-bound check, and no G0–G4 ID is complete until all of its applicable checks pass.\n\n| Gate | Acceptance IDs | Spec |\n|---|---|---|\n| Safety | ACC-SAFE-01 to ACC-SAFE-10 | SPEC-01 |\n| Process ownership | ACC-PROC-01 to ACC-PROC-08 (ACC-PROC-07 is the load test, run in E3) | SPEC-02 |\n| Untrusted inputs | ACC-TRUST-01 to ACC-TRUST-09 | SPEC-03 |\n| Continuity | ACC-CONT-01 to ACC-CONT-09 (ACC-CONT-10 is in §8) | SPEC-04 |\n| Inference | ACC-INF-01 to ACC-INF-09 (ACC-INF-10 is in §4) | SPEC-05 |\n| Packaging | ACC-PKG-01 to ACC-PKG-09 | SPEC-06 |\n| Supply chain | ACC-SUP-01 to ACC-SUP-08 (artifact-bound ACC-SUP-01/02/03/06/08 after RC construction) | SPEC-07 |\n| Persistence | ACC-PER-01 to ACC-PER-07 | SPEC-08 |\n| Governance | ACC-GOV-01 to ACC-GOV-06 | SPEC-09 |\n| Verification | ACC-VER-01 to ACC-VER-09 | SPEC-11 |\n| Upgrade | ACC-UPG-01 to ACC-UPG-14 | SPEC-12 |\n\n\n### 3.1 Acceptance IDs defined in this file\n\nThese are retained commitments from REQUIREMENTS §2 and cross-cutting checks.\n\n| ID | Check | Pass condition |\n|---|---|---|\n| ACC-TUI-STEER | PTY: submit a task; while a tool runs, type steering text and press Enter; also queue a steer before a cancel | Steering is applied at the next step boundary. Unapplied steering is returned to the composer. Nothing is dropped silently (existing `sidecar_steering_diff` plus PTY s6). |\n| ACC-TUI-A11Y | PTY with `NO_COLOR=1` and with `TERM=dumb` at 40×14 and 100×30 | Zero colour SGR codes. Every state is distinguishable by glyph and word. Hints are complete at 40 columns (TUI-10). |\n| ACC-SEC-JAIL | `core/tests` plus harness-core calls with `..`, absolute, symlinked-file, symlinked-dir and symlinked-parent payloads | Every one is refused (C §4 R1 set). |\n| ACC-SEC-B6 | Re-run `docs/reviews/evidence/qualification_2026-10-12/repro/zz_trust_repro.test.ts`. Seeded-secret scan of `~/.nexus` and `.nexus` after a scripted turn. | Zero plaintext seeded secrets in durable stores or outbound bodies. |\n| ACC-PRV-LIVE | `nexus providers verify --provider <p> -m <pinned model> -j` for each provider listed as supported (DEC-06) | `passed: true`. Receipts archived. |\n| ACC-PRV-STANDALONE | §4.2 on the installed RC through the approved stripped proxy, with gateway credentials absent from the child environment | Every required profile completes through the proxy and the absent-gateway boundary holds; receipts archived. |\n| ACC-PLAT | E2 matrix, §7 | All rows pass. |\n| ACC-QUAL-T2 | §6.1 + §6.4 | Thresholds met. |\n| ACC-QUAL-T3 | §6.3 + §6.4 | Thresholds met. |\n| ACC-QUAL-T4 | §6.2 + §6.4 | Thresholds met. |\n| ACC-QUAL-SMOKE | `make test` includes the T1 self-test and the T4 smoke | Present and passing. |\n| ACC-TUI-MANUAL | §5.3 on the installed RC across five required terminal environments and three required sizes | Every cell passes; screenshots and per-cell verdicts are archived. |\n\n## 4. Standalone and provider qualification (REQ-PRV-106, REQ-PRV-111, REQ-QUAL-107)\n\n### 4.1 Clean-HOME procedure\n\n1. `export HOME=$(mktemp -d)`.\n2. Install the RC with the documented command.\n3. Create `~/.config/nexus/config.env` containing only:\n   - `LOCAL_LLM_ENDPOINT=http://127.0.0.1:<proxy>/v1`\n   - `LOCAL_LLM_MODEL=<id as listed by the proxy>`\n   - `LOCAL_LLM_API_KEY=REDACTED\n\n   No gateway token file, no homelab paths, no `NODE_*` overrides.\n4. Start `node eval/standalone/plain_proxy.mjs --upstream <gateway> --token-file <operator token> [--emulate <kind>]`. The gateway token stays with the proxy and never reaches the Nexus HOME.\n5. Run `nexus doctor --json` and archive it. It must report the server kind and context source with no `gateway` capability.\n\n### 4.2 Standalone matrix\n\n| Profile | What Nexus sees | Runs | Pass condition |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| P-plain | Bare OpenAI-compatible `/models` and chat. No tokenize, no capacity headers. | Standalone T2 subset (≥ 10 held-out tasks) × 3 runs; T4 classes 1, 3, 4, 7 × 3 | T2 correctness ≥ (gateway-direct T2 correctness on the same tasks − 10 pts). False VERIFIED = 0. T4 truthful = 100%. Context source reported as `client_default` or an operator override, with no error. |\n| P-llamacpp | Emulated llama.cpp `/props` and overflow body | Same tasks × 1 run; plus the forced-overflow case (context limit set to 8k) | Context discovered from `/props`. Overflow gives one compact-and-retry, then success or an actionable error. |\n| P-vllm | Emulated `max_model_len` and vLLM overflow body | Same as P-llamacpp | Same, with the context source `max_model_len` |\n| P-ollama | Emulated `/api/show` and Ollama overflow body | Same as P-llamacpp | Same, with the context source `ollama_show` |\n| Conformance | CI fixtures for llama.cpp, vLLM, LM Studio and Ollama shapes | CI | All pass (ACC-INF-01, -02, -05) |\n\nACC-INF-10 passes only when every row passes. The release notes state the scope in the form required by DEC-16.\n\n### 4.3 Provider matrix (E5)\n\n| Provider | Tier (DEC-06) | Required for v1.0.0 |\n|---|---|---|\n| OpenRouter, pinned model | Supported | `providers verify` PASS, plus one live small task (a §6-style bug fix) reaching a correct outcome |\n| ChatGPT sign-in | Experimental | Verify PASS recorded (already PASS at db1ca55; repeat on the RC) |\n| OpenAI API key, Anthropic | Experimental unless keys are added | If promoted: verify PASS plus one live task. Otherwise NOT RUN, and they are labelled experimental. |\n| Copilot | Experimental | Not required |\n\n## 5. Terminal acceptance (REQ-QUAL-108)\n\n### 5.1 CI PTY suites (E1)\n\nThese must pass:\n\n- `tui_approval_input_e2e`\n- `tui_diff_e2e`\n- `tui_maturity_e2e`\n- `tui_model_picker_e2e`\n- `tui_multiline_e2e`\n- `tui_surface_e2e`\n56:| REQ-AGT-002 | quickstart; TOP_TIER B3; EXEC-005 | Truthful outcome taxonomy. VERIFIED requires a passing, deliverable-bound verifier run, plus fail-before/pass-after independence for discovered verifiers. UNVERIFIED, REGRESSION_FREE, BLOCKED and LIMIT_REACHED are distinct, with exit codes 0/2/1/130. | `agent.ts:5726-5764`; `tester.ts:371-430,541-627`; `turn.ts:318-351` | TEST at db1ca55; candidate suite at `6151a23` passes ACC-VER-03/04/09 regression tests. Historical VER-04/05 findings and tuned-set/live evidence remain in [A2_verification.md](evidence/A2_verification.md) and the dated evidence files. | partial | N | M5 false-VERIFIED threshold remains unqualified pending held-out T2/T3/T4 evidence; historical VER-04/05 implementation defects have regression coverage at the candidate. | ACC-VER-03/04/09, ACC-QUAL-T2 | B | SPEC-11 |\n103:| REL-001 byte-identical builds | deferred | Same-runner proven | REQ-REL-114 (RR, cross-runner once for the RC) |\n163:| REQ-AGT-110 | HIST-09 | Independent acceptance of continuity, compaction and truncation recovery. | qualification | — | DOC (\"pending\") | open | ACC-CONT-10, ACC-GOV-06 | RR | HIST-09 | SPEC-04 / PLAN-09 |\n179:| REQ-PRV-111 | DEC-06 | Live `providers verify` for each provider listed as supported. The others are labelled experimental. | compatibility claims | `provider_cli.ts` | **RT 2026-10-14 @db1ca55:** chatgpt (gpt-6-luna) PASS, openrouter (openrouter/free) PASS. **RT 2026-10-16 @6151a23+4d82578, pinned models:** openrouter `nvidia/nemotron-3-super-120b-a12b:free` PASS (one model served every request), chatgpt `gpt-6-luna` PASS (`evidence/live/verify_*_pinned_2026-10-16.json`). The run found and fixed the option-scope regression (4d82578). openai-key and anthropic not connected. | partial (repeat on the RC) | ACC-PRV-LIVE | RR | B §6 G2 | SPEC-05 / PLAN-10 |\n203:| REQ-REL-114 | REL-001 (carried) | Cross-runner reproducibility, demonstrated once for the RC. | supply chain | `repro.yml` | UNV | open | ACC-SUP-08 | RR | E §6 | SPEC-07 / PLAN-07 |\n234:| REQ-QUAL-101 | TOP_TIER Q1; DEC-05 | Held-out T2 evaluation: 40 tasks, ≥ 50% external, sealed manifest. | product maturity | `eval/` | HIST (6 tuned tasks) | open | ACCEPTANCE §6.1 | **B** | EVL-001 | SPEC-10 / PLAN-10 |\n240:| REQ-QUAL-107 | Standalone; DEC-06 | Standalone and provider live matrix. | standalone | — | HIST | open | ACCEPTANCE §4.2, §4.3 | **B** | HIST-08 | SPEC-10 / PLAN-10 |\n241:| REQ-QUAL-108 | Audit | PTY CI plus a manual real-terminal matrix. | terminal acceptance | `cli/test/tui_*`; ACCEPTANCE §5.3 | TEST (PTY suites in CI); UNV (real terminals) | partial | ACCEPTANCE §5 | RR | D §6 | SPEC-10 / PLAN-10 |\n242:| REQ-QUAL-109 | eval/README T3 | T3 long tasks: 8 × 5. | long-task workflow | `eval/` | — | open | ACCEPTANCE §6.3 | RR | EVL-001 | SPEC-10 / PLAN-10 |\n276:| New v1 rows (§3) | 92 | **31 B**, 58 RR, 3 P. 79 open, 9 partial (REQ-SEC-118, REQ-PRV-101, REQ-PRV-103, REQ-PRV-105, REQ-PRV-111, REQ-PER-106, REQ-OPS-101, REQ-QUAL-108, REQ-QUAL-110), 1 implemented (REQ-OPS-103), 4 tested (REQ-SEC-103, REQ-SEC-119, REQ-PER-101, REQ-PER-102). |\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":3,"nanos":393260069}},"started_at_ms":1792863990207,"completed_at_ms":1792863993601}}
