{"timestamp":"2026-10-24T17:47:00.036Z","ordinal":299859,"type":"token_usage_record","payload":{"thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a16f03-b5c2-7ab2-ba06-07db849a401d","session_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","root_turn_id":"01a16f03-b5c2-7ab2-ba06-07db849a401d","response_id":"resp_060b64278a9dfb15016adcef104fb481a0b5ce992655057926","usage":{"input_tokens":141109,"cached_input_tokens":139520,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":322,"reasoning_output_tokens":305,"total_tokens":141431},"turn_token_usage":{"input_tokens":2217972,"cached_input_tokens":2168192,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":9738,"reasoning_output_tokens":6696,"total_tokens":2227710},"thread_token_usage":{"input_tokens":5447004843,"cached_input_tokens":5388760192,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":15213590,"reasoning_output_tokens":8687809,"total_tokens":5462218433}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-24T17:47:00.853Z","ordinal":299860,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"function_call_output","id":"fco_01a16f05-e974-7111-b147-5facff65e57c","call_id":"call_175e5f93ec4e40e18f21937f0711f94b","output":"{\"agents\":[{\"agent_name\":\"/root\",\"agent_status\":\"running\"},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/context_rc_gate_audit\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"**Read-only audit at `origin/main@41b381ddac182b7f0c783b33df5f1355518f465b`.** No evaluator qualification or tests were run, and no held-out payloads or private validators were read. The worktree was already dirty; I left it untouched.\\n\\n**Containment controls:** Source and synthetic fixtures cover all requested limits. `eval/resources.mjs:15-75, 78-105` validates the resource profile, requires a dedicated size-capped tmpfs and delegated systemd scope, then reads back a successful containment probe. `eval/cgroup_supervisor.mjs:25-45` applies and verifies CPU, memory, swap, and pids limits before starting the payload. `eval/run.mjs:107-113, 176-181, 322-325, 544-558, 624-650` requires these resources for qualification and passes them to setup, candidate, and check execution. The resource wrapper permits an uncontained path when `resources` is absent (`eval/resources.mjs:111-114`), but qualification preflight rejects that configuration.\\n\\n`cli/test/eval_integrity.test.ts:580-652` contains production-helper fixtures for memory, pids, tmpfs storage, CPU throttling, timeouts, and processes escaping their session. The host preflight evidence from `6383623` reports 10/10 synthetic checks passed, including applied limits and cleanup; evaluator source files have not changed between that commit and this main revision. This is host-preflight evidence, not held-out qualification.\\n\\n**Process cleanup fails closed in source:** `eval/cgroup_supervisor.mjs:61-90` kills remaining cgroup processes and reports failure unless the cgroup becomes empty. `eval/resources.mjs:143-148` treats a missing report, supervisor error, or unclean cgroup as a containment problem. The synthetic fixtures at `eval_integrity.test.ts:638-648` exercise an escaped process.\\n\\n**Hidden-test boundary:** Qualification rejects legacy in-process hidden validators (`eval/validate.mjs:39-48`; `eval/run.mjs:641-643`). The black-box oracle keeps expected values in the evaluator and executes the candidate entrypoint in a separate sandbox (`eval/oracle.mjs:64-115, 125-150`). The synthetic oracle fixture at `eval_integrity.test.ts:266-328` probes access and output leakage. Legacy hardening is explicitly limited to pilot use in `eval/README.md:213-219`.\\n\\n**Git and filesystem isolation:** `eval/workspace.mjs:13-20, 23-37` builds a fresh workspace from the pinned commit and rejects alternates, remotes, extra refs/reflog commits, and unreachable objects. `eval/isolate.mjs:92-115, 139-215, 266-311` verifies sandbox mount sources against protected paths, creates isolated user/PID/network namespaces, and mounts the workspace, isolated home, proxy socket, and approved runtime paths. `eval/run.mjs:33-47` includes task and configured custody paths in the protected set for qualification. The synthetic fixture at `eval_integrity.test.ts:654-792` combines the production workspace stager with `agentSandboxArgv`, checks future solution and dangling Git objects, and probes synthetic external-store paths. This is source inspection of a fixture; it was not executed in this audit.\\n\\n**Fixture composition gap:** The test exercises workspace staging plus candidate sandbox together, while the resource stress test exercises `runIsolated`/`spawnContained`. I did not find one fixture that composes `agentSandboxArgv` with `spawnContained` and asserts both the candidate boundary and cgroup limits in the same run. Source wiring does pass the candidate’s wrapped sandbox to `spawnContained` (`eval/run.mjs:544-558`), so this is an additional integration-proof gap, not a confirmed production defect.\\n\\n**Claims and next safe slice:** The current claim ledger shows the host-preflight claim released and candidate-integrity work archived as merged. I found no active claim on the evaluator files; PR #200 and its active Git-exclusion claim concern separate `git_exclude` paths. The smallest useful follow-up is a **test-only** synthetic regression in `cli/test/eval_integrity.test.ts` that runs `agentSandboxArgv` through `spawnContained` with a pinned synthetic repo, future-object canary, and external private-file canary, then verifies denied reads and clean cgroup termination. Claim that test file and SUITE before implementing or running it.\"}},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/heldout_public_coverage_audit\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"No change since the prior check at `origin/main@be2cd2f255414f554572c86baa884d9271ff5ea1`: Issue #1 still ends with coordinator comment #6378649211, with no custodian acknowledgment or handoff. PR #16 remains closed with no new custody acceptance, and current claims show no held-out author/custodian owner.\\n\\nThe manifests and historical attestations are unchanged. Qualification remains blocked pending explicit independent custodian ownership and acceptance, plus a custodian-approved T2 compatibility or supersession path. No files or private material were accessed.\"}},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/plan05_readonly_review\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"**ACCEPT** for the uncommitted diff at `3d5fd0912d91839de6e6c0fb528046ad1b09afff`, SHA-256 `9518852b8ad6f9c2242a8b08f7b661925beed1d492f72847a75216dae17ec8f1`.\\n\\nThe retry guard prevents repeated appends when a higher-priority `.gitignore` conflict makes the check fail. A later negation within `info/exclude` still permits appending a final positive rule; the regression verifies that retries under the higher-priority conflict leave the file unchanged. No remaining blocker found. `git diff --check` is clean; I did not run tests.\"}}]}","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a16f03-b5c2-7ab2-ba06-07db849a401d","create_time":1792864020.852947}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
