pose the production workspace staging, `agentSandboxArgv`, and `spawnContained` paths. The future-commit lookup and external canary read are meaningful, and the cgroup limits, survivor report, cleanup flag, and delayed-marker assertion provide useful evidence.\\n\\nOne fixture-cleanup gap remains in [eval_integrity.test.ts](/home/mike/nexus-code/cli/test/eval_integrity.test.ts:660): `base` is created before the `try/finally` begins at line 678, so setup failures can leave it behind. Also, if the 20-second timeout fires at line 721, the test requests containment cleanup but rejects immediately, then removes the fixture without awaiting supervisor completion. Enclose setup in the cleanup scope and await containment shutdown on timeout/error. I did not run tests.\"}}]}","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a16f0d-3055-7c13-8ac8-f65e99c34ef5","create_time":1792864527.2471282}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
