{"timestamp":"2026-10-24T18:05:41.990Z","ordinal":300622,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a16f0d-3055-7c13-8ac8-f65e99c34ef5","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016adcf372924081a088cdb4f3ed8b2a78","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"**Release convergence is still active; acceptance remains `IN_PROGRESS`.** No stable v1.0.0 has been published.\n\n- **Startup trust prompt:** It is present in RC4 source. The `nexus` installed on this machine is RC3, which predates it. I made no installation changes.\n- **Main CI:** On `676abb371c8c91970af6d920d5c516497e3ccdef`, Node 22 and 24 passed, as did CodeQL and the requirements check. Linux packaging is still running.\n- **PR #200:** Updated to rebased head `56bc1dcef066bae949e7ebe04346a45cb60bf362` on `676abb3`. Its focused tests passed 11/11, independent review accepted the exact diff, and CodeQL passed. Node 22/24 checks are running. [PR #200](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/200)\n- **PR #201:** Opened for the synthetic evaluator containment and workspace-isolation regression fixture at `dfb3880d43fb2ba5574c8ac42221cfe4d138fe59`. Its focused test passed 1/1, independent review accepted it, and CodeQL passed. Node 22/24 checks are running. No held-out content was accessed. [PR #201](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/201)\n- **PR #199:** Node 22/24 and CodeQL passed; Linux packaging is running. It is based on stale `41b381d`, and its OpenCode owner still has the active claim, so I left that lane with them. [PR #199](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/199)\n- **Terminal setup:** I reached `ubuntu-desktop` at `10.0.8.3` directly. xterm, kitty, GNOME Terminal, VS Code, and tmux 3.6 are installed, and a GNOME Wayland session is active. The required 15-cell manual matrix has not started because there is no eligible RC to test. It still needs interactive operator checks and screenshots for each cell.\n- **Remaining qualification blockers:** The held-out custodian has not replied to the latest status request; no private corpus data was accessed and no held-out run has begun. RC4 remains the latest public candidate; exact-RC qualification and independent acceptance are incomplete.\n\nI preserved the dirty shared checkout. The next integration decisions depend on the running exact-head CI results."}],"phase":"final_answer"},"started_at_ms":1792865140845,"completed_at_ms":1792865141990}}
