{"timestamp":"2026-10-24T18:08:49.116Z","ordinal":300772,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a16f19-0668-7a11-98a1-7e4c57605ec6","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016adcf42f749881a0be73b15eee86adf0","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"The latest check confirms `main` is the active release base: it is GitHub’s default branch at `676abb371c8c91970af6d920d5c516497e3ccdef`. `v1/integration` (`7d6673f`) is an ancestor, 313 commits behind, with no unique commits. I’m preserving it without rewriting it.\n\nOn `main`, Node 22 and 24 CI, CodeQL, and requirements enforcement passed. The Linux package job is still running its full CLI test stage. PRs #200 and #201 also still have Node checks running; PR #199’s Linux check remains active, and its owner’s claim is still in place. No failures have been reported, so there is no basis to merge yet.\n\nRC4 is still the latest public candidate, and v1.0.0 remains unreleased. Held-out custody and exact-RC qualification are still outstanding."}],"phase":"final_answer"},"started_at_ms":1792865327481,"completed_at_ms":1792865329116}}
