{"timestamp":"2026-10-24T18:12:22.071Z","ordinal":300954,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a16f1a-0d89-7262-a71e-eb3a6dfcc08e","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016adcf5057a4881a09bfec3093540274c","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"The refreshed review found a real issue: although reads are capped at 8 MiB, the parser stores each line as a separate owned `String`, so newline-dense input can amplify memory far beyond that limit. I’m treating this as a defect and will fix it with a regression test before updating PR #199. The focused test run is currently compiling."}],"phase":"commentary"},"started_at_ms":1792865541502,"completed_at_ms":1792865542071}}
