{"timestamp":"2026-10-24T18:12:24.261Z","ordinal":300960,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","id":"msg_01a16f1d-2845-75f1-856d-87084e04f166","role":"developer","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Current: 2026-10-24 6:12pm UTC\nThis file has prior observations — supplementary context follows. The Read result below is the full requested section.\n- **Need details on a past observation?** get_observations([IDs]) — ~300 tokens each.\n- **Need a structural map first?** smart_outline(\"core/src/cst.rs\") — line numbers only, cheaper than re-reading.\n### Oct 4, 2026\n11628 3:03a 🔵 CLI Architecture: 47 TypeScript Files, ~19.7K Lines, Core Subsystem Identified\n### Oct 12, 2026\n16086 6:38a 🔵 Rust Core Search/FileTree Output Fields — total_matches, max_results, total_files Confirmed in Rust\n### Oct 13, 2026\n16722 2:47a 🔴 Surface Driver Approval Step: Arrow-Right Settle Time Increased to 0.6s for Dwell Timer\n### Oct 14, 2026\n17498 12:44p 🔵 Rust Core Has Dedicated Adversarial Path Traversal and Segregation Boundary Tests"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a16f1a-0d89-7262-a71e-eb3a6dfcc08e","create_time":1792865544.2614522,"content_item_kinds":["hooks.additional_context"]}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-24T18:12:25.318Z","ordinal":300961,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a16f1a-0d89-7262-a71e-eb3a6dfcc08e","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-8f12eca1-da99-41da-adeb-5d647a640e34","process_id":"93042","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","nl -ba core/src/cst.rs | sed -n '1,190p'; nl -ba core/src/cst.rs | sed -n '230,365p'; nl -ba docs/reviews/evidence/v1/DEFECT-CST-UNBOUNDED-20261024/README.md | sed -n '1,100p'"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-wt/cst-unbounded-rebase","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"read","cmd":"nl -ba core/src/cst.rs","name":"cst.rs","path":"core/src/cst.rs"},{"type":"read","cmd":"nl -ba docs/reviews/evidence/v1/DEFECT-CST-UNBOUNDED-20261024/README.md","name":"README.md","path":"docs/reviews/evidence/v1/DEFECT-CST-UNBOUNDED-20261024/README.md"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"     1\tuse regex::Regex;\n     2\tuse serde::{Deserialize, Serialize};\n     3\tuse std::fs::File;\n     4\tuse std::io::{BufReader, Read};\n     5\tuse std::path::Path;\n     6\tuse walkdir::WalkDir;\n     7\t\n     8\tuse crate::file_ops::MAX_READ_BYTES;\n     9\t\n    10\t/// Reads a source file for symbol parsing, bounded like the file tools: a huge file must not allocate unbounded\n    11\t/// memory here. The cap also covers growth after the size check.\n    12\tfn read_source_file(file_path: &Path) -> Result<String, String> {\n    13\t    let file = File::open(file_path).map_err(|e| format!(\"Failed to open file: {e}\"))?;\n    14\t    let size = file.metadata().map_err(|e| format!(\"Failed to get metadata: {e}\"))?.len();\n    15\t    if size > MAX_READ_BYTES as u64 {\n    16\t        return Err(format!(\n    17\t            \"File is too large to parse: {size} bytes exceeds the 8 MB limit ({MAX_READ_BYTES} bytes)\"\n    18\t        ));\n    19\t    }\n    20\t    let mut content = String::new();\n    21\t    BufReader::new(file)\n    22\t        .take(MAX_READ_BYTES as u64 + 1)\n    23\t        .read_to_string(&mut content)\n    24\t        .map_err(|e| format!(\"Failed to read file: {e}\"))?;\n    25\t    if content.len() > MAX_READ_BYTES {\n    26\t        return Err(format!(\n    27\t            \"File is too large to parse: it grew beyond the 8 MB limit ({MAX_READ_BYTES} bytes)\"\n    28\t        ));\n    29\t    }\n    30\t    Ok(content)\n    31\t}\n    32\t\n    33\t#[derive(Debug, Serialize, Deserialize, Clone)]\n    34\tpub struct CstSymbol {\n    35\t    pub name: String,\n    36\t    pub kind: String,\n    37\t    pub visibility: String,\n    38\t    pub scope: Option<String>,\n    39\t    pub file: String,\n    40\t    pub start_line: usize,\n    41\t    pub end_line: usize,\n    42\t    pub signature: String,\n    43\t    pub doc_comment: Option<String>,\n    44\t}\n    45\t\n    46\t#[derive(Debug, Serialize, Deserialize)]\n    47\tpub struct CstParseArgs {\n    48\t    pub path: String,\n    49\t    pub query: Option<String>,\n    50\t}\n    51\t\n    52\t#[derive(Debug, Serialize, Deserialize)]\n    53\tpub struct CstParseResult {\n    54\t    pub total_symbols: usize,\n    55\t    pub symbols: Vec<CstSymbol>,\n    56\t}\n    57\t\n    58\t/**\n    59\t * Concrete Syntax Tree (CST) Symbol Parser (Candidate #04)\n    60\t * Parses multiline signatures, doc comments, visibility, and scopes across languages.\n    61\t */\n    62\tpub fn parse_cst_symbols(file_path: &Path, rel_path: &str, query_filter: Option<&str>) -> Result<Vec<CstSymbol>, String> {\n    63\t    let content = read_source_file(file_path)?;\n    64\t    let ext = file_path.extension().and_then(|s| s.to_str()).unwrap_or(\"\");\n    65\t    Ok(parse_cst_content(&content, rel_path, query_filter, ext))\n    66\t}\n    67\t\n    68\t/// Parses already-bounded source text, so a caller that has the content (an outline) does not read the file again.\n    69\tfn parse_cst_content(content: &str, rel_path: &str, query_filter: Option<&str>, ext: &str) -> Vec<CstSymbol> {\n    70\t    let lines: Vec<String> = content.lines().map(|line| line.to_string()).collect();\n    71\t    let mut symbols = Vec::new();\n    72\t\n    73\t    let doc_regex = Regex::new(r\"^\\s*(?://[/!]|\\s*\\*\\s*|#\\s*|/\\*\\*|<!--)(.*)\").unwrap();\n    74\t    let current_scope: Option<String> = None;\n    75\t\n    76\t    // Pattern matching declaration headers\n    77\t    let decl_regex = Regex::new(\n    78\t        r\"(?m)^\\s*(pub(?:\\([^)]+\\))?\\s+)?(async\\s+)?(export\\s+)?(default\\s+)?(fn|function|def|class|struct|interface|trait|type|enum|func)\\s+([A-Za-z0-9_]+)(.*)\"\n    79\t    ).unwrap();\n    80\t\n    81\t    let mut pending_doc = Vec::new();\n    82\t    let mut i = 0;\n    83\t\n    84\t    while i < lines.len() {\n    85\t        let line = &lines[i];\n    86\t        let trimmed = line.trim();\n    87\t\n    88\t        // Accumulate preceding doc comments\n    89\t        if (trimmed.starts_with(\"///\") || trimmed.starts_with(\"//!\") || trimmed.starts_with(\"/**\") || (trimmed.starts_with('*') && !trimmed.starts_with(\"*/\")) || (ext == \"py\" && trimmed.starts_with('#'))) && !trimmed.starts_with(\"/*\") {\n    90\t            if let Some(caps) = doc_regex.captures(trimmed) {\n    91\t                let comment = caps.get(1).map(|m| m.as_str().trim()).unwrap_or(\"\");\n    92\t                if !comment.is_empty() {\n    93\t                    pending_doc.push(comment.to_string());\n    94\t                }\n    95\t            }\n    96\t            i += 1;\n    97\t            continue;\n    98\t        }\n    99\t\n   100\t        if let Some(caps) = decl_regex.captures(trimmed) {\n   101\t            let vis_raw = caps.get(1).map(|m| m.as_str().trim()).unwrap_or(\"\");\n   102\t            let export_raw = caps.get(3).map(|m| m.as_str().trim()).unwrap_or(\"\");\n   103\t            let kind = caps.get(5).map(|m| m.as_str().trim()).unwrap_or(\"unknown\").to_string();\n   104\t            let name = caps.get(6).map(|m| m.as_str().trim()).unwrap_or(\"\").to_string();\n   105\t\n   106\t            let visibility = if !vis_raw.is_empty() {\n   107\t                vis_raw.to_string()\n   108\t            } else if !export_raw.is_empty() {\n   109\t                \"exported\".to_string()\n   110\t            } else {\n   111\t                \"private\".to_string()\n   112\t            };\n   113\t\n   114\t            let start_line = i + 1;\n   115\t            let mut sig_lines = vec![trimmed.to_string()];\n   116\t            let mut end_line = start_line;\n   117\t\n   118\t            // Multiline signature accumulation until '{', ';', or ':' (python)\n   119\t            if !trimmed.contains('{') && !trimmed.contains(';') && !(ext == \"py\" && trimmed.ends_with(':')) {\n   120\t                let mut j = i + 1;\n   121\t                while j < lines.len() && j < i + 10 {\n   122\t                    let next_trimmed = lines[j].trim();\n   123\t                    sig_lines.push(next_trimmed.to_string());\n   124\t                    if next_trimmed.contains('{') || next_trimmed.contains(';') || (ext == \"py\" && next_trimmed.ends_with(':')) {\n   125\t                        end_line = j + 1;\n   126\t                        i = j;\n   127\t                        break;\n   128\t                    }\n   129\t                    j += 1;\n   130\t                }\n   131\t            }\n   132\t\n   133\t            let full_sig = sig_lines.join(\" \");\n   134\t            let doc_text = if !pending_doc.is_empty() {\n   135\t                Some(pending_doc.join(\"\\n\"))\n   136\t            } else {\n   137\t                None\n   138\t            };\n   139\t            pending_doc.clear();\n   140\t\n   141\t            let matches_query = match query_filter {\n   142\t                Some(q) => name.to_lowercase().contains(&q.to_lowercase()),\n   143\t                None => true,\n   144\t            };\n   145\t\n   146\t            if matches_query && !name.is_empty() {\n   147\t                symbols.push(CstSymbol {\n   148\t                    name,\n   149\t                    kind,\n   150\t                    visibility,\n   151\t                    scope: current_scope.clone(),\n   152\t                    file: rel_path.to_string(),\n   153\t                    start_line,\n   154\t                    end_line,\n   155\t                    signature: full_sig,\n   156\t                    doc_comment: doc_text,\n   157\t                });\n   158\t            }\n   159\t        } else if !trimmed.is_empty() {\n   160\t            pending_doc.clear();\n   161\t        }\n   162\t\n   163\t        i += 1;\n   164\t    }\n   165\t\n   166\t    symbols\n   167\t}\n   168\t\n   169\t/**\n   170\t * Scan workspace files and parse CST symbols\n   171\t */\n   172\tpub fn scan_workspace_cst(base_dir: &Path, args: CstParseArgs) -> Result<CstParseResult, String> {\n   173\t    let target = crate::file_ops::resolve_safe_path(base_dir, &args.path)?;\n   174\t    let mut all_symbols = Vec::new();\n   175\t\n   176\t    if target.is_file() {\n   177\t        let rel_path = target.strip_prefix(base_dir).unwrap_or(&target).to_string_lossy().to_string();\n   178\t        let syms = parse_cst_symbols(&target, &rel_path, args.query.as_deref())?;\n   179\t        all_symbols.extend(syms);\n   180\t    } else if target.is_dir() {\n   181\t        for entry in WalkDir::new(&target).max_depth(5).into_iter().filter_map(|e| e.ok()) {\n   182\t            let p = entry.path();\n   183\t            if p.is_file() {\n   184\t                let ext = p.extension().and_then(|s| s.to_str()).unwrap_or(\"\");\n   185\t                if matches!(ext, \"rs\" | \"ts\" | \"tsx\" | \"js\" | \"jsx\" | \"py\" | \"go\") {\n   186\t                    let rel_path = p.strip_prefix(base_dir).unwrap_or(p).to_string_lossy().to_string();\n   187\t                    if let Ok(syms) = parse_cst_symbols(p, &rel_path, args.query.as_deref()) {\n   188\t                        all_symbols.extend(syms);\n   189\t                    }\n   190\t                }\n   230\t    } else {\n   231\t        for s in &symbols {\n   232\t            let doc_hint = s.doc_comment.as_ref()\n   233\t                .and_then(|d| d.lines().next())\n   234\t                .map(|line| format!(\" - \\\"{}\\\"\", line.trim()))\n   235\t                .unwrap_or_default();\n   236\t            outline_str.push_str(&format!(\n   237\t                \"- [{}] {} (lines {}-{}) [{}]{}\\n\",\n   238\t                s.kind, s.name, s.start_line, s.end_line, s.visibility, doc_hint\n   239\t            ));\n   240\t        }\n   241\t    }\n   242\t\n   243\t    Ok(OutlineFileResult {\n   244\t        path: args.path,\n   245\t        total_lines,\n   246\t        symbol_count: symbols.len(),\n   247\t        outline: outline_str,\n   248\t    })\n   249\t}\n   250\t\n   251\t#[cfg(test)]\n   252\tmod tests {\n   253\t    use super::*;\n   254\t\n   255\t    #[test]\n   256\t    fn test_cst_symbol_parsing() {\n   257\t        let tmp = std::env::temp_dir().join(\"nexus_cst_test.rs\");\n   258\t        let code = r#\"\n   259\t/// High-level engine runner\n   260\tpub async fn execute_task(\n   261\t    id: &str,\n   262\t    timeout: u64,\n   263\t) -> Result<bool, String> {\n   264\t    Ok(true)\n   265\t}\n   266\t\"#;\n   267\t        std::fs::write(&tmp, code).unwrap();\n   268\t        let syms = parse_cst_symbols(&tmp, \"test.rs\", None).unwrap();\n   269\t        assert_eq!(syms.len(), 1);\n   270\t        let s = &syms[0];\n   271\t        assert_eq!(s.name, \"execute_task\");\n   272\t        assert_eq!(s.kind, \"fn\");\n   273\t        assert_eq!(s.visibility, \"pub\");\n   274\t        assert!(s.signature.contains(\"-> Result<bool, String>\"));\n   275\t        assert!(s.doc_comment.as_ref().unwrap().contains(\"High-level engine runner\"));\n   276\t\n   277\t        let outline_res = generate_file_outline(&std::env::temp_dir(), OutlineFileArgs {\n   278\t            path: \"nexus_cst_test.rs\".into(),\n   279\t        }).unwrap();\n   280\t        assert_eq!(outline_res.symbol_count, 1);\n   281\t        assert!(outline_res.outline.contains(\"- [fn] execute_task\"));\n   282\t        assert!(outline_res.outline.contains(\"lines\"));\n   283\t\n   284\t        let _ = std::fs::remove_file(tmp);\n   285\t    }\n   286\t\n   287\t    struct TempSource(std::path::PathBuf);\n   288\t\n   289\t    impl TempSource {\n   290\t        fn new(name: &str) -> Self {\n   291\t            Self(std::env::temp_dir().join(name))\n   292\t        }\n   293\t\n   294\t        fn path(&self) -> &Path {\n   295\t            &self.0\n   296\t        }\n   297\t\n   298\t        fn file_name(&self) -> String {\n   299\t            self.0.file_name().unwrap().to_string_lossy().to_string()\n   300\t        }\n   301\t    }\n   302\t\n   303\t    impl Drop for TempSource {\n   304\t        fn drop(&mut self) {\n   305\t            let _ = std::fs::remove_file(&self.0);\n   306\t        }\n   307\t    }\n   308\t\n   309\t    fn oversized_source(name: &str) -> TempSource {\n   310\t        let tmp = TempSource::new(name);\n   311\t        let mut code = String::from(\"pub fn first() {}\\n\");\n   312\t        while code.len() <= MAX_READ_BYTES {\n   313\t            code.push_str(\"// filler comment line\\n\");\n   314\t        }\n   315\t        std::fs::write(tmp.path(), &code).unwrap();\n   316\t        tmp\n   317\t    }\n   318\t\n   319\t    #[test]\n   320\t    fn test_cst_refuses_files_above_the_read_limit() {\n   321\t        let tmp = oversized_source(&format!(\"nexus_cst_big_{}.rs\", std::process::id()));\n   322\t        let parsed = parse_cst_symbols(tmp.path(), &tmp.file_name(), None);\n   323\t        assert!(parsed.is_err(), \"parse_cst_symbols must refuse a file above the read limit\");\n   324\t        assert!(parsed.unwrap_err().contains(\"8 MB\"));\n   325\t    }\n   326\t\n   327\t    #[test]\n   328\t    fn test_cst_outline_refuses_files_above_the_read_limit() {\n   329\t        let tmp = oversized_source(&format!(\"nexus_cst_big_outline_{}.rs\", std::process::id()));\n   330\t        // generate_file_outline must enforce the limit itself, not rely on the parser's refusal.\n   331\t        let outline = generate_file_outline(&std::env::temp_dir(), OutlineFileArgs { path: tmp.file_name() });\n   332\t        assert!(outline.is_err(), \"generate_file_outline must refuse a file above the read limit\");\n   333\t        assert!(outline.unwrap_err().contains(\"8 MB\"));\n   334\t    }\n   335\t\n   336\t    #[test]\n   337\t    fn test_cst_accepts_the_read_limit_and_empty_files() {\n   338\t        let at_limit = TempSource::new(&format!(\"nexus_cst_at_limit_{}.rs\", std::process::id()));\n   339\t        let first = \"pub fn first() {}\\n\";\n   340\t        let mut code = String::from(first);\n   341\t        code.push_str(&\"x\".repeat(MAX_READ_BYTES - first.len()));\n   342\t        std::fs::write(at_limit.path(), &code).unwrap();\n   343\t        let parsed = parse_cst_symbols(at_limit.path(), &at_limit.file_name(), None).unwrap();\n   344\t        assert_eq!(parsed.len(), 1);\n   345\t        let outline = generate_file_outline(&std::env::temp_dir(), OutlineFileArgs { path: at_limit.file_name() }).unwrap();\n   346\t        assert_eq!(outline.total_lines, 2);\n   347\t        assert_eq!(outline.symbol_count, 1);\n   348\t\n   349\t        let empty = TempSource::new(&format!(\"nexus_cst_empty_{}.rs\", std::process::id()));\n   350\t        std::fs::write(empty.path(), \"\").unwrap();\n   351\t        assert!(parse_cst_symbols(empty.path(), &empty.file_name(), None).unwrap().is_empty());\n   352\t        let empty_outline = generate_file_outline(&std::env::temp_dir(), OutlineFileArgs { path: empty.file_name() }).unwrap();\n   353\t        assert_eq!(empty_outline.total_lines, 0);\n   354\t        assert_eq!(empty_outline.symbol_count, 0);\n   355\t    }\n   356\t}\n     1\t# DEFECT: CST symbol/outline tools read an unbounded file\n     2\t\n     3\t| | |\n     4\t|---|---|\n     5\t| Base revision | `41b381ddac182b7f0c783b33df5f1355518f465b` (`origin/main`) |\n     6\t| Branch | `v1/defect-cst-unbounded` |\n     7\t| Affected behavior | `parse_cst_symbols` collected every line of the target into memory, and `generate_file_outline` then read the whole file again with `std::fs::read_to_string`. Both are reachable from the model through `cst_symbols`, `outline_file` and `scan_workspace_cst`, with no `MAX_READ_BYTES` check. A multi-gigabyte source file therefore allocates the whole file in the single Rust bridge, blocking or OOM-ing the agent, even though `read_file`/`file_info`/`edit_file` now stop at 8 MB. |\n     8\t| Severity | Medium: same bridge-wide availability impact as the previous whole-file-read defects, triggered by a workspace file the model is asked to outline or scan. |\n     9\t\n    10\t## Reproduction (pre-fix)\n    11\t\n    12\tUnit probe: create a `.rs` file of `MAX_READ_BYTES + 1` bytes (one declaration plus filler comments) and call\n    13\t`parse_cst_symbols` / `generate_file_outline`.\n    14\t\n    15\t```\n    16\tthread panicked: parse_cst_symbols must refuse a file above the read limit\n    17\t```\n    18\t\n    19\tBoth returned `Ok` on the base source after reading the whole 8 MB + 1 file (the pre-fix test took ~2 s for that\n    20\tsize; the cost is linear in file size).\n    21\t\n    22\t## Fix\n    23\t\n    24\tAdd one bounded `read_source_file` helper: `fstat` the opened file, refuse above `MAX_READ_BYTES`, and read through\n    25\t`take(MAX_READ_BYTES + 1)` with a re-check so growth after the check cannot allocate without bound.\n    26\t`parse_cst_symbols` reads once and delegates to a new `parse_cst_content`; `generate_file_outline` also reads once\n    27\tthrough the helper and parses that same content, so it no longer has a second unchecked `read_to_string` and its\n    28\tsize refusal does not depend on the parser's.\n    29\t\n    30\t## Verification\n    31\t\n    32\t- Separate `test_cst_refuses_files_above_the_read_limit` and\n    33\t  `test_cst_outline_refuses_files_above_the_read_limit` tests: both fail independently on the base source\n    34\t  (`parse_cst_symbols` and `generate_file_outline` each returned `Ok` for 8 MB + 1) and pass after the change. The\n    35\t  outline test pins its own read path rather than relying on the parser's error.\n    36\t- `test_cst_accepts_the_read_limit_and_empty_files` pins the exact 8 MB boundary (still parsed/outlined), a zero-byte\n    37\t  file, and their line/symbol counts.\n    38\t- Existing symbol-parsing/outline test still passes; full `cargo test --bin harness-core` 40/40; `cargo check` has no\n    39\t  warnings.\n    40\t- `cargo check --bin harness-core` has no unused-import warning; `git diff --check`: pass.\n    41\t\n    42\t## Residual risk\n    43\t\n    44\t- The bound is per file. `scan_workspace_cst` still walks up to depth 5 and accumulates symbols from every source file;\n    45\t  total work is proportional to workspace size (each individual file is now capped). Directory scans use\n    46\t  `if let Ok(syms)`, so an oversized file inside a directory is silently omitted (the same path passed as a file\n    47\t  returns the 8 MB error).\n    48\t- The bounded text and its line vector are retained together while parsing, so peak memory at the cap is somewhat\n    49\t  above the file size; an 8 MB file no longer scales with larger input.\n    50\t- Query filtering still happens after parsing; the whole (bounded) file is parsed even when only one symbol matches.\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":875940133}},"started_at_ms":1792865544442,"completed_at_ms":1792865545318}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-24T18:12:26.505Z","ordinal":300962,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a16f1d-3109-7153-a34a-b652e6bc46c8","call_id":"call_4ff1b6e3c9434fc2973039008bea3f8f","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 3.6 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"     1\tuse regex::Regex;\n     2\tuse serde::{Deserialize, Serialize};\n     3\tuse std::fs::File;\n     4\tuse std::io::{BufReader, Read};\n     5\tuse std::path::Path;\n     6\tuse walkdir::WalkDir;\n     7\t\n     8\tuse crate::file_ops::MAX_READ_BYTES;\n     9\t\n    10\t/// Reads a source file for symbol parsing, bounded like the file tools: a huge file must not allocate unbounded\n    11\t/// memory here. The cap also covers growth after the size check.\n    12\tfn read_source_file(file_path: &Path) -> Result<String, String> {\n    13\t    let file = File::open(file_path).map_err(|e| format!(\"Failed to open file: {e}\"))?;\n    14\t    let size = file.metadata().map_err(|e| format!(\"Failed to get metadata: {e}\"))?.len();\n    15\t    if size > MAX_READ_BYTES as u64 {\n    16\t        return Err(format!(\n    17\t            \"File is too large to parse: {size} bytes exceeds the 8 MB limit ({MAX_READ_BYTES} bytes)\"\n    18\t        ));\n    19\t    }\n    20\t    let mut content = String::new();\n    21\t    BufReader::new(file)\n    22\t        .take(MAX_READ_BYTES as u64 + 1)\n    23\t        .read_to_string(&mut content)\n    24\t        .map_err(|e| format!(\"Failed to read file: {e}\"))?;\n    25\t    if content.len() > MAX_READ_BYTES {\n    26\t        return Err(format!(\n    27\t            \"File is too large to parse: it grew beyond the 8 MB limit ({MAX_READ_BYTES} bytes)\"\n    28\t        ));\n    29\t    }\n    30\t    Ok(content)\n    31\t}\n    32\t\n    33\t#[derive(Debug, Serialize, Deserialize, Clone)]\n    34\tpub struct CstSymbol {\n    35\t    pub name: String,\n    36\t    pub kind: String,\n    37\t    pub visibility: String,\n    38\t    pub scope: Option<String>,\n    39\t    pub file: String,\n    40\t    pub start_line: usize,\n    41\t    pub end_line: usize,\n    42\t    pub signature: String,\n    43\t    pub doc_comment: Option<String>,\n    44\t}\n    45\t\n    46\t#[derive(Debug, Serialize, Deserialize)]\n    47\tpub struct CstParseArgs {\n    48\t    pub path: String,\n    49\t    pub query: Option<String>,\n    50\t}\n    51\t\n    52\t#[derive(Debug, Serialize, Deserialize)]\n    53\tpub struct CstParseResult {\n    54\t    pub total_symbols: usize,\n    55\t    pub symbols: Vec<CstSymbol>,\n    56\t}\n    57\t\n    58\t/**\n    59\t * Concrete Syntax Tree (CST) Symbol Parser (Candidate #04)\n    60\t * Parses multiline signatures, doc comments, visibility, and scopes across languages.\n    61\t */\n    62\tpub fn parse_cst_symbols(file_path: &Path, rel_path: &str, query_filter: Option<&str>) -> Result<Vec<CstSymbol>, String> {\n    63\t    let content = read_source_file(file_path)?;\n    64\t    let ext = file_path.extension().and_then(|s| s.to_str()).unwrap_or(\"\");\n    65\t    Ok(parse_cst_content(&content, rel_path, query_filter, ext))\n    66\t}\n    67\t\n    68\t/// Parses already-bounded source text, so a caller that has the content (an outline) does not read the file again.\n    69\tfn parse_cst_content(content: &str, rel_path: &str, query_filter: Option<&str>, ext: &str) -> Vec<CstSymbol> {\n    70\t    let lines: Vec<String> = content.lines().map(|line| line.to_string()).collect();\n    71\t    let mut symbols = Vec::new();\n    72\t\n    73\t    let doc_regex = Regex::new(r\"^\\s*(?://[/!]|\\s*\\*\\s*|#\\s*|/\\*\\*|<!--)(.*)\").unwrap();\n    74\t    let current_scope: Option<String> = None;\n    75\t\n    76\t    // Pattern matching declaration headers\n    77\t    let decl_regex = Regex::new(\n    78\t        r\"(?m)^\\s*(pub(?:\\([^)]+\\))?\\s+)?(async\\s+)?(export\\s+)?(default\\s+)?(fn|function|def|class|struct|interface|trait|type|enum|func)\\s+([A-Za-z0-9_]+)(.*)\"\n    79\t    ).unwrap();\n    80\t\n    81\t    let mut pending_doc = Vec::new();\n    82\t    let mut i = 0;\n    83\t\n    84\t    while i < lines.len() {\n    85\t        let line = &lines[i];\n    86\t        let trimmed = line.trim();\n    87\t\n    88\t        // Accumulate preceding doc comments\n    89\t        if (trimmed.starts_with(\"///\") || trimmed.starts_with(\"//!\") || trimmed.starts_with(\"/**\") || (trimmed.starts_with('*') && !trimmed.starts_with(\"*/\")) || (ext == \"py\" && trimmed.starts_with('#'))) && !trimmed.starts_with(\"/*\") {\n    90\t            if let Some(caps) = doc_regex.captures(trimmed) {\n    91\t                let comment = caps.get(1).map(|m| m.as_str().trim()).unwrap_or(\"\");\n    92\t                if !comment.is_empty() {\n    93\t                    pending_doc.push(comment.to_string());\n    94\t                }\n    95\t            }\n    96\t            i += 1;\n    97\t            continue;\n    98\t        }\n    99\t\n   100\t        if let Some(caps) = decl_regex.captures(trimmed) {\n   101\t            let vis_raw = caps.get(1).map(|m| m.as_str().trim()).unwrap_or(\"\");\n   102\t            let export_raw = caps.get(3).map(|m| m.as_str().trim()).unwrap_or(\"\");\n   103\t            let kind = caps.get(5).map(|m| m.as_str().trim()).unwrap_or(\"unknown\").to_string();\n   104\t            let name = caps.get(6).map(|m| m.as_str().trim()).unwrap_or(\"\").to_string();\n   105\t\n   106\t            let visibility = if !vis_raw.is_empty() {\n   107\t                vis_raw.to_string()\n   108\t            } else if !export_raw.is_empty() {\n   109\t                \"exported\".to_string()\n   110\t            } else {\n   111\t                \"private\".to_string()\n   112\t            };\n   113\t\n   114\t            let start_line = i + 1;\n   115\t            let mut sig_lines = vec![trimmed.to_string()];\n   116\t            let mut end_line = start_line;\n   117\t\n   118\t            // Multiline signature accumulation until '{', ';', or ':' (python)\n   119\t            if !trimmed.contains('{') && !trimmed.contains(';') && !(ext == \"py\" && trimmed.ends_with(':')) {\n   120\t                let mut j = i + 1;\n   121\t                while j < lines.len() && j < i + 10 {\n   122\t                    let next_trimmed = lines[j].trim();\n   123\t                    sig_lines.push(next_trimmed.to_string());\n   124\t                    if next_trimmed.contains('{') || next_trimmed.contains(';') || (ext == \"py\" && next_trimmed.ends_with(':')) {\n   125\t                        end_line = j + 1;\n   126\t                        i = j;\n   127\t                        break;\n   128\t                    }\n   129\t                    j += 1;\n   130\t                }\n   131\t            }\n   132\t\n   133\t            let full_sig = sig_lines.join(\" \");\n   134\t            let doc_text = if !pending_doc.is_empty() {\n   135\t                Some(pending_doc.join(\"\\n\"))\n   136\t            } else {\n   137\t                None\n   138\t            };\n   139\t            pending_doc.clear();\n   140\t\n   141\t            let matches_query = match query_filter {\n   142\t                Some(q) => name.to_lowercase().contains(&q.to_lowercase()),\n   143\t                None => true,\n   144\t            };\n   145\t\n   146\t            if matches_query && !name.is_empty() {\n   147\t                symbols.push(CstSymbol {\n   148\t                    name,\n   149\t                    kind,\n   150\t                    visibility,\n   151\t                    scope: current_scope.clone(),\n   152\t                    file: rel_path.to_string(),\n   153\t                    start_line,\n   154\t                    end_line,\n   155\t                    signature: full_sig,\n   156\t                    doc_comment: doc_text,\n   157\t                });\n   158\t            }\n   159\t        } else if !trimmed.is_empty() {\n   160\t            pending_doc.clear();\n   161\t        }\n   162\t\n   163\t        i += 1;\n   164\t    }\n   165\t\n   166\t    symbols\n   167\t}\n   168\t\n   169\t/**\n   170\t * Scan workspace files and parse CST symbols\n   171\t */\n   172\tpub fn scan_workspace_cst(base_dir: &Path, args: CstParseArgs) -> Result<CstParseResult, String> {\n   173\t    let target = crate::file_ops::resolve_safe_path(base_dir, &args.path)?;\n   174\t    let mut all_symbols = Vec::new();\n   175\t\n   176\t    if target.is_file() {\n   177\t        let rel_path = target.strip_prefix(base_dir).unwrap_or(&target).to_string_lossy().to_string();\n   178\t        let syms = parse_cst_symbols(&target, &rel_path, args.query.as_deref())?;\n   179\t        all_symbols.extend(syms);\n   180\t    } else if target.is_dir() {\n   181\t        for entry in WalkDir::new(&target).max_depth(5).into_iter().filter_map(|e| e.ok()) {\n   182\t            let p = entry.path();\n   183\t            if p.is_file() {\n   184\t                let ext = p.extension().and_then(|s| s.to_str()).unwrap_or(\"\");\n   185\t                if matches!(ext, \"rs\" | \"ts\" | \"tsx\" | \"js\" | \"jsx\" | \"py\" | \"go\") {\n   186\t                    let rel_path = p.strip_prefix(base_dir).unwrap_or(p).to_string_lossy().to_string();\n   187\t                    if let Ok(syms) = parse_cst_symbols(p, &rel_path, args.query.as_deref()) {\n   188\t                        all_symbols.extend(syms);\n   189\t                    }\n   190\t                }\n   230\t    } else {\n   231\t        for s in &symbols {\n   232\t            let doc_hint = s.doc_comment.as_ref()\n   233\t                .and_then(|d| d.lines().next())\n   234\t                .map(|line| format!(\" - \\\"{}\\\"\", line.trim()))\n   235\t                .unwrap_or_default();\n   236\t            outline_str.push_str(&format!(\n   237\t                \"- [{}] {} (lines {}-{}) [{}]{}\\n\",\n   238\t                s.kind, s.name, s.start_line, s.end_line, s.visibility, doc_hint\n   239\t            ));\n   240\t        }\n   241\t    }\n   242\t\n   243\t    Ok(OutlineFileResult {\n   244\t        path: args.path,\n   245\t        total_lines,\n   246\t        symbol_count: symbols.len(),\n   247\t        outline: outline_str,\n   248\t    })\n   249\t}\n   250\t\n   251\t#[cfg(test)]\n   252\tmod tests {\n   253\t    use super::*;\n   254\t\n   255\t    #[test]\n   256\t    fn test_cst_symbol_parsing() {\n   257\t        let tmp = std::env::temp_dir().join(\"nexus_cst_test.rs\");\n   258\t        let code = r#\"\n   259\t/// High-level engine runner\n   260\tpub async fn execute_task(\n   261\t    id: &str,\n   262\t    timeout: u64,\n   263\t) -> Result<bool, String> {\n   264\t    Ok(true)\n   265\t}\n   266\t\"#;\n   267\t        std::fs::write(&tmp, code).unwrap();\n   268\t        let syms = parse_cst_symbols(&tmp, \"test.rs\", None).unwrap();\n   269\t        assert_eq!(syms.len(), 1);\n   270\t        let s = &syms[0];\n   271\t        assert_eq!(s.name, \"execute_task\");\n   272\t        assert_eq!(s.kind, \"fn\");\n   273\t        assert_eq!(s.visibility, \"pub\");\n   274\t        assert!(s.signature.contains(\"-> Result<bool, String>\"));\n   275\t        assert!(s.doc_comment.as_ref().unwrap().contains(\"High-level engine runner\"));\n   276\t\n   277\t        let outline_res = generate_file_outline(&std::env::temp_dir(), OutlineFileArgs {\n   278\t            path: \"nexus_cst_test.rs\".into(),\n   279\t        }).unwrap();\n   280\t        assert_eq!(outline_res.symbol_count, 1);\n   281\t        assert!(outline_res.outline.contains(\"- [fn] execute_task\"));\n   282\t        assert!(outline_res.outline.contains(\"lines\"));\n   283\t\n   284\t        let _ = std::fs::remove_file(tmp);\n   285\t    }\n   286\t\n   287\t    struct TempSource(std::path::PathBuf);\n   288\t\n   289\t    impl TempSource {\n   290\t        fn new(name: &str) -> Self {\n   291\t            Self(std::env::temp_dir().join(name))\n   292\t        }\n   293\t\n   294\t        fn path(&self) -> &Path {\n   295\t            &self.0\n   296\t        }\n   297\t\n   298\t        fn file_name(&self) -> String {\n   299\t            self.0.file_name().unwrap().to_string_lossy().to_string()\n   300\t        }\n   301\t    }\n   302\t\n   303\t    impl Drop for TempSource {\n   304\t        fn drop(&mut self) {\n   305\t            let _ = std::fs::remove_file(&self.0);\n   306\t        }\n   307\t    }\n   308\t\n   309\t    fn oversized_source(name: &str) -> TempSource {\n   310\t        let tmp = TempSource::new(name);\n   311\t        let mut code = String::from(\"pub fn first() {}\\n\");\n   312\t        while code.len() <= MAX_READ_BYTES {\n   313\t            code.push_str(\"// filler comment line\\n\");\n   314\t        }\n   315\t        std::fs::write(tmp.path(), &code).unwrap();\n   316\t        tmp\n   317\t    }\n   318\t\n   319\t    #[test]\n   320\t    fn test_cst_refuses_files_above_the_read_limit() {\n   321\t        let tmp = oversized_source(&format!(\"nexus_cst_big_{}.rs\", std::process::id()));\n   322\t        let parsed = parse_cst_symbols(tmp.path(), &tmp.file_name(), None);\n   323\t        assert!(parsed.is_err(), \"parse_cst_symbols must refuse a file above the read limit\");\n   324\t        assert!(parsed.unwrap_err().contains(\"8 MB\"));\n   325\t    }\n   326\t\n   327\t    #[test]\n   328\t    fn test_cst_outline_refuses_files_above_the_read_limit() {\n   329\t        let tmp = oversized_source(&format!(\"nexus_cst_big_outline_{}.rs\", std::process::id()));\n   330\t        // generate_file_outline must enforce the limit itself, not rely on the parser's refusal.\n   331\t        let outline = generate_file_outline(&std::env::temp_dir(), OutlineFileArgs { path: tmp.file_name() });\n   332\t        assert!(outline.is_err(), \"generate_file_outline must refuse a file above the read limit\");\n   333\t        assert!(outline.unwrap_err().contains(\"8 MB\"));\n   334\t    }\n   335\t\n   336\t    #[test]\n   337\t    fn test_cst_accepts_the_read_limit_and_empty_files() {\n   338\t        let at_limit = TempSource::new(&format!(\"nexus_cst_at_limit_{}.rs\", std::process::id()));\n   339\t        let first = \"pub fn first() {}\\n\";\n   340\t        let mut code = String::from(first);\n   341\t        code.push_str(&\"x\".repeat(MAX_READ_BYTES - first.len()));\n   342\t        std::fs::write(at_limit.path(), &code).unwrap();\n   343\t        let parsed = parse_cst_symbols(at_limit.path(), &at_limit.file_name(), None).unwrap();\n   344\t        assert_eq!(parsed.len(), 1);\n   345\t        let outline = generate_file_outline(&std::env::temp_dir(), OutlineFileArgs { path: at_limit.file_name() }).unwrap();\n   346\t        assert_eq!(outline.total_lines, 2);\n   347\t        assert_eq!(outline.symbol_count, 1);\n   348\t\n   349\t        let empty = TempSource::new(&format!(\"nexus_cst_empty_{}.rs\", std::process::id()));\n   350\t        std::fs::write(empty.path(), \"\").unwrap();\n   351\t        assert!(parse_cst_symbols(empty.path(), &empty.file_name(), None).unwrap().is_empty());\n   352\t        let empty_outline = generate_file_outline(&std::env::temp_dir(), OutlineFileArgs { path: empty.file_name() }).unwrap();\n   353\t        assert_eq!(empty_outline.total_lines, 0);\n   354\t        assert_eq!(empty_outline.symbol_count, 0);\n   355\t    }\n   356\t}\n     1\t# DEFECT: CST symbol/outline tools read an unbounded file\n     2\t\n     3\t| | |\n     4\t|---|---|\n     5\t| Base revision | `41b381ddac182b7f0c783b33df5f1355518f465b` (`origin/main`) |\n     6\t| Branch | `v1/defect-cst-unbounded` |\n     7\t| Affected behavior | `parse_cst_symbols` collected every line of the target into memory, and `generate_file_outline` then read the whole file again with `std::fs::read_to_string`. Both are reachable from the model through `cst_symbols`, `outline_file` and `scan_workspace_cst`, with no `MAX_READ_BYTES` check. A multi-gigabyte source file therefore allocates the whole file in the single Rust bridge, blocking or OOM-ing the agent, even though `read_file`/`file_info`/`edit_file` now stop at 8 MB. |\n     8\t| Severity | Medium: same bridge-wide availability impact as the previous whole-file-read defects, triggered by a workspace file the model is asked to outline or scan. |\n     9\t\n    10\t## Reproduction (pre-fix)\n    11\t\n    12\tUnit probe: create a `.rs` file of `MAX_READ_BYTES + 1` bytes (one declaration plus filler comments) and call\n    13\t`parse_cst_symbols` / `generate_file_outline`.\n    14\t\n    15\t```\n    16\tthread panicked: parse_cst_symbols must refuse a file above the read limit\n    17\t```\n    18\t\n    19\tBoth returned `Ok` on the base source after reading the whole 8 MB + 1 file (the pre-fix test took ~2 s for that\n    20\tsize; the cost is linear in file size).\n    21\t\n    22\t## Fix\n    23\t\n    24\tAdd one bounded `read_source_file` helper: `fstat` the opened file, refuse above `MAX_READ_BYTES`, and read through\n    25\t`take(MAX_READ_BYTES + 1)` with a re-check so growth after the check cannot allocate without bound.\n    26\t`parse_cst_symbols` reads once and delegates to a new `parse_cst_content`; `generate_file_outline` also reads once\n    27\tthrough the helper and parses that same content, so it no longer has a second unchecked `read_to_string` and its\n    28\tsize refusal does not depend on the parser's.\n    29\t\n    30\t## Verification\n    31\t\n    32\t- Separate `test_cst_refuses_files_above_the_read_limit` and\n    33\t  `test_cst_outline_refuses_files_above_the_read_limit` tests: both fail independently on the base source\n    34\t  (`parse_cst_symbols` and `generate_file_outline` each returned `Ok` for 8 MB + 1) and pass after the change. The\n    35\t  outline test pins its own read path rather than relying on the parser's error.\n    36\t- `test_cst_accepts_the_read_limit_and_empty_files` pins the exact 8 MB boundary (still parsed/outlined), a zero-byte\n    37\t  file, and their line/symbol counts.\n    38\t- Existing symbol-parsing/outline test still passes; full `cargo test --bin harness-core` 40/40; `cargo check` has no\n    39\t  warnings.\n    40\t- `cargo check --bin harness-core` has no unused-import warning; `git diff --check`: pass.\n    41\t\n    42\t## Residual risk\n    43\t\n    44\t- The bound is per file. `scan_workspace_cst` still walks up to depth 5 and accumulates symbols from every source file;\n    45\t  total work is proportional to workspace size (each individual file is now capped). Directory scans use\n    46\t  `if let Ok(syms)`, so an oversized file inside a directory is silently omitted (the same path passed as a file\n    47\t  returns the 8 MB error).\n    48\t- The bounded text and its line vector are retained together while parsing, so peak memory at the cap is somewhat\n    49\t  above the file size; an 8 MB file no longer scales with larger input.\n    50\t- Query filtering still happens after parsing; the whole (bounded) file is parsed even when only one symbol matches.\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a16f1a-0d89-7262-a71e-eb3a6dfcc08e","create_time":1792865546.5050933}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
