-and-egress.md) | M1 | SEC-110, 111, 115, 116 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/EVIDENCE.md:72:3. **Files created or changed in the repository.** The audit created `docs/v1.0.0/**`. At the owner's request, it appended a short \"v1.0.0 work and concurrent agents\" section to the root `AGENTS.md`, without changing the existing content. Nothing else in the repository was modified.\ndocs/v1.0.0/AUDIT.md:148:| tasks/, AGENTS.md, README, quickstart | 5 | Full read | lead | — |\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:9:| [DEC-01](#dec-01-default-execution-posture) | Default execution posture | Review by default; auto only in trusted workspaces | No (resolved) |\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:36:| **C (chosen)** | Posture follows workspace trust. **Untrusted workspace → review** for `write_workspace`, `exec`, `egress` and `context_inject`. **Trusted workspace → auto** for `write_workspace` and `exec`; `egress` asks once per origin per session. `--yes` or `NEXUS_APPROVAL_MODE=auto` force auto. `--sandbox` stays available. | Safe for cloned or unknown repos. Low friction on the operator's own repos after one `nexus trust .`. Reuses the existing trust store, so there is no new concept. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:119:| REQ-SEC-101 | Audit; DEC-01 | Without opt-in, no model-initiated exec or egress happens without a decision. Untrusted workspace → review; trusted → auto. | safety | `config.ts`, `sidecar.ts:935`, `repl.ts:69`, `index.ts:93,115` | TEST `approval_policy.test.ts`, `tui_surface_e2e.test.ts`, `repl_approval_e2e.test.ts` | tested | ACC-SAFE-01 | **B** | SEC-01, TUI-07 | SPEC-01 / PLAN-01 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md:3:These rules apply to every agent (Claude Code, Codex, Cursor, Nexus itself, or a human) that implements any part of this package at the same time as another. The repository's root `AGENTS.md` points here. The rules come from incidents recorded in `tasks/lessons.md`:\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-01-safe-execution-defaults.md:5:| Status | Ready. Default posture resolved by [DEC-01](../DECISIONS.md#dec-01-default-execution-posture) (option C: review in untrusted workspaces, auto in trusted ones). |\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-01-safe-execution-defaults.md:62:   - In an untrusted workspace, the first verifier run requires a one-time approval. The approval shows the exact command and the script body it resolves to (for example the `scripts.test` entry, or the Makefile `test:` recipe).\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-01-safe-execution-defaults.md:63:   - In a trusted workspace, they run without asking under the auto posture.\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-01-safe-execution-defaults.md:144:- Changing the default for untrusted workspaces from `auto` to review (DEC-01 option C) is a user-visible change. Release notes and the startup banner must state it. Provide `NEXUS_APPROVAL_MODE=auto` and `nexus trust .` + `--yes` for scripted users.\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-01-safe-execution-defaults.md:168:| ACC-SAFE-01 | Fresh HOME, `nexus` (TUI) and `nexus repl`, mock gateway scripted to call `run_command \"echo x > ../outside\"`: in an untrusted workspace the call is not executed without an approval panel. After `nexus trust .` it runs without a panel (DEC-01 option C). | PTY |\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-01-safe-execution-defaults.md:181:- **DEC-01** is resolved as option C (review in untrusted workspaces, auto in trusted ones). Nothing in this spec is blocked.\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-03-untrusted-inputs-and-egress.md:1:# PLAN-03: Untrusted workspace inputs and the egress boundary\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-03-untrusted-inputs-and-egress.md:1:# SPEC-03: Untrusted workspace inputs and the egress boundary\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-03-untrusted-inputs-and-egress.md:42:4. **REQ-SEC-113.** Workspace skills and workspace `knowledge.json` are loaded only for trusted workspaces. In an untrusted workspace they are listed by `/skills` as \"untrusted (not loaded)\", and `activate_skill` on one is refused with the `nexus trust` hint.\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-03-untrusted-inputs-and-egress.md:46:6. **REQ-SEC-115.** Nexus loads plugins only from its own documented directories (`~/.config/nexus/plugins`, `~/.nexus/plugins`, and trusted workspace dirs). `~/.config/opencode/plugins` is removed.\ncli/test/inference_transport.test.ts:95:      frame({ choices: [{ index: 0, delta: { tool_calls: [{ index: 0, function: { arguments: 'th\":\"AGENTS.md\"}' } }] } }] }) +\ncli/test/inference_transport.test.ts:104:        assert.deepEqual(m.tool_calls?.map((t) => [t.id, t.function.name, t.function.arguments]), [[\"c1\", \"read_file\", '{\"path\":\"AGENTS.md\"}']]);\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/A2_verification.md:134:| R-VER-1 | Repo-defined verifier commands (discovered) run only in a trusted workspace or after one approval that shows the command and script body. They run sandboxed when a sandbox is available. | safety | RELEASE-REQUIRED | An untrusted temp repo with `\"test\":\"touch /tmp/pwn\"` plus an edit request: no file created without a prompt, in both default and --approve modes. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/C_tools_security_persistence.md:37:  - `.nexus-security.json` is read from the untrusted workspace (security.ts:48). It can only add entries, except that `allowedDomains` narrows egress and `allowExternalSymlinks` is never consumed.\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/D_terminal.md:63:| TUI-07 | S2 | Default safety posture | sidecar.ts:935; repl.ts:69; quickstart.md:55 | SOURCE + DOC-CLAIM: default mode is `auto` (no approvals) for both surfaces; quickstart says \"Enter a small task, review requested actions\" | New users unknowingly grant the model unprompted write/shell authority | Decide v1 default (recommend review on first run / untrusted workspace); fix quickstart wording |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/D_terminal.md:147:| TUI-R6 | Default approval posture is an explicit, documented decision; first run in an untrusted workspace states the mode and how to change it | safety (TUI-07) | RELEASE-REQUIRED | PTY first-run screen contains mode + switch hint; docs match |\ncli/src/slash/catalog.ts:114:  { name