{"timestamp":"2026-10-24T18:14:01.298Z","ordinal":301040,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a16f1a-0d89-7262-a71e-eb3a6dfcc08e","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-41318e43-a19e-413c-9bcb-3ed28b65660e","process_id":"9831","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","sed -n '1,170p' /home/mike/nexus-wt/cst-unbounded-rebase/core/src/cst.rs; sed -n '170,280p' /home/mike/nexus-wt/cst-unbounded-rebase/core/src/cst.rs; sed -n '1,110p' /home/mike/nexus-wt/cst-unbounded-rebase/docs/reviews/evidence/v1/DEFECT-CST-UNBOUNDED-20261024/README.md; git -C /home/mike/nexus-wt/cst-unbounded-rebase status --short --branch; cat /home/mike/nexus-code/.git/nexus-claims/DEFECT_CST_UNBOUNDED_REBASE_20261024/owner.json"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"sed -n '1,170p' /home/mike/nexus-wt/cst-unbounded-rebase/core/src/cst.rs; sed -n '170,280p' /home/mike/nexus-wt/cst-unbounded-rebase/core/src/cst.rs; sed -n '1,110p' /home/mike/nexus-wt/cst-unbounded-rebase/docs/reviews/evidence/v1/DEFECT-CST-UNBOUNDED-20261024/README.md; git -C /home/mike/nexus-wt/cst-unbounded-rebase status --short --branch; cat /home/mike/nexus-code/.git/nexus-claims/DEFECT_CST_UNBOUNDED_REBASE_20261024/owner.json"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"use regex::Regex;\nuse serde::{Deserialize, Serialize};\nuse std::fs::File;\nuse std::io::{BufReader, Read};\nuse std::path::Path;\nuse walkdir::WalkDir;\n\nuse crate::file_ops::MAX_READ_BYTES;\n\n/// Reads a source file for symbol parsing, bounded like the file tools: a huge file must not allocate unbounded\n/// memory here. The cap also covers growth after the size check.\nfn read_source_file(file_path: &Path) -> Result<String, String> {\n    let file = File::open(file_path).map_err(|e| format!(\"Failed to open file: {e}\"))?;\n    let size = file.metadata().map_err(|e| format!(\"Failed to get metadata: {e}\"))?.len();\n    if size > MAX_READ_BYTES as u64 {\n        return Err(format!(\n            \"File is too large to parse: {size} bytes exceeds the 8 MB limit ({MAX_READ_BYTES} bytes)\"\n        ));\n    }\n    let mut content = String::new();\n    BufReader::new(file)\n        .take(MAX_READ_BYTES as u64 + 1)\n        .read_to_string(&mut content)\n        .map_err(|e| format!(\"Failed to read file: {e}\"))?;\n    if content.len() > MAX_READ_BYTES {\n        return Err(format!(\n            \"File is too large to parse: it grew beyond the 8 MB limit ({MAX_READ_BYTES} bytes)\"\n        ));\n    }\n    Ok(content)\n}\n\n#[derive(Debug, Serialize, Deserialize, Clone)]\npub struct CstSymbol {\n    pub name: String,\n    pub kind: String,\n    pub visibility: String,\n    pub scope: Option<String>,\n    pub file: String,\n    pub start_line: usize,\n    pub end_line: usize,\n    pub signature: String,\n    pub doc_comment: Option<String>,\n}\n\n#[derive(Debug, Serialize, Deserialize)]\npub struct CstParseArgs {\n    pub path: String,\n    pub query: Option<String>,\n}\n\n#[derive(Debug, Serialize, Deserialize)]\npub struct CstParseResult {\n    pub total_symbols: usize,\n    pub symbols: Vec<CstSymbol>,\n}\n\n/**\n * Concrete Syntax Tree (CST) Symbol Parser (Candidate #04)\n * Parses multiline signatures, doc comments, visibility, and scopes across languages.\n */\npub fn parse_cst_symbols(file_path: &Path, rel_path: &str, query_filter: Option<&str>) -> Result<Vec<CstSymbol>, String> {\n    let content = read_source_file(file_path)?;\n    let ext = file_path.extension().and_then(|s| s.to_str()).unwrap_or(\"\");\n    Ok(parse_cst_content(&content, rel_path, query_filter, ext))\n}\n\n/// Parses already-bounded source text, so a caller that has the content (an outline) does not read the file again.\nfn parse_cst_content(content: &str, rel_path: &str, query_filter: Option<&str>, ext: &str) -> Vec<CstSymbol> {\n    let lines: Vec<String> = content.lines().map(|line| line.to_string()).collect();\n    let mut symbols = Vec::new();\n\n    let doc_regex = Regex::new(r\"^\\s*(?://[/!]|\\s*\\*\\s*|#\\s*|/\\*\\*|<!--)(.*)\").unwrap();\n    let current_scope: Option<String> = None;\n\n    // Pattern matching declaration headers\n    let decl_regex = Regex::new(\n        r\"(?m)^\\s*(pub(?:\\([^)]+\\))?\\s+)?(async\\s+)?(export\\s+)?(default\\s+)?(fn|function|def|class|struct|interface|trait|type|enum|func)\\s+([A-Za-z0-9_]+)(.*)\"\n    ).unwrap();\n\n    let mut pending_doc = Vec::new();\n    let mut i = 0;\n\n    while i < lines.len() {\n        let line = &lines[i];\n        let trimmed = line.trim();\n\n        // Accumulate preceding doc comments\n        if (trimmed.starts_with(\"///\") || trimmed.starts_with(\"//!\") || trimmed.starts_with(\"/**\") || (trimmed.starts_with('*') && !trimmed.starts_with(\"*/\")) || (ext == \"py\" && trimmed.starts_with('#'))) && !trimmed.starts_with(\"/*\") {\n            if let Some(caps) = doc_regex.captures(trimmed) {\n                let comment = caps.get(1).map(|m| m.as_str().trim()).unwrap_or(\"\");\n                if !comment.is_empty() {\n                    pending_doc.push(comment.to_string());\n                }\n            }\n            i += 1;\n            continue;\n        }\n\n        if let Some(caps) = decl_regex.captures(trimmed) {\n            let vis_raw = caps.get(1).map(|m| m.as_str().trim()).unwrap_or(\"\");\n            let export_raw = caps.get(3).map(|m| m.as_str().trim()).unwrap_or(\"\");\n            let kind = caps.get(5).map(|m| m.as_str().trim()).unwrap_or(\"unknown\").to_string();\n            let name = caps.get(6).map(|m| m.as_str().trim()).unwrap_or(\"\").to_string();\n\n            let visibility = if !vis_raw.is_empty() {\n                vis_raw.to_string()\n            } else if !export_raw.is_empty() {\n                \"exported\".to_string()\n            } else {\n                \"private\".to_string()\n            };\n\n            let start_line = i + 1;\n            let mut sig_lines = vec![trimmed.to_string()];\n            let mut end_line = start_line;\n\n            // Multiline signature accumulation until '{', ';', or ':' (python)\n            if !trimmed.contains('{') && !trimmed.contains(';') && !(ext == \"py\" && trimmed.ends_with(':')) {\n                let mut j = i + 1;\n                while j < lines.len() && j < i + 10 {\n                    let next_trimmed = lines[j].trim();\n                    sig_lines.push(next_trimmed.to_string());\n                    if next_trimmed.contains('{') || next_trimmed.contains(';') || (ext == \"py\" && next_trimmed.ends_with(':')) {\n                        end_line = j + 1;\n                        i = j;\n                        break;\n                    }\n                    j += 1;\n                }\n            }\n\n            let full_sig = sig_lines.join(\" \");\n            let doc_text = if !pending_doc.is_empty() {\n                Some(pending_doc.join(\"\\n\"))\n            } else {\n                None\n            };\n            pending_doc.clear();\n\n            let matches_query = match query_filter {\n                Some(q) => name.to_lowercase().contains(&q.to_lowercase()),\n                None => true,\n            };\n\n            if matches_query && !name.is_empty() {\n                symbols.push(CstSymbol {\n                    name,\n                    kind,\n                    visibility,\n                    scope: current_scope.clone(),\n                    file: rel_path.to_string(),\n                    start_line,\n                    end_line,\n                    signature: full_sig,\n                    doc_comment: doc_text,\n                });\n            }\n        } else if !trimmed.is_empty() {\n            pending_doc.clear();\n        }\n\n        i += 1;\n    }\n\n    symbols\n}\n\n/**\n * Scan workspace files and parse CST symbols\n * Scan workspace files and parse CST symbols\n */\npub fn scan_workspace_cst(base_dir: &Path, args: CstParseArgs) -> Result<CstParseResult, String> {\n    let target = crate::file_ops::resolve_safe_path(base_dir, &args.path)?;\n    let mut all_symbols = Vec::new();\n\n    if target.is_file() {\n        let rel_path = target.strip_prefix(base_dir).unwrap_or(&target).to_string_lossy().to_string();\n        let syms = parse_cst_symbols(&target, &rel_path, args.query.as_deref())?;\n        all_symbols.extend(syms);\n    } else if target.is_dir() {\n        for entry in WalkDir::new(&target).max_depth(5).into_iter().filter_map(|e| e.ok()) {\n            let p = entry.path();\n            if p.is_file() {\n                let ext = p.extension().and_then(|s| s.to_str()).unwrap_or(\"\");\n                if matches!(ext, \"rs\" | \"ts\" | \"tsx\" | \"js\" | \"jsx\" | \"py\" | \"go\") {\n                    let rel_path = p.strip_prefix(base_dir).unwrap_or(p).to_string_lossy().to_string();\n                    if let Ok(syms) = parse_cst_symbols(p, &rel_path, args.query.as_deref()) {\n                        all_symbols.extend(syms);\n                    }\n                }\n            }\n        }\n    }\n\n    Ok(CstParseResult {\n        total_symbols: all_symbols.len(),\n        symbols: all_symbols,\n    })\n}\n\n#[derive(Debug, Serialize, Deserialize)]\npub struct OutlineFileArgs {\n    pub path: String,\n}\n\n#[derive(Debug, Serialize, Deserialize)]\npub struct OutlineFileResult {\n    pub path: String,\n    pub total_lines: usize,\n    pub symbol_count: usize,\n    pub outline: String,\n}\n\n/// Generates a compact AST symbol outline for a source file to conserve local LLM context\npub fn generate_file_outline(base_dir: &Path, args: OutlineFileArgs) -> Result<OutlineFileResult, String> {\n    let target = crate::file_ops::resolve_safe_path(base_dir, &args.path)?;\n    if !target.is_file() {\n        return Err(format!(\"File does not exist or is not a file: {}\", args.path));\n    }\n\n    let rel_path = target.strip_prefix(base_dir).unwrap_or(&target).to_string_lossy().to_string();\n    let content = read_source_file(&target)?;\n    let ext = target.extension().and_then(|s| s.to_str()).unwrap_or(\"\");\n    let symbols = parse_cst_content(&content, &rel_path, None, ext);\n    let total_lines = content.lines().count();\n\n    let mut outline_str = format!(\"File: {} ({} lines, {} symbols)\\n\", rel_path, total_lines, symbols.len());\n    if symbols.is_empty() {\n        outline_str.push_str(\"No top-level declarations or exported symbols detected.\\n\");\n    } else {\n        for s in &symbols {\n            let doc_hint = s.doc_comment.as_ref()\n                .and_then(|d| d.lines().next())\n                .map(|line| format!(\" - \\\"{}\\\"\", line.trim()))\n                .unwrap_or_default();\n            outline_str.push_str(&format!(\n                \"- [{}] {} (lines {}-{}) [{}]{}\\n\",\n                s.kind, s.name, s.start_line, s.end_line, s.visibility, doc_hint\n            ));\n        }\n    }\n\n    Ok(OutlineFileResult {\n        path: args.path,\n        total_lines,\n        symbol_count: symbols.len(),\n        outline: outline_str,\n    })\n}\n\n#[cfg(test)]\nmod tests {\n    use super::*;\n\n    #[test]\n    fn test_cst_symbol_parsing() {\n        let tmp = std::env::temp_dir().join(\"nexus_cst_test.rs\");\n        let code = r#\"\n/// High-level engine runner\npub async fn execute_task(\n    id: &str,\n    timeout: u64,\n) -> Result<bool, String> {\n    Ok(true)\n}\n\"#;\n        std::fs::write(&tmp, code).unwrap();\n        let syms = parse_cst_symbols(&tmp, \"test.rs\", None).unwrap();\n        assert_eq!(syms.len(), 1);\n        let s = &syms[0];\n        assert_eq!(s.name, \"execute_task\");\n        assert_eq!(s.kind, \"fn\");\n        assert_eq!(s.visibility, \"pub\");\n        assert!(s.signature.contains(\"-> Result<bool, String>\"));\n        assert!(s.doc_comment.as_ref().unwrap().contains(\"High-level engine runner\"));\n\n        let outline_res = generate_file_outline(&std::env::temp_dir(), OutlineFileArgs {\n            path: \"nexus_cst_test.rs\".into(),\n        }).unwrap();\n        assert_eq!(outline_res.symbol_count, 1);\n# DEFECT: CST symbol/outline tools read an unbounded file\n\n| | |\n|---|---|\n| Base revision | `41b381ddac182b7f0c783b33df5f1355518f465b` (`origin/main`) |\n| Branch | `v1/defect-cst-unbounded` |\n| Affected behavior | `parse_cst_symbols` collected every line of the target into memory, and `generate_file_outline` then read the whole file again with `std::fs::read_to_string`. Both are reachable from the model through `cst_symbols`, `outline_file` and `scan_workspace_cst`, with no `MAX_READ_BYTES` check. A multi-gigabyte source file therefore allocates the whole file in the single Rust bridge, blocking or OOM-ing the agent, even though `read_file`/`file_info`/`edit_file` now stop at 8 MB. |\n| Severity | Medium: same bridge-wide availability impact as the previous whole-file-read defects, triggered by a workspace file the model is asked to outline or scan. |\n\n## Reproduction (pre-fix)\n\nUnit probe: create a `.rs` file of `MAX_READ_BYTES + 1` bytes (one declaration plus filler comments) and call\n`parse_cst_symbols` / `generate_file_outline`.\n\n```\nthread panicked: parse_cst_symbols must refuse a file above the read limit\n```\n\nBoth returned `Ok` on the base source after reading the whole 8 MB + 1 file (the pre-fix test took ~2 s for that\nsize; the cost is linear in file size).\n\n## Fix\n\nAdd one bounded `read_source_file` helper: `fstat` the opened file, refuse above `MAX_READ_BYTES`, and read through\n`take(MAX_READ_BYTES + 1)` with a re-check so growth after the check cannot allocate without bound.\n`parse_cst_symbols` reads once and delegates to a new `parse_cst_content`; `generate_file_outline` also reads once\nthrough the helper and parses that same content, so it no longer has a second unchecked `read_to_string` and its\nsize refusal does not depend on the parser's.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Separate `test_cst_refuses_files_above_the_read_limit` and\n  `test_cst_outline_refuses_files_above_the_read_limit` tests: both fail independently on the base source\n  (`parse_cst_symbols` and `generate_file_outline` each returned `Ok` for 8 MB + 1) and pass after the change. The\n  outline test pins its own read path rather than relying on the parser's error.\n- `test_cst_accepts_the_read_limit_and_empty_files` pins the exact 8 MB boundary (still parsed/outlined), a zero-byte\n  file, and their line/symbol counts.\n- Existing symbol-parsing/outline test still passes; full `cargo test --bin harness-core` 40/40; `cargo check` has no\n  warnings.\n- `cargo check --bin harness-core` has no unused-import warning; `git diff --check`: pass.\n\n## Residual risk\n\n- The bound is per file. `scan_workspace_cst` still walks up to depth 5 and accumulates symbols from every source file;\n  total work is proportional to workspace size (each individual file is now capped). Directory scans use\n  `if let Ok(syms)`, so an oversized file inside a directory is silently omitted (the same path passed as a file\n  returns the 8 MB error).\n- The bounded text and its line vector are retained together while parsing, so peak memory at the cap is somewhat\n  above the file size; an 8 MB file no longer scales with larger input.\n- Query filtering still happens after parsing; the whole (bounded) file is parsed even when only one symbol matches.\n## v1/defect-cst-unbounded-rebase...origin/main [ahead 2]\n{\"agent\":\"codex-root\",\"host\":\"mike-dev\",\"branch\":\"v1/defect-cst-unbounded-rebase\",\"worktree\":\"/home/mike/nexus-wt/cst-unbounded-rebase\",\"base\":\"676abb371c8c91970af6d920d5c516497e3ccdef\",\"since\":\"2026-10-24T18:10:00Z\",\"scope\":\"refresh stalled PR199 CST resource-bound fix onto authoritative main and requalify exact head; preserve prior branch\",\"status\":\"claim recovered after recorded safe-boundary request; owner inactive on recorded host; PR199 CI green on stale base\"}","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":27840}},"started_at_ms":1792865641297,"completed_at_ms":1792865641298}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-24T18:14:02.287Z","ordinal":301041,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a16f1e-a72f-77f1-b67e-6013c50ba8a7","call_id":"call_6194cf349da14c1a8608ed9901d658ac","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 2.1 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"use regex::Regex;\nuse serde::{Deserialize, Serialize};\nuse std::fs::File;\nuse std::io::{BufReader, Read};\nuse std::path::Path;\nuse walkdir::WalkDir;\n\nuse crate::file_ops::MAX_READ_BYTES;\n\n/// Reads a source file for symbol parsing, bounded like the file tools: a huge file must not allocate unbounded\n/// memory here. The cap also covers growth after the size check.\nfn read_source_file(file_path: &Path) -> Result<String, String> {\n    let file = File::open(file_path).map_err(|e| format!(\"Failed to open file: {e}\"))?;\n    let size = file.metadata().map_err(|e| format!(\"Failed to get metadata: {e}\"))?.len();\n    if size > MAX_READ_BYTES as u64 {\n        return Err(format!(\n            \"File is too large to parse: {size} bytes exceeds the 8 MB limit ({MAX_READ_BYTES} bytes)\"\n        ));\n    }\n    let mut content = String::new();\n    BufReader::new(file)\n        .take(MAX_READ_BYTES as u64 + 1)\n        .read_to_string(&mut content)\n        .map_err(|e| format!(\"Failed to read file: {e}\"))?;\n    if content.len() > MAX_READ_BYTES {\n        return Err(format!(\n            \"File is too large to parse: it grew beyond the 8 MB limit ({MAX_READ_BYTES} bytes)\"\n        ));\n    }\n    Ok(content)\n}\n\n#[derive(Debug, Serialize, Deserialize, Clone)]\npub struct CstSymbol {\n    pub name: String,\n    pub kind: String,\n    pub visibility: String,\n    pub scope: Option<String>,\n    pub file: String,\n    pub start_line: usize,\n    pub end_line: usize,\n    pub signature: String,\n    pub doc_comment: Option<String>,\n}\n\n#[derive(Debug, Serialize, Deserialize)]\npub struct CstParseArgs {\n    pub path: String,\n    pub query: Option<String>,\n}\n\n#[derive(Debug, Serialize, Deserialize)]\npub struct CstParseResult {\n    pub total_symbols: usize,\n    pub symbols: Vec<CstSymbol>,\n}\n\n/**\n * Concrete Syntax Tree (CST) Symbol Parser (Candidate #04)\n * Parses multiline signatures, doc comments, visibility, and scopes across languages.\n */\npub fn parse_cst_symbols(file_path: &Path, rel_path: &str, query_filter: Option<&str>) -> Result<Vec<CstSymbol>, String> {\n    let content = read_source_file(file_path)?;\n    let ext = file_path.extension().and_then(|s| s.to_str()).unwrap_or(\"\");\n    Ok(parse_cst_content(&content, rel_path, query_filter, ext))\n}\n\n/// Parses already-bounded source text, so a caller that has the content (an outline) does not read the file again.\nfn parse_cst_content(content: &str, rel_path: &str, query_filter: Option<&str>, ext: &str) -> Vec<CstSymbol> {\n    let lines: Vec<String> = content.lines().map(|line| line.to_string()).collect();\n    let mut symbols = Vec::new();\n\n    let doc_regex = Regex::new(r\"^\\s*(?://[/!]|\\s*\\*\\s*|#\\s*|/\\*\\*|<!--)(.*)\").unwrap();\n    let current_scope: Option<String> = None;\n\n    // Pattern matching declaration headers\n    let decl_regex = Regex::new(\n        r\"(?m)^\\s*(pub(?:\\([^)]+\\))?\\s+)?(async\\s+)?(export\\s+)?(default\\s+)?(fn|function|def|class|struct|interface|trait|type|enum|func)\\s+([A-Za-z0-9_]+)(.*)\"\n    ).unwrap();\n\n    let mut pending_doc = Vec::new();\n    let mut i = 0;\n\n    while i < lines.len() {\n        let line = &lines[i];\n        let trimmed = line.trim();\n\n        // Accumulate preceding doc comments\n        if (trimmed.starts_with(\"///\") || trimmed.starts_with(\"//!\") || trimmed.starts_with(\"/**\") || (trimmed.starts_with('*') && !trimmed.starts_with(\"*/\")) || (ext == \"py\" && trimmed.starts_with('#'))) && !trimmed.starts_with(\"/*\") {\n            if let Some(caps) = doc_regex.captures(trimmed) {\n                let comment = caps.get(1).map(|m| m.as_str().trim()).unwrap_or(\"\");\n                if !comment.is_empty() {\n                    pending_doc.push(comment.to_string());\n                }\n            }\n            i += 1;\n            continue;\n        }\n\n        if let Some(caps) = decl_regex.captures(trimmed) {\n            let vis_raw = caps.get(1).map(|m| m.as_str().trim()).unwrap_or(\"\");\n            let export_raw = caps.get(3).map(|m| m.as_str().trim()).unwrap_or(\"\");\n            let kind = caps.get(5).map(|m| m.as_str().trim()).unwrap_or(\"unknown\").to_string();\n            let name = caps.get(6).map(|m| m.as_str().trim()).unwrap_or(\"\").to_string();\n\n            let visibility = if !vis_raw.is_empty() {\n                vis_raw.to_string()\n            } else if !export_raw.is_empty() {\n                \"exported\".to_string()\n            } else {\n                \"private\".to_string()\n            };\n\n            let start_line = i + 1;\n            let mut sig_lines = vec![trimmed.to_string()];\n            let mut end_line = start_line;\n\n            // Multiline signature accumulation until '{', ';', or ':' (python)\n            if !trimmed.contains('{') && !trimmed.contains(';') && !(ext == \"py\" && trimmed.ends_with(':')) {\n                let mut j = i + 1;\n                while j < lines.len() && j < i + 10 {\n                    let next_trimmed = lines[j].trim();\n                    sig_lines.push(next_trimmed.to_string());\n                    if next_trimmed.contains('{') || next_trimmed.contains(';') || (ext == \"py\" && next_trimmed.ends_with(':')) {\n                        end_line = j + 1;\n                        i = j;\n                        break;\n                    }\n                    j += 1;\n                }\n            }\n\n            let full_sig = sig_lines.join(\" \");\n            let doc_text = if !pending_doc.is_empty() {\n                Some(pending_doc.join(\"\\n\"))\n            } else {\n                None\n            };\n            pending_doc.clear();\n\n            let matches_query = match query_filter {\n                Some(q) => name.to_lowercase().contains(&q.to_lowercase()),\n                None => true,\n            };\n\n            if matches_query && !name.is_empty() {\n                symbols.push(CstSymbol {\n                    name,\n                    kind,\n                    visibility,\n                    scope: current_scope.clone(),\n                    file: rel_path.to_string(),\n                    start_line,\n                    end_line,\n                    signature: full_sig,\n                    doc_comment: doc_text,\n                });\n            }\n        } else if !trimmed.is_empty() {\n            pending_doc.clear();\n        }\n\n        i += 1;\n    }\n\n    symbols\n}\n\n/**\n * Scan workspace files and parse CST symbols\n * Scan workspace files and parse CST symbols\n */\npub fn scan_workspace_cst(base_dir: &Path, args: CstParseArgs) -> Result<CstParseResult, String> {\n    let target = crate::file_ops::resolve_safe_path(base_dir, &args.path)?;\n    let mut all_symbols = Vec::new();\n\n    if target.is_file() {\n        let rel_path = target.strip_prefix(base_dir).unwrap_or(&target).to_string_lossy().to_string();\n        let syms = parse_cst_symbols(&target, &rel_path, args.query.as_deref())?;\n        all_symbols.extend(syms);\n    } else if target.is_dir() {\n        for entry in WalkDir::new(&target).max_depth(5).into_iter().filter_map(|e| e.ok()) {\n            let p = entry.path();\n            if p.is_file() {\n                let ext = p.extension().and_then(|s| s.to_str()).unwrap_or(\"\");\n                if matches!(ext, \"rs\" | \"ts\" | \"tsx\" | \"js\" | \"jsx\" | \"py\" | \"go\") {\n                    let rel_path = p.strip_prefix(base_dir).unwrap_or(p).to_string_lossy().to_string();\n                    if let Ok(syms) = parse_cst_symbols(p, &rel_path, args.query.as_deref()) {\n                        all_symbols.extend(syms);\n                    }\n                }\n            }\n        }\n    }\n\n    Ok(CstParseResult {\n        total_symbols: all_symbols.len(),\n        symbols: all_symbols,\n    })\n}\n\n#[derive(Debug, Serialize, Deserialize)]\npub struct OutlineFileArgs {\n    pub path: String,\n}\n\n#[derive(Debug, Serialize, Deserialize)]\npub struct OutlineFileResult {\n    pub path: String,\n    pub total_lines: usize,\n    pub symbol_count: usize,\n    pub outline: String,\n}\n\n/// Generates a compact AST symbol outline for a source file to conserve local LLM context\npub fn generate_file_outline(base_dir: &Path, args: OutlineFileArgs) -> Result<OutlineFileResult, String> {\n    let target = crate::file_ops::resolve_safe_path(base_dir, &args.path)?;\n    if !target.is_file() {\n        return Err(format!(\"File does not exist or is not a file: {}\", args.path));\n    }\n\n    let rel_path = target.strip_prefix(base_dir).unwrap_or(&target).to_string_lossy().to_string();\n    let content = read_source_file(&target)?;\n    let ext = target.extension().and_then(|s| s.to_str()).unwrap_or(\"\");\n    let symbols = parse_cst_content(&content, &rel_path, None, ext);\n    let total_lines = content.lines().count();\n\n    let mut outline_str = format!(\"File: {} ({} lines, {} symbols)\\n\", rel_path, total_lines, symbols.len());\n    if symbols.is_empty() {\n        outline_str.push_str(\"No top-level declarations or exported symbols detected.\\n\");\n    } else {\n        for s in &symbols {\n            let doc_hint = s.doc_comment.as_ref()\n                .and_then(|d| d.lines().next())\n                .map(|line| format!(\" - \\\"{}\\\"\", line.trim()))\n                .unwrap_or_default();\n            outline_str.push_str(&format!(\n                \"- [{}] {} (lines {}-{}) [{}]{}\\n\",\n                s.kind, s.name, s.start_line, s.end_line, s.visibility, doc_hint\n            ));\n        }\n    }\n\n    Ok(OutlineFileResult {\n        path: args.path,\n        total_lines,\n        symbol_count: symbols.len(),\n        outline: outline_str,\n    })\n}\n\n#[cfg(test)]\nmod tests {\n    use super::*;\n\n    #[test]\n    fn test_cst_symbol_parsing() {\n        let tmp = std::env::temp_dir().join(\"nexus_cst_test.rs\");\n        let code = r#\"\n/// High-level engine runner\npub async fn execute_task(\n    id: &str,\n    timeout: u64,\n) -> Result<bool, String> {\n    Ok(true)\n}\n\"#;\n        std::fs::write(&tmp, code).unwrap();\n        let syms = parse_cst_symbols(&tmp, \"test.rs\", None).unwrap();\n        assert_eq!(syms.len(), 1);\n        let s = &syms[0];\n        assert_eq!(s.name, \"execute_task\");\n        assert_eq!(s.kind, \"fn\");\n        assert_eq!(s.visibility, \"pub\");\n        assert!(s.signature.contains(\"-> Result<bool, String>\"));\n        assert!(s.doc_comment.as_ref().unwrap().contains(\"High-level engine runner\"));\n\n        let outline_res = generate_file_outline(&std::env::temp_dir(), OutlineFileArgs {\n            path: \"nexus_cst_test.rs\".into(),\n        }).unwrap();\n        assert_eq!(outline_res.symbol_count, 1);\n# DEFECT: CST symbol/outline tools read an unbounded file\n\n| | |\n|---|---|\n| Base revision | `41b381ddac182b7f0c783b33df5f1355518f465b` (`origin/main`) |\n| Branch | `v1/defect-cst-unbounded` |\n| Affected behavior | `parse_cst_symbols` collected every line of the target into memory, and `generate_file_outline` then read the whole file again with `std::fs::read_to_string`. Both are reachable from the model through `cst_symbols`, `outline_file` and `scan_workspace_cst`, with no `MAX_READ_BYTES` check. A multi-gigabyte source file therefore allocates the whole file in the single Rust bridge, blocking or OOM-ing the agent, even though `read_file`/`file_info`/`edit_file` now stop at 8 MB. |\n| Severity | Medium: same bridge-wide availability impact as the previous whole-file-read defects, triggered by a workspace file the model is asked to outline or scan. |\n\n## Reproduction (pre-fix)\n\nUnit probe: create a `.rs` file of `MAX_READ_BYTES + 1` bytes (one declaration plus filler comments) and call\n`parse_cst_symbols` / `generate_file_outline`.\n\n```\nthread panicked: parse_cst_symbols must refuse a file above the read limit\n```\n\nBoth returned `Ok` on the base source after reading the whole 8 MB + 1 file (the pre-fix test took ~2 s for that\nsize; the cost is linear in file size).\n\n## Fix\n\nAdd one bounded `read_source_file` helper: `fstat` the opened file, refuse above `MAX_READ_BYTES`, and read through\n`take(MAX_READ_BYTES + 1)` with a re-check so growth after the check cannot allocate without bound.\n`parse_cst_symbols` reads once and delegates to a new `parse_cst_content`; `generate_file_outline` also reads once\nthrough the helper and parses that same content, so it no longer has a second unchecked `read_to_string` and its\nsize refusal does not depend on the parser's.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Separate `test_cst_refuses_files_above_the_read_limit` and\n  `test_cst_outline_refuses_files_above_the_read_limit` tests: both fail independently on the base source\n  (`parse_cst_symbols` and `generate_file_outline` each returned `Ok` for 8 MB + 1) and pass after the change. The\n  outline test pins its own read path rather than relying on the parser's error.\n- `test_cst_accepts_the_read_limit_and_empty_files` pins the exact 8 MB boundary (still parsed/outlined), a zero-byte\n  file, and their line/symbol counts.\n- Existing symbol-parsing/outline test still passes; full `cargo test --bin harness-core` 40/40; `cargo check` has no\n  warnings.\n- `cargo check --bin harness-core` has no unused-import warning; `git diff --check`: pass.\n\n## Residual risk\n\n- The bound is per file. `scan_workspace_cst` still walks up to depth 5 and accumulates symbols from every source file;\n  total work is proportional to workspace size (each individual file is now capped). Directory scans use\n  `if let Ok(syms)`, so an oversized file inside a directory is silently omitted (the same path passed as a file\n  returns the 8 MB error).\n- The bounded text and its line vector are retained together while parsing, so peak memory at the cap is somewhat\n  above the file size; an 8 MB file no longer scales with larger input.\n- Query filtering still happens after parsing; the whole (bounded) file is parsed even when only one symbol matches.\n## v1/defect-cst-unbounded-rebase...origin/main [ahead 2]\n{\"agent\":\"codex-root\",\"host\":\"mike-dev\",\"branch\":\"v1/defect-cst-unbounded-rebase\",\"worktree\":\"/home/mike/nexus-wt/cst-unbounded-rebase\",\"base\":\"676abb371c8c91970af6d920d5c516497e3ccdef\",\"since\":\"2026-10-24T18:10:00Z\",\"scope\":\"refresh stalled PR199 CST resource-bound fix onto authoritative main and requalify exact head; preserve prior branch\",\"status\":\"claim recovered after recorded safe-boundary request; owner inactive on recorded host; PR199 CI green on stale base\"}"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a16f1a-0d89-7262-a71e-eb3a6dfcc08e","create_time":1792865642.2871954}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
