Concurrent load caused a false failure on 2026-10-15: `cloud_providers` saw an extra provider request after a load-induced timeout. Release the claim when the run ends. |\n51:| Inference | There is one inference host (DEC-16). Any run that uses the gateway takes the claim `GATEWAY` first. That includes eval runs, live checks and stripped-proxy runs. One gateway run at a time, which keeps eval timings valid and prevents overload. Small cloud checks (E5) take `CLOUD` to avoid duplicate spend. |\n56:These files are touched by several plans. An agent editing one must hold its `FILE_` claim for the **shortest** period: edit, test, push, merge, then release.\n76:| `docs/USER_MANUAL.md`, `ARCHITECTURE.md`, `CLOUD_PROVIDERS.md`, `quickstart.md` | 05, 09 and doc tasks in every plan | Edit only the sections your slice changes. Hold a short `FILE_` claim. |\n86:3. Merge order follows the precedence rules in §4 and the ROADMAP milestone order. Within a milestone, the slice with fewer hot-file claims merges first.\n95:| Claims | `$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims/` | Who owns which slice or file right now |\n96:| Claim log | `$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims.log` (append-only, one line per event) | Claim, release, broken claim, boundary request |\n97:| Boundary requests and discovered requirements | The PR description, under the heading `Needs from other slices`. Mirrored as one line in the claim log. | So the owning slice's agent can pick it up. Never fixed silently out of scope. |\n102:The following groupings can run at the same time with no hot-file contention beyond §4 claims. They are listed by milestone.\n110:| M4 (alongside M3) | PLAN-08 PR-8b..8e. Coordinate with PLAN-04 on `state.ts` through `FILE_` claims. |\n111:| M5 | **Serial on `GATEWAY`.** The eval runner, the stripped-proxy runs and the independent reviewer's live task each take the `GATEWAY` claim. The terminal matrix (E3) and the install matrix (E2) can run in parallel with gateway runs. |\n2026-10-24T12:55:35Z PERPETUAL_REVIEW_CI_SUCCESS pr=192 head=03a8db1 runs=CodeQL:completed(success), CI:completed(success) all_pass=yes\n2026-10-24T12:56:01.743Z PERPETUAL_REVIEW_MAIN_LANDING prev=b024027 new=13f25f4 commits=13f25f4 fix(test): reap REPL PTY before fixture cleanup | 03a8db1 test(cli): preserve REPL fixture on shutdown failure | 410fdf1 test(cli): reap REPL PTY process before cleanup\n2026-10-24T13:27:37.825Z PERPETUAL_REVIEW_CI_SUCCESS pr=193 head=7f03553 runs=CodeQL:completed(success), CI:completed(success)\n2026-10-24T13:30:08.830Z PERPETUAL_REVIEW_MAIN_LANDING prev=13f25f4 new=be2cd2f commits=be2cd2f Merge pull request #193 from mikeholownych/v1/defect-mcp-config-persist | 7f03553 test(mcp): prove parse errors cannot echo config content | 3eac5df fix(mcp): sanitize persistence errors and reject unusable config shapes | eaba306 fix(mcp): save server config owner-only and never clobber it\n2026-10-24T13:33:55Z MAIN_POST_MERGE_CI_SUCCESS sha=13f25f40bc3a251fafa1c08b3f6d4d9c22d463ef run=40095968632 codeql=40095968617 jobs=test-matrix(22,24)_linux-x86_64 all_pass=yes\n2026-10-24T13:53:26Z INDEPENDENT_REVIEW branch=v1/repro-tar-metadata head=6e79dc7 base=be2cd2f disposition=ACCEPT diff=a34a2211eef52d580c6ce300b2ce88b7115b23e4cf60fb011b896af4cd009f20 notes=\"Pinned-container tar/gzip change reviewed; reviewer did not run tests. Candidate awaits exact-main CI terminal and SUITE safe-boundary handoff; no candidate tests or PR l…1086 tokens truncated…e boundary at MAX_READ_BYTES; 18/18 file_ops tests pass; git diff --check PASS; clean merge-tree; CodeQL 40109386876 PASS; CI 40109386846 active'\n2026-10-24T16:25:04.397Z PERPETUAL_REVIEW_MAIN_LANDING prev=e624de0 new=f827d51 commits=f827d51 Merge pull request #196 from mikeholownych/v1/repro-crossrunner-bundle | da5f269 fix(release): normalize package archives across runners\n2026-10-24T16:21:00Z PERPETUAL_REVIEW_CI_SUCCESS pr=196 head=da5f269 runs=CodeQL:completed(success), CI:completed(success) all_p