{"timestamp":"2026-10-24T18:34:08.045Z","ordinal":302027,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a16f2a-3ce8-7e02-bf87-a11cb7ed706b","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-0ba5709c-158f-47b4-a657-492f1c190c55","process_id":"39810","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","gh pr view 200 --json body --jq .body | sed -n '1,180p'; rg -n 'git.exclude|exclude|REQ-PER-105' docs/v1.0.0/plans docs/v1.0.0/specs"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"gh pr view 200 --json body --jq .body | sed -n '1,180p'; rg -n 'git.exclude|exclude|REQ-PER-105' docs/v1.0.0/plans docs/v1.0.0/specs"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"## Summary\n\n- Keep `.nexus/` exclusion fail-closed when Git still considers protected Nexus state visible.\n- Avoid appending duplicate rules on every retry when a higher-priority repository ignore rule defeats `info/exclude`.\n- Still append a final positive rule when a later negation in `info/exclude` can be overridden.\n- Add a regression that retries the ineffective rule and verifies the exclude file no longer grows.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `npx tsx --test test/git_exclude.test.ts`: 8/8 passed with isolated `HOME` and `XDG_CONFIG_HOME`.\n- `npx tsc --noEmit`: passed.\n- `git diff --check`: passed.\n- Independent read-only review: ACCEPT on exact diff SHA-256 `9518852b8ad6f9c2242a8b08f7b661925beed1d492f72847a75216dae17ec8f1`.\n- Exact-head CI is required before integration.\n\n## Base\n\n- `main` at `41b381ddac182b7f0c783b33df5f1355518f465b`.\n\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md:78:   - Contaminated runs are excluded from pooled rates.\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md:81:   - `nexus eval` is labelled experimental and excluded from claims (DEC-07).\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md:92:  - exclude `contaminated: true` runs from pooled rates;\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md:25:| 2 | Scorer: log replacements; exclude contaminated runs from pooled rates; add metric columns for intervention, recovery, bounded-failure truthfulness, cost per correct task, and pre/post regression diff. | `score.mjs:16-21,48-84` | 1 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md:52:  - contamination: an agent that `cat`s the hidden path is flagged and excluded from the pool;\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-08-persistence-hygiene.md:7:| Requirements | REQ-PER-101, REQ-PER-102, REQ-PER-103, REQ-PER-104, REQ-PER-105, REQ-PER-106 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-08-persistence-hygiene.md:40:**PER-06.** Flight logs live in `<workspace>/.nexus/flights`. They are excluded from git only when a worktree is created, so they can be committed together with the prompts and output snippets they contain.\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-08-persistence-hygiene.md:57:5. **REQ-PER-105.** Flight logs and other per-workspace telemetry are never committable by default. They are stored under `~/.nexus/flights/<workspace-hash>/`, or `.nexus/` is always added to `.git/info/exclude` when Nexus first writes there.\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-08-persistence-hygiene.md:32:| 8 | Flight logs: always add `.nexus/` to `.git/info/exclude` on first workspace write (and keep the exclude in `worktree.ts:84`). | `flight.ts:55-59`; shared helper | — |\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-08-persistence-hygiene.md:54:| ACC-PER-05 | `flight_exclude.test.ts` |\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-11-verification-and-tool-call-integrity.md:73:8. **REQ-AGT-119.** Experimental surfaces (DEC-07: `nexus eval`, `/tdd`, team roles) are labelled experimental in help and docs and excluded from qualification claims. `nexus eval` runs in a worktree and never touches the operator's checkout. Team reviewer and researcher roles run with a read-only tool set.\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":409945044}},"started_at_ms":1792866847634,"completed_at_ms":1792866848045}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-24T18:34:09.076Z","ordinal":302028,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a16f31-1134-7d62-af0e-7c74951f0c97","call_id":"call_adbe285ef543435c8ba4d020fccba77d","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 2.6 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"## Summary\n\n- Keep `.nexus/` exclusion fail-closed when Git still considers protected Nexus state visible.\n- Avoid appending duplicate rules on every retry when a higher-priority repository ignore rule defeats `info/exclude`.\n- Still append a final positive rule when a later negation in `info/exclude` can be overridden.\n- Add a regression that retries the ineffective rule and verifies the exclude file no longer grows.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `npx tsx --test test/git_exclude.test.ts`: 8/8 passed with isolated `HOME` and `XDG_CONFIG_HOME`.\n- `npx tsc --noEmit`: passed.\n- `git diff --check`: passed.\n- Independent read-only review: ACCEPT on exact diff SHA-256 `9518852b8ad6f9c2242a8b08f7b661925beed1d492f72847a75216dae17ec8f1`.\n- Exact-head CI is required before integration.\n\n## Base\n\n- `main` at `41b381ddac182b7f0c783b33df5f1355518f465b`.\n\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md:78:   - Contaminated runs are excluded from pooled rates.\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md:81:   - `nexus eval` is labelled experimental and excluded from claims (DEC-07).\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md:92:  - exclude `contaminated: true` runs from pooled rates;\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md:25:| 2 | Scorer: log replacements; exclude contaminated runs from pooled rates; add metric columns for intervention, recovery, bounded-failure truthfulness, cost per correct task, and pre/post regression diff. | `score.mjs:16-21,48-84` | 1 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md:52:  - contamination: an agent that `cat`s the hidden path is flagged and excluded from the pool;\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-08-persistence-hygiene.md:7:| Requirements | REQ-PER-101, REQ-PER-102, REQ-PER-103, REQ-PER-104, REQ-PER-105, REQ-PER-106 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-08-persistence-hygiene.md:40:**PER-06.** Flight logs live in `<workspace>/.nexus/flights`. They are excluded from git only when a worktree is created, so they can be committed together with the prompts and output snippets they contain.\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-08-persistence-hygiene.md:57:5. **REQ-PER-105.** Flight logs and other per-workspace telemetry are never committable by default. They are stored under `~/.nexus/flights/<workspace-hash>/`, or `.nexus/` is always added to `.git/info/exclude` when Nexus first writes there.\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-08-persistence-hygiene.md:32:| 8 | Flight logs: always add `.nexus/` to `.git/info/exclude` on first workspace write (and keep the exclude in `worktree.ts:84`). | `flight.ts:55-59`; shared helper | — |\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-08-persistence-hygiene.md:54:| ACC-PER-05 | `flight_exclude.test.ts` |\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-11-verification-and-tool-call-integrity.md:73:8. **REQ-AGT-119.** Experimental surfaces (DEC-07: `nexus eval`, `/tdd`, team roles) are labelled experimental in help and docs and excluded from qualification claims. `nexus eval` runs in a worktree and never touches the operator's checkout. Team reviewer and researcher roles run with a read-only tool set.\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a16f2a-3ce8-7e02-bf87-a11cb7ed706b","create_time":1792866849.076766}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
