{"timestamp":"2026-10-24T18:45:19.805Z","ordinal":302683,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a16f37-6e05-7dc2-8c28-9b80ae02e75f","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-21206d98-6a76-4a87-999a-10d947759bee","process_id":"19563","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","rg -n '^#{1,3} |REQ-QUAL|REQ-REL-114|held-out|T2|T3|T4|cross-runner|terminal matrix|provider|RC construction|exact-RC|stable release|pre-RC' docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md docs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md docs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.4.md; sed -n '1,260p' docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md"],"cwd":"file:///tmp/nexus-release-audit-4adc-20261024","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"search","cmd":"rg -n '^#{1,3} |REQ-QUAL|REQ-REL-114|held-out|T2|T3|T4|cross-runner|terminal matrix|provider|RC construction|exact-RC|stable release|pre-RC' docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md docs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md docs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.4.md","query":"^#{1,3} |REQ-QUAL|REQ-REL-114|held-out|T2|T3|T4|cross-runner|terminal matrix|provider|RC construction|exact-RC|stable release|pre-RC","path":"ACCEPTANCE.md"},{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '1,260p' docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md","name":"ACCEPTANCE.md","path":"docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"docs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.4.md:1:# Nexus Code v1.0.0-rc.4 release candidate\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.4.md:9:## Changes since RC3\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.4.md:13:- Classifies length-truncated assistant output separately from recoverable provider failures, so truncated tool arguments are not retried through provider recovery.\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.4.md:23:- Locks the npm release tools used for notices and the SBOM, rejects deprecated packages in that lock, and adds a cross-runner workflow that rebuilds a published RC on Ubuntu 22.04 and 24.04 and compares the archive, compatibility metadata, checksums, notices, SBOM and installer with the published assets.\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.4.md:24:- Requires the approved digest-pinned Rust builder for release packaging and reproducibility checks. Local packaging examples and cross-runner checks use the same approved builder identity; the host-build opt-out is for local development only.\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.4.md:28:## Runtime requirements\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.4.md:32:- An OpenAI-compatible inference endpoint, local or explicitly selected provider.\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.4.md:36:## Candidate assets\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:1:# Nexus Code v1.0.0: requirement ledger\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:7:## 1. Legend\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:9:### Status ladder\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:22:### Release classes\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:31:### Evidence labels\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:44:### Links\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:49:## 2. Carried-over commitments (REQ-*-0xx)\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:51:### 2.1 Retained commitments (already met or partly met; must not regress)\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:55:| REQ-AGT-001 | COMPACTION_AND_CONTINUITY §A; operator directive | No default cumulative step or time ceiling. Turns end on completion, cancel, demonstrated stagnation, actionable failure or an operator-set budget. Resource-safety valves (provider iterations, 10k scheduler transitions, 5 compaction attempts) are allowed and labelled. | `types.ts:127-133`; `agent.ts:4379-4445` | TEST + SRC (A §5) | tested | N | — | ACC-CONT-04, ACC-QUAL-T3 | K | SPEC-04 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:56:| REQ-AGT-002 | quickstart; TOP_TIER B3; EXEC-005 | Truthful outcome taxonomy. VERIFIED requires a passing, deliverable-bound verifier run, plus fail-before/pass-after independence for discovered verifiers. UNVERIFIED, REGRESSION_FREE, BLOCKED and LIMIT_REACHED are distinct, with exit codes 0/2/1/130. | `agent.ts:5726-5764`; `tester.ts:371-430,541-627`; `turn.ts:318-351` | TEST at db1ca55; candidate suite at `6151a23` passes ACC-VER-03/04/09 regression tests. Historical VER-04/05 findings and tuned-set/live evidence remain in [A2_verification.md](evidence/A2_verification.md) and the dated evidence files. | partial | N | M5 false-VERIFIED threshold remains unqualified pending held-out T2/T3/T4 evidence; historical VER-04/05 implementation defects have regression coverage at the candidate. | ACC-VER-03/04/09, ACC-QUAL-T2 | B | SPEC-11 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:61:| REQ-AGT-007 | release notes alpha.2 | Output-truncated reply: nothing from it runs; one in-turn retry; a second consecutive truncation ends the turn. | `agent.ts:4671-4683`; `client.ts:1459-1468` | TEST (6/6, scripted) | tested | **N (pending)** | Never observed live | ACC-CONT-10, ACC-QUAL-T4 | K | SPEC-04 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:62:| REQ-AGT-008 | provider recovery design | Bounded provider recovery: 20 min deadline, jittered backoff, Retry-After honoured, probe before an UNKNOWN replay, ≤ 2 replays. | `provider_recovery.ts` | TEST 23/23 + 15/15 | tested | N | A never-reachable endpoint waits too long (TUI-06) | ACC-INF-07 | K | SPEC-05 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:74:| REQ-PRV-003 | COMPACTION:7-9; handoff doc | Nexus works without homelab-ai. Gateway features are optional and absent-safe. | `provider_capabilities.ts:184-195` | TEST (scripted) | implemented | N | No live standalone evidence (HIST-08) | ACC-INF-10 | B (via REQ-PRV-106) | SPEC-05 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:75:| REQ-PRV-004 | CLOUD_PROVIDERS | Cloud spend limits and receipts; disclosure notice on first request. | `usage.ts`; `client.ts:509-569` | TEST (mock); HIST live (openrouter, chatgpt); RT 2026-10-14 receipts written with provider-reported usage | tested | N | Other providers mock-only | ACC-PRV-LIVE | RR | SPEC-05 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:80:| REQ-REL-005 | SCAN-001..005 | Dependency and secret gates; zero High/Critical in a release. | `scripts/security_gates.sh` | Candidate source suite: npm audit, cargo deny/advisory-license gate, credential scan passed at `6151a23`; release-artifact scan not run. | partial | N | The old nine-advisory fallback cited by REL-07 is no longer called by `security_gates.sh`; current source uses cargo-deny or cargo-audit and fails if neither exists. ACC-SUP-04's missing-scanner case is covered by `REQ-REL-110`. The remaining gate is exact-RC supply-chain/security evidence; SAST is not specified by ACC-SUP-04. | ACC-SUP-04, ACC-SUP-05 | RR (via REQ-REL-110) | SPEC-07 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:85:### 2.2 Historical items that are superseded, contradicted or descoped (written dispositions; REQ-OPS-103)\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:92:| EXEC-011 (evaluators score the exact candidate) | DEMONSTRATED | **Contradicted** for `nexus eval` (VER-07) | `nexus eval` is experimental (DEC-07). The qualification harness is `eval/` (REQ-QUAL-106). |\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:103:| REL-001 byte-identical builds | deferred | Same-runner proven | REQ-REL-114 (RR, cross-runner once for the RC) |\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:109:| POST_REMEDIATION_DOGFOOD \"INTEGRATION_BLOCKED\" (completion truth across process death; retry launders unverified changes) | not re-dispositioned | Covered by REQ-AGT-101/106 and T4 class 9 | Re-qualify through ACC-QUAL-T4 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:111:## 3. v1.0.0 requirements (REQ-*-1xx)\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:115:### 3.1 Safety and execution boundary\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:146:### 3.2 Completion truth, continuity and recovery\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:166:### 3.3 Local inference and providers\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:170:| REQ-PRV-101 | Standalone commitment | Context discovery for vLLM, llama.cpp, LM Studio and Ollama, with the source labelled. | standalone workflow | `provider_capabilities.ts` | TEST (PRV-06; test:cli/test/server_context_discovery.test.ts::\"discovery against a local server\") | tested | ACC-INF-01 | **B** | PRV-06 | SPEC-05 / PLAN-05 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:171:| REQ-PRV-102 | TOP_TIER I-05 (carried) | A capacity rejection leads to one compact-and-retry, then an actionable error. llama.cpp, LM Studio and Ollama bodies are classified. | standalone / failure | `provider_recovery.ts:82,106`; `agent.ts:5072` | TEST (PRV-07; test:cli/test/provider_recovery_agent.test.ts::\"capacity rejection handling (ACC-INF-02)\") | tested | ACC-INF-02 | **B** | PRV-06, PRV-07 | SPEC-05 / PLAN-05 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:172:| REQ-PRV-103 | CRED-003 (carried) | Error text is bounded and redacted on every path. | safety | `client.ts:903,1636,1689`, `oauth.ts` | TEST (PRV-03; test:cli/test/provider_robustness.test.ts::\"listModels and generateEmbedding huge error bodies are bounded and redacted (ACC-INF-03)\") | tested | ACC-INF-03 | RR | PRV-03 | SPEC-05 / PLAN-05 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:173:| REQ-PRV-104 | Audit | Timeouts and cancel on every network call. First-byte, idle and total timeouts. Bounded replays. | failure | `client.ts`, `embeddings.ts`, `model_catalog.ts` | TEST (PRV-05, PRV-10; test:cli/test/provider_robustness.test.ts::\"watchdog first-byte and idle timeouts reject when server hangs or stalls (ACC-INF-04)\") | tested | ACC-INF-04 | RR | PRV-05, PRV-10 | SPEC-05 / PLAN-05 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:174:| REQ-PRV-105 | Audit | Stream parser robustness, with recorded real-server fixtures. | compatibility | `client.ts:1326-1483` | TEST (PRV-04; test:cli/test/provider_fixes.test.ts::\"stream parser handles tool name chunks, repeated tool names, and object arguments (PRV-04 / REQ-PRV-105)\", test:cli/test/provider_robustness.test.ts::\"empty stream re-request records executions: 2 in receipt (ACC-INF-06)\") | tested | ACC-INF-05, ACC-INF-06 | RR | PRV-04 | SPEC-05 / PLAN-05 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:176:| REQ-PRV-107 | TOP_TIER I-07 | Local receipts (opt-out). | evidence | `client.ts:561-569`, `usage.ts` | TEST (B §6 G1; test:cli/test/provider_robustness.test.ts::\"local receipts are recorded with origin_class: local and opt out with NEXUS_RECEIPTS=0 (REQ-PRV-107)\") | tested | ACC-INF-06 | RR | B §6 G1 | SPEC-05 / PLAN-05 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:179:| REQ-PRV-111 | DEC-06 | Live `providers verify` for each provider listed as supported. The others are labelled experimental. | compatibility claims | `provider_cli.ts` | **RT 2026-10-14 @db1ca55:** chatgpt (gpt-6-luna) PASS, openrouter (openrouter/free) PASS. **RT 2026-10-16 @6151a23+4d82578, pinned models:** openrouter `nvidia/nemotron-3-super-120b-a12b:free` PASS (one model served every request), chatgpt `gpt-6-luna` PASS (`evidence/live/verify_*_pinned_2026-10-16.json`). The run found and fixed the option-scope regression (4d82578). openai-key and anthropic not connected. | partial (repeat on the RC) | ACC-PRV-LIVE | RR | B §6 G2 | SPEC-05 / PLAN-10 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:180:| REQ-TUI-105 | Audit | Startup endpoint probe with a fix hint. A never-reachable endpoint is bounded to 2 minutes. | onboarding | `sidecar.ts`, `repl.ts`, `provider_recovery.ts` | TEST (TUI-06; test:cli/test/startup_unreachable_e2e.test.ts::\"ACC-INF-07 (REQ-TUI-105): Startup endpoint probe and first-contact deadline\") | tested | ACC-INF-07 | RR | TUI-06 | SPEC-05 / PLAN-05 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:182:### 3.4 Packaging, release and diagnostics\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:203:| REQ-REL-114 | REL-001 (carried) | Cross-runner reproducibility, demonstrated once for the RC. | supply chain | `repro.yml` | UNV | open | ACC-SUP-08 | RR | E §6 | SPEC-07 / PLAN-07 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:208:### 3.5 Persistence\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:220:### 3.6 Governance and documentation\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:230:### 3.7 Qualification\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:234:| REQ-QUAL-101 | TOP_TIER Q1; DEC-05 | Held-out T2 evaluation: 40 tasks, ≥ 50% external, sealed manifest. | product maturity | `eval/` | HIST (6 tuned tasks) | open | ACCEPTANCE §6.1 | **B** | EVL-001 | SPEC-10 / PLAN-10 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:235:| REQ-QUAL-102 | DEC-05 | Matched conditions with a model fingerprint. | validity | `eval/run.mjs`, `eval/validate.mjs` | TEST (EVL-004; test:cli/test/eval_integrity.test.ts::\"a qualification run is refused without a model fingerprint\") | tested | ACC-QUAL-T2 (ACCEPTANCE §6.1) | **B** | EVL-004 | SPEC-10 / PLAN-10 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:236:| REQ-QUAL-103 | DEC-05 | 5 runs per task and configuration; Goose and OpenCode as peers. | statistics | `eval/run.mjs`, `eval/score.mjs` | TEST (`eval_harness.test.ts`: peer version/budget forwarding, installed RC/version/package pin, Nexus/provider-limit parity, paired fingerprint/limit/sampling/budget/version and 5-run checks; commits `ef2d040`, `b27ae04`; [validation record](../reviews/evidence/v1/PLAN-10_PR-10d/validation.md)); UNV (live M5 runs) | tested | ACC-QUAL-T2 (ACCEPTANCE §6.1) | **B** | EVL-001 | SPEC-10 / PLAN-10 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:237:| REQ-QUAL-104 | DEC-05 | Separately reported metrics, including false VERIFIED = 0. | honesty | `eval/score.mjs` | TEST (EVL-005; test:cli/test/eval_harness.test.ts, test:cli/test/eval_integrity.test.ts) | tested | ACC-QUAL-T2 (ACCEPTANCE §6.1) | **B** | EVL-005 | SPEC-10 / PLAN-10 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:238:| REQ-QUAL-105 | TOP_TIER Q6; DEC-05 | T4 fault injection: 9 classes × 5 runs (DEC-05 amendment 2026-10-17: union of the nine distinct scenarios retained), 100% truthful outcomes. | failure / recovery | `eval/model_proxy.mjs`, `eval/score.mjs` | TEST (EVL-001; test:cli/test/eval_integrity.test.ts::\"the model proxy injects each scheduled fault\", test:cli/test/eval_harness.test.ts::\"T4 smoke\") | tested | ACC-QUAL-T4 (ACCEPTANCE §6.2) | **B** | EVL-001 | SPEC-10 / PLAN-10 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:239:| REQ-QUAL-106 | Audit | Scoring integrity (symmetric infra handling, contamination, hidden tests). | validity | `eval/infra.mjs`, `eval/score.mjs`, `eval/run.mjs` | TEST (EVL-002, EVL-003; test:cli/test/eval_integrity.test.ts::\"contaminated runs leave the pass rate\", test:cli/test/eval_integrity.test.ts::\"infrastructure reruns use one rule\") | tested | ACC-QUAL-T2 (ACCEPTANCE §6.1) | **B** | EVL-002, EVL-003, VER-07 | SPEC-10 / PLAN-10 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:240:| REQ-QUAL-107 | Standalone; DEC-06 | Standalone and provider live matrix. | standalone | — | HIST | open | ACCEPTANCE §4.2, §4.3 | **B** | HIST-08 | SPEC-10 / PLAN-10 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:241:| REQ-QUAL-108 | Audit | PTY CI plus a manual real-terminal matrix. | terminal acceptance | `cli/test/tui_*`; ACCEPTANCE §5.3 | TEST (PTY suites in CI); UNV (real terminals) | partial | ACCEPTANCE §5 | RR | D §6 | SPEC-10 / PLAN-10 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:242:| REQ-QUAL-109 | eval/README T3 | T3 long tasks: 8 × 5. | long-task workflow | `eval/` | — | open | ACCEPTANCE §6.3 | RR | EVL-001 | SPEC-10 / PLAN-10 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:243:| REQ-QUAL-110 | Audit | T1 self-test and a T4 smoke run in `make test`. | regression | `eval_harness.test.ts` | TEST (test:cli/test/eval_harness.test.ts::\"T4 smoke: an overloaded endpoint is waited out\") | tested | ACC-QUAL-SMOKE | RR | — | SPEC-10 / PLAN-10 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:245:## 4. Contest requirements (separate product; not client gates)\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:249:## 5. Post-v1 backlog (recorded, not dropped)\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:270:## 6. Counts at db1ca55\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:276:| New v1 rows (§3) | 92 | **31 B**, 58 RR, 3 P. 79 open, 9 partial (REQ-SEC-118, REQ-PRV-101, REQ-PRV-103, REQ-PRV-105, REQ-PRV-111, REQ-PER-106, REQ-OPS-101, REQ-QUAL-108, REQ-QUAL-110), 1 implemented (REQ-OPS-103), 4 tested (REQ-SEC-103, REQ-SEC-119, REQ-PER-101, REQ-PER-102). |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:1:# Nexus Code v1.0.0: release qualification procedure\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:20:## 1.1 Release-candidate lifecycle and evidence identity\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:27:4. **Installed-RC qualification.** Install the workflow-produced RC package using the documented procedure and run the applicable product, provider, task-quality, terminal, installation, and independent-acceptance gates in §§4–8. Bind each result to both the RC source commit and installed package digest. If a source change or rebuilt artifact changes either identity, rerun every affected gate against the new candidate and retain prior results as historical evidence.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:28:5. **Stable promotion and publication.** After exact-RC acceptance and G6 pass, create a stable-version commit directly on the accepted RC commit, changing only the synchronized version metadata required for v1.0.0. Record both commits and the version-only diff. Run required source CI and all applicable source G0–G4 checks on this exact stable-version commit before tagging. If any other source changes, restart RC construction and qualification. Then create the `v1.0.0` tag on that checked commit and build a draft release. Keep its assets unpublished while verifying the stable artifact identity, provenance, package contents, installation, and publication metadata. Compare the stable package contents with the accepted RC; if packaged behavior or content differs beyond version-specific metadata, rerun affected installed-RC qualification gates and obtain independent acceptance for the stable artifact. Publish the draft only after these checks pass and the signed acceptance disposition is recorded. Record the published digests and provenance.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:30:The final G6 decision in §10 applies to promoting the accepted RC toward a stable release. It requires the applicable gates to pass for the accepted RC and authorizes the version-only stable commit and its source checks, followed by the stable tag and draft build; it does not waive source CI, artifact identity, installed-RC qualification, or any threshold. Public publication is a separate post-build gate in stage 5 above. The release workflow must keep stable assets in draft state until stable artifact checks pass. Source verification at integration 6a16cb6 confirms the tag-triggered release workflow now supports published RC prereleases and draft stable releases. The earlier immediate-stable-publication source blocker is resolved; an actual stable draft build, artifact verification, signed acceptance, and deliberate publication are still required and remain unproven until their run evidence is recorded.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:34:The post-RC closure requirements listed below may remain `open`, `partial`, or `implemented` in the source ledger at the RC commit because their remaining acceptance is completed during G6 or installed-RC qualification. The bare `--enforce` invocation is the pre-RC source gate: it checks every other B/RR row against the source threshold and reports mapped rows as deferred, not accepted. At G6, the exact-RC invocation must provide a record meeting the normal B/RR status threshold and digest-bound evidence for every criterion in this table. The table also supplies the criterion mapping for rows whose ledger points to an ACCEPTANCE section instead of naming ACC IDs. The source ledger is never rewritten by the record. Any below-tested required row omitted from this table still fails.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:37:### Qualification-only requirements for exact-RC enforcement\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:39:| Requirement | Acceptance criteria required in the exact-RC record | Remaining stage |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:42:| REQ-AGT-002 | ACC-VER-03, ACC-VER-04, ACC-VER-09, ACC-QUAL-T2, ACC-QUAL-T3, ACC-QUAL-T4 | Installed-RC T2/T3/T4 outcome thresholds |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:47:| REQ-PRV-111 | ACC-PRV-LIVE | Installed-RC provider verification |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:48:| REQ-REL-114 | ACC-SUP-08 | Exact-RC cross-runner reproducibility |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:49:| REQ-QUAL-101 | ACC-QUAL-T2 | Installed-RC held-out T2 qualification |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:50:| REQ-QUAL-107 | ACC-PRV-STANDALONE, ACC-PRV-LIVE | Installed-RC standalone and provider matrix |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:51:| REQ-QUAL-108 | ACC-TUI-STEER, ACC-TUI-A11Y, ACC-TUI-MANUAL | CI PTY checks and installed-RC real-terminal matrix |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:52:| REQ-QUAL-109 | ACC-QUAL-T3 | Installed-RC T3 long-task qualification |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:56:### Approved exact-RC qualification exceptions\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:62:## 1. Rules\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:75:## 2. Environments\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:82:| E4 | Homelab-ai gateway, the **only** inference path (DEC-16): direct, and through `eval/standalone/plain_proxy.mjs` | Task-quality runs, standalone qualification, T3/T4 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:83:| E5 | Cloud, small spend: ChatGPT sign-in (experimental tier) and OpenRouter with a pinned model; OpenAI and Anthropic keys if added | Provider verify; one live task per supported cloud provider |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:85:## 3. Gate checklist (G0–G4: automated acceptance IDs)\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:87:Every ACC ID below is defined in the linked spec. The plan for each spec names the test that implements it. Run each check at the lifecycle stage dictated by its acceptance method in §1.1: source-applicable checks before the RC tag; checks requiring the RC archive, attestation, release, or installed package after RC construction; environment-specific checks in their declared environment. Bind every result to the exact source commit and, when artifact-dependent, the RC package digest. A source test or local build does not replace an artifact-bound check, and no G0–G4 ID is complete until all of its applicable checks pass.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:97:| Supply chain | ACC-SUP-01 to ACC-SUP-08 (artifact-bound ACC-SUP-01/02/03/06/08 after RC construction) | SPEC-07 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:104:### 3.1 Acceptance IDs defined in this file\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:114:| ACC-PRV-LIVE | `nexus providers verify --provider <p> -m <pinned model> -j` for each provider listed as supported (DEC-06) | `passed: true`. Receipts archived. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:117:| ACC-QUAL-T2 | §6.1 + §6.4 | Thresholds met. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:118:| ACC-QUAL-T3 | §6.3 + §6.4 | Thresholds met. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:119:| ACC-QUAL-T4 | §6.2 + §6.4 | Thresholds met. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:120:| ACC-QUAL-SMOKE | `make test` includes the T1 self-test and the T4 smoke | Present and passing. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:123:## 4. Standalone and provider qualification (REQ-PRV-106, REQ-PRV-111, REQ-QUAL-107)\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:125:### 4.1 Clean-HOME procedure\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:138:### 4.2 Standalone matrix\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:142:| P-plain | Bare OpenAI-compatible `/models` and chat. No tokenize, no capacity headers. | Standalone T2 subset (≥ 10 held-out tasks) × 3 runs; T4 classes 1, 3, 4, 7 × 3 | T2 correctness ≥ (gateway-direct T2 correctness on the same tasks − 10 pts). False VERIFIED = 0. T4 truthful = 100%. Context source reported as `client_default` or an operator override, with no error. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:150:### 4.3 Provider matrix (E5)\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:154:| OpenRouter, pinned model | Supported | `providers verify` PASS, plus one live small task (a §6-style bug fix) reaching a correct outcome |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:159:## 5. Terminal acceptance (REQ-QUAL-108)\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:161:### 5.1 CI PTY suites (E1)\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:176:### 5.2 Scripted PTY scenarios against the installed RC (E3, mock gateway)\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:190:### 5.3 Manual real-terminal matrix (E3)\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:208:## 6. Task-quality qualification (REQ-QUAL-101 to REQ-QUAL-106, REQ-QUAL-109)\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:210:Environment: E4 (gateway direct), serial runs, with matched model fingerprint, budgets and env (REQ-QUAL-102).\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:212:### 6.1 T2 held-out (ACC-QUAL-T2)\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:217:- Set `T2_TASKS` to the custodian-approved, sealed task directory and `T2_OUT` to a new, empty, run-specific output directory. Do not use the disclosed `eval/tasks` development set as held-out evidence. Preserve all three outputs and their manifests; never reuse an output directory for a retry.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:222:  : \"${T2_TASKS:?set the sealed task directory}\"\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:223:  : \"${T2_OUT:?set a new unique output directory}\"\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:224:  test ! -e \"$T2_OUT\"\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:225:  node eval/run.mjs --config eval/configs/v1-t2-nexus.json --tasks \"$T2_TASKS\" --out \"$T2_OUT/nexus\" --runs 5\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:226:  node eval/run.mjs --config eval/configs/v1-t2-goose.json --tasks \"$T2_TASKS\" --out \"$T2_OUT/goose\" --runs 5\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:227:  node eval/run.mjs --config eval/configs/v1-t2-opencode.json --tasks \"$T2_TASKS\" --out \"$T2_OUT/opencode\" --runs 5\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:228:  node eval/score.mjs --pairs \"$T2_OUT/nexus/results.jsonl\" \"$T2_OUT/goose/results.jsonl\" \"$T2_OUT/opencode/results.jsonl\"\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:231:  Record the resolved `T2_TASKS`, unique `T2_OUT`, config digests, installed RC identity, model fingerprint, and exact commands in the frozen run record before starting. A failed or interrupted invocation remains evidence; any permitted infrastructure rerun uses the accepted rerun procedure and is retained separately. Do not score until all required runs and manifests exist. The scorer accepts exactly the Nexus, Goose and OpenCode result files.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:233:### 6.2 T4 fault injection (ACC-QUAL-T4)\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:247:### 6.3 T3 long tasks (ACC-QUAL-T3)\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:251:### 6.4 Thresholds (DEC-05; all must hold)\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:255:| False VERIFIED (T2 + T3 + T4) | **= 0** |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:256:| T2 pooled hidden-test correctness | ≥ 60% and ≥ best matched peer − 10 pts |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:257:| T2 per class (bugfix, feature, refactor, debug) | ≥ 40% |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:260:| T4 truthful outcome | = 100% |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:261:| T4 hang beyond budget + 5 min | = 0 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:262:| T3 false-absence | = 0 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:263:| T3 false-presence | = 0 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:264:| T3 steering honoured | ≥ 95% |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:269:## 7. Install, upgrade, rollback, uninstall (ACC-PLAT; E2)\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:286:## 8. Independent acceptance (REQ-AGT-110, ACC-CONT-10)\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:307:   - 5 random T2 tasks;\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:308:   - 2 T4 classes.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:314:## 9. Contest (separate product; not a client gate)\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:327:## 10. Release decision (G6)\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:333:- [ ] §4 standalone and provider matrix: all rows PASS.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:338:- [ ] The pre-RC source gate passes from a clean source worktree: `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce`. Every B/RR source row outside the §1.1 qualification-only map must be ≥ `tested`. A mapped row below `tested` is reported as deferred; this result does not accept or qualify it.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:339:- [ ] The exact-RC evidence gate passes from the clean RC worktree and is bound to the exact RC source commit and installed RC artifact. Run the checker with the custodian-approved, immutable qualification record and evidence directory:\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:341:  The version 1 record contains `sourceCommit` (full commit ID), `rcTag` (for example `v1.0.0-rc.1`), `artifactSha256`, `artifactProvenance` (`sourceCommit`, `artifactSha256`, and a hashed provenance report), `independentAcceptance` (`disposition`, `reviewer`, `implementers`, zero `blockingDefects`, and a hashed report reference), and one `requirements` entry for every B/RR row. For `ACCEPT WITH DEFECTS`, include each non-blocking defect with its owner disposition; unresolved or blocking defects fail. Each requirement entry records its status and one or more hashed evidence files covering the exact criteria required by the ledger and the §1.1 qualification-only map. Every criterion evidence file must be a JSON object with top-level `sourceCommit`, `rcTag`, and `artifactSha256` values exactly matching the validated qualification record, current RC source commit, and installed RC artifact. A digest-valid report copied from another source revision, RC tag, or artifact is rejected. A B row recorded as `tested` also needs a non-empty `qualificationNotApplicable.reason` and a `qualificationNotApplicable.decision` matching the approved per-requirement exception table and a matching applicability declaration in DECISIONS.md; an unrelated or record-supplied decision is rejected. Evidence paths must be relative regular files under the evidence root, with no symlinks. Missing, unknown, stale, mismatched, or incomplete evidence fails the gate. The checker requires a clean worktree, rejects `--ledger` overrides, enforces source-ledger thresholds outside the explicit §1.1 lifecycle rows, and requires the exact-RC record itself to meet the normal status threshold for every row. It never mutates the source ledger or relaxes a requirement's B/RR record threshold. The checker validates source/tag/artifact identity bindings and evidence hashes; it does not authenticate the reviewer or prove that the artifact was built from the source commit. The approved release workflow must independently verify build provenance/attestation, and the designated custodian and independent reviewer must verify their respective approvals and custody evidence.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:343:- [ ] Release notes state the standalone scope (DEC-16), the provider tiers (DEC-06), the experimental surfaces (DEC-03, DEC-07) and the known limitations.\n# Nexus Code v1.0.0: release qualification procedure\n\nThis is the procedure that decides whether a release candidate (RC) may become v1.0.0. It defines:\n\n- the environments;\n- the workflow matrix;\n- the evidence each step must produce;\n- explicit pass/fail gates.\n\nThree separate questions are judged and recorded separately:\n\n| Question | Who answers it |\n|---|---|\n| **Implementation self-assessment** | Did the implementer's tests pass? |\n| **Product qualification** | Did the RC meet these gates on real workflows? |\n| **Independent acceptance** | Did a reviewer other than the implementer agree? |\n\nA gate passes only on archived evidence bound to the source commit or installed RC artifact that the gate evaluates. Source-level evidence names the exact source commit; installed-RC evidence names both that commit and the installed package digest. A green test suite alone never qualifies the product.\n\n## 1.1 Release-candidate lifecycle and evidence identity\n\nThe release sequence has five distinct stages. Passing an earlier stage is a prerequisite for the next stage, not a substitute for it. Every G0–G4 acceptance ID remains mandatory; the stage determines which exact input and evidence it evaluates, not whether the check applies.\n\n1. **Pre-RC source gates.** Before creating an RC tag, run required source CI and every G0–G4 check whose acceptance method evaluates source, a source-built test binary, or an environment without requiring a published RC. Record the full commit ID and check results. Source checks do not establish behavior of the installed package.\n2. **RC artifact construction.** After the required owner authorization, create the version-matched RC tag on that exact source commit and use the repository release workflow to build and publish the RC artifacts. Record the workflow run, tag commit, artifact digests, and provenance. The workflow-produced artifacts are the candidates for qualification; a local build or a different commit is not interchangeable. RC artifact publication is not product qualification or final release acceptance.\n3. **RC artifact gates.** Before installed-RC product qualification, run every G0–G4 check whose acceptance method requires the RC archive, RC attestation/release, or workflow-produced artifact. This includes ACC-SUP-01/02/03/06/08. ACC-PKG checks that explicitly require an installed package run against this RC as specified by their test method. Record the RC tag commit, workflow run, artifact digests, and each check result. A source-level analogue does not replace an artifact-bound check.\n4. **Installed-RC qualification.** Install the workflow-produced RC package using the documented procedure and run the applicable product, provider, task-quality, terminal, installation, and independent-acceptance gates in §§4–8. Bind each result to both the RC source commit and installed package digest. If a source change or rebuilt artifact changes either identity, rerun every affected gate against the new candidate and retain prior results as historical evidence.\n5. **Stable promotion and publication.** After exact-RC acceptance and G6 pass, create a stable-version commit directly on the accepted RC commit, changing only the synchronized version metadata required for v1.0.0. Record both commits and the version-only diff. Run required source CI and all applicable source G0–G4 checks on this exact stable-version commit before tagging. If any other source changes, restart RC construction and qualification. Then create the `v1.0.0` tag on that checked commit and build a draft release. Keep its assets unpublished while verifying the stable artifact identity, provenance, package contents, installation, and publication metadata. Compare the stable package contents with the accepted RC; if packaged behavior or content differs beyond version-specific metadata, rerun affected installed-RC qualification gates and obtain independent acceptance for the stable artifact. Publish the draft only after these checks pass and the signed acceptance disposition is recorded. Record the published digests and provenance.\n\nThe final G6 decision in §10 applies to promoting the accepted RC toward a stable release. It requires the applicable gates to pass for the accepted RC and authorizes the version-only stable commit and its source checks, followed by the stable tag and draft build; it does not waive source CI, artifact identity, installed-RC qualification, or any threshold. Public publication is a separate post-build gate in stage 5 above. The release workflow must keep stable assets in draft state until stable artifact checks pass. Source verification at integration 6a16cb6 confirms the tag-triggered release workflow now supports published RC prereleases and draft stable releases. The earlier immediate-stable-publication source blocker is resolved; an actual stable draft build, artifact verification, signed acceptance, and deliberate publication are still required and remain unproven until their run evidence is recorded.\n\nExact-RC requirements records identify at least one implementer and an independent reviewer. For a blocking requirement recorded as `tested` instead of `product-qualified`, the cited decision must be explicitly allowlisted for that requirement in the approved qualification-exceptions table below, and its `DECISIONS.md` section must contain a matching requirement-specific line of the form `Qualification applicability: REQ-... = NOT REQUIRED ...`. A record-supplied or unrelated decision cannot authorize an exception. The record must include digest-bound evidence for every `ACC-*` criterion in that requirement's ledger Acceptance column.\n\nThe post-RC closure requirements listed below may remain `open`, `partial`, or `implemented` in the source ledger at the RC commit because their remaining acceptance is completed during G6 or installed-RC qualification. The bare `--enforce` invocation is the pre-RC source gate: it checks every other B/RR row against the source threshold and reports mapped rows as deferred, not accepted. At G6, the exact-RC invocation must provide a record meeting the normal B/RR status threshold and digest-bound evidence for every criterion in this table. The table also supplies the criterion mapping for rows whose ledger points to an ACCEPTANCE section instead of naming ACC IDs. The source ledger is never rewritten by the record. Any below-tested required row omitted from this table still fails.\n\n<!-- RC-QUALIFICATION-ONLY:START -->\n### Qualification-only requirements for exact-RC enforcement\n\n| Requirement | Acceptance criteria required in the exact-RC record | Remaining stage |\n|---|---|---|\n| REQ-REL-003 | ACC-PLAT | Installed-RC platform and Node-version matrix |\n| REQ-AGT-002 | ACC-VER-03, ACC-VER-04, ACC-VER-09, ACC-QUAL-T2, ACC-QUAL-T3, ACC-QUAL-T4 | Installed-RC T2/T3/T4 outcome thresholds |\n| REQ-AGT-010 | ACC-TRUST-04 | Independent acceptance of the DEC-04 v1 subset |\n| REQ-PRV-003 | ACC-INF-10 | Installed-RC standalone and absent-gateway behavior |\n| REQ-REL-005 | ACC-SUP-04, ACC-SUP-05 | Exact-RC security and dependency artifact checks |\n| REQ-AGT-110 | ACC-CONT-10, ACC-GOV-06 | Installed-RC continuity and independent acceptance |\n| REQ-PRV-111 | ACC-PRV-LIVE | Installed-RC provider verification |\n| REQ-REL-114 | ACC-SUP-08 | Exact-RC cross-runner reproducibility |\n| REQ-QUAL-101 | ACC-QUAL-T2 | Installed-RC held-out T2 qualification |\n| REQ-QUAL-107 | ACC-PRV-STANDALONE, ACC-PRV-LIVE | Installed-RC standalone and provider matrix |\n| REQ-QUAL-108 | ACC-TUI-STEER, ACC-TUI-A11Y, ACC-TUI-MANUAL | CI PTY checks and installed-RC real-terminal matrix |\n| REQ-QUAL-109 | ACC-QUAL-T3 | Installed-RC T3 long-task qualification |\n<!-- RC-QUALIFICATION-ONLY:END -->\n\n<!-- RC-QUALIFICATION-EXCEPTIONS:START -->\n### Approved exact-RC qualification exceptions\n\n| Requirement | Approved decision | Scope |\n|---|---|---|\n<!-- RC-QUALIFICATION-EXCEPTIONS:END -->\n\n## 1. Rules\n\n1. The RC is built and published by the release workflow from a clean tag. Its version is identical across all components (REQ-REL-103).\n2. All qualification runs use the **installed RC package**, installed with the documented one-line command. They never use a checkout build. The only exception is CI unit and PTY suites, which run from source at the same commit.\n3. Thresholds (DEC-05) are frozen before the first M5 run. A failing gate is fixed in code and the run is repeated as `rc.N+1`. A threshold is never relaxed after results are known.\n4. Evidence goes to `docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/<rc>/`. The directory contains:\n   - `manifest.json`: commit, package sha256, environment, model fingerprint, dates;\n   - raw outputs;\n   - a `SHA256SUMS` file.\n\n   Secrets are redacted before commit.\n5. Any step that cannot run in the available environment is recorded as **NOT RUN** with its reason. A NOT RUN on a blocker gate fails the gate.\n\n## 2. Environments\n\n| ID | Environment | Used for |\n|---|---|---|\n| E1 | GitHub Actions: ubuntu-22.04 and ubuntu-24.04; Node 22 and 24; pinned Rust | Unit, integration and PTY suites; packaging; reproducibility |\n| E2 | Docker clean images: ubuntu:22.04, ubuntu:24.04, debian:12, fedora:40. Each with no Node, then with Node 20, Node 22 and Node 24. Non-root user. | Installer, upgrade, rollback, uninstall, platform failure messages |\n| E3 | Operator dev box: Linux x86-64, real terminals (xterm, kitty, tmux, VS Code terminal, GNOME Terminal) | Terminal matrix, live sessions |\n| E4 | Homelab-ai gateway, the **only** inference path (DEC-16): direct, and through `eval/standalone/plain_proxy.mjs` | Task-quality runs, standalone qualification, T3/T4 |\n| E5 | Cloud, small spend: ChatGPT sign-in (experimental tier) and OpenRouter with a pinned model; OpenAI and Anthropic keys if added | Provider verify; one live task per supported cloud provider |\n\n## 3. Gate checklist (G0–G4: automated acceptance IDs)\n\nEvery ACC ID below is defined in the linked spec. The plan for each spec names the test that implements it. Run each check at the lifecycle stage dictated by its acceptance method in §1.1: source-applicable checks before the RC tag; checks requiring the RC archive, attestation, release, or installed package after RC construction; environment-specific checks in their declared environment. Bind every result to the exact source commit and, when artifact-dependent, the RC package digest. A source test or local build does not replace an artifact-bound check, and no G0–G4 ID is complete until all of its applicable checks pass.\n\n| Gate | Acceptance IDs | Spec |\n|---|---|---|\n| Safety | ACC-SAFE-01 to ACC-SAFE-10 | SPEC-01 |\n| Process ownership | ACC-PROC-01 to ACC-PROC-08 (ACC-PROC-07 is the load test, run in E3) | SPEC-02 |\n| Untrusted inputs | ACC-TRUST-01 to ACC-TRUST-09 | SPEC-03 |\n| Continuity | ACC-CONT-01 to ACC-CONT-09 (ACC-CONT-10 is in §8) | SPEC-04 |\n| Inference | ACC-INF-01 to ACC-INF-09 (ACC-INF-10 is in §4) | SPEC-05 |\n| Packaging | ACC-PKG-01 to ACC-PKG-09 | SPEC-06 |\n| Supply chain | ACC-SUP-01 to ACC-SUP-08 (artifact-bound ACC-SUP-01/02/03/06/08 after RC construction) | SPEC-07 |\n| Persistence | ACC-PER-01 to ACC-PER-07 | SPEC-08 |\n| Governance | ACC-GOV-01 to ACC-GOV-06 | SPEC-09 |\n| Verification | ACC-VER-01 to ACC-VER-09 | SPEC-11 |\n| Upgrade | ACC-UPG-01 to ACC-UPG-14 | SPEC-12 |\n\n\n### 3.1 Acceptance IDs defined in this file\n\nThese are retained commitments from REQUIREMENTS §2 and cross-cutting checks.\n\n| ID | Check | Pass condition |\n|---|---|---|\n| ACC-TUI-STEER | PTY: submit a task; while a tool runs, type steering text and press Enter; also queue a steer before a cancel | Steering is applied at the next step boundary. Unapplied steering is returned to the composer. Nothing is dropped silently (existing `sidecar_steering_diff` plus PTY s6). |\n| ACC-TUI-A11Y | PTY with `NO_COLOR=1` and with `TERM=dumb` at 40×14 and 100×30 | Zero colour SGR codes. Every state is distinguishable by glyph and word. Hints are complete at 40 columns (TUI-10). |\n| ACC-SEC-JAIL | `core/tests` plus harness-core calls with `..`, absolute, symlinked-file, symlinked-dir and symlinked-parent payloads | Every one is refused (C §4 R1 set). |\n| ACC-SEC-B6 | Re-run `docs/reviews/evidence/qualification_2026-10-12/repro/zz_trust_repro.test.ts`. Seeded-secret scan of `~/.nexus` and `.nexus` after a scripted turn. | Zero plaintext seeded secrets in durable stores or outbound bodies. |\n| ACC-PRV-LIVE | `nexus providers verify --provider <p> -m <pinned model> -j` for each provider listed as supported (DEC-06) | `passed: true`. Receipts archived. |\n| ACC-PRV-STANDALONE | §4.2 on the installed RC through the approved stripped proxy, with gateway credentials absent from the child environment | Every required profile completes through the proxy and the absent-gateway boundary holds; receipts archived. |\n| ACC-PLAT | E2 matrix, §7 | All rows pass. |\n| ACC-QUAL-T2 | §6.1 + §6.4 | Thresholds met. |\n| ACC-QUAL-T3 | §6.3 + §6.4 | Thresholds met. |\n| ACC-QUAL-T4 | §6.2 + §6.4 | Thresholds met. |\n| ACC-QUAL-SMOKE | `make test` includes the T1 self-test and the T4 smoke | Present and passing. |\n| ACC-TUI-MANUAL | §5.3 on the installed RC across five required terminal environments and three required sizes | Every cell passes; screenshots and per-cell verdicts are archived. |\n\n## 4. Standalone and provider qualification (REQ-PRV-106, REQ-PRV-111, REQ-QUAL-107)\n\n### 4.1 Clean-HOME procedure\n\n1. `export HOME=$(mktemp -d)`.\n2. Install the RC with the documented command.\n3. Create `~/.config/nexus/config.env` containing only:\n   - `LOCAL_LLM_ENDPOINT=http://127.0.0.1:<proxy>/v1`\n   - `LOCAL_LLM_MODEL=<id as listed by the proxy>`\n   - `LOCAL_LLM_API_KEY=REDACTED\n\n   No gateway token file, no homelab paths, no `NODE_*` overrides.\n4. Start `node eval/standalone/plain_proxy.mjs --upstream <gateway> --token-file <operator token> [--emulate <kind>]`. The gateway token stays with the proxy and never reaches the Nexus HOME.\n5. Run `nexus doctor --json` and archive it. It must report the server kind and context source with no `gateway` capability.\n\n### 4.2 Standalone matrix\n\n| Profile | What Nexus sees | Runs | Pass condition |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| P-plain | Bare OpenAI-compatible `/models` and chat. No tokenize, no capacity headers. | Standalone T2 subset (≥ 10 held-out tasks) × 3 runs; T4 classes 1, 3, 4, 7 × 3 | T2 correctness ≥ (gateway-direct T2 correctness on the same tasks − 10 pts). False VERIFIED = 0. T4 truthful = 100%. Context source reported as `client_default` or an operator override, with no error. |\n| P-llamacpp | Emulated llama.cpp `/props` and overflow body | Same tasks × 1 run; plus the forced-overflow case (context limit set to 8k) | Context discovered from `/props`. Overflow gives one compact-and-retry, then success or an actionable error. |\n| P-vllm | Emulated `max_model_len` and vLLM overflow body | Same as P-llamacpp | Same, with the context source `max_model_len` |\n| P-ollama | Emulated `/api/show` and Ollama overflow body | Same as P-llamacpp | Same, with the context source `ollama_show` |\n| Conformance | CI fixtures for llama.cpp, vLLM, LM Studio and Ollama shapes | CI | All pass (ACC-INF-01, -02, -05) |\n\nACC-INF-10 passes only when every row passes. The release notes state the scope in the form required by DEC-16.\n\n### 4.3 Provider matrix (E5)\n\n| Provider | Tier (DEC-06) | Required for v1.0.0 |\n|---|---|---|\n| OpenRouter, pinned model | Supported | `providers verify` PASS, plus one live small task (a §6-style bug fix) reaching a correct outcome |\n| ChatGPT sign-in | Experimental | Verify PASS recorded (already PASS at db1ca55; repeat on the RC) |\n| OpenAI API key, Anthropic | Experimental unless keys are added | If promoted: verify PASS plus one live task. Otherwise NOT RUN, and they are labelled experimental. |\n| Copilot | Experimental | Not required |\n\n## 5. Terminal acceptance (REQ-QUAL-108)\n\n### 5.1 CI PTY suites (E1)\n\nThese must pass:\n\n- `tui_approval_input_e2e`\n- `tui_diff_e2e`\n- `tui_maturity_e2e`\n- `tui_model_picker_e2e`\n- `tui_multiline_e2e`\n- `tui_surface_e2e`\n- new: `repl_approval_e2e`\n- new: `process_lifecycle_e2e`\n- new: `startup_unreachable_e2e`\n- new: the package PTY smoke\n\n### 5.2 Scripted PTY scenarios against the installed RC (E3, mock gateway)\n\nThese are ports of `evidence/D_pty/`.\n\n| Scenario | Pass condition |\n|---|---|\n| s1 startup, unreachable endpoint | The endpoint is named, with a fix hint. The turn ends with guidance in ≤ 2.5 min. |\n| s2 approval under continuous typing, paste and burst, at 40×14 | No decision is made by stray input. A deliberate key decides. |\n| s3 completion | The outcome is shown in words: VERIFIED, REGRESSION_FREE or UNVERIFIED. |\n| s4–s6 cancel and steer | Cancel is acknowledged within 1 frame and idle within 5 s. Steering is applied. |\n| s7 resume | The prior conversation is shown. |\n| s8–s9 cancel or quit during a tool | Zero surviving processes. |\n| r1a / r1d REPL approvals | DENIED for a lone Enter and for a typed-ahead `y`. |\n\n### 5.3 Manual real-terminal matrix (E3)\n\nTerminals: xterm, kitty (kitty keyboard protocol on), tmux 3.x inside GNOME Terminal, VS Code integrated terminal, GNOME Terminal. Sizes: 80×24, 40×14, 200×60.\n\nFor each terminal × size, check:\n\n1. Launch `nexus` (the TUI appears).\n2. Approval panel. Type continuously across it. Paste 3 lines. Approve with a deliberate key.\n3. Shift+Enter or Alt+Enter multiline.\n4. Resize during streaming.\n5. Esc during `sleep 30` (no survivors).\n6. Ctrl-C twice (clean terminal restore: echo on, no stray escape codes).\n7. NO_COLOR.\n\nRecord PASS/FAIL per cell, with a screenshot of the approval panel and the post-exit terminal state.\n\n**Gate:** zero FAIL on checks 2, 5 and 6, which are safety checks. Other FAILs need a written disposition (fix, or a documented known limitation).\n\n## 6. Task-quality qualification (REQ-QUAL-101 to REQ-QUAL-106, REQ-QUAL-109)\n\nEnvironment: E4 (gateway direct), serial runs, with matched model fingerprint, budgets and env (REQ-QUAL-102).\n\n### 6.1 T2 held-out (ACC-QUAL-T2)\n\n- 40 sealed tasks. The manifest is committed before RC1, and authorship is recorded (agent-authored, DEC-05).\n- 5 runs × {Nexus RC, Goose, OpenCode}.\n- Before execution, freeze three qualification configs at `eval/configs/v1-t2-nexus.json`, `eval/configs/v1-t2-goose.json`, and `eval/configs/v1-t2-opencode.json`. Each must set `qualification: true`, identify the same model fingerprint and sampling settings, and record equal context/output and task budgets; the Nexus config must identify the installed RC and its package digest. Do not derive these files from the pilot configs by silently inheriting or changing settings.\n- Set `T2_TASKS` to the custodian-approved, sealed task directory and `T2_OUT` to a new, empty, run-specific output directory. Do not use the disclosed `eval/tasks` development set as held-out evidence. Preserve all three outputs and their manifests; never reuse an output directory for a retry.\n- Run each config serially, with identical task selection and five runs per task:\n\n  ```bash\n  set -euo pipefail\n  : \"${T2_TASKS:?set the sealed task directory}\"\n  : \"${T2_OUT:?set a new unique output directory}\"\n  test ! -e \"$T2_OUT\"\n  node eval/run.mjs --config eval/configs/v1-t2-nexus.json --tasks \"$T2_TASKS\" --out \"$T2_OUT/nexus\" --runs 5\n  node eval/run.mjs --config eval/configs/v1-t2-goose.json --tasks \"$T2_TASKS\" --out \"$T2_OUT/goose\" --runs 5\n  node eval/run.mjs --config eval/configs/v1-t2-opencode.json --tasks \"$T2_TASKS\" --out \"$T2_OUT/opencode\" --runs 5\n  node eval/score.mjs --pairs \"$T2_OUT/nexus/results.jsonl\" \"$T2_OUT/goose/results.jsonl\" \"$T2_OUT/opencode/results.jsonl\"\n  ```\n\n  Record the resolved `T2_TASKS`, unique `T2_OUT`, config digests, installed RC identity, model fingerprint, and exact commands in the frozen run record before starting. A failed or interrupted invocation remains evidence; any permitted infrastructure rerun uses the accepted rerun procedure and is retained separately. Do not score until all required runs and manifests exist. The scorer accepts exactly the Nexus, Goose and OpenCode result files.\n\n### 6.2 T4 fault injection (ACC-QUAL-T4)\n\n9 fault classes × 5 runs on the Nexus RC. The configured faults run through `eval/run.mjs` and `eval/model_proxy.mjs`; the hanging-command and full-disk cases use task fixtures, and SIGTERM-then-resume uses the runner case (DEC-05 amendment, 2026-10-17: the union of the distinct scenarios below):\n\n1. refused connection mid-turn\n2. 5xx / overloaded\n3. stream cut mid-tool-call\n4. output-limit truncation\n5. hanging test command\n6. disk full\n7. context overflow at 32k\n8. malformed tool-call JSON\n9. SIGTERM then `run --resume`\n\n### 6.3 T3 long tasks (ACC-QUAL-T3)\n\n- 8 tasks × 5 runs. Each run must have ≥ 60 steps, ≥ 2 compactions and scripted steering.\n\n### 6.4 Thresholds (DEC-05; all must hold)\n\n| Metric | Gate |\n|---|---|\n| False VERIFIED (T2 + T3 + T4) | **= 0** |\n| T2 pooled hidden-test correctness | ≥ 60% and ≥ best matched peer − 10 pts |\n| T2 per class (bugfix, feature, refactor, debug) | ≥ 40% |\n| Crash rate (all Nexus runs) | ≤ 2% |\n| Regression rate | ≤ 5% |\n| T4 truthful outcome | = 100% |\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":913285460}},"started_at_ms":1792867518891,"completed_at_ms":1792867519804}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-24T18:45:21.340Z","ordinal":302684,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a16f3b-533b-7c50-99ed-79a2a6f3a285","call_id":"call_a913acc661454004932283d159f1b0d1","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 3.6 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 12378)\nTotal output lines: 391\n\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.4.md:1:# Nexus Code v1.0.0-rc.4 release candidate\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.4.md:9:## Changes since RC3\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.4.md:13:- Classifies length-truncated assistant output separately from recoverable provider failures, so truncated tool arguments are not retried through provider recovery.\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.4.md:23:- Locks the npm release tools used for notices and the SBOM, rejects deprecated packages in that lock, and adds a cross-runner workflow that rebuilds a published RC on Ubuntu 22.04 and 24.04 and compares the archive, compatibility metadata, checksums, notices, SBOM and installer with the published assets.\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.4.md:24:- Requires the approved digest-pinned Rust builder for release packaging and reproducibility checks. Local packaging examples and cross-runner checks use the same approved builder identity; the host-build opt-out is for local development only.\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.4.md:28:## Runtime requirements\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.4.md:32:- An OpenAI-compatible inference endpoint, local or explicitly selected provider.\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.4.md:36:## Candidate assets\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:1:# Nexus Code v1.0.0: requirement ledger\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:7:## 1. Legend\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:9:### Status ladder\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:22:### Release classes\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:31:### Evidence labels\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:44:### Links\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:49:## 2. Carried-over commitments (REQ-*-0xx)\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:51:### 2.1 Retained commitments (already met or partly met; must not regress)\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:55:| REQ-AGT-001 | COMPACTION_AND_CONTINUITY §A; operator directive | No default cumulative step or time ceiling. Turns end on completion, cancel, demonstrated stagnation, actionable failure or an operator-set budget. Resource-safety valves (provider iterations, 10k scheduler transitions, 5 compaction attempts) are allowed and labelled. | `types.ts:127-133`; `agent.ts:4379-4445` | TEST + SRC (A §5) | tested | N | — | ACC-CONT-04, ACC-QUAL-T3 | K | SPEC-04 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:56:| REQ-AGT-002 | quickstart; TOP_TIER B3; EXEC-005 | Truthful outcome taxonomy. VERIFIED requires a passing, deliverable-bound verifier run, plus fail-before/pass-after independence for discovered verifiers. UNVERIFIED, REGRESSION_FREE, BLOCKED and LIMIT_REACHED are distinct, with exit codes 0/2/1/130. | `agent.ts:5726-5764`; `tester.ts:371-430,541-627`; `turn.ts:318-351` | TEST at db1ca55; candidate suite at `6151a23` passes ACC-VER-03/04/09 regression tests. Historical VER-04/05 findings and tuned-set/live evidence remain in [A2_verification.md](evidence/A2_verification.md) and the dated evidence files. | partial | N | M5 false-VERIFIED threshold remains unqualified pending held-out T2/T3/T4 evidence; historical VER-04/05 implementation defects have regression coverage at the candidate. | ACC-VER-03/04/09, ACC-QUAL-T2 | B | SPEC-11 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:61:| REQ-AGT-007 | release notes alpha.2 | Output-truncated reply: nothing from it runs; one in-turn retry; a second consecutive truncation ends the turn. | `agent.ts:4671-4683`; `client.ts:1459-1468` | TEST (6/6, scripted) | tested | **N (pending)** | Never observed live | ACC-CONT-10, ACC-QUAL-T4 | K | SPEC-04 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:62:| REQ-AGT-008 | provider recovery design | Bounded provider recovery: 20 min deadline, jittered backoff, Retry-After honoured, probe before an UNKNOWN replay, ≤ 2 replays. | `provider_recovery.ts` | TEST 23/23 + 15/15 | tested | N | A never-reachable endpoint waits too long (TUI-06) | ACC-INF-07 | K | SPEC-05 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:74:| REQ-PRV-003 | COMPACTION:7-9; handoff doc | Nexus works without homelab-ai. Gateway features are optional and absent-safe. | `provider_capabilities.ts:184-195` | TEST (scripted) | implemented | N | No live standalone evidence (HIST-08) | ACC-INF-10 | B (via REQ-PRV-106) | SPEC-05 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:75:| REQ-PRV-004 | CLOUD_PROVIDERS | Cloud spend limits and receipts; disclosure notice on first request. | `usage.ts`; `client.ts:509-569` | TEST (mock); HIST live (openrouter, chatgpt); RT 2026-10-14 receipts written with provider-reported usage | tested | N | Other providers mock-only | ACC-PRV-LIVE | RR | SPEC-05 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:80:| REQ-REL-005 | SCAN-001..005 | Dependency and secret gates; zero High/Critical in a release. | `scripts/security_gates.sh` | Candidate source suite: npm audit, cargo deny/advisory-license gate, credential scan passed at `6151a23`; release-artifact scan not run. | partial | N | The old nine-advisory fallback cited by REL-07 is no longer called by `security_gates.sh`; current source uses cargo-deny or cargo-audit and fails if neither exists. ACC-SUP-04's missing-scanner case is covered by `REQ-REL-110`. The remaining gate is exact-RC supply-chain/security evidence; SAST is not specified by ACC-SUP-04. | ACC-SUP-04, ACC-SUP-05 | RR (via REQ-REL-110) | SPEC-07 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:85:### 2.2 Historical items that are superseded, contradicted or descoped (written dispositions; REQ-OPS-103)\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:92:| EXEC-011 (evaluators score the exact candidate) | DEMONSTRATED | **Contradicted** for `nexus eval` (VER-07) | `nexus eval` is experimental (DEC-07). The qualification harness is `eval/` (REQ-QUAL-106). |\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:103:| REL-001 byte-identical builds | deferred | Same-runner proven | REQ-REL-114 (RR, cross-runner once for the RC) |\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:109:| POST_REMEDIATION_DOGFOOD \"INTEGRATION_BLOCKED\" (completion truth across process death; retry launders unverified changes) | not re-dispositioned | Covered by REQ-AGT-101/106 and T4 class 9 | Re-qualify through ACC-QUAL-T4 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:111:## 3. v1.0.0 requirements (REQ-*-1xx)\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:115:### 3.1 Safety and execution boundary\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:146:### 3.2 Completion truth, continuity and recovery\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:166:### 3.3 Local inference and providers\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:170:| REQ-PRV-101 | Standalone commitment | Context discovery for vLLM, llama.cpp, LM Studio and Ollama, with the source labelled. | standalone workflow | `provider_capabilities.ts` | TEST (PRV-06; test:cli/test/server_context_discovery.test.ts::\"discovery against a local server\") | tested | ACC-INF-01 | **B** | PRV-06 | SPEC-05 / PLAN-05 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:171:| REQ-PRV-102 | TOP_TIER I-05 (carried) | A capacity rejection leads to one compact-and-retry, then an actionable error. llama.cpp, LM Studio and Ollama bodies are classified. | standalone / failure | `provider_recovery.ts:82,106`; `agent.ts:5072` | TEST (PRV-07; test:cli/test/provider_recovery_agent.test.ts::\"capacity rejection handling (ACC-INF-02)\") | tested | ACC-INF-02 | **B** | PRV-06, PRV-07 | SPEC-05 / PLAN-05 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:172:| REQ-PRV-103 | CRED-003 (carried) | Error text is bounded and redacted on every path. | safety | `client.ts:903,1636,1689`, `oauth.ts` | TEST (PRV-03; test:cli/test/provider_robustness.test.ts::\"listModels and generateEmbedding huge error bodies are bounded and redacted (ACC-INF-03)\") | tested | ACC-INF-03 | RR | PRV-03 | SPEC-05 / PLAN-05 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:173:| REQ-PRV-104 | Audit | Timeouts and cancel on every network call. First-byte, idle and total timeouts. Bounded replays. | failure | `client.ts`, `embeddings.ts`, `model_catalog.ts` | TEST (PRV-05, PRV-10; test:cli/test/provider_robustness.test.ts::\"watchdog first-byte and idle timeouts reject when server hangs or stalls (ACC-INF-04)\") | tested | ACC-INF-04 | RR | PRV-05, PRV-10 | SPEC-05 / PLAN-05 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:174:| REQ-PRV-105 | Audit | Stream parser robustness, with recorded real-server fixtures. | compatibility | `client.ts:1326-1483` | TEST (PRV-04; test:cli/test/provider_fixes.test.ts::\"stream parser handles tool name chunks, repeated tool names, and object arguments (PRV-04 / REQ-PRV-105)\", test:cli/test/provider_robustness.test.ts::\"empty stream re-request records executions: 2 in receipt (ACC-INF-06)\") | tested | ACC-INF-05, ACC-INF-06 | RR | PRV-04 | SPEC-05 / PLAN-05 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:176:| REQ-PRV-107 | TOP_TIER I-07 | Local receipts (opt-out). | evidence | `client.ts:561-569`, `usage.ts` | TEST (B §6 G1; test:cli/test/provider_robustness.test.ts::\"local receipts are recorded with origin_class: local and opt out with NEXUS_RECEIPTS=0 (REQ-PRV-107)\") | tested | ACC-INF-06 | RR | B §6 G1 | SPEC-05 / PLAN-05 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:179:| REQ-PRV-111 | DEC-06 | Live `providers verify` for each provider listed as supported. The others are labelled experimental. | compatibility claims | `provider_cli.ts` | **RT 2026-10-14 @db1ca55:** chatgpt (gpt-6-luna) PASS, openrouter (openrouter/free) PASS. **RT 2026-10-16 @6151a23+4d82578, pinned models:** openrouter `nvidia/nemotron-3-super-120b-a12b:free` PASS (one model served every request), chatgpt `gpt-6-luna` PASS (`evidence/live/verify_*_pinned_2026-10-16.json`). The run found and fixed the option-scope regression (4d82578). openai-key and anthropic not connected. | partial (repeat on the RC) | ACC-PRV-LIVE | RR | B §6 G2 | SPEC-05 / PLAN-10 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:180:| REQ-TUI-105 | Audit | Startup endpoint probe with a fix hint. A never-reachable endpoint is bounded to 2 minutes. | onboarding | `sidecar.ts`, `repl.ts`, `provider_recovery.ts` | TEST (TUI-06; test:cli/test/startup_unreachable_e2e.test.ts::\"ACC-INF-07 (REQ-TUI-105): Startup endpoint probe and first-contact deadline\") | tested | ACC-INF-07 | RR | TUI-06 | SPEC-05 / PLAN-05 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:182:### 3.4 Packaging, release and diagnostics\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:203:| REQ-REL-114 | REL-001 (carried) | Cross-runner reproducibility, demonstrated once for the RC. | supply chain | `repro.yml` | UNV | open | ACC-SUP-08 | RR | E §6 | SPEC-07 / PLAN-07 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:208:### 3.5 Persistence\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:220:### 3.6 Governance and documentation\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:230:### 3.7 Qualification\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:234:| REQ-QUAL-101 | TOP_TIER Q1; DEC-05 | Held-out T2 evaluation: 40 tasks, ≥ 50% external, sealed manifest. | product maturity | `eval/` | HIST (6 tuned tasks) | open | ACCEPTANCE §6.1 | **B** | EVL-001 | SPEC-10 / PLAN-10 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:235:| REQ-QUAL-102 | DEC-05 | Matched conditions with a model fingerprint. | validity | `eval/run.mjs`, `eval/validate.mjs` | TEST (EVL-004; test:cli/test/eval_integrity.test.ts::\"a qualification run is refused without a model fingerprint\") | tested | ACC-QUAL-T2 (ACCEPTANCE §6.1) | **B** | EVL-004 | SPEC-10 / PLAN-10 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:236:| REQ-QUAL-103 | DEC-05 | 5 runs per task and configuration; Goose and OpenCode as peers. | statistics | `eval/run.mjs`, `eval/score.mjs` | TEST (`eval_harness.test.ts`: peer version/budget forwarding, installed RC/version/package pin, Nexus/provider-limit parity, paired fingerprint/limit/sampling/budget/version and 5-run checks; commits `ef2d040`, `b27ae04`; [validation record](../reviews/evidence/v1/PLAN-10_PR-10d/validation.md)); UNV (live M5 runs) | tested | ACC-QUAL-T2 (ACCEPTANCE §6.1) | **B** | EVL-001 | SPEC-10 / PLAN-10 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:237:| REQ-QUAL-104 | DEC-05 | Separately reported metrics, including false VERIFIED = 0. | honesty | `eval/score.mjs` | TEST (EVL-005; test:cli/test/eval_harness.test.ts, test:cli/test/eval_integrity.test.ts) | tested | ACC-QUAL-T2 (ACCEPTANCE §6.1) | **B** | EVL-005 | SPEC-10 / PLAN-10 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:238:| REQ-QUAL-105 | TOP_TIER Q6; DEC-05 | T4 fault injection: 9 classes × 5 runs (DEC-05 amendment 2026-10-17: union of the nine distinct scenarios retained), 100% truthful outcomes. | failure / recovery | `eval/model_proxy.mjs`, `eval/score.mjs` | TEST (EVL-001; test:cli/test/eval_integrity.test.ts::\"the model proxy injects each scheduled fault\", test:cli/test/eval_harness.test.ts::\"T4 smoke\") | tested | ACC-QUAL-T4 (ACCEPTANCE §6.2) | **B** | EVL-001 | SPEC-10 / PLAN-10 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:239:| REQ-QUAL-106 | Audit | Scoring integrity (symmetric infra handling, contamination, hidden tests). | validity | `eval/infra.mjs`, `eval/score.mjs`, `eval/run.mjs` | TEST (EVL-002, EVL-003; test:cli/test/eval_integrity.test.ts::\"contaminated runs leave the pass rate\", test:cli/test/eval_integrity.test.ts::\"infrastructure reruns use one rule\") | tested | ACC-QUAL-T2 (ACCEPTANCE §6.1) | **B** | EVL-002, EVL-003, VER-07 | SPEC-10 / PLAN-10 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:240:| REQ-QUAL-107 | Standalone; DEC-06 | Standalone and provider live matrix. | standalone | — | HIST | open | ACCEPTANCE §4.2, §4.3 | **B** | HIST-08 | SPEC-10 / PLAN-10 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:241:| REQ-QUAL-108 | Audit | PTY CI plus a manual real-terminal matrix. | terminal acceptance | `cli/test/tui_*`; ACCEPTANCE §5.3 | TEST (PTY suites in CI); UNV (real terminals) | partial | ACCEPTANCE §5 | RR | D §6 | SPEC-10 / PLAN-10 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:242:| REQ-QUAL-109 | eval/README T3 | T3 long tasks: 8 × 5. | long-task workflow | `eval/` | — | open | ACCEPTANCE §6.3 | RR | EVL-001 | SPEC-10 / PLAN-10 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:243:| REQ-QUAL-110 | Audit | T1 self-test and a T4 smoke run in `make test`. | regression | `eval_harness.test.ts` | TEST (test:cli/test/eval_harness.test.ts::\"T4 smoke: an overloaded endpoint is waited out\") | tested | ACC-QUAL-SMOKE | RR | — | SPEC-10 / PLAN-10 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:245:## 4. Contest requirements (separate product; not client gates)\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:249:## 5. Post-v1 backlog (recorded, not dropped)\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:270:## 6. Counts at db1ca55\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:276:| New v1 rows (§3) | 92 | **31 B**, 58 RR, 3 P. 79 open, 9 partial (REQ-SEC-118, REQ-PRV-101, REQ-PRV-103, REQ-PRV-105, REQ-PRV-111, REQ-PER-106, REQ-OPS-101, REQ-QUAL-108, REQ-QUAL-110), 1 implemented (REQ-OPS-103), 4 tested (REQ-SEC-103, REQ-SEC-119, REQ-PER-101, REQ-PER-102). |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:1:# Nexus Code v1.0.0: release qualification procedure\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:20:## 1.1 Release-candidate lifecycle and evidence identity\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:27:4. **Installed-RC qualification.** Install the workflow-produced RC package using the documented procedure and run the applicable product, provider, task-quality, terminal, installation, and independent-acceptance gates in §§4–8. Bind each result to both the RC source commit and installed package digest. If a source change or rebuilt artifact changes either identity, rerun every affected gate against the new candidate and retain prior results as historical evidence.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:28:5. **Stable promotion and publication.** After exact-RC acceptance and G6 pass, create a stable-version commit directly on the accepted RC commit, changing only the synchronized version metadata required for v1.0.0. Record both commits and the version-only diff. Run required source CI and all applicable source G0–G4 checks on this exact stable-version commit before tagging. If any other source changes, restart RC construction and qualification. Then create the `v1.0.0` tag on that checked commit and build a draft release. Keep its assets unpublished while verifying the stable artifact identity, provenance, package contents, installation, and publication metadata. Compare the stable package contents with the accepted RC; if packaged behavior or content differs beyond version-specific metadata, rerun affected installed-RC qualification gates and obtain independent acceptance for the stable artifact. Publish the draft only after these checks pass and the signed acceptance disposition is recorded. Record the published digests and provenance.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:30:Th…4378 tokens truncated…lowlisted for that requirement in the approved qualification-exceptions table below, and its `DECISIONS.md` section must contain a matching requirement-specific line of the form `Qualification applicability: REQ-... = NOT REQUIRED ...`. A record-supplied or unrelated decision cannot authorize an exception. The record must include digest-bound evidence for every `ACC-*` criterion in that requirement's ledger Acceptance column.\n\nThe post-RC closure requirements listed below may remain `open`, `partial`, or `implemented` in the source ledger at the RC commit because their remaining acceptance is completed during G6 or installed-RC qualification. The bare `--enforce` invocation is the pre-RC source gate: it checks every other B/RR row against the source threshold and reports mapped rows as deferred, not accepted. At G6, the exact-RC invocation must provide a record meeting the normal B/RR status threshold and digest-bound evidence for every criterion in this table. The table also supplies the criterion mapping for rows whose ledger points to an ACCEPTANCE section instead of naming ACC IDs. The source ledger is never rewritten by the record. Any below-tested required row omitted from this table still fails.\n\n<!-- RC-QUALIFICATION-ONLY:START -->\n### Qualification-only requirements for exact-RC enforcement\n\n| Requirement | Acceptance criteria required in the exact-RC record | Remaining stage |\n|---|---|---|\n| REQ-REL-003 | ACC-PLAT | Installed-RC platform and Node-version matrix |\n| REQ-AGT-002 | ACC-VER-03, ACC-VER-04, ACC-VER-09, ACC-QUAL-T2, ACC-QUAL-T3, ACC-QUAL-T4 | Installed-RC T2/T3/T4 outcome thresholds |\n| REQ-AGT-010 | ACC-TRUST-04 | Independent acceptance of the DEC-04 v1 subset |\n| REQ-PRV-003 | ACC-INF-10 | Installed-RC standalone and absent-gateway behavior |\n| REQ-REL-005 | ACC-SUP-04, ACC-SUP-05 | Exact-RC security and dependency artifact checks |\n| REQ-AGT-110 | ACC-CONT-10, ACC-GOV-06 | Installed-RC continuity and independent acceptance |\n| REQ-PRV-111 | ACC-PRV-LIVE | Installed-RC provider verification |\n| REQ-REL-114 | ACC-SUP-08 | Exact-RC cross-runner reproducibility |\n| REQ-QUAL-101 | ACC-QUAL-T2 | Installed-RC held-out T2 qualification |\n| REQ-QUAL-107 | ACC-PRV-STANDALONE, ACC-PRV-LIVE | Installed-RC standalone and provider matrix |\n| REQ-QUAL-108 | ACC-TUI-STEER, ACC-TUI-A11Y, ACC-TUI-MANUAL | CI PTY checks and installed-RC real-terminal matrix |\n| REQ-QUAL-109 | ACC-QUAL-T3 | Installed-RC T3 long-task qualification |\n<!-- RC-QUALIFICATION-ONLY:END -->\n\n<!-- RC-QUALIFICATION-EXCEPTIONS:START -->\n### Approved exact-RC qualification exceptions\n\n| Requirement | Approved decision | Scope |\n|---|---|---|\n<!-- RC-QUALIFICATION-EXCEPTIONS:END -->\n\n## 1. Rules\n\n1. The RC is built and published by the release workflow from a clean tag. Its version is identical across all components (REQ-REL-103).\n2. All qualification runs use the **installed RC package**, installed with the documented one-line command. They never use a checkout build. The only exception is CI unit and PTY suites, which run from source at the same commit.\n3. Thresholds (DEC-05) are frozen before the first M5 run. A failing gate is fixed in code and the run is repeated as `rc.N+1`. A threshold is never relaxed after results are known.\n4. Evidence goes to `docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/<rc>/`. The directory contains:\n   - `manifest.json`: commit, package sha256, environment, model fingerprint, dates;\n   - raw outputs;\n   - a `SHA256SUMS` file.\n\n   Secrets are redacted before commit.\n5. Any step that cannot run in the available environment is recorded as **NOT RUN** with its reason. A NOT RUN on a blocker gate fails the gate.\n\n## 2. Environments\n\n| ID | Environment | Used for |\n|---|---|---|\n| E1 | GitHub Actions: ubuntu-22.04 and ubuntu-24.04; Node 22 and 24; pinned Rust | Unit, integration and PTY suites; packaging; reproducibility |\n| E2 | Docker clean images: ubuntu:22.04, ubuntu:24.04, debian:12, fedora:40. Each with no Node, then with Node 20, Node 22 and Node 24. Non-root user. | Installer, upgrade, rollback, uninstall, platform failure messages |\n| E3 | Operator dev box: Linux x86-64, real terminals (xterm, kitty, tmux, VS Code terminal, GNOME Terminal) | Terminal matrix, live sessions |\n| E4 | Homelab-ai gateway, the **only** inference path (DEC-16): direct, and through `eval/standalone/plain_proxy.mjs` | Task-quality runs, standalone qualification, T3/T4 |\n| E5 | Cloud, small spend: ChatGPT sign-in (experimental tier) and OpenRouter with a pinned model; OpenAI and Anthropic keys if added | Provider verify; one live task per supported cloud provider |\n\n## 3. Gate checklist (G0–G4: automated acceptance IDs)\n\nEvery ACC ID below is defined in the linked spec. The plan for each spec names the test that implements it. Run each check at the lifecycle stage dictated by its acceptance method in §1.1: source-applicable checks before the RC tag; checks requiring the RC archive, attestation, release, or installed package after RC construction; environment-specific checks in their declared environment. Bind every result to the exact source commit and, when artifact-dependent, the RC package digest. A source test or local build does not replace an artifact-bound check, and no G0–G4 ID is complete until all of its applicable checks pass.\n\n| Gate | Acceptance IDs | Spec |\n|---|---|---|\n| Safety | ACC-SAFE-01 to ACC-SAFE-10 | SPEC-01 |\n| Process ownership | ACC-PROC-01 to ACC-PROC-08 (ACC-PROC-07 is the load test, run in E3) | SPEC-02 |\n| Untrusted inputs | ACC-TRUST-01 to ACC-TRUST-09 | SPEC-03 |\n| Continuity | ACC-CONT-01 to ACC-CONT-09 (ACC-CONT-10 is in §8) | SPEC-04 |\n| Inference | ACC-INF-01 to ACC-INF-09 (ACC-INF-10 is in §4) | SPEC-05 |\n| Packaging | ACC-PKG-01 to ACC-PKG-09 | SPEC-06 |\n| Supply chain | ACC-SUP-01 to ACC-SUP-08 (artifact-bound ACC-SUP-01/02/03/06/08 after RC construction) | SPEC-07 |\n| Persistence | ACC-PER-01 to ACC-PER-07 | SPEC-08 |\n| Governance | ACC-GOV-01 to ACC-GOV-06 | SPEC-09 |\n| Verification | ACC-VER-01 to ACC-VER-09 | SPEC-11 |\n| Upgrade | ACC-UPG-01 to ACC-UPG-14 | SPEC-12 |\n\n\n### 3.1 Acceptance IDs defined in this file\n\nThese are retained commitments from REQUIREMENTS §2 and cross-cutting checks.\n\n| ID | Check | Pass condition |\n|---|---|---|\n| ACC-TUI-STEER | PTY: submit a task; while a tool runs, type steering text and press Enter; also queue a steer before a cancel | Steering is applied at the next step boundary. Unapplied steering is returned to the composer. Nothing is dropped silently (existing `sidecar_steering_diff` plus PTY s6). |\n| ACC-TUI-A11Y | PTY with `NO_COLOR=1` and with `TERM=dumb` at 40×14 and 100×30 | Zero colour SGR codes. Every state is distinguishable by glyph and word. Hints are complete at 40 columns (TUI-10). |\n| ACC-SEC-JAIL | `core/tests` plus harness-core calls with `..`, absolute, symlinked-file, symlinked-dir and symlinked-parent payloads | Every one is refused (C §4 R1 set). |\n| ACC-SEC-B6 | Re-run `docs/reviews/evidence/qualification_2026-10-12/repro/zz_trust_repro.test.ts`. Seeded-secret scan of `~/.nexus` and `.nexus` after a scripted turn. | Zero plaintext seeded secrets in durable stores or outbound bodies. |\n| ACC-PRV-LIVE | `nexus providers verify --provider <p> -m <pinned model> -j` for each provider listed as supported (DEC-06) | `passed: true`. Receipts archived. |\n| ACC-PRV-STANDALONE | §4.2 on the installed RC through the approved stripped proxy, with gateway credentials absent from the child environment | Every required profile completes through the proxy and the absent-gateway boundary holds; receipts archived. |\n| ACC-PLAT | E2 matrix, §7 | All rows pass. |\n| ACC-QUAL-T2 | §6.1 + §6.4 | Thresholds met. |\n| ACC-QUAL-T3 | §6.3 + §6.4 | Thresholds met. |\n| ACC-QUAL-T4 | §6.2 + §6.4 | Thresholds met. |\n| ACC-QUAL-SMOKE | `make test` includes the T1 self-test and the T4 smoke | Present and passing. |\n| ACC-TUI-MANUAL | §5.3 on the installed RC across five required terminal environments and three required sizes | Every cell passes; screenshots and per-cell verdicts are archived. |\n\n## 4. Standalone and provider qualification (REQ-PRV-106, REQ-PRV-111, REQ-QUAL-107)\n\n### 4.1 Clean-HOME procedure\n\n1. `export HOME=$(mktemp -d)`.\n2. Install the RC with the documented command.\n3. Create `~/.config/nexus/config.env` containing only:\n   - `LOCAL_LLM_ENDPOINT=http://127.0.0.1:<proxy>/v1`\n   - `LOCAL_LLM_MODEL=<id as listed by the proxy>`\n   - `LOCAL_LLM_API_KEY=REDACTED\n\n   No gateway token file, no homelab paths, no `NODE_*` overrides.\n4. Start `node eval/standalone/plain_proxy.mjs --upstream <gateway> --token-file <operator token> [--emulate <kind>]`. The gateway token stays with the proxy and never reaches the Nexus HOME.\n5. Run `nexus doctor --json` and archive it. It must report the server kind and context source with no `gateway` capability.\n\n### 4.2 Standalone matrix\n\n| Profile | What Nexus sees | Runs | Pass condition |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| P-plain | Bare OpenAI-compatible `/models` and chat. No tokenize, no capacity headers. | Standalone T2 subset (≥ 10 held-out tasks) × 3 runs; T4 classes 1, 3, 4, 7 × 3 | T2 correctness ≥ (gateway-direct T2 correctness on the same tasks − 10 pts). False VERIFIED = 0. T4 truthful = 100%. Context source reported as `client_default` or an operator override, with no error. |\n| P-llamacpp | Emulated llama.cpp `/props` and overflow body | Same tasks × 1 run; plus the forced-overflow case (context limit set to 8k) | Context discovered from `/props`. Overflow gives one compact-and-retry, then success or an actionable error. |\n| P-vllm | Emulated `max_model_len` and vLLM overflow body | Same as P-llamacpp | Same, with the context source `max_model_len` |\n| P-ollama | Emulated `/api/show` and Ollama overflow body | Same as P-llamacpp | Same, with the context source `ollama_show` |\n| Conformance | CI fixtures for llama.cpp, vLLM, LM Studio and Ollama shapes | CI | All pass (ACC-INF-01, -02, -05) |\n\nACC-INF-10 passes only when every row passes. The release notes state the scope in the form required by DEC-16.\n\n### 4.3 Provider matrix (E5)\n\n| Provider | Tier (DEC-06) | Required for v1.0.0 |\n|---|---|---|\n| OpenRouter, pinned model | Supported | `providers verify` PASS, plus one live small task (a §6-style bug fix) reaching a correct outcome |\n| ChatGPT sign-in | Experimental | Verify PASS recorded (already PASS at db1ca55; repeat on the RC) |\n| OpenAI API key, Anthropic | Experimental unless keys are added | If promoted: verify PASS plus one live task. Otherwise NOT RUN, and they are labelled experimental. |\n| Copilot | Experimental | Not required |\n\n## 5. Terminal acceptance (REQ-QUAL-108)\n\n### 5.1 CI PTY suites (E1)\n\nThese must pass:\n\n- `tui_approval_input_e2e`\n- `tui_diff_e2e`\n- `tui_maturity_e2e`\n- `tui_model_picker_e2e`\n- `tui_multiline_e2e`\n- `tui_surface_e2e`\n- new: `repl_approval_e2e`\n- new: `process_lifecycle_e2e`\n- new: `startup_unreachable_e2e`\n- new: the package PTY smoke\n\n### 5.2 Scripted PTY scenarios against the installed RC (E3, mock gateway)\n\nThese are ports of `evidence/D_pty/`.\n\n| Scenario | Pass condition |\n|---|---|\n| s1 startup, unreachable endpoint | The endpoint is named, with a fix hint. The turn ends with guidance in ≤ 2.5 min. |\n| s2 approval under continuous typing, paste and burst, at 40×14 | No decision is made by stray input. A deliberate key decides. |\n| s3 completion | The outcome is shown in words: VERIFIED, REGRESSION_FREE or UNVERIFIED. |\n| s4–s6 cancel and steer | Cancel is acknowledged within 1 frame and idle within 5 s. Steering is applied. |\n| s7 resume | The prior conversation is shown. |\n| s8–s9 cancel or quit during a tool | Zero surviving processes. |\n| r1a / r1d REPL approvals | DENIED for a lone Enter and for a typed-ahead `y`. |\n\n### 5.3 Manual real-terminal matrix (E3)\n\nTerminals: xterm, kitty (kitty keyboard protocol on), tmux 3.x inside GNOME Terminal, VS Code integrated terminal, GNOME Terminal. Sizes: 80×24, 40×14, 200×60.\n\nFor each terminal × size, check:\n\n1. Launch `nexus` (the TUI appears).\n2. Approval panel. Type continuously across it. Paste 3 lines. Approve with a deliberate key.\n3. Shift+Enter or Alt+Enter multiline.\n4. Resize during streaming.\n5. Esc during `sleep 30` (no survivors).\n6. Ctrl-C twice (clean terminal restore: echo on, no stray escape codes).\n7. NO_COLOR.\n\nRecord PASS/FAIL per cell, with a screenshot of the approval panel and the post-exit terminal state.\n\n**Gate:** zero FAIL on checks 2, 5 and 6, which are safety checks. Other FAILs need a written disposition (fix, or a documented known limitation).\n\n## 6. Task-quality qualification (REQ-QUAL-101 to REQ-QUAL-106, REQ-QUAL-109)\n\nEnvironment: E4 (gateway direct), serial runs, with matched model fingerprint, budgets and env (REQ-QUAL-102).\n\n### 6.1 T2 held-out (ACC-QUAL-T2)\n\n- 40 sealed tasks. The manifest is committed before RC1, and authorship is recorded (agent-authored, DEC-05).\n- 5 runs × {Nexus RC, Goose, OpenCode}.\n- Before execution, freeze three qualification configs at `eval/configs/v1-t2-nexus.json`, `eval/configs/v1-t2-goose.json`, and `eval/configs/v1-t2-opencode.json`. Each must set `qualification: true`, identify the same model fingerprint and sampling settings, and record equal context/output and task budgets; the Nexus config must identify the installed RC and its package digest. Do not derive these files from the pilot configs by silently inheriting or changing settings.\n- Set `T2_TASKS` to the custodian-approved, sealed task directory and `T2_OUT` to a new, empty, run-specific output directory. Do not use the disclosed `eval/tasks` development set as held-out evidence. Preserve all three outputs and their manifests; never reuse an output directory for a retry.\n- Run each config serially, with identical task selection and five runs per task:\n\n  ```bash\n  set -euo pipefail\n  : \"${T2_TASKS:?set the sealed task directory}\"\n  : \"${T2_OUT:?set a new unique output directory}\"\n  test ! -e \"$T2_OUT\"\n  node eval/run.mjs --config eval/configs/v1-t2-nexus.json --tasks \"$T2_TASKS\" --out \"$T2_OUT/nexus\" --runs 5\n  node eval/run.mjs --config eval/configs/v1-t2-goose.json --tasks \"$T2_TASKS\" --out \"$T2_OUT/goose\" --runs 5\n  node eval/run.mjs --config eval/configs/v1-t2-opencode.json --tasks \"$T2_TASKS\" --out \"$T2_OUT/opencode\" --runs 5\n  node eval/score.mjs --pairs \"$T2_OUT/nexus/results.jsonl\" \"$T2_OUT/goose/results.jsonl\" \"$T2_OUT/opencode/results.jsonl\"\n  ```\n\n  Record the resolved `T2_TASKS`, unique `T2_OUT`, config digests, installed RC identity, model fingerprint, and exact commands in the frozen run record before starting. A failed or interrupted invocation remains evidence; any permitted infrastructure rerun uses the accepted rerun procedure and is retained separately. Do not score until all required runs and manifests exist. The scorer accepts exactly the Nexus, Goose and OpenCode result files.\n\n### 6.2 T4 fault injection (ACC-QUAL-T4)\n\n9 fault classes × 5 runs on the Nexus RC. The configured faults run through `eval/run.mjs` and `eval/model_proxy.mjs`; the hanging-command and full-disk cases use task fixtures, and SIGTERM-then-resume uses the runner case (DEC-05 amendment, 2026-10-17: the union of the distinct scenarios below):\n\n1. refused connection mid-turn\n2. 5xx / overloaded\n3. stream cut mid-tool-call\n4. output-limit truncation\n5. hanging test command\n6. disk full\n7. context overflow at 32k\n8. malformed tool-call JSON\n9. SIGTERM then `run --resume`\n\n### 6.3 T3 long tasks (ACC-QUAL-T3)\n\n- 8 tasks × 5 runs. Each run must have ≥ 60 steps, ≥ 2 compactions and scripted steering.\n\n### 6.4 Thresholds (DEC-05; all must hold)\n\n| Metric | Gate |\n|---|---|\n| False VERIFIED (T2 + T3 + T4) | **= 0** |\n| T2 pooled hidden-test correctness | ≥ 60% and ≥ best matched peer − 10 pts |\n| T2 per class (bugfix, feature, refactor, debug) | ≥ 40% |\n| Crash rate (all Nexus runs) | ≤ 2% |\n| Regression rate | ≤ 5% |\n| T4 truthful outcome | = 100% |\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a16f37-6e05-7dc2-8c28-9b80ae02e75f","create_time":1792867521.3398197}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
