{"timestamp":"2026-10-24T18:46:41.289Z","ordinal":302746,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a16f37-6e05-7dc2-8c28-9b80ae02e75f","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016adcfd0f3d5881a09fefdd57bd8d8cde","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"**I see what you meant:** Nexus should ask whether to trust the project folder before starting, and show which project instructions it will load.\n\nThat startup prompt is in **RC4** (`127c5b8`), but it is absent from RC1 and RC3. The `nexus` command on this machine reports **RC3**, which explains why you don’t see it. The prompt is called from the normal interactive startup path in [index.ts](/tmp/nexus-release-audit-4adc-20261024/cli/src/index.ts:208) and rendered in [startup_trust.ts](/tmp/nexus-release-audit-4adc-20261024/cli/src/startup_trust.ts:132).\n\nThere are a couple of differences from the screenshot: Nexus also offers **“Continue without trusting,”** and explains that trust affects its default approval mode. RC4’s source has the startup feature; your installed RC3 doesn’t.\n\n"}],"phase":"final_answer","memory_citation":{"entries":[{"path":"MEMORY.md","lineStart":777,"lineEnd":816,"note":"Nexus release qualification and exact-RC gate context"}],"rolloutIds":["01a14262-6554-7912-9e3b-5f24d58b12c0"]}},"started_at_ms":1792867599276,"completed_at_ms":1792867601289}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-24T18:46:41.293Z","ordinal":302747,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","status":"completed","id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016adcfd0f3d5881a09fefdd57bd8d8cde","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"output_text","text":"**I see what you meant:** Nexus should ask whether to trust the project folder before starting, and show which project instructions it will load.\n\nThat startup prompt is in **RC4** (`127c5b8`), but it is absent from RC1 and RC3. The `nexus` command on this machine reports **RC3**, which explains why you don’t see it. The prompt is called from the normal interactive startup path in [index.ts](/tmp/nexus-release-audit-4adc-20261024/cli/src/index.ts:208) and rendered in [startup_trust.ts](/tmp/nexus-release-audit-4adc-20261024/cli/src/startup_trust.ts:132).\n\nThere are a couple of differences from the screenshot: Nexus also offers **“Continue without trusting,”** and explains that trust affects its default approval mode. RC4’s source has the startup feature; your installed RC3 doesn’t.\n\n<oai-mem-citation>\n<citation_entries>\nMEMORY.md:777-816|note=[Nexus release qualification and exact-RC gate context]\n</citation_entries>\n<rollout_ids>\n01a14262-6554-7912-9e3b-5f24d58b12c0\n</rollout_ids>\n</oai-mem-citation>","annotations":[],"logprobs":[]}],"phase":"final_answer","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a16f37-6e05-7dc2-8c28-9b80ae02e75f","create_time":1792867599.2418182,"content_item_kinds":["unknown"]}},"metadata":{"retained_source":{"id":{"message_id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016adcfd0f3d5881a09fefdd57bd8d8cde","turn_id":"01a16f37-6e05-7dc2-8c28-9b80ae02e75f","role":"assistant"},"revision":"retained_01a16f3c-8b8d-7301-b592-cea0866c5318","complete":true},"client_authored":false,"user_input_order":15401}}
