ts at rc.4; SUITE released; no tests or version writes\n2026-10-24T18:23:53Z PR202 opened head=8d2288e9a4f139bf88dffd33c643869899166bd8 base=4adc61ac98616c5e1dccaf6065e7f2332443d468; focused_cst=5/5 newline_dense_8MiB=PASS; diff_check=PASS; independent_review=ACCEPT diff_sha256=63c3f3f46b040d98b9d5a8a169007c6aa91df027d25fb3200ef5bde2187af96c; CI40120241547 in_progress CodeQL40120241400 success\n2026-10-24T18:23:53Z PR200_201_REFRESH observed owner-pushed rebases after PR199 merge; PR200 head=89d7416 base=4adc61a CI40120298254 running CodeQL40120298213 success; PR201 head=b0240b4 base=4adc61a CI40120440206 and CodeQL40120440205 running; previous exact-head reviews no longer apply; fresh independent review requested\n2026-10-24T18:23:53Z STARTUP_TRUST_RECONCILIATION local_nexus=/home/mike/.local/bin/nexus version=1.0.0-rc.3 commit=1b9791f07d30; PR186 merge=a2f2fba; RC4 includes chooser, RC1-3 predate; existing PR186 CI all required checks passed\n2026-10-24T19:03:00Z INDEPENDENT_REVIEW PR201 exact rebased head=b0240b43aaad16df9c2663218949970c4dac513b base=4adc61ac98616c5e1dccaf6065e7f2332443d468 ACCEPT reviewer=rc1_docs_review diff_sha256=27516531b17dee24e1335280cb45bf1e57d26b32b3f415b0a8469cc3cdaebe28; verifies production sandbox/resource composition, staged baseline/canary isolation, kernel limits and descendant cleanup fail-safe behavior\n2026-10-24T19:03:00Z PR200 exact new head 89d7416 on base 4adc61a checks Node22/24 in progress, JS/TS+CodeQL pass; fresh CI after PR199 merge\n2026-10-24T19:03:00Z PR201 exact new head b0240b4 on base 4adc61a fresh CI active; focused 1/1 and exact independent ACCEPT recorded\n2026-10-24T18:25:34Z claude-code RE_REVIEW PR200 head=89d7416fc5a54e3d0d9fd43d70192f12c540f93f REQUEST_CHANGES stands: unwritable info/exclude still aborts Agent startup; the new hasExactRule&&isIgnored skip widens it to repos already ignoring .nexus via .gitignore. No owner reply yet.\n2026-10-24T19:07:00Z RC5_NOTES update commit=1e295f905cc91fde910ab29bd77a20d298e3d536 adds PR199's bounded CST behavior with precise skip-vs-error wording; source main 4adc61a contains PR199; diff-check PASS; exact note SHA256 e3e29e525ffcfb840fa4125035ccfbc04136f85dac542e5d2464d1840eec04d1 independently ACCEPTed by rc1_docs_review; no tests/version/tag/push\n2026-10-24T19:14:00Z POST_MERGE_INDEPENDENT_REVIEW PR199 exact head=0667947d4e581e8ba996b8cca91438697f640500 vs base=41b381d ACCEPT reviewer=rc1_docs_review diff_sha256=b10d57ca01b7d026bb611202b7cae83eb616e78cb02d01bdbe58da0171c3ff9c; confirms metadata + bounded read/recheck, outline reuse, tests for oversized/exact-limit/empty, and directory-scan skip vs direct error behavior; no tests by reviewer\n2026-10-24T18:58:00Z PR200 exact rebased head=89d7416fc5a54e3d0d9fd43d70192f12c540f93f on 4adc61a received independent ACCEPT reviewer=rc1_docs_review; diff_sha256=29be45b58fbf78915c8c65d246140caf0d731ff82e8cd0f271ee46d035fe1e16; reviewer confirms explicit .nexus/worktrees/.flights exclusions and fail-closed verification, no PR199 interaction\n2026-10-24T19:03:00Z PR201 exact rebased head=b0240b43aaad16df9c2663218949970c4dac513b on 4adc61a received independent ACCEPT reviewer=rc1_docs_review; diff_sha256=27516531b17dee24e1335280cb45bf1e57d26b32b3f415b0a8469cc3cdaebe28; production sandbox/resource supervisor composition, canary isolation, limits and descendant cleanup confirmed\n2026-10-24T18:34:29Z PR200_BOUNDARY_EXTENSION requested_by=claude-code finding=unwritable_info_exclude_aborts_startup scope=worktree.ts+flight_exclude.test.ts basis=PLAN-08_first_workspace_write no_existing_claim_conflict coordinator=coded-root accepted_for_same_slice=yes\n2026-10-24T18:34:34Z CLAIM_LOG_CORRECTION previous coordinator label typo only; actual coordinator=codex-root\n2026-10-24T18:38:45Z CLAIM_REFRESH STARTUP_TRUST_INSTRUCTIONS_GATE_20261024 + FILE_cli_src_agent.ts + FILE_cli_test_startup_trust_prompt_test.ts agent=codex-root branch=v1/trust-instructions-gate base=4adc61ac98616c5e1dccaf6065e7f2332443d468 scope=trust-gate-project-instruction-injection; previous startup chooser is already on main; no docs change needed\n2026-10-24T18:40:12Z RELEASE STARTUP_TRUST_INSTRUCTIONS_GATE_20261024; duplicate remediation not needed: origin/main=4adc61ac98616c5e1dccaf6065e7f2332443d468 already includes startup chooser and trustedProjectRules in AutonomousAgent; current trust prompt regression test passes 11/11 on isolated HOME; installed nexus is RC3 and predates feature; no source changes\n2026-10-24T18:42:11Z PR_UPDATE #200 head=dfea9e2f010f194718f01e9da13fed7dbd80d069 base=4adc61ac98616c5e1dccaf6065e7f2332443d468 pushed_fast_forward=yes; PR body reconciled to current base and documented boundary correction; focused_tests=12/12 tsc=PASS diff_check=PASS independent_review=ACCEPT exact_diff_sha256=c0705f527e3a05a38b12ec0680708f98a2819978c0a6e934b881ec09748f2fe0; fresh_CI=pending\n2026-10-24T18:43:46Z INDEPENDENT_REVIEW PR202 head=8d2288e9a4f139bf88dffd33c643869899166bd8 base=4adc61ac98616c5e1dccaf6065e7f2332443d468 reviewer=plan05_readonly_review disposition=ACCEPT diff_sha256=63c3f3f46b040d98b9d5a8a169007c6aa91df027d25fb3200ef5bde2187af96c; bounded borrowed-line iteration preserves multiline parser lookahead and avoids per-line String allocation; reviewer did not run tests\n{\"body\":\"## Summary\\n\\n- Keep `.nexus/` exclusion fail-closed when Git still considers protected Nexus state visible.\\n- Avoid appending duplicate rules on every retry when a higher-priority repository ignore rule defeats `info/exclude`.\\n- Still append a final positive rule when a later negation in `info/exclude` can be overridden.\\n- Defer exclusion-file mutation from `WorktreeManager` construction until an actual worktree is created. Startup remains non-mutating, while worktree creation checks the exclusion before creating `.nexus/worktrees` and fails closed if Git metadata is unavailable.\\n- Add regressions for retry behavior, non-mutating manager construction, and fail-closed worktree creation.\\n\\n## Validation\\n\\n- `node --import tsx --test test/git_exclude.test.ts test/flight_exclude.test.ts`: 12/12 passed with isolated `HOME` and `XDG_CONFIG_HOME`.\\n- `npx tsc --noEmit`: passed.\\n- `git diff --check`: passed.\\n- Independent read-only review: ACCEPT on exact head `dfea9e2f010f194718f01e9da13fed7dbd80d069`, diff SHA-256 `c0705f527e3a05a38b12ec0680708f98a2819978c0a6e934b881ec09748f2fe0`.\\n- Fresh exact-head CI is pending and required before integration.\\n\\n## Base\\n\\n- `main` at `4adc61ac98616c5e1dccaf6065e7f2332443d468`.\\n\",\"commits\":[{\"authoredDate\":\"2026-10-24T05:23:25Z\",\"authors\":[{\"email\":\"mike@holownych.com\",\"id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjc3NTE3ODA=\",\"login\":\"mikeholownych\",\"name\":\"Mike Holownych\"}],\"committedDate\":\"2026-10-24T18:20:26Z\",\"messageBody\":\"\",\"messageHeadline\":\"fix(git): verify nexus state exclusions\",\"oid\":\"ddbbb320c3d583b89e2d9916c7966bf84376a7df\"},{\"authoredDate\":\"2026-10-24T17:35:00Z\",\"authors\":[{\"email\":\"mike@holownych.com\",\"id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjc3NTE3ODA=\",\"login\":\"mikeholownych\",\"name\":\"Mike Holownych\"}],\"committedDate\":\"2026-10-24T18:20:27Z\",\"messageBody\":\"\",\"messageHeadline\":\"fix(git): avoid duplicate ineffective exclusion rules\",\"oid\":\"7a84ccf6f56f3ccaeffe2fc7dda19180f8596035\"},{\"authoredDate\":\"2026-10-24T17:52:25Z\",\"authors\":[{\"email\":\"mike@holownych.com\",\"id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjc3NTE3ODA=\",\"login\":\"mikeholownych\",\"name\":\"Mike Holownych\"}],\"committedDate\":\"2026-10-24T18:20:27Z\",\"messageBody\":\"\",\"messageHeadline\":\"fix(git): preserve explicit Nexus exclude rules\",\"oid\":\"89d7416fc5a54e3d0d9fd43d70192f12c540f93f\"},{\"authoredDate\":\"2026-10-24T18:36:06Z\",\"authors\":[{\"email\":\"mike@holownych.com\",\"id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjc3NTE3ODA=\",\"login\":\"mikeholownych\",\"name\":\"Mike Holownych\"}],\"committedDate\":\"2026-10-24T18:36:06Z\",\"messageBody\":\"\",\"messageHeadline\":\"fix(git): defer exclusion write until needed\",\"oid\":\"dfea9e2f010f194718f01e9da13fed7dbd80d069\"}],\"files\":[{\"path\":\"cli/src/core/git_exclude.ts\",\"additions\":55,\"deletions\":41,\"changeType\":\"MODIFIED\"},{\"path\":\"cli/src/worktree.ts\",\"additions\":4,\"deletions\":1,\"changeType\":\"MODIFIED\"},{\"path\":\"cli/test/flight_exclude.test.ts\",\"additions\":21,\"deletions\":1,\"changeType\":\"MODIFIED\"},{\"path\":\"cli/test/git_exclude.test.ts\",\"additions\":52,\"deletions\":1,\"changeType\":\"MODIFIED\"}]}\n{\"body\":\"## Summary\\n\\nAdd an infrastructure regression fixture that exercises the evaluator's real workspace staging and contained task launch path. The fixture plants a known solution canary in prohibited Git history and an external validator store, then checks that task execution cannot retrieve either. It also verifies the configured resource envelope and supervisor cleanup behavior.\\n\\nThe fixture uses synthetic data only; it does not access or expose held-out task payloads.\\n\\n## Evidence\\n\\n- Base: `676abb371c8c91970af6d920d5c516497e3ccdef`\\n- Candidate head: `dfb3880d43fb2ba5574c8ac42221cfe4d138fe59`\\n- Patch SHA-256: `27516531b17dee24e1335280cb45bf1e57d26b32b3f415b0a8469cc3cdaebe28`\\n- Focused fixture: 1/1 passed with isolated HOME/XDG.\\n- `git diff --check`: passed.\\n- Independent read-only review: ACCEPT on exact head and patch hash.\\n\\nFull exact-head CI is required before integration. This test does not constitute held-out qualification or release acceptance.\\n\",\"commits\":[{\"authoredDate\":\"2026-10-24T17:50:33Z\",\"authors\":[{\"email\":\"mike@holownych.com\",\"id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjc3NTE3ODA=\",\"login\":\"mikeholownych\",\"name\":\"Mike Holownych\"}],\"committedDate\":\"2026-10-24T18:21:55Z\",\"messageBody\":\"\",\"messageHeadline\":\"test(eval): compose candidate sandbox with resource limits\",\"oid\":\"281014f5888a927fbcee41a6a11aebbcb732b726\"},{\"authoredDate\":\"2026-10-24T17:54:29Z\",\"authors\":[{\"email\":\"mike@holownych.com\",\"id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjc3NTE3ODA=\",\"login\":\"mikeholownych\",\"name\":\"Mike Holownych\"}],\"committedDate\":\"2026-10-24T18:21:55Z\",\"messageBody\":\"\",\"messageHeadline\":\"test(eval): await containment cleanup on fixture failure\",\"oid\":\"b0240b43aaad16df9c2663218949970c4dac513b\"}],\"files\":[{\"path\":\"cli/test/eval_integrity.test.ts\",\"additions\":140,\"deletions\":0,\"changeType\":\"MODIFIED\"}]}\n{\"body\":\"## Summary\\n- Replace the per-line `Vec<String>` with borrowed source lines and a nine-line signature lookahead window.\\n- Accumulate documentation comments in one string rather than allocating a vector entry per line.\\n- Add an 8 MiB newline-dense regression and update the CST evidence note with the remaining output-memory bound.\\n\\n## Context\\nThis is a follow-up to #199, merged at `4adc61ac98616c5e1dccaf6065e7f2332443d468`. The accepted review found that a newline-dense file at the existing 8 MiB input limit could still amplify memory through millions of owned line strings. The change keeps the current input limit and parsing behavior.\\n\\n## Verification\\n- Focused Rust CST tests on exact base `4adc61ac98616c5e1dccaf6065e7f2332443d468`: 5 passed, including the newline-dense 8 MiB case.\\n- `git diff --check`: passed.\\n- Independent read-only review: ACCEPT on the exact two-file diff and exact base.\\n- `cargo fmt --check` reports existing formatting differences across unrelated Rust files; no unrelated formatting changes were included.\\n\\nFull PR CI is required before merge.\\n\",\"commits\":[{\"authoredDate\":\"2026-10-24T18:20:00Z\",\"authors\":[{\"email\":\"mike@holownych.com\",\"id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjc3NTE3ODA=\",\"login\":\"mikeholownych\",\"name\":\"Mike Holownych\"}],\"committedDate\":\"2026-10-24T18:20:00Z\",\"messageBody\":\"\",\"messageHeadline\":\"fix(cst): avoid line allocation amplification\",\"oid\":\"8d2288e9a4f139bf88dffd33c643869899166bd8\"}],\"files\":[{\"path\":\"core/src/cst.rs\",\"additions\":36,\"deletions\":16,\"changeType\":\"MODIFIED\"},{\"path\":\"docs/reviews/evidence/v1/DEFECT-CST-UNBOUNDED-20261024/README.md\",\"additions\":5,\"deletions\":2,\"changeType\":\"MODIFIED\"}]}\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":1,"nanos":555077335}},"started_at_ms":1792867691755,"completed_at_ms":1792867693311}}
