{"timestamp":"2026-10-24T18:49:19.607Z","ordinal":302900,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a16f3c-d2bf-7c20-9739-5c085f717ae0","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-c7e1c1a1-8afd-4378-9538-9c518ad8d306","process_id":"99764","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","git -C /tmp/nexus-release-audit-4adc-20261024 status --short; ls docs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md docs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.5.md 2>/dev/null || true; rg -n \"TERMINAL-MATRIX|manual terminal|xterm|kitty\" docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md docs/v1.0.0/README.md docs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md 2>/dev/null | head -50; gh issue view 1 --json state,updatedAt,comments --jq '{state,updatedAt,comments:[.comments[-3:][]|{author:.author.login,createdAt,body:.body}]}'"],"cwd":"file:///tmp/nexus-release-audit-4adc-20261024","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"git -C /tmp/nexus-release-audit-4adc-20261024 status --short; ls docs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md docs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.5.md 2>/dev/null || true; rg -n \"TERMINAL-MATRIX|manual terminal|xterm|kitty\" docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md docs/v1.0.0/README.md docs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md 2>/dev/null | head -50; gh issue view 1 --json state,updatedAt,comments --jq '{state,updatedAt,comments:[.comments[-3:][]|{author:.author.login,createdAt,body:.body}]}'"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"docs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md\ndocs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md:19:Record the actual terminal versions/protocol configuration used. Kitty must have the kitty keyboard protocol on; record the tmux 3.x version and its GNOME Terminal host version.\ndocs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md:23:| xterm | |\ndocs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md:24:| kitty (kitty keyboard protocol on) | |\ndocs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md:49:| 1 | xterm | 80×24 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | | | |\ndocs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md:50:| 2 | xterm | 40×14 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | | | |\ndocs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md:51:| 3 | xterm | 200×60 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | | | |\ndocs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md:52:| 4 | kitty (kitty keyboard protocol on) | 80×24 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | | | |\ndocs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md:53:| 5 | kitty (kitty keyboard protocol on) | 40×14 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | | | |\ndocs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md:54:| 6 | kitty (kitty keyboard protocol on) | 200×60 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | | | |\ndocs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md:92:This worksheet records manual terminal evidence only. It does not replace the separate CI PTY, installed-RC, or independent acceptance gates in `ACCEPTANCE.md`.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:81:| E3 | Operator dev box: Linux x86-64, real terminals (xterm, kitty, tmux, VS Code terminal, GNOME Terminal) | Terminal matrix, live sessions |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:192:Terminals: xterm, kitty (kitty keyboard protocol on), tmux 3.x inside GNOME Terminal, VS Code integrated terminal, GNOME Terminal. Sizes: 80×24, 40×14, 200×60.\ndocs/v1.0.0/README.md:5:**Verdict: v1.0.0 readiness is BLOCKED.** Candidate source revision `6151a231e9179c109cfbe8cff87e0a4148587b6a` passed an isolated `make build` and full `make test` run on 2026-10-16 (Rust 281/281; CLI 1087/1087; zero skipped). This is source-suite evidence, not RC qualification. Held-out task quality, T3/T4 qualification, standalone/provider qualification, the manual terminal matrix, package/install matrix on the RC, and independent RC acceptance remain incomplete. See [the current readiness reconciliation](READINESS.md) for exact open requirements and gates. The contest entry remains a separate track; judging has concluded and no contest freeze applies.\n{\"comments\":[{\"author\":\"mikeholownych\",\"body\":\"Metadata-only checkpoint request for the independent held-out custodian. No private corpus material has been accessed.\\n\\nRC3 (`v1.0.0-rc.3`) is published, but no held-out qualification has started. The public 40-task manifest still uses the legacy `hidden.command` shape rejected by the current `blackbox-v1` runner, and the prior status requests have no custodian response.\\n\\nPlease provide only safe status metadata:\\n- current author/custodian owner and claim or handoff reference;\\n- whether lossless conversion is being done by the custodian or a new immutable manifest is needed, with next checkpoint/ETA;\\n- whether completeness, coverage, setup/reference validation, integrity, access controls, and author-session independence have been independently accepted;\\n- if no custodian is active, confirm that so an authorized replacement can be assigned.\\n\\nPlease do not include task content, objectives, validators, answers, patches, author logs, credentials, or private digests. Qualification remains closed until custody acceptance and runner compatibility are documented.\\n\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-23T10:23:00Z\"},{\"author\":\"mikeholownych\",\"body\":\"Metadata-only custody checkpoint from the release coordinator. I found no current held-out author/custodian claim in the shared claim ledger; the last public custodian response request was October 23 10:23 UTC. Please reply only with safe status metadata: (1) current independent author and custodian, including the acknowledged claim/handoff; (2) whether the 40-task corpus and setup/reference validation are complete; (3) whether the legacy runner-format incompatibility has a custodian-approved immutable resolution; and (4) whether access separation, digests, independence, and custody have been accepted. If the current custodian is unavailable, please state that explicitly and identify the authorized handoff needed. Do not post task payloads, answers, validators, author logs, credentials, or private digests. Qualification remains closed until independent custody acceptance.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-24T00:19:17Z\"},{\"author\":\"mikeholownych\",\"body\":\"Metadata-only custody status request: please confirm the current author/custodian owner and progress toward the 40-task corpus, including coverage/validation counts, setup and reference-validation status, private digest re-derivation, store and parent access controls, exposure-history review, immutable seal status, and expected custody acceptance. Please do not post task prompts, answers, validators, or other protected payloads here. Held-out qualification remains blocked until the independent custodian verifies completeness, coverage, integrity, and execution-boundary separation.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-24T02:16:57Z\"}],\"state\":\"OPEN\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-10-24T02:16:57Z\"}\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":1,"nanos":379458045}},"started_at_ms":1792867758227,"completed_at_ms":1792867759607}}
