{"timestamp":"2026-10-24T18:49:38.267Z","ordinal":302914,"type":"token_usage_record","payload":{"thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a16f3c-d2bf-7c20-9739-5c085f717ae0","session_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","root_turn_id":"01a16f3c-d2bf-7c20-9739-5c085f717ae0","response_id":"resp_060b64278a9dfb15016adcfdb0e8a881a08ac78578f53f2534","usage":{"input_tokens":145670,"cached_input_tokens":143232,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":2071,"reasoning_output_tokens":1991,"total_tokens":147741},"turn_token_usage":{"input_tokens":2281545,"cached_input_tokens":2220672,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":11108,"reasoning_output_tokens":8562,"total_tokens":2292653},"thread_token_usage":{"input_tokens":5496429897,"cached_input_tokens":5437492224,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":15431609,"reasoning_output_tokens":8829792,"total_tokens":5511861506}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-24T18:49:39.709Z","ordinal":302915,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a16f3c-d2bf-7c20-9739-5c085f717ae0","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-abab77b2-8017-42ab-80ee-1c30d875a6e6","process_id":"43674","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","gh pr view 200 --json comments --jq '.comments[-4:][] | {author:.author.login,createdAt,body}'"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"gh pr view 200 --json comments --jq '.comments[-4:][] | {author:.author.login,createdAt,body}'"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"{\"author\":\"mikeholownych\",\"body\":\"### CI Failure Finding: `cli/test/flight_exclude.test.ts`\\n\\nCI Run [40116819381](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40116819381) failed on `test-matrix (24)` ([Job 120939693293](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40116819381/job/120939693293)):\\n\\n```\\n✖ WorktreeManager ensures .nexus/ is excluded (29.568274ms)\\n  AssertionError [ERR_ASSERTION]: The expression evaluated to a falsy value:\\n    assert.ok(content.includes(\\\".nexus/worktrees/\\\"))\\n\\n✖ ensureGitExclude is idempotent and does not duplicate entries (41.185252ms)\\n  AssertionError [ERR_ASSERTION]: Idempotent exclude calls must not duplicate entries\\n```\\n\\n#### Cause\\nIn `cli/src/core/git_exclude.ts`:\\n```ts\\nfor (const { path: relativePath, rule } of protectedPaths) {\\n  ...\\n  if (isIgnored(relativePath)) continue;\\n```\\nOnce `.nexus/` is appended to `info/exclude`, Git considers all descendants (`.nexus/worktrees/...`, `.nexus/flights/...`) ignored. As a result, `isIgnored(relativePath)` returns `true` for the subsequent entries, skipping their addition to `info/exclude`.\\n`info/exclude` is left with only `.nexus/` rather than the complete set of required entries (`.nexus/`, `.nexus/worktrees/`, `.nexus/flights/`), failing the assertions in `cli/test/flight_exclude.test.ts`.\\n\\nA follow-up commit should ensure explicit rules for all protected paths are established while preserving the fail-closed and loop-prevention behavior.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-24T17:51:57Z\"}\n{\"author\":\"mikeholownych\",\"body\":\"**Independent review (claude-code) at exact head `18abef6e6e43d3b1a23f761128f808a5cd2bc7f5` (base `41b381dd`): REQUEST_CHANGES. Startup regression.**\\n\\nRemoving the outer `try/catch` makes `ensureGitExclude` throw on any write failure. It's called unconditionally from `new WorktreeManager(ws)` in the `Agent` constructor (agent.ts:1115), and also from `FlightRecorder`, `evaluator.ts:157` and `index.ts:964`. So Nexus now refuses to start, `--read-only` included, in any git repository whose `.git/info/exclude` the user can't write and that doesn't already ignore `.nexus/`. Typical cases are a checkout owned by someone else, a read-only mount, or a CI cache.\\n\\n**Reproduced** with a fresh `git init` repo and `chmod a-w .git/info/exclude`, calling `ensureGitExclude(repo)` through tsx:\\n- `18abef6e`: `THROW: EACCES: permission denied, open '.../.git/info/exclude'`\\n- `41b381dd` (base): `OK`\\n\\nFailing closed on a negation that can't be overridden is right in intent. But the commit path is already protected independently by #198's `:(top,exclude).nexus` pathspecs, so making startup fatal isn't needed to keep state out of commits. Suggested fix, either of:\\n1. In read-only mode, skip writing `info/exclude` entirely. Read-only shouldn't mutate `.git`.\\n2. Catch in the `WorktreeManager` and `FlightRecorder` constructors and fail at the point where `.nexus` state is actually written, with an actionable message.\\n\\nPlease add a regression test for the unwritable-exclude case.\\n\\nThe rest looks correct: the exact-rule plus later-negation logic, `check-ignore --no-index` exit-1 handling, and the leading-whitespace test.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-24T17:54:44Z\"}\n{\"author\":\"mikeholownych\",\"body\":\"**Suggested fix (claude-code), in place of the fatal `info/exclude` check: make `.nexus/` ignore itself.**\\n\\nWhen Nexus creates `.nexus/`, it writes `.nexus/.gitignore` containing `*`. pytest, ruff and mypy handle their cache directories this way.\\n\\n- **It changes nothing the user owns:** no tracked file and nothing under `.git/`. Writing to the repo's root `.gitignore` would create an uncommitted change that `/commit` would stage, and it would affect collaborators.\\n- **It fails at the real write, not at startup.** It's written only when `.nexus/` itself is being created, so a read-only repo or `--read-only` session never needs a `.git` write. That removes the startup regression.\\n- **It overrides the negation case this PR fails closed on.** A rule in a deeper `.gitignore` beats one in a parent directory, while `info/exclude` has the lowest priority of all. Verified in a scratch repo: with a root `.gitignore` of `!.nexus/` and `!.nexus/**`, `git add -A` staged only the root `.gitignore`, and `git check-ignore -v` reported `.nexus/.gitignore:1:*` for both `.nexus/flights/a.flightlog` and `.nexus/.gitignore`.\\n- **It works the same in worktrees and subdirectory workspaces**, with no `rev-parse --git-path` lookup.\\n\\nFiles that are already tracked are still covered at commit time by #198's `:(top,exclude).nexus` pathspecs, so the two together are complete. The existing `info/exclude` append can stay as a best-effort, non-fatal extra. This is a suggestion only; the slice remains with its owner.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-24T18:03:49Z\"}\n{\"author\":\"mikeholownych\",\"body\":\"**Re-review (claude-code) at exact head `89d7416fc5a54e3d0d9fd43d70192f12c540f93f` (base `4adc61ac`): REQUEST_CHANGES still stands.** This head is a rebase plus a stricter loop condition. The unwritable-`info/exclude` startup regression from my 17:54Z review is not addressed, and there's no reply on the thread yet.\\n\\n- `ensureGitExclude` still has no outer catch. `WorktreeManager` is still built unconditionally in the `Agent` constructor, so an `EACCES`/`EROFS` on `info/exclude` still aborts startup, `--read-only` included.\\n- The new `if (hasExactRule \\u0026\\u0026 isIgnored(...)) continue` **widens** the regression. Before, a path already ignored through `.gitignore` or `core.excludesFile` skipped the write. Now it writes to `info/exclude` unless the file contains the exact rule. So a repo that already ignores `.nexus/` in its tracked `.gitignore`, a common setup, now also fails to start when `info/exclude` is read-only.\\n\\nMerge criteria: startup must not depend on `.git` being writable. Please add a regression test (a fresh repo with read-only `info/exclude` where constructing `WorktreeManager` doesn't throw). The self-ignoring `.nexus/.gitignore` approach I suggested at 18:03Z covers both points and also handles the negation case.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-24T18:25:34Z\"}\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":435340449}},"started_at_ms":1792867779271,"completed_at_ms":1792867779707}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-24T18:49:40.892Z","ordinal":302916,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a16f3f-491c-7222-8a96-6ff9d32b28d4","call_id":"call_c20b8fe5f14f4f3f9f67342a168d5c24","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 2.7 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 1539)\nTotal output lines: 4\n\n{\"author\":\"mikeholownych\",\"body\":\"### CI Failure Finding: `cli/test/flight_exclude.test.ts`\\n\\nCI Run [40116819381](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40116819381) failed on `test-matrix (24)` ([Job 120939693293](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40116819381/job/120939693293)):\\n\\n```\\n✖ WorktreeManager ensures .nexus/ is excluded (29.568274ms)\\n  AssertionError [ERR_ASSERTION]: The expression evaluated to a falsy value:\\n    assert.ok(content.includes(\\\".nexus/worktrees/\\\"))\\n\\n✖ ensureGitExclude is idempotent and does not duplicate entries (41.185252ms)\\n  AssertionError [ERR_ASSERTION]: Idempotent exclude calls must not duplicate entries\\n```\\n\\n#### Cause\\nIn `cli/src/core/git_exclude.ts`:\\n```ts\\nfor (const { path: relativePath, rule } of protectedPaths) {\\n  ...\\n  if (isIgnored(relativePath)) continue;\\n```\\nOnce `.nexus/` is appended to `info/exclude`, Git considers all descendants (`.nexus/worktrees/...`, `.nexus/flights/...`) ignored. As a result, `isIgnored(relativePath)` returns `true` for the subsequent entries, skipping their addition to `info/exclude`.\\n`info/exclude` is left with only `.nexus/` rather than the complete set of required entries (`.nexus/`, `.nexus/worktrees/`, `.nexus/flights/`), failing the assertions in `cli/test/flight_exclude.test.ts`.\\n\\nA follow-up commit should ensure explicit rules for all protected paths are established while preserving the fail-closed and loop-prevention behavior.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-24T17:51:57Z\"}\n{\"author\":\"mikeholownych\",\"body\":\"**Independent review (claude-code) at exact head `18abef6e6e43d3b1a23f761128f808a5cd2bc7f5` (base `41b381dd`): REQUEST_CHANGES. Startup regression.**\\n\\nRemoving the outer `try/catch` makes `ensureGitExclude` throw on any write failure. It's called unconditionally from `new WorktreeManager(ws)` in the `Agent` constructor (agent.ts:1115), and also from `FlightRecorder`, `evaluator.ts:157` and `index.ts:964`. So Nexus now refuses to start, `--read-only` included, in any git repository whose `.git/info/exclude` the user can't write and that doesn't already ignore `.nexus/`. Typical cases are a checkout owned by someone else, a read-only mount, or a CI cache.\\n\\n**Reproduced** with a fresh `git init` repo and `chmod a-w .git/info/exclude`, calling `ensureGitExclude(repo)` through tsx:\\n- `18abef6e`: `THROW: EACCES: permission denied, open '.../.git/info/exclude'`\\n- `41b381dd` (base): `OK`\\n\\nFailing closed on a negation that can't be overridden is right in intent. But the commit path is already protected independently by #198's `:(top,exclude).nexus` pathspecs, so making startup fatal isn't needed to keep state out of commits. Suggested fix, either of:\\n1. In read-only mode, skip writing `info/exclude` entirely. Read-only shouldn't mutate `.git`.\\n2. Catch in the `WorktreeManager` and `FlightRecorder` constructors and fail at the point where `.nexus` state is actually written, with an actionable message.\\n\\nPlease …39 tokens truncated…-1 handling, and the leading-whitespace test.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-24T17:54:44Z\"}\n{\"author\":\"mikeholownych\",\"body\":\"**Suggested fix (claude-code), in place of the fatal `info/exclude` check: make `.nexus/` ignore itself.**\\n\\nWhen Nexus creates `.nexus/`, it writes `.nexus/.gitignore` containing `*`. pytest, ruff and mypy handle their cache directories this way.\\n\\n- **It changes nothing the user owns:** no tracked file and nothing under `.git/`. Writing to the repo's root `.gitignore` would create an uncommitted change that `/commit` would stage, and it would affect collaborators.\\n- **It fails at the real write, not at startup.** It's written only when `.nexus/` itself is being created, so a read-only repo or `--read-only` session never needs a `.git` write. That removes the startup regression.\\n- **It overrides the negation case this PR fails closed on.** A rule in a deeper `.gitignore` beats one in a parent directory, while `info/exclude` has the lowest priority of all. Verified in a scratch repo: with a root `.gitignore` of `!.nexus/` and `!.nexus/**`, `git add -A` staged only the root `.gitignore`, and `git check-ignore -v` reported `.nexus/.gitignore:1:*` for both `.nexus/flights/a.flightlog` and `.nexus/.gitignore`.\\n- **It works the same in worktrees and subdirectory workspaces**, with no `rev-parse --git-path` lookup.\\n\\nFiles that are already tracked are still covered at commit time by #198's `:(top,exclude).nexus` pathspecs, so the two together are complete. The existing `info/exclude` append can stay as a best-effort, non-fatal extra. This is a suggestion only; the slice remains with its owner.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-24T18:03:49Z\"}\n{\"author\":\"mikeholownych\",\"body\":\"**Re-review (claude-code) at exact head `89d7416fc5a54e3d0d9fd43d70192f12c540f93f` (base `4adc61ac`): REQUEST_CHANGES still stands.** This head is a rebase plus a stricter loop condition. The unwritable-`info/exclude` startup regression from my 17:54Z review is not addressed, and there's no reply on the thread yet.\\n\\n- `ensureGitExclude` still has no outer catch. `WorktreeManager` is still built unconditionally in the `Agent` constructor, so an `EACCES`/`EROFS` on `info/exclude` still aborts startup, `--read-only` included.\\n- The new `if (hasExactRule \\u0026\\u0026 isIgnored(...)) continue` **widens** the regression. Before, a path already ignored through `.gitignore` or `core.excludesFile` skipped the write. Now it writes to `info/exclude` unless the file contains the exact rule. So a repo that already ignores `.nexus/` in its tracked `.gitignore`, a common setup, now also fails to start when `info/exclude` is read-only.\\n\\nMerge criteria: startup must not depend on `.git` being writable. Please add a regression test (a fresh repo with read-only `info/exclude` where constructing `WorktreeManager` doesn't throw). The self-ignoring `.nexus/.gitignore` approach I suggested at 18:03Z covers both points and also handles the negation case.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-24T18:25:34Z\"}\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a16f3c-d2bf-7c20-9739-5c085f717ae0","create_time":1792867780.8923054}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
